var e={"12-01":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Prophet Nahum`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY PROPHET NAHUM`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 1st DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-01.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the prophet at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-01 entry. The page prints three stichera of the Theotokos to be sung first "if Alleluia be chanted at Matins" (a weekday of the Nativity Fast; ODS 2nd ed. Appendix A-II). No Glory of the saint, no aposticha and no aposticha rubric are printed at Vespers. At Matins: one canon (no acrostic is printed), the sessional hymn after Ode III, the kontakion after Ode VI with NO ikos, and no exapostilarion. Three ODE headings (VI, VIII, IX) are printed with every glyph doubled. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed: no prokeimenon, readings, alleluia or communion verse.`,troparion:{text:`Celebrating the memory of Thy prophet Nahum, O Lord, * through him we entreat Thee: ** Save Thou our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 Troparion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p1 end of Vespers`,tone:2},{locus:`p5 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy prophet, in Tone II`,tone:2},kontakion:{text:`Thy pure heart, enlightened by the Spirit, * became the dwelling-place of most splendid prophecy; * for it beheld things far off as though near. * Wherefore, we honor thee, ** O blessed and glorious prophet Nahum.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Kontakion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p4 after Ode VI`,tone:4},{locus:`p5 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared today ...`,tone:4},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy prophet, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`The grace of the Holy Spirit dwelt within thee, O prophet of God, and with its light made thee a most radiant lamp; and through thee preached to Nineveh the great things which were to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:3,spec_mel:`Great are the powers of Thy Cross ...`},{text:`Thou wast revealed to be a luminous cloud, O Nahum, prophet of God, letting fall a shower of divine knowledge; straightway giving the city of Nineveh the judgment of God to drink, for it was sickened with impiety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Great are the powers of Thy Cross ...`},{text:`As a partaker of incorrupt glory, ineffable renown, unutterable joy and divine sweetness, O divinely inspired Nahum, prophet of God, pray for us to the Master of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Great are the powers of Thy Cross ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`With the balm of thy prayer, O maiden, heal me who have been wounded by the fangs of the serpent and lie, barely alive, on the bed of despair, and make me a servant of thy Son and God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Knowing the weakness of my body, the sickness of my soul and the tribulation of my heart, grant unto me divine visitation, O all-immaculate Virgin, and save me, I pray, by thy fervent prayer.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I have surpassed all in mine offenses, O Lady; but, having cleansed me of them, O Virgin, entreat thy Son and God, that for the sake of thy mercy, I may be granted forgiveness at the judgment which is to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`O Virgin, beseech Him Who was born of thee, that He preserve thy flock unharmed from every temptation of our adversary, the devil, and strengthen us to fulfill all the will of thy Son, O maiden.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`A sword pierced thy heart, O most pure one, when thou didst behold thy Son upon the Cross; whereupon thou didst cry aloud: “Show me not to be childless, O my Son and my God, Thou Who hast kept me a Virgin even after I gave birth!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and this canon of the holy prophet, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and this canon of the holy prophet, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone V:`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:5,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Anointed by the divine Spirit, O God-pleasing Nahum, thou art enlightened by His grace; wherefore, honoring the divine foresight of thy mind, we bless thee, O most excellent one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Instructing thy soul from on high, the grace of the Spirit breathed prophetic activity into thee as is meet, and rendered thy tongue divinely inspired, O right wondrous prophet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Plucked with the plectrum of the Spirit, thou wast revealed to be an instrument hymning God Who loveth us, and proclaiming to all the impartiality of His divine judgment, O right glorious one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most blessed and all-pure Virgin, from misfortunes save those who with faith and love hymn thee as the pure Mother of God, quelling unrestrained savagery.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Through communion with the life-creating and divine Spirit thou didst become godly of soul; wherefore, at the behest of God thou wast purified beforehand, manifestly to declare to all things which are far distant, O divinely inspired one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O blessed God-seer, thou didst foresee the judgment of retribution for the impious enemies who with incurable wickedness offend the long-suffering, mercy and goodness of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, the Lover of mankind Who of old brought all things into existence, hath come forth from thy holy womb in His love for mankind, that He might deliver us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Shining with the radiance of the Spirit, thou didst proclaim the threat of destruction to the Ninevites, revealing the inescapable power of God, O divinely manifest one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-blessed Nahum, prophet of God, thou didst declare the righteous judgment of the Creator, and in prophecy didst declare grievous destruction to an adverse people.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The soul of Thy prophet, O good One, adorned with humility of mind, was supra-naturally caught up to the divine sight of Thee and the splendor of divine vision.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Mary, Sovereign Lady of creation who hast given birth to the King of all, who alone art all-hymned: By thy supplications show me to be free of the tyranny of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O wondrous prophet Nahum, thou wast deemed worthy of a blameless and pure life through the activity and enlightenment of the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst make thy flesh subject to thy governing mind, zealously appointing ascents in thy heart; wherefore, thou hast received divine revelations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Beyond visible honors are those who are honored by prophecy, for by the Holy Spirit the supremely good God speaketh through them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Not even a heavenly intelligence can truly hymn thee as is meet, O Mother of God; for thou hast given birth to the Creator Who is hymned by the hosts of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ye faithful, let us hymn him who was revealed as the temple of the grace of God and who, beyond understanding, became the most pure receptacle of divine revelations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Receiving the never-waning radiance of the divine Spirit, and acquiring a noble and godly mind, Nahum hath taught hymnody to the pious.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The noetic powers and all the generations of mankind ever glorify thee as the one who hast given birth to God, O blessed and all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having the godly prophet as the leader of our choirs, we honorably and divinely celebrate, chanting: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Recognizing thee as an instrument played by the Spirit, a divinely inspired flute, we call upon thee as our helper, chanting in hymnody: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord crowned thee a prophet, O wondrous one, and gave thee the grace to foretell things to come. To Him do we all chant: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The prophet beheld thee as an impassable gate, O most pure Virgin, which only One passed through. To Him do we all chant: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Forming a universal chorus in the furnace, * the children chanted to Thee, * the Fashioner of all: * All ye works praise ye the Lord, * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Deified by the immaterial radiance of the ruling Trinity, O prophet, thou chantest, rejoicing: Hymn the Lord, all ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Honoring thy sanctified memory in sacred manner, O prophet, we chant: Hymn the Lord, all ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, strengthen my soul which hath become paralyzed through transgressions and passions, that I may hymn Thy supremely glorious birthgiving throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst lead a truly angelic life on earth, and hast now made thine abode with the angelic choirs in the heavens, nigh unto the three-Sunned Light. Enjoying it, watch over those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O blessed prophet, we appoint thee as an intercessor before God for the world, in that thou hast boldness, that He grant to the faithful wondrously abiding and everlasting deliverance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-holy Bride of God, with wholly true names and divine eloquence we, the faithful, call thee the most pure Theotokos, in that thou hast given birth to God in two natures, and we proclaim thine honored birthgiving.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having acquired an intelligence unconfused by lowliness, O glorious Nahum, thou didst become a most pure receptacle of the divine Spirit, radiantly receiving His effulgence and illumining all; wherefore, we beseech thee: Pray thou for peace for the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy prophet, in Tone V`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word ...`,tone:5},{text:`O pure one, earnestly entreat the Lord God Who for our sake assumed flesh from Thee, that He take pity on us who have become corrupt in transgressions, and avert His wrath and anger from those who with faith unceasingly honor and praise His power and might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone V`,tone:5},{text:`Beholding Thee suspended on the Cross between two thieves of Thine own will, O Christ, Thy Mother, her womb rent asunder maternally, said: “O my sinless Son, how is it that Thou art unjustly nailed to the Cross like a malefactor, desiring to give life to the human race, in that Thou art compassionate?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}},{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy and righteous Philaret the Merciful`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY AND RIGHTEOUS PHILARET THE MERCIFUL OF AMNIA IN ASIA MINOR`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 1st DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-01A.pdf`,note:`Second file of 1 December. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the righteous one at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-01 entry. Unlike the first file (the Prophet Nahum) this service prints a Glory at Lord I have cried and a Glory at the aposticha, each with a Stavrotheotokion; the aposticha Stavrotheotokion is printed with no inline label. No aposticha stichera are printed ("After the Aposticha, Glory" is the only heading). One canon "with four Troparia"; kontakion and ikos after Ode VI; an exapostilarion with its Theotokion, no tone printed. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed. How the two services of the day are combined is not stated in either file.`,troparion:{text:`Emulating Abraham in faith and following after Job in patience, * O father Philaret, * thou didst distribute the blessings of the earth to the needy * and didst manfully endure the lack thereof. * Wherefore, Christ our God, the Judge of the contest, * hath crowned thee with a crown of light. ** Him do thou entreat, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the righteous one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the righteous one, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Truly thy most excellent commerce * is seen and judged to be wise * by all the divinely wise, * for thou didst forgive transitory debts, * seeking that which is lofty and eternal. * Wherefore, thou hast acquired eternal glory as is meet, ** O merciful Philaret.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the righteous one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:3},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the righteous one, in Tone III`,tone:3},ikos:{text:`Every virtue acquired for Christ's sake is comely and loving; fasting is honorable, and abstinence is pleasing to God; meekness doth inherit the earth, and humility leadeth to the heavens; repentance doth conquer every sin, and vision of God is granted to the pure of heart; yet charity and love are exalted above all of these, and, before all else, are received back from the righteous Judge at the dread tribunal of Christ; and on that day shalt thou hear from Him, O righteous one: Come, thou blessed of the heavenly Father, inherit eternal glory and the Kingdom prepared for thee from before the ages, O merciful Philaret!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the righteous one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Like a divinely adorned sun, in thy love thou hast shone upon the evil and the good, O merciful Philaret, enlightening the whole world with the rays of thy beneficence, enkindling the hearts of the faithful and moving them to praise thee. Wherefore, in a godly manner, we are now gladdened by thy memory and cry out to thee in compunction: Do thou ever pour forth thy mercy upon us who honor thy yearly festival with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8},{text:`Emulating the most perfect God, thou didst pour forth thy mercy upon all peoples. Wherefore, having impoverished thyself for the sake of Christ's love, thou didst thereby receive from Him recompense an hundredfold, shining forth like the sun in thy repose, O right loving Philaret, cease not to remember us who honor thy yearly festival with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Truly didst thou love as is meet, O Philaret wise in love, being a lover of truly good works. Illumining all with love patterned after God thou didst loan thy possessions to God, laying up the blessings of heaven as thy treasure; wherefore, we now glorify thee with a mighty voice, and cry out to thee with love: Rejoice, O Philaret, beloved of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_glory:{text:`When thou didst pass from the sight of those who loved thee, O Philaret, shining like the sun in thy repose, all the imperial city was shaken, hastening to thy bier in countless multitudes, and compassionate weeping was heard throughout the streets of the city, the orphaned and the poor fervently crying out to thee: To whom hast thou abandoned us, O merciful father? To whose care have we been entrusted? Yet cease not to concern thyself for our souls in the land of thine earthly sojourn.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone II`,tone:2},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Beholding Thee nailed to the Tree of the Cross. O Jesus, she who kneweth not wedlock said weeping: “O sweet Child, why hast Thou abandoned me who alone gave birth to Thee, O unapproachable Light of the beginningless Father? Hasten Thou, and glorify Thyself, that those who glorify Thy divine sufferings may receive divine glory!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:2,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,provenance_note:`The melody line is printed "Spec. Mel:" without the full stop after "Mel" (p1).`},aposticha_glory:{text:`O Philaret, emulator of the merciful God, in the days of thine earthly life thou didst do good unto all who came unto thee, spiritually perceiving their need, and distributing gold, silver and copper coins to each according to their needs. Wherefore, accept even me who now approach thee, and disdain not mine impoverished heart, but by thy gifts enrich it as much as thou seest fit, that I may cry out to thee in thanksgiving: Rejoice, O most merciful father Philaret!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`After the Aposticha, Glory ..., in Tone III`,tone:3},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`A sword pierced thy heart, O most pure one, * when thou didst behold thy Son upon the Cross; * whereupon thou didst cry aloud: * “Show me not to be childless, O my Son and my God, ** Thou Who hast kept me a Virgin even after birthgiving!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:3,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone III`}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`],canon_rubric:{text:`Canon to the holy and righteous Philaret the Merciful, with four Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I praise the sun-like remembrance of Philaret,” the composition of Valeria, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon to the holy and righteous Philaret the Merciful, with four Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I praise the sun-like remembrance of Philaret,” the composition of Valeria, in Tone II:`,composer:`Valeria`,acrostic:`I praise the sun-like remembrance of Philaret`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Come, O ye people, * let us sing a song to Christ our God, * Who divided the sea, * and made a way for the nation * which He had brought up out of the bondage of Egypt; * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Come ye, and let us celebrate today the memory of Philaret, radiant in our gladness, forming an harmonious chorus, for Christ God hath wondrously glorified him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst give thy property to God in loan, O Philaret, purchasing things eternal with that which is transitory, O wise one. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to receive a twofold reward, being crowned with honor on earth and with glory in heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Being truly a beacon of the love of Christ, in no wise extinguished by the winds of tribulations and temptations, with divine love thou hast enkindled the hearts of the faithful that they may cry to thee: Rejoice, O Philaret, beloved of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Unceasingly we cry unto thee, chanting the archangel's greeting: Rejoice! For thou art the cause of all joy, O Lady, who hast given birth unto the Salvation of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The bow of the mighty hath been broken * by Thy might, O Christ, * and the enfeebled * have girded themselves with power.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst open thy hands unto the poor and the wretched, and thy lips unto the praise of thy Creator and God, O righteous one. Wherefore, the gates of paradise have been opened unto thee with joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When thou didst beggar thyself for a while, when God tested thy love, O Philaret, in no wise despondent, thou didst place all thy trust in God, Who humbleth, exalteth and bestoweth wealth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst not set thy heart on fleeting riches, but established it in the will of God, O wise Philaret, truly well-beloved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice radiantly with Joachim, O righteous Anna, for in but a few days thou shalt joyously cry out: Lo! the most glorious root of the Tree of life hath been sown within me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard report of Thy dispensation, O Lord, * and have glorified Thee * Who alone lovest mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Distributing silver, gold, and copper coins unto the people who begged of thee, thou didst spiritually perceive the need of each, O merciful one, wisely managing the property of Christ, the almighty Master of the house.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The right loving and divinely wise Philaret showed himself to be a father to orphans and paupers and made love the dominion of his might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Bearing reproaches and insults with love, and deprived of thy wealth as was Job, thou didst cry aloud: The Lord is my God and my power, and He will set my feet toward perfection!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst come forth unto the salvation of Thy people, O Savior, willingly incarnate of the foreordained Virgin, whom we unceasingly glorify.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`The burning Ember was revealed to Isaiah, * and the Sun hath shone forth from the Virgin's womb, * granting the enlightenment of the knowledge of God * to those who in darkness have gone astray.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Being a kinsman of the emperor, O Philaret, thou didst not exalt thyself, honoring the King of kings in the guise of the orphaned and the wretched, and adorning thyself with love, the queen of the virtues.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Living in accordance with the Gospel, O Philaret, and bearing fruit an hundredfold for the Savior, thou didst show thyself to be a good and fertile land for Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast shown us an example of godly mercy, letting thy light shine before all in accordance with the word of the Lord, moving them to glorify the heavenly Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Magnifying the Theotokos, the Mother of Emmanuel, with unceasing hymns, and beholding Him Who was born of her, we cry out: God is with us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`O Master, hearkening unto the sound of entreaties * from a soul in pain, * do Thou deliver me from my grievous sins, * for Thou alone art the Cause of our salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst sanctify thy hands with the blessings of almsgiving, enkindling thy heart with mercy, putting an end to sorrows, comforting the afflicted and bringing joy to all in place of grief.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating Abraham the hospitable, O Philaret, thou didst honor the life-creating Trinity, which did not reveal itself to thee in the guise of three strangers, but in the guise of a multitude of the wretched to whom thou didst zealously minister.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Accepting tribulations from the hand of the Lord as blessings, thou didst show forth the patience of Job; and, tempest-tossed by tribulations and deprivation, thou didst bless God, inheriting the blessing of all the righteous.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We have no hope; there is no hope for us, if thou dost not help us and deliver us from misfortunes O Theotokos, by thine all-powerful intercession, which Thy mighty Son doth not disdain.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Of old the youths revealed themselves to be rhetors * with a supreme love for wisdom, * for from the depths of their God-pleasing souls, * they theologized with their lips as they sang: * O supremely divine God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having prepared a great feast, thou didst announce to thy household the coming of the King and His servants; and having filled thy house with the poor and wretched, thou didst cry aloud: Behold the servants of the King! In their midst hath the most divine King, the blessed God of our fathers, come invisibly unto me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Young men and elders, orphans and widows, blessed thy compassionate right hand, O Philaret, giving thanks unto Christ God for thee; and they cried out in compunction: O supremely divine God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, ye blessed of My Father, inherit the Kingdom, for ye ministered unto Me in the thirsty, the hungry and the sick! Thus shall Christ the Judge cry to the merciful at His dread Judgment. And at that time, O father, thou shalt be exceeding glad.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Theotokos, entreat thou the Lamb of God, that taketh away the sins of the world and hath washed Christians in His Blood, that He take away our sins; for, lo! with contrite heart we seek the countenance of Him Who is blessed by all creation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Disdaining the golden image, the thrice-blessed children, * beholding the immutable and living image of God, * chanted in the midst of the flame: * Let all existing creation hymn the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Emulating the merciful Samaritan, pass me not by, for I have fallen among thieves through my many sins, O Philaret, and pour forth the oil of thy prayers upon my grievously wounded soul. O merciful one, that, healed, I may thankfully chant unto God: Let all creation hymn the Lord Who is wondrous in His saints!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast revealed to us to be a wise gatherer of treasures which rust doth not corrupt, nor worm devour, and which thou dost lay up in the treasuries of heaven. Wherefore, thy heart doth abide there, and thy mouth, knowing not satiety, doth hymn the Lord throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`They, that of old did foolishly worship the golden calf, were condemned, and the most wise youths, that did not bow down before the golden image set up by the king in Babylon, were blessed; and thou, O Philaret, didst emulate the latter and not the former, joyously casting down the idol of wealth, and chanting: Let all creation hymn the Lord throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The cherubim bow down before thee in awe, O Theotokos, and the seraphim hymn thee unceasingly, for truly the King of heaven hath desired thy beauty, calling thee His own Mother. Wherefore, the people confess thee always, and unto the ages of ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thou art all desire, Thou art all sweetness, * O Word of God, Son of the Virgin, * God of gods, most holy Lord of the saints. * Wherefore, we magnify Thee * and her who hath given birth to Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Pouring forth thy wealth in faith, thou didst receive all of it back again from God. And receiving and nourishing the wretched with faith, thou didst receive God Himself. Having lived by faith, and through faith passed on to the eternal mansions, thou dost ever magnify God with the choirs of the righteous.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As an emulator of Abraham and entertainer of the beginningless Trinity, a servant and most intimate friend of the Master, thou didst have mercy on every creature, thereby inclining the mercy of God toward thyself. Wherefore, in thy mercy do thou also visit us who magnify thee with all our heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Enlighten us with thy love, O Philaret, who shone like the sun in thy righteous repose, that, radiantly rejoicing in thee, we may magnify God, Who is wondrous in His saints.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Young men and elders, rich men and paupers, monks and laymen, righteous and penitents: Come ye, let us fall down before the Mother of God, crying out to her: Ever preserve under thy protection, us who magnify thee O Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Come ye, and let us prepare a great feast, and a banquet of honor, thus didst thou say to thy household, O Philaret, announcing the arrival at thy house of the King Himself and His servants; and when the time was come, thou didst go forth to meet those who were invited: the poor and wretched of the imperial city; and to all who marveled, beholding them, thou didst cry aloud: These are the servants of the King, and in them the King Himself hath arrived! Truly, therefore, Christ, the King of kings, came invisibly to thy feast, and with love dost thou now serve Him in unwaning light, reclining with the saints at His banquet and chanting the awesome thrice-holy hymn sung by the seraphim.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p3-p4 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the righteous one, in Tone VII`,tone:7},{text:`Thou hast surpassed the hosts of heaven, * O blessed Theotokos, * for thou hast been shown to be a divine temple, * in that thou hast given birth unto Christ, ** the Savior of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VII`,tone:7},{text:`Ever protected by the Cross of thy Son, O Virgin, we escape the demons' assault. Wherefore, raising a song as is meet, we glorify thee, O all-hymned Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`Having outshone the sun in thy beneficence, O true lover of good, thou dost now clearly behold the Sun of righteousness. Him do thou unceasingly beseech, O merciful one, that He deliver us from misfortunes.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the righteous one`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`By thy mighty protection, O pure one, preserve all of us, thy servants, unharmed by the assaults of the enemy, for thee alone have we found to be a refuge in need.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-01A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-02":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Prophet Habbakuk`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY PROPHET HABBAKUK`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 2nd DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-02.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the prophet at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-02 entry. The page prints three stichera of the Theotokos to be sung first "if Alleluia be chanted at Matins". The Glory/Both now Theotokion and the Stavrotheotokion are both labelled "in the same melody" (Tone IV, of the stichera). No Glory of the saint, no aposticha and no aposticha rubric are printed at Vespers. At Matins: one canon, whose title is printed under the ODE I heading; the sessional hymn after Ode III; the kontakion after Ode VI with NO ikos; no exapostilarion. The kontakion is printed twice and the two sites differ in pointing and punctuation: the Liturgy site is stored at its own position. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`Celebrating the memory of Thy prophet Habbakuk, O Lord, * through him we entreat Thee: ** Save Thou our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:2},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy prophet, in Tone II`,tone:2},kontakion:{text:`Having announced to the world God's coming forth from the south, from the Virgin, * standing on divine watch O divinely eloquent Habbakuk, * thou didst receive report from the radiant angel: * and proclaimed the resurrection of Christ to the world. * Wherefore, in gladness we cry out to thee: ** Rejoice, O splendid adornment of the prophets!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`To thee, the champion leader ...`,tone:8},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy prophet, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`The wondrous Habbakuk, * having received the effulgence of the Spirit, * became wholly divine; * and, seeing the dishonesty of the judges * and their unjust judgment, * he was displeased, * exhibiting the rightness of the justice of Christ the Master * with divine love and fervent thought, ** and he burned as one justly angered.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Standing on divine watch, * the honored Habbakuk * heard the ineffable mystery * of Thy coming unto us, O Christ, * and he most openly prophesied * the proclamation of Thee, * foreseeing the most wise apostles as steeds * roiling the sea ** of the many nations of the gentiles.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Rejoicing in the Lord God thy Savior, * O divinely eloquent and glorious one, * and filled with gladness, * receiving the effulgence of heavenly radiance, * and noetically illumined * with deifying light, * by thy supplications deliver from perils and misfortunes * those who with faith celebrate ** thy most festive memory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`With the showers of the Holy Spirit * bedew thou my mind, O most pure one, * who hast given birth to Christ, * the infinite Drop of rain * Who with His compassions doth wash away * the iniquities of mortals. * Dry up the well-spring of my passions, * and grant unto me a torrent of sweetness ** by thine ever-vivifying prayer.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`I have been cast down beneath the ground, * slain by my sins * and my passions, spiritual and bodily; * wherefore, I am covered by the darkness of despair. * But raise me up now * to life incorruptible, * guiding me to the homeland on high, * where the voice of those who keep festival is heard, ** and where the light of Thy countenance shines, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, who held within thy womb the uncontainable God * Who, in His love for mankind, became a man * and received from thee our nature, * manifestly deifying it: * Disdain me not, * who now am afflicted! * But quickly take pity one me, * and free me from all the malice ** and harm of the evil one.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`Tens of thousands of times have I promised * to repent of mine offenses, O most pure one, * yet the cherished habits of mine evil ways * will not depart from me; * wherefore, I cry unto thee * and fall down, praying: * O Lady, rescue me from such tyranny, * guiding me to things that are higher, ** which are nigh unto salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in the same melody`},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon beholding Thee, the Lamb and Shepherd, upon the Tree, * the ewe-lamb who gave birth to Thee * lamented and maternally cried aloud to Thee: * “O my Son most desired, * How is it that Thou art suspended upon the Tree of the Cross, * O Long-suffering One? * How have Thy hands and feet * been pierced with nails by the iniquitous, O Word! ** And how hast Thou shed Thy blood, O Master?`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion, in the same melody`}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and one of the holy prophet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the holy prophet, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn thee, O blessed prophet Habbakuk,” the composition of Theophanes, in Tone IV:`,composer:`Theophanes`,acrostic:`I hymn thee, O blessed prophet Habbakuk`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`I hymn Thee, O Lord my God, * for Thou hast led Thy people out of the bondage of Egypt, * and hast drowned in the waters * the chariots and the might of Pharaoh.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Make me wise, O Lord my God, that I may hymn Thy divine prophet Habbakuk, and illumine my heart with Thy grace O good One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“How long, O Lord, will I cry unto Thee, and Thou wilt not hearken?” said the prophet “Wherefore hast Thou shown me the injustice of the judges?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thine entreaties, O prophet, deliver from misfortunes and cruel circumstances, those who piously celebrate thine honored memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`When the fullness of time drew nigh, our holy God appeared from thee, O Theotokos, becoming a man, that He might save mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The bow of the mighty hath waxed feeble * and the weak have girded themselves with strength: * therefore is my heart established * in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Raised on high by elevating thy gaze unto God, and illumined by the effulgence emanating from Him, thou didst foresee the form of things to come, O thou divinely revealed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Possessing every virtue, and hating all wickedness of mind, O all-blessed one; thou didst justly revile the iniquitous.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As one pure, O right wondrous one, and entrusted with speech by the Holy Spirit, thou didst clearly prophesy the fulfillment of things to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-pure one, thou hast been revealed to be the mountain overshadowed by the virtues, from whence the Master hath issued forth as a servant, to free mankind from slavery.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Proclaiming the advent of Thine appearance on earth, O Christ God, * the prophet cried aloud with gladness: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast shown to be radiant in virtue O divinely inspired one, and announced the never-waning Light. To Him do we now cry out with faith: Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The most radiant grace of the Spirit, dwelling abundantly within thee, O all-wise one, made thee a prophet announcing the Savior unto all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Instructed by hearing of the Almighty, O wondrous one, thou wast seized with reverent fear, and, understanding His words, thou wast filled with awe.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Word Who is equally everlasting with the Father described thee O Virgin, as the ark of witness, truly containing the Bread of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast caused the light to shine, * who hast made bright the dawn and revealed the day; * glory be to Thee, glory be to Thee, * O Jesus Thou Son of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The honored Church doth now see the Sun lifted up upon the Tree, as Thou didst foretell, O most sacred Habbakuk.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving wings to thy mind, thou didst stand watch, O most noetically rich prophet, perceiving the advent of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I rejoice aloud in God my Savior and am glad!” didst thou cry aloud, O wise and all-blessed Habbakuk.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Weighed down by the fetters of my many transgressions, I flee to thee, O Lady Theotokos. Save me, thou boast of the faithful!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Prefiguring Thy three-day burial * prophet Jonah praying in the belly of the sea-monster cried aloud: * Deliver me from corruption * O Jesus Thou King of hosts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`God incarnate hath come from the south as thou didst foretell, O thrice blessed Habbakuk, and, radiantly enlightened by Him, thou hast illumined the world with light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O God, by the supplications of the honored and divinely wise Habbakuk illumine the souls of those who hymn Thee, for by divine inspiration Thou didst enlighten his mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thine announcement and the power of thy divine words passed over all the ends of the earth, O divinely eloquent one, prophesying to us the divine advent of the Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin, thou hast given birth to the Son, Who is consubstantial with the Father, is clearly understood to be with Him Who begat Him outside time, and Who in the latter times assumed flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Of old the children of Abraham in Babylon * trampled down the flame of the furnace, * crying aloud with hymns: * O God of our Fathers, blessed art Thou.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Taught understanding which transcendeth all telling, and prophesying concerning the abundantly radiant lamp, O blessed one, thou dost now cry aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ, Whom thou didst glorify, hath given thee thrice-radiant effulgence and a share in never-waning glory, for thou didst cry aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Among all generations thou hast been revealed to be the blessed Virgin Mother who, in a manner past understanding, hast given birth to the incarnate Word; wherefore, we hymn thee, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O all ye works of God and all creation, * bless ye the Lord, * ye venerable and humble of spirit * chant ye and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Illumined with the light of the threefold Sun, O most excellent one, thou wast deemed worthy of divine and supra-natural visions, crying aloud: supremely exalt God throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Drinking from the torrent of sweetness, full of immaterial vision, partaking of the glory and eminence of the prophets, rejoicing, thou dost hymn God throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divine and honored is the comeliness of the prophet Habbakuk! For, joining chorus with the angelic hosts, rejoicing he hymneth Christ throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast truly shown to be the Mother of Him Who shone forth from the Father before all ages; for thou alone wast more holy than all others. Thee, the pure one, do we supremely exalt throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thy birthgiving was revealed to be incorrupt, * God came forth from thy womb, * and He appeared upon earth in mortal flesh * and dwelt among mankind; * Wherefore we all magnify thee, O Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy memory shineth forth, O prophet, emitting the radiant effulgence of thy divine eloquence, thy mystic teachings and prophecies, for those who honor thee, O most blessed Habbakuk.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having preached the Lord of glory and clearly foretold His advent from the holy Virgin, O divinely blessed Habbakuk, thou wast filled with gladness, seeing it come to pass.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`All the prophets rejoice in gladness on this thy joyous day, O divinely wise one, sharing in thy joy and divine glory. And, praying with them, save those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the sprinkling of thy compassions, O pure maiden, wash away the defilement of my soul, and unceasingly cause torrents of tears to pour forth in me, staunching the torrents of my passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Thou didst stand on divine watch, O blessed and divinely inspired Habbakuk, and with the eyes of prophecy perceived the coming of God; wherefore, thou didst cry out with fear: O Lord, I have heard of Thy dread coming, and I hymn Thee, Who hast willed to bear the flesh of clay which Thou didst receive from the Virgin!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn; in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Having been lifted up ...`,tone:4},{text:`O Theotokos, fleeing to thy divine protection after God, * I humbly fall down and beseech thee: * Have mercy, O most pure one, * for my sins have submerged my being, * and trembling O Lady, I fear the torments to come, * O pure one, entreat thy Son, ** that I may be delivered from them.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`She who in latter times gave birth to Thee in the flesh, * O Christ Who wast begotten of the beginningless Father, * when she saw Thee hanging upon the Cross, cried out: * “Woe is me, O Jesus most beloved! * How is it that Thou Who art worshipped as God by the angels, * art now crucified by iniquitous men? ** I hymn Thee, O Long-suffering One!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`liturgy_kontakion`],liturgy_kontakion:{text:`Having announced to the world God's coming forth from the south, from the Virgin, * standing on divine watch O divinely eloquent Habbakuk, * thou didst receive report from the radiant angel, and proclaimed the resurrection of Christ to the world. * Wherefore, in gladness we cry out to thee: ** Rejoice, O splendid adornment of the prophets!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02.pdf`,locus:`p7 Kontakion at Liturgy`},sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}}},{kind:`saint`,name:`our venerable fathers John, Heraclemon, Andrew and Theophilus of Egypt`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE VENERABLE JOHN, HERACLEMON, ANDREW AND THEOPHILUS OF EGYPT`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 2nd DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER (AND THE 12th DAY OF THE MONTH OF JUNE)`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-02A.pdf`,note:`Second file of 2 December. The heading reads "THE 2nd DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER (AND THE 12th DAY OF THE MONTH OF JUNE)": the same service serves both dates. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the venerable fathers at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-02 entry. A Glory at Lord I have cried and a Glory at the aposticha are printed; the Theotokia are named and not printed, and the rubric after the first Glory reads "Glory ..., Both now ..." though a Glory precedes it. One canon, no composer named; one sessional hymn with no Theotokion; kontakion and ikos. "After the Exapostilarion, Glory" prints a hymn, but no exapostilarion itself is printed. The troparion is the general one of the fathers, with no name in it. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`O God of our fathers, * ever deal with us according to Thy meekness. * Take not Thy mercy from us, * but by the prayers of these saints ** direct our life in peace.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Troparion of the venerable fathers`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p1 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable fathers, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Come ye, let us hymn those who were brethren in the flesh, yet more so in spirit: * the glorious John with the faithful Heraclemon, wondrous Andrew, and Theophilus, beloved of God. * For, lo! loving the cruel life of the desert, they attained unto the longed-for heavenly homeland; ** where, abiding now in blessedness, they pray with boldness for our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the venerable fathers`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:8},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable fathers, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},ikos:{text:`Tell us, O venerable ones, what is the sweetness of the desert? What is the joy of a life of silence? What is the consolation of labors day and night? For we behold you as having a radiant countenance, resplendent with exceeding great joy. Wherefore, ye teach us to walk the narrow path, and lead us to the mansions of eternal repose, where with you all those who have been pleasing to Christ now pray with boldness for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_glory`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the venerable fathers, in Tone VIII,`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Oh, wondrous the life! * Oh, great the endurance! * The right fruitful trees of paradise * flourished in the desert, * springing forth from a single root * were grafted onto the one true Vine, * O John, Heraclemon, Andrew and Theophilus, * fill ye with the sweetness of spiritual fruit ** us who honor and hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`,tone:8,provenance_note:`The melody line is printed "Spec. Mel:" without the full stop after "Mel" (p1).`},{text:`Enduring the noonday sun in the desert, * ye freed yourselves from the burning heat of the passions, * and by your thirst for salvation * overcoming natural thirst, * ye discovered a fountain overflowing unto eternal life * and gave drink to your souls with the streams thereof. * Wherefore, by your prayers * bedew our desiccated souls, ** granting us to bring forth the fruits of the virtues.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`Emulators of the Forerunner * and imitators of the feats of Elijah, * offspring of the desert, * glory and adornment of fasters, * by your life ye amazed the bodiless ones. * Wherefore, ye have become fellow citizens with the incorporeal ones; * and now, therefore, from heaven watch ye over those who struggle spiritually * and show them speedy aid, ** guiding them to the eternal mansions.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Laying aside today all the cares of life, come ye, let us make haste to the temple of the Lord, celebrating the radiant memory of the venerable ones; and having been well instructed in their life, let us purify our senses and sanctify our lips with prayer; and sighing over our offenses from the depths of our hearts, let us cry out to our Savior, Jesus most sweet: By their prayers, O Christ God, have mercy upon us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VII`,tone:7},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},aposticha_glory:{text:`With what praises shall we honor you, O venerable ones? What hymns shall we sing to you, who from your youth gave your life over to Christ, emulating the feats of him who is the greatest of those who born of woman? The mind is not able, and every tongue that speaketh boastful words falls silent, yet our hearts are inflamed all the more with eagerness; wherefore, we entreat you, instead of hymns accept our faith and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`On the Aposticha, Glory ..., in Tone V`,tone:5}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion_glory`,`exapostilarion_closer_rubric`],canon_rubric:{text:`The Canon of the venerable fathers, the acrostic whereof is: “We glorify your holy memory, O venerable ones,” in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`The Canon of the venerable fathers, the acrostic whereof is: “We glorify your holy memory, O venerable ones,” in Tone VIII:`,acrostic:`We glorify your holy memory, O venerable ones`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`The wonderworking staff of Moses, * striking and dividing the sea in the figure of a cross, * once drowned pharaoh the pursuing charioteer, * while it saved the fleeing people of Israel * as they fled on foot, * chanting a hymn unto God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Behold now, what is so good or so joyous as for brethren to dwell together in unity? Attentive to this divinely inspired word, and working out your salvation together, ye persisted in prayers and labors in singleness of mind, chanting with one mouth and one heart unto the consubstantial and undivided Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Purchasing that which is eternal with that which is transient and corruptible, ye brought about a blessed exchange in your earthly life; for, lo! ye labored and struggled, that ye might obtain heavenly rest, and loved the desert, that ye might delight in the garden of paradise; ye bore the burning heat of noonday, that ye might abide eternally in a place of refreshment; and endured hunger and thirst, that ye might give drink to your souls with the streams of immortality, nourishing yourselves with the most sweet sight of the countenance of God, and chanting with the angels a new hymn unto Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Departing from this sin-loving world as did the chosen people from Egypt, and delivered from the demonic hordes as from the warriors of Pharaoh, ye reached the Thebaid, strengthened by the right hand of God; and laboring there ascetically, ye made your abode in the wilderness. Wherefore, delighting now, not in an earthly promised land, but in heaven, ye chant to Christ God a hymn of victory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art an aid to those who travel the narrow way, O Theotokos, for by thee are the afflicted strengthened and in thee do the weak become strong; in thee do the saints boast and by thee are sinners saved. We hymn thine ineffable tender compassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Christ fortify me on the rock of Thy commandments, * Thou who in the beginning didst establish the heavens with understanding * and didst establish the earth upon the waters, * for there is none holy save Thee, O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O venerable ones, establish us in the love of Christ, wherein ye were established by God, that having loved our neighbor as ourselves and forgiving the trespasses of those who trespass against us, we may obtain forgiveness of our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ye were revealed to be young in years, but elders in understanding, O venerable ones, when, forsaking all the beauties of this world and looking toward the end of all things, ye made your abode in the desert; that there following after Christ with diligence, ye might, by the narrow and exceedingly sorrowful path, rather than by the most opportune one, enter in unto the Kingdom of heaven. Wherefore, ye now abide in the mansions of paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Taught by faith and the fear of God, protected by the grace of the Holy Spirit, having Christ alone as Instructor after the repose of your abba, ye acquired sure salvation, and amazed the angels with your great patience. Wherefore, be ye now our instructors, and teach us to fulfill the commandments of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art the unceasing amazement of the angels, and the never-ending routing of demons, and the salvation of mankind, O all-immaculate Virgin. In thee do we confidently boast. With thee do we lay low our adversaries, and through thee do we hope to obtain eternal life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, art my strength and Thou art my power, * Thou art my God and Thou art my joy, * Thou Who, while never leaving the bosom of Thy Father, * hast visited our poverty. * Therefore with the prophet Habbakuk I cry unto Thee, * “Glory to Thy power, O Lover of mankind!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Wishing to flee the wide path that leadeth to destruction, O venerable ones, ye chose the desert as a habitation for yourselves and adopted voluntary poverty, laying up spiritual treasure in heaven. Wherefore, ye discovered Christ, the priceless Pearl, and ye glorified His most wondrous economy for you.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The ranks of angels were amazed, beholding mortal men who took upon themselves the ministry of the angels, and were nourished most wondrously with the most pure Body and Blood of Christ; and with awe cried out to God: Glory to Thy loving-kindness, O Lover of mankind! Glory to Thy condescension, O Christ! Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ, Thou didst glorify Thy servants, bestowing strength upon them to confront the demons, ever strengthening them for their struggles, and especially, sending them an angel, mystically granting them the divine communion of Thy Body and Blood. Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art truly the daughter of mortal Adam, and the Mother of God, O Theotokos, for thou hast given birth ineffably to thy Creator and Lord, Who hath redeemed the generation of Adam from corruption. Glory to the ineffable counsel of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Light never-waning, * why hast Thou turned Thy face from me * and why hath the alien darkness surrounded me, * wretched though I be? * But do Thou guide my steps I implore Thee * and turn me back towards the light of Thy commandments.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Contemplating the ineffable light of Tabor with noetic eyes, dwelling on earth in the flesh, but in spirit with the angels, ye truly became citizens of heaven, O venerable ones. Wherefore, from an angel ye received the holy Mysteries of Christ. Honored, therefore, on earth by God with such a concern for you, what glories have ye now been deemed worthy of in heaven? But having boldness before the Holy Trinity, pray ye unceasingly for us sinners, that He enlighten and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In the firmament of heaven four noetic stars have been revealed unto us, shining brightly with rays of the virtues, driving away the oppressive gloom of sin: our vener-able and God-bearing fathers John, Heraclemon, Andrew and Theophilus. Wherefore, by their supplications, O Christ God, grant us cleansing from our sins, for Thou art compassionate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Driving away the dark forms of the evil spirits with the Name of Christ, and striking them with the precious Cross as with a sword of fire, ye were revealed to be conquerors of temptations and deception. Wherefore, having shone forth like the sun with the righteous in the Kingdom of heaven, ye delight in the vision of the most radiant countenance of God. Beseech Christ God, O venerable ones, that He grant us might against all the power of the enemy and save us, for He is the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Enlighten our hearts which have been darkened by evil passions, O all-hymned one, for thou art the Mother of the Sun of righteousness and Mother of the never-waning Light, that, illumined by His rays and shining with the radiance of undimmed glory, we may put on the bright vesture of salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Cleanse me, O Savior, * for many are mine iniquities; * lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee, * for unto Thee have I cried, * and Thou hast hearkened unto me, * O God of my salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Pondering your life, which equaled that of the angels, O venerable ones, we are beset by fear and trembling. How did ye survive in the impassable desert? How did ye endure burning heat and cold, hunger and thirst? How did ye put to shame demonic assaults? We hymn your struggles, we honor your repose, and we beseech you to ask of Christ the forgiveness of our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Bound by bonds of natural love, ye were united by the most mighty bonds of divine love; brethren in the flesh, ye became brethren in Christ, and with one mouth ye offered up prayer to the Triune God; wherefore, inseparable, ye dwell in the heavens. Pray ye now for us sinners, O venerable ones, that having eternally put aside all evil, we may learn unfeigned brotherly love, and thus fulfill the foremost commandment of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In Christ-like fashion ye crucified your flesh with its passions and lusts, O venerable ones; wherefore, having ascended to the heights of dispassion, ye have become citizens of heaven. And now, dwelling with the bodiless ones, pray ye boldly, O holy ones, that having lifted up our mind which hath fallen, and having raised up our earthly eyes from this earthly vale, we may cry out to God from the depths of our degradation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`From the foul pit of vile passions and vain imaginings lead us up, O all-immaculate Virgin, for thou art an inexhaustible treasury of purity and an abyss of tender compassion. Through thee strength against the demons is bestowed; through thee victory over the passions is granted; through thee do we who call upon thy most pure name hope to be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe * of God's condescension; * for which sake the youths in the furnace, * dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Truly ye were virgins, desert-dwellers, fasters, ascetics, earthly angels and heavenly men, O venerable ones, instructed by the grace of the Holy Spirit, to Whom we now cry out, honoring your memory: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Consuming the passions, like a dry branch, with the fire of prayer, and moistening your hearts with the dew of tears, tried like gold in the furnace of patience, ye shone forth with rays of the virtues, O venerable ones. Amazed thereby, we cry out to the Maker of all, Whom ye glorified by your life: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A brother helped by a brother is like a strong city, thus, O venerable ones, bearing one another's burdens, and struggling in unity of mind, offering prayer to God with one mouth, delivered from the gaping jaws of hell as from the lions' jaws, like the children saved of old in the furnace, ye cried aloud: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Theotokos, who remained unconsumed by the fire of the Divinity and quenched the furnace of deception in the world, who bore in thy womb Him that is borne upon high by the cherubim: With the dew of thy prayers quench thou the flame of the passions, that saved by thee we may unceasingly cry out to thy Son: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In his wrath the Chaldean tyrant made the furnace blaze, * with heat fanned sevenfold for the servants of God; * but when he perceived that they had been saved by a greater power * he cried aloud to the Creator and Redeemer; * “Ye children bless, ye priests praise, * ye people, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages”.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Emulating John, the Forerunner of the Lord, ye took up your abode in the desert, learning true repentance in silence, and cutting the tares of the passions down to the root with the sickle of the fear of God, that ye be not cast into everlasting fire like a dry branch. Hence, like fruitful olive trees ye flourished, and full of good works, transplanted from this earthly and burdensome life, ye praise God for ever in the paradise of sweetness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Following Elijah of the fiery chariot in your life, abiding in the desert, more than he were ye nourished most gloriously. For a raven brought him tangible food, but an angel of the Lord placed before you the true Body and Blood of Christ. Oh, strange mystery! Oh, the good will of God! May His Name be blessed throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Your prayer was like unto a pillar of fire, reaching from the earth to the heavens, O venerable ones. For, lo! it was offered from hearts consumed by divine fire, with oneness of soul and unity of mind. Wherefore, instruct us in prayer, O holy ones, that having acquired boldness before God, we may glorify the Father, and the Son, and the Holy Spirit throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Our hearts are inflamed with the fire of divine love for thee, O Virgin, yet we know not the fullness of thy praise, O all-hymned one; for every tongue that speaketh boastful words doth fail, desiring to make known thy greatness, O Queen. Yet, O most good one, with silent mouths and yet more silent hearts may we be acceptable unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Heaven was stricken with awe, * and the ends of the earth were filled with amazement, * for God hath appeared in the flesh, * and thy womb was rendered more spacious than the heavens. * Wherefore, the ranks of men and of angels * magnify thee as the Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having acquired the-guilelessness of Abel and the chastity of Joseph, the faith of Abraham, and the meekness of David, O venerable ones, ye have been rightfully numbered among the choir of the righteous. But knowing that you live even after death and yet more, are concerned for our salvation, we magnify you with heartfelt love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Glorifying your most festive memory, and faithfully hymning your ascetic struggles, may we not be forgotten by you, O holy ones. Be ye mindful of us sinners when ye raise your venerable hands on high to God, praying for the whole world; that, deemed worthy of divine gifts through your mediation, we may unceasingly magnify God Who is wondrous in His saints.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With love we honor your memory, O venerable ones, and with faith we venerate your ascetic feats; with fear we praise your great patience. Wherefore, we earnestly pray: Remember us, O blessed ones, who stand at the throne of the King of glory, fulfilling our humble requests which are of benefit, that we may magnify your aid and God's love for mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst name for Thyself a Mother, O Savior, to whom Thou didst give the human race by adoption. Be Thou well pleased to obey her, O Christ, when, praying for us sinners, she boldly stretcheth forth her most pure hands to Thee, our God; and save us, for the sake of the Theotokos, that with joy and love we may magnify her intercession.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Traversing the desert of the virtues, and tormented by spiritual thirst, we have found you to be like the four rivers of paradise, O venerable ones; for upon all who follow your life ye abundantly pour forth streams of grace, and bedew withered hearts by your prayers, and with joy ye give drink to the souls of the faithful. Now celebrating your most glorious memory, we humbly entreat you, O blessed ones, that by your fervent supplications ye rain down upon us the mercy of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the venerable fathers, in Tone VII`,tone:7}],exapostilarion_glory:{text:`Desert-loving doves, swallows of heaven, announcing the spring of the Spirit in the world, taking flight from the winter of sin to the summer of dispassion, ever borne up on the wings of divine desire, taking shelter from the burning noonday heat of the passions beneath the shadow of the Tree of the Cross, ye thereby avoided the talons of the cruel hawk; wherefore, abiding now in the heavenly garden, ye praise God, the Creator of all, for ever.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 After the Exapostilarion, Glory`},sourceLabel:`After the Exapostilarion, Glory`},exapostilarion_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-02A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Both now rubric`}}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-03":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Prophet Zephaniah`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY PROPHET ZEPHANIAH`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 3rd DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-03.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the prophet at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-03 entry. The page prints three stichera of the Theotokos to be sung first "if Alleluia be chanted at Matins". The Glory/Both now Theotokion and the Stavrotheotokion are both labelled "in the same melody" (Tone IV, of the stichera). No Glory of the saint, no aposticha and no aposticha rubric are printed at Vespers. At Matins: one canon of two troparia and a Theotokion to the ode; the sessional hymn after Ode III; the kontakion after Ode VI with NO ikos; no exapostilarion. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`Celebrating the memory of Thy prophet Zephaniah, O Lord, * through him we entreat Thee: ** Save Thou our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:2},{locus:`p6 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy prophet, in Tone II`,tone:2},kontakion:{text:`Thou wast shown to be brilliant by the divine Spirit, O prophet Zephaniah, * proclaiming the coming of God: * Rejoice exceedingly, O daughter of Zion! * Proclaim Him, O Jerusalem! ** Behold, thy King cometh to save mankind!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy prophet`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:4},{locus:`p6 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy prophet, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared ...`,tone:4},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy prophet, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`As a divine prophet, * a proclaimer and herald * of the words of God, * having received the radiance of the splendor of the Godhead * through the purity of thy mind, * thou wast revealed to be * a divinely inspired mouth of the Spirit. * Proclaiming things shown to thee by Him, * and relating to all the nations * the salvation given to mankind * and the kingdom of Christ, O all-honored one, * entreat Him ** to save and enlighten our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`},{text:`O divinely inspired one, who shinest forth, * as is meet, in the vision of God, * honored with a chief place * among the prophets and with grace, * and deemed worthy of divine blessedness, * possessed now of thy boldness toward the supremely good One * and sympathy, * cease thou never to pray * on behalf of those who praise thee with faith * and honor thee as one of godly eloquence, * honorable and pleasing to God, * that He deliver us from misfortunes ** and save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`},{text:`Thou hast shown forth, O Immortal One, * Thy prophet * as an animate cloud * pouring forth water unto life which is truly everlasting, * having sent him forth * and richly bestowed upon him the all-holy Spirit, * Who is consubstantial with Thee, the Almighty Father, * and Thy Son, * Who shone forth from Thine Essence, * whereby he prophesied the saving Advent * of Christ our God ** and proclaimed salvation to all the nations.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`As the intercessor for our whole race, * O most immaculate Birthgiver of God, * from every attack of the enemy * save those who piously worship thine Offspring; * for we have all now acquired thee * as a help, refuge and confirmation, * and a mediatress before Christ, the Lord and Master. * Him do thou entreat, we pray thee, * that He grant the world peace * and remission of sins ** unto those who have re-course to thy protection.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Behold, I expose to thee the sores of my soul * and show thee the grievous stripes * which the robbers, * my wicked thoughts * and the tumults of the demons, * have inflicted upon me. * O all-immaculate Lady, * who hast given birth * unto the Healer of men's souls and bodies, * do thou grant me healing thereof, * pouring forth the oil * of thy tender compassion and goodness, ** unto the good disposition of salvation and health.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I do not cover my wicked deeds, * for, wretch that I am, * I have acquired all things which God hateth: * I have defiled my flesh, spirit and mind * by impious thoughts, * vile deeds and words; * with tongue I condemn sinners, * while I myself commit worse things, O Birthgiver of God. * Grant me correction of all these things, * that, having rid myself of mine evil habits, * I may fall down and weep * over what I have wickedly done ** in the course of my life.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p2 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`In that I have fallen into the abyss of many offenses, * wretch that I am, * because of my slothfulness, despondency and ignorance, * I am now held fast by despair. * Be thou my help and purification * and my salvation, O most pure one, * readily granting me consolation; * and I beseech thee, implore and fall down before thee, * and with faith cry out to thee, * that I not utterly appear ** to be the plaything of the deceiver.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in the same melody`},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Lament Me not, O Mother, * beholding thy Son and God hanging upon the Tree, * Who suspended the earth freely upon the waters * and fashioned all creation; * for I shall arise and glorify Myself, * and shall break the might of the kingdom of hell, * destroy its power, * and deliver those who have been bound * by its villainy, in that I am compassionate; * and I shall lead them to my Father, ** as I love mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Or this Stavrotheotokion, in the same melody`}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, that of the holy prophet, the acrostic whereof is: “May the glory of Zephaniah illumine me,” by Theophanes, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, that of the holy prophet, the acrostic whereof is: “May the glory of Zephaniah illumine me,” by Theophanes, in Tone VI:`,composer:`Theophanes`,acrostic:`May the glory of Zephaniah illumine me`,tone:6,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`When Israel walked on foot in the sea as on dry land, * on seeing their pursuer Pharaoh drowned, * they cried: * Let us sing to God * a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`We beseech thee, O prophet, who standest before the throne of God, that thou earnestly entreat Him to grant enlightenment to us who with faith hymn thine honored memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a divine instrument containing enlightenment and the gifts of the divine Spirit, O all-wise Zephaniah; wherefore, rejoicing, we, the faithful, call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Sun which shone forth from thy holy womb, O Lady, illumineth all the earth with most brilliant rays; and enlightened thereby, we honor thee as the Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`There is none as holy as Thou, * O Lord my God, * who hast exalted the horn of Thy faithful O good One, * and strengthened us upon the rock * of Thy confession.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He Who, as God, seeth all things, O blessed and right wondrous one, in a godly manner manifestly revealed and showed thee the knowledge of the future and what is to be.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having strengthened thy mind with the boldness of piety, O blessed one, thou didst bow thyself down before the divine Spirit and received divine inspirations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Behold, with faith all generations call thee blessed who, in a manner transcending nature, hast given birth in the flesh within time unto the timeless Word, yet remained a virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Christ is my power, * my God and my Lord, * the holy Church divinely singeth, * crying with a pure mind, * keeping festival in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The Lord of all appeared to us in accordance with thy prophecy, O blessed one, calling all to knowledge of Him; and freeing us from slavery.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined by grace, thou didst make proclamation, speaking to those who bow low to labor beneath the one yoke, who follow the Faith and serve the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-pure Mary, still thou the tumult of the passions of my mind and the storm of temptations, as thou hast given birth unto the Wellspring of dispassion, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Illumine with Thy divine light, I pray, O good One, * the souls of those who with love rise early to pray to Thee, * that they may know Thee, O Word of God, * as the true God, * Who recalleth us from the darkness of sin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`By thine entreaties, O blessed and glorious prophet, convert me from unrighteousness to virtue, and from the captivity of the passions lead me to the light of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having enlightened thy soul with the comeliness of the virtues, thou didst show it to be pleasing to the splendors of the divine Spirit, by Whom thou hast been enriched by the grace of prophecy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In many forms the words of the prophets proclaim thy birthgiving, O most pure one; and we, beholding now their fulfillment, truly declare thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Beholding the sea of life surging with the tempest of temptations, * I run to Thy calm haven, and cry to Thee: * Raise up my life from corruption, * O greatly merciful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Receiving the rays of the Spirit through revelation, O glorious one, like a mirror thou didst reflect the splendors of divine prophecy upon the world, prophesying the things of the future as though they were present.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The King hath come! Rejoice and adorn thyself, O Zion, beholding Him! He hath enlightened the world with the brilliant rays of His divinity and hath put the delusion of the demons to shame!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thy womb the Only-begotten of the Father united Himself to flesh of clay; He Who is One Person of two natures issued forth from thee without corruption, preserving thy pure virginity intact, O all-hymned one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`An angel made the furnace bedew the holy children. * But the command of God consumed the Chaldeans * and prevailed upon the tyrant to cry: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy memory hath shone upon the world like the sun, illumining with the grace of thy prophecy those who with faith chant together: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Revealed to be like a cloud heavy laden with showers, thou didst let fall upon us a shower of divine knowledge from the springs of salvation, O blessed one, whereby we are enlightened to cry out: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring in His divine will to restore mankind, the Word, Who of old gave existence to all things, made His abode within thy womb, O pure and blessed one, who hast given birth to God in the flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst make flame bedew the holy children, * and didst burn the sacrifice of a righteous man with water. * For Thou alone, O Christ, dost do all as Thou willest, * Thee do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Offered wholly to the Almighty, thou wast instructed in the mysteries by way of foreknowledge, teaching the Gentiles in accordance with God's providence. Wherefore, we hymn thee, O divinely eloquent prophet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Offer up a hymn of supplication on behalf of those who hymn thee, O divinely blessed one, and put an end to the turmoil of temptations, that we may hymn thee, O divinely eloquent prophet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving birth to God, the Lord and Bestower of life, O most pure one, thou didst abolish the unrestrained tyranny of death, slaying it. Wherefore, we hymn thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`It is impossible for mankind to see God * upon Whom the orders of angels dare not gaze; * but through thee, O all-pure one, * did the Word Incarnate become a man * and with the heavenly Hosts * Him we magnify and thee we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou madest thine abode in the land of the meek, where, after thy repose, thou dost behold the splendors of the angels, O all-wise Zephaniah, thou prophet of God, shining with grace in that thou art meek. Wherefore, rejoicing, we, the faithful, call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Radiantly beholding the fulfillment of thy prophecies, O most glorious one, we marvel at the grace given thee and the purity of thy mind, and we are struck with wonder at thy godly soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`No other like thee hath ever been given to us from generations of old, O all-immaculate Mother of God; for thou, alone of all, hast incomparable sanctity and purity. Wherefore, thou didst receive within thyself God incarnate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having cleansed thy mind of defilement, O all-wise one, thou didst make it a divine mirror reflecting the rays of the Spirit of God; and now, rejoicing, thou hast departed unto the Source of effulgence, O prophet Zephaniah.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy prophet, in Tone VI`,spec_mel:`The portals of compassion...`,tone:6},{text:`Groaning from my heart and inmost parts do I offer thee, O all-immaculate one, asking thine aid, which is accompanied by good. Have mercy upon my greatly suffering soul. Move thou the greatly merciful God to pity, that He deliver me from damnation and the lake of fire, O thou who alone art blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion in Tone VI`,tone:6},{text:`The ever-virgin maiden who gaveth birth unto Thee, O Christ, beholding Thee suspended upon the Cross for our sake, was wounded heart and soul by the sword of grief, and wept, lamenting maternally. By her supplications have mercy upon us, O Merciful One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-03.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-04":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Great-martyr Barbara and our venerable father John of Damascus`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY GREAT-MARTYR BARBARA & OF OUR VENERABLE FATHER JOHN OF DAMASCUS`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 4th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2B`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-04.pdf`,note:'ONE printed service for two saints: one entry, items tagged with `saint`. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 6: six stichera at Lord I have cried split 3 + 3 between two saints, no Little Vespers, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology; ODS vol. III has no 12-04 entry. Fekula 2B (a double service). The page DOES print "On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the holy great-martyr" with a Glory, and then "On the Aposticha, Stichera from the Oktoechos" with a Glory of the venerable one: Praises stichera and a Matins aposticha together, with no Great Doxology named. Two canons, both in Tone II on the same irmoi, three troparia to the ode as printed (the great-martyr\'s has no Theotokion; the first troparion of several odes is marked "Twice"); the rubric appoints the Oktoechos canon with six. The kontakion and ikos of the venerable one stand after Ode III, those of the great-martyr after Ode VI; at Liturgy the kontakia are printed venerable one first. At Liturgy eight Beatitude troparia (Ode III of the great-martyr, Ode VI of the venerable one) and ONE set of prokeimenon, Epistle, Alleluia, Gospel and communion verse.',vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`troparia`,`troparion_closer_rubric`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera: 3 of the holy great-martyr, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`When at the dreadful tribunal, * the all-blessed Juliana, * beholding the glorious martyr Barbara, * who was covered with wounds, * her whole body lacerated by divers tortures, * cried out with fervent tears: * “O Word of God Who lovest mankind, * grant that I may now share ** in her torments!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,tone:2,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`The holy Barbara and Juliana, * possessed of a single yearning * towards piety, * contended against the enemy, * and, having mightily vanquished him, * they were deemed worthy of glory * by Christ God. * Wherefore, having done away with destructive passions, ** they bestow healings upon all the faithful.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`When sweet death was pronounced upon thee, * O most honored martyr Barbara, * thou didst quickly end thy course, rejoicing; * and thou wast slaughtered by * the all-iniquitous hands of thine ungodly father, * offering thyself up to God as comely fruit. * Wherefore, truly joining chorus with the wise virgins, * thou dost behold the effulgence ** of Christ thy Bridegroom.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`O all-wise father John, * thou hast adorned the Church of Christ with thy hymns, * sweetly chanting things most divine * through the activity of the Spirit, * O all-glorious father, * striking thy harp * and emulating all the musical modes of David. * And causing it to sound, ** thou hast drawn all to thee with divine hymns.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`And 3 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`,tone:8},{text:`O glorious father John, * having forsaken, the tumultuous turmoil of the world, * thou didst hasten to the tranquility of Christ, * O venerable one, * and wast truly enriched * with divine visions and acts * and manifest most noetically rich splendors. * These hast thou imparted to the faithful, ** O most blessed one, resplendent in thy godly life.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`Come, O ye earthborn, * and with hymns let us piously hymn today * the sacred and honorable festival * of the venerable John; * for he was truly deemed worthy * to receive divine illumination. * O Thine ineffable compassion, O Lord, * whereby we have come to know ** how to glorify Thee, the supremely good One!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Forsaking homeland, birthright and possessions, O Barbara, * and spurning thine ungodly father, * thou didst come to love God, * to Whom thou didst betroth thyself; * and thou didst become known as a great merchant. * Him do thou entreat, ** that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., of the holy great-martyr, in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Thy pure Virgin Mother, * beholding the most iniquitous people * who unjustly nailed Thee to the Tree, ** was wounded within, as Symeon foretold.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:6,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`On the third day ...`},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera of the Oktoechos, and`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha_glory:{text:`O venerable father, report of thy corrections hath gone forth into all the earth. Wherefore, thou hast received the reward of thy labors in the heavens, and having destroyed hordes of the demons, thou hast attained unto the ranks of the angels, whose life thou didst blamelessly emulate. As thou hast boldness before Christ God, ask thou peace for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory`},saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., of the venerable one, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon seeing Thee crucified, O Christ, * she who gaveth birth to Thee cried aloud: * “What is this strange mystery that I see, * O my Son How is it that Thou diest?, * suspended upon the Tree, ** O Bestower of life?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:6,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},troparia:[{text:`Let us honor the holy Barbara; for the most honored one * broke the snares of the enemy and was delivered from them like a bird, ** with the help and aid of the Cross.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy great-martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy great-martyr, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Teacher of Orthodoxy, instructor of piety and chastity, * luminary of the Church, God-inspired nourishment of monastics, * O supremely wise John, thou spiritual flute illumining all, ** entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},label:`glory`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],troparion_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion Theotokion rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`troparia`,`troparia_closing_rubric`,`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`kontakia_ode3`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakia_ode6`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_glory`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`praises_rubric`,`praises`,`praises_glory`,`praises_closer_rubric`,`praises_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`],troparia:[{text:`Let us honor the holy Barbara; for the most honored one * broke the snares of the enemy and was delivered from them like a bird, ** with the help and aid of the Cross.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Troparion of the holy great-martyr at God is the Lord`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the holy great-martyr, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Teacher of Orthodoxy, instructor of piety and chastity, * luminary of the Church, God-inspired nourishment of monastics, * O supremely wise John, thou spiritual flute illumining all, ** entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Troparion of the venerable one at God is the Lord`},label:`glory`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., that of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],troparia_closing_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Both now, Theotokion or Stavrotheotokion`}},canon_rubric:{text:`One canon from the Oktoechos, with 6 Troparia; and one canon for each of the saints, each with 4 Troparia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the holy great-martyr, in Tone II:`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`In the deep of old the infinite Power overwhelmed Pharaoh's whole army. * But the Incarnate Word annihilated pernicious sin. * Exceedingly glorious is the Lord, * for gloriously hath He been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O most blessed and honored Trinity Who givest gifts to Thy servants which are beyond understanding, breathe Thou a ray of splendor into my darkened mind, that I may praise the ever-memorable martyr Barbara.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`The glory of Thy martyrs hath truly passed every bound of praise, O Lover of mankind; yet, accepting the praise we offer thee with faith according to our measure, O Master, send down upon us rich rewards.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A most beauteous rose sprang forth from a thorny root and hath perfumed the Church of Christ: the glorious Barbara, who dyed her vesture in the blood of her suffering. Her do we hymn as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The desert of the barren Church of the nations * blossomed like a lily * at Thy coming, O Lord, * therein hath my heart been established.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Wounded by the love of Thee, her Bridegroom, O Master, the passion-bearer Barbara rejected all the ungodliness of her father with unrestrained vehemence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Neither the sweet beauty and comeliness of flowers, nor riches, nor yet the sweetness of youth satisfied thee, O goodly virgin, glorious Barbara, who had become the bride of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Neither the hindrance of a feminine nature or youthful stature impeded the martyr's perfect struggles, O Christ; for she was fortified by Thine invisible power.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`From a Virgin didst Thou come forth, not as an ambassador, * nor as an angel, * but the very Lord himself incarnate, * and didst save me, the whole man; * wherefore I cry unto Thee: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Thou Who wast born of the Virgin, Thou hast given to virgin maidens the boldness to cast down the deceiver. Wherefore, the right victorious Barbara put his arrogance to shame`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Our first mother, led astray of old by the machinations of the deceiver, wast driven from the food of paradise; but Barbara, putting him to shame, hath now made her abode in the bridal-chamber of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst destroy the power of death by Thy Cross; wherefore, the maiden Barbara, sparing not her body, most valiantly endured wounding with steadfast mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ God Thou art a mediator between God and man; * for by Thee, O Master, * we have been led from the night of ignorance, * to Thy Father, the Source of light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Commanding that the bath-house be lighted by three windows, O Barbara, thou didst mystically describe baptism, which, through the light of the Trinity, is the radiant cleansing of thy soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Aflame with zeal for God, the all-praised maiden Barbara spat upon the vile faces of the false deities, putting to shame the prince of this world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Opening for Barbara, who was fleeing the savagery of her cruel father, the mountain straightway received her, like the ever-memorable protomartyr Thecla of old, Christ having wrought a miracle.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`I am held fast in the depths of sin O Savior, * and am overwhelmed by the sea of life, * but as Jonah was delivered from the sea-monster, * so also deliver me from the passions, * and save me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As Thou didst promise to give divinely inspired wisdom to those who stand before the tyrants' tribunals for Thy sake, the martyr Barbara was filled therewith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`With divinely wise words thou didst denounce the falsehood of the ungodly, O glorious Barbara, and in enduring the deeds of the torments thou didst astonish the wise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The blameless spiritual athlete gave her body over to be pitilessly afflicted with wounds and to be scraped thoroughly with rags of horse-hair, for the sake of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The godless order of the lawless tyrant * fanned the roaring flame; * but Christ bedewed the God-fearing children with the Spirit, * therefore He is blessed and supremely exalted.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The tyrant who rageth in vain to destroy the earth and annihilate the sea lieth like a plaything beneath the feet of the maiden Barbara; for Christ, having trampled Him down, hath bound him like a vile bird.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`When thy whole body was wracked with unbearable wounds and empurpled with the drops of thy blood, O all-praised glorious martyr Barbara, thou didst yet endure scorching of thy sides by candles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O the inhuman and pitiless savagery and exceeding ungodliness of the torments! For with swords they cruelly severed the breasts of the martyr as though in a butcher's shop, but her mind was set steadfastly on Christ, the Judge of the contest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In Babylon, the activity of the fire was once divided, * for, by the command of God it consumed the Chaldeans, * but bedewed the faithful, who chant: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Christ appeared to thee in prison, O Barbara, surrounded by unapproachable light, commanding thee to be of good cheer, healing thy wounds and granting thee joy; wherefore, thou hast lovingly taken wing to thy Bridegroom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Manifestly hath Thy prophecy been fulfilled, O Christ; for the father gave his own child over to death, the wretched parent having become the instigator of Thy martyr's slaughter. Wherefore, he was destroyed by fire from heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`An angel of light arrayed thee like a bride in brilliant vesture, O Barbara, who wast stripped naked for Christ's sake and wast subjected to suffering; for thou didst shed thy garments, receiving divine transformation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Son of the beginningless Father, God and Lord, * hath appeared to us incarnate of a virgin, * to enlighten those in darkness, * and to gather the dispersed; * therefore the all-hymned Theotokos do we magnify`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Meeting the glorious end of thy martyrdom under the sword, O Barbara, and deemed worthy of a crown of martyrdom with Juliana, thou didst hear the voice of God, which filled thee with power.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`United now with Christ thy Bridegroom, shining with the glory of the divine light in the mansions of heaven, O Barbara, look down upon those who hymn thee, lightening our sufferings and leading us to the living God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ, fulfilling thy request, O Barbara, granteth healings to those who with faith keep thine annual memorial. For truly thy right glorious miracles have surpassed the sands of the sea in number.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon of the venerable one, in Tone II:`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`In the deep of old the infinite Power overwhelmed Pharaoh's whole army. * But the Incarnate Word annihilated pernicious sin. * Exceedingly glorious is the Lord, * for gloriously hath He been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`To me who desires to begin thy praises, grant me now thy honeyed voice, O venerable one, wherewith thou didst with hymns illumine the Orthodox Church which honoreth thy memory, O father John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Perceiving the nature of things most excellently, as a wise judge keen of intellect, thou didst prefer eternal things to those which do not last; for thou didst trade transitory things for those which are abiding, O John, where Christ hath now glorified thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast been shown to surpass all creation, visible and invisible, O pure Ever-virgin; for thou gayest birth to the Creator, in that it was His good pleasure to become incarnate in thy womb. Him do thou entreat with boldness, that He save those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The desert of the barren Church of the nations * blossomed like a lily * at Thy coming, O Lord, * therein hath my heart been established.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst distribute thy wealth, thereby giving it back to God; wherefore, the kingdom in the heavens hath been prepared for thee, and thou hast now received abundant rewards, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Receiving a talant of wisdom, O John, thou didst adorn the Church of Christ, adorning it with thy deeds; and, departing this life, thou hast increased it exceedingly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The ranks of angels were astonished, O most pure one, and the hearts of mortals were filled with awe at thy birthgiving. Wherefore, we honor thee, the Theotokos, with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`From a Virgin didst Thou come forth, not as an ambassador, * nor as an angel, * but the very Lord himself incarnate, * and didst save me, the whole man; * wherefore I cry unto Thee: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Submitting to the command of Christ, thou didst forsake the beauty, wealth, sweetness and splendor of the world; and taking up thy cross for His sake, O wise John, thou didst follow after Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Impoverishing thyself for Christ Who impoverished Himself for the sake of our salvation, thou wast glorified with Him as He promised, and dost now reign with Him Who reigneth forever, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`All of us, the faithful, know thee to be the haven of salvation and an invincible rampart, O Lady Theotokos; for by thy supplications thou dost deliver our souls from tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ God Thou art a mediator between God and man; * for by Thee, O Master, * we have been led from the night of ignorance, * to Thy Father, the Source of light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Made steadfast in the divine life by the fear of Christ, O father John, thou didst subject all thy carnal mind to thy spirit, cleansing thy senses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having assiduously purified body, mind and soul of all defilement, O divinely wise one, thou didst receive the splendor of the threefold Sun, Who hath enriched thee with radiant gifts.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Entreat thy Son and Lord, O pure Virgin; that He grant deliverance from the assaults of the adversary to all captives and peace to those who place their hope on thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`I am held fast in the depths of sin O Savior, * and am overwhelmed by the sea of life, * but as Jonah was delivered from the sea-monster, * so also deliver me from the passions, * and save me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Illumined by the grace of the Spirit, and clearly enriched by the knowledge of secular things, thou didst generously give thy wealth to the needy, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like the choirs of heaven didst thou adorn the Church in Orthodox manner, intoning divine harmonious hymns to the Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou gavest birth without knowing a man, O Virgin, and remainest eternally virgin, revealing the true Godhead of thy Son and God in images.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The godless order of the lawless tyrant * fanned the roaring flame; * but Christ bedewed the God-fearing children with the Spirit, * therefore He is blessed and supremely exalted.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Afire with zeal, thou didst strike down all the false knowledge of God-opposing heresies with thy splendid writings, O John, manifestly making clear what had been sown of old by the wise and written carefully.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the discourses and the dogmas compiled by thee, thou didst fervently de-nounce the blasphemous impiety of the abominable disciples of Manes, who strove to infect the Church of Christ, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O undefiled Virgin, Mother unwedded, we know thee to be more holy than the saints, in that thou alone hast given birth to the immutable God; for thou hast poured forth incorruption upon all the faithful by thy divine birth giving.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In Babylon, the activity of the fire was once divided, * for, by the command of God it consumed the Chaldeans, * but bedewed the faithful, who chant: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst openly denounce the division of Nestorius, the confusion of Severus and the monothelite foolishness, O thrice-blessed John, shining forth the radiance of Orthodoxy upon all the ends of the earth in the one true Faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The enemy abundantly sowed the tares of heresy in the Church of Christ, that the worship of Christ in His precious icons might be eliminated; but he did not find thee sleeping, O all-blessed John, who uprooted every seed of evil.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Without seed didst thou conceive Him Who is inseparable from the Father and dwelt in thy womb as God and man, and thou hast given birth to Him ineffably, O most pure Birthgiver of God. Wherefore, we confess thee to be the salvation of us all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Son of the beginningless Father, God and Lord, * hath appeared to us incarnate of a virgin, * to enlighten those in darkness, * and to gather the dispersed; * therefore the all-hymned Theotokos do we magnify`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast taught all the children of the Church to hymn in an Orthodox fashion the adored Unity in Trinity, and to clearly theologize concerning the divine incarnation of the Word, O John, explaining those things which many find difficult to understand in the sacred Scriptures.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having hymned the ranks of the saints, the pure Theotokos, the forerunner of Christ, the apostles, the prophets, fasters and wise teachers, the righteous and the martyrs, O John, thou dost now abide in their mansions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In a manner beyond understanding, O Virgin Birthgiver of God, thou didst become the bridal-chamber of the incarnation of the Word, arrayed and embroidered with the glory of the virtues. Wherefore, we proclaim thee to be the Theotokos, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`Let us hymn John, the honored and divinely eloquent speaker and hymnographer, * the instructor and teacher of the Church, * the opponent of the enemy; * for taking up the Cross of the Lord as a sword, * he hath cut down all the falsehood of heresies, * and as a fervent intercessor before God ** he bestoweth forgiveness of transgressions upon all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Kontakion of the venerable one (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Having been lifted up upon the Cross ...`,tone:4},{text:`Together let us cry out to the instructor, teacher and priest of the Church, as an initiate of ineffable mysteries: By thy supplications to God open our mouths and grant that we may speak the words of thy doctrines; for thou didst appear in the world as one who shares in the Trinity, shining forth in too world like another sun, illumining all with thy miracles and teachings, like Moses ever instructing in the law of the Lord. And thou wast a luminary in word and deed, praying unceasingly, that forgiveness of transgressions be given to all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ikos of the venerable one`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`In thy suffering thou didst amaze all, for thou didst endure the wounding, bonds, tortures and imprisonment inflicted upon thee by the tormenters, O all-famed Barbara. Wherefore, Christ hath given thee a crown in heaven, and it is to Him that thou didst flee, desiring Him earnestly. He hath imparted grace to thee, O martyr, to pour forth healings upon all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (Barbara)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy great-martyr, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Awed by the beauty of thy virginity ...`,tone:3},{text:`Thou hast been shown to us to be a melodious and sanctified trumpet, O most sacred one, sounding forth in hymnody the teachings of the Lord and Savior to the ends of the earth; and by thy words thou hast illumined the earth, O venerable John, entreat Christ God, that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (John)`},label:`glory`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone III`,tone:3},{text:`Thou wast the divine tabernacle of the Word, * O only most pure Virgin Mother, * who hast surpassed the angels in purity. * With the divine waters of thy supplications cleanse me, * who more than all others am dust and defiled * by carnal transgressions, O pure one, ** and grant me great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3},{text:`The unblemished ewe-lamb of the Word, * the incorrupt Virgin Mother, * beholding Him Who sprang forth from her without pain * suspended upon the Cross, cried out, maternally lamenting: * “Woe is me, O my Child! * How is it that Thou dost suffer willingly, * desiring to redeem mankind ** from the indignity of the passions?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],kontakia_ode6:[{text:`Following God Who is piously hymned in Trinity, * thou didst dim the pagan temples O spiritual athlete; * and suffering amid thy contest, * O Barbara of manly mind, * thou wast not afraid of the threats of the tyrants, * ever chanting aloud: ** “I worship the Trinity, the one God!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Kontakion of the holy great-martyr (after Ode VI)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy great-martyr, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Having been lifted up upon the Cross ...`,tone:4},{text:`Assembling, let us honor, as is meet, Barbara, who made herself the bride of Christ through martyrdom; for delivered from soul-corrupting danger, destruction and earthquake through her supplications, we lead our life in peace, and are granted Thy mercies, O Savior, with all the saints who have pleased Thee from ages past, to walk in the light and to chant with them. And Thou hast astonished all those who confess with faith: We worship the Trinity, the one God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ikos of the holy great-martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`Like a most beautiful rose, dyed with the blood of thy sacred suffering, thou didst spring forth from a thorny root, O virgin martyr Barbara, do thou now lovingly save from misfortunes those who keep thy divine memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Exapostilarion of the holy great-martyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the Oktoechos, and that of the holy great-martyr`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_glory:{text:`Thou didst shine forth like a divine light upon the Church, O father, illumining it with the splendor of thy hymns and the radiance of thy character, whereby thou hast been revealed adorned by the dogmas of Christ, to Whom do thou never cease to pray for us, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Exapostilarion of the venerable one`},saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., that of the venerable one`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Saved by thee, we confess thee to be the true Theotokos, O Lady; for thou didst ineffably give birth to God Who destroyed death by His Cross and drew to Himself the assemblies of the venerable, with whom we praise thee, O Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the holy great-martyr:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Disdaining the sweetness of earthly food and the riches of thy father, and despising glory as well, thou didst love the heavenly Bridegroom, O all-glorious Barbara; for, beheaded by the sword, thou didst enter unto Christ the Bridegroom with the wise virgins. Wherefore, dispelling the deadly plague, thou dost heal the faithful by the activity of the Holy Spirit, praying unceasingly for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Praises 1`},tone:1,composer:`Anatolius`,label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`In Tone I, the composition of Anatolius`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The wicked enemy who lured our first-mother into sin, hath been put to shame, vanquished by a woman; for Christ, the Word of the Father who became incarnate from the Virgin without change or commingling, as He Himself knew, lifted the curse from Eve and Adam, and He crowned the martyr Barbara as is meet, granting the world cleansing and great mercy for her sake.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Praises 2`},tone:2,composer:`Byzantius`,label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`In Tone II, the composition of Byzantius`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The divinely called martyr Barbara, suffering in the tribunal, said: “Cruel are my present torments, O ye torturers, but joyful will it be to receive everlasting life! I shall never prefer earthly things to those of heaven! Wherefore, cut ye and lacerate my flesh, and give me over the fire, that, rejoicing, I may depart unto Christ my Bridegroom!” Through her supplications, O Christ God, send down Thy mercies and save us who with faith celebrate her sufferings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`},{text:`Come, ye people, let us hymn the festival of the spiritual athlete Barbara today; for neither sword, nor fire, nor any torment, nor the crafty snares of Belial was able to triumph over her. To her do we cry out with faith: Entreat Christ, O good and all-glorious martyr, that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p10 Praises 4`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`}],praises_glory:{text:`Treading the path of suffering, O most honored Barbara, thou didst avoid the counsel of thy father. Bearing a lamp like a wise virgin, thou didst enter into the courts of thy Lord, and as a manly-wise martyr thou hast received the grace to heal carnal passions. Deliver us all, who hymn thee, from spiritual sickness by thy prayers unto God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises Glory`},composer:`John the Monk`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of John the Monk, in Tone VI`,tone:6},praises_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises Both now rubric`}},praises_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon seeing Thee hanging upon the Cross * the all-pure one weeping, cried aloud with a mother’s grief: * ‘O my Son and my God, O my sweetest Child, ** how dost Thou endure this shameful suffering?’`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:6,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, Stichera from the Oktoechos:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Matins Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha_glory:{text:`We, the multitude of monks , honor thee, our instructor, O John our father; for by thy footsteps we have truly learned to walk the straight path. Blessed art thou who, laboring for Christ, didst denounce the power of the enemy, O converser with angels, companion of the venerable and the righteous. With them pray thou to the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Matins Aposticha Glory`},saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`And Glory ..., of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Matins Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`'I cannot bear O my child, to behold Thee, * Who dost grant life and health unto all, * hung upon the Tree; * for of old those who were lulled into the sleep of death * by the fruit of the transgression * have been awakened * and granted divine and salvific life and health by Thee', * thus said the Virgin weeping, ** whom we magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p11 Matins Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,tone:8,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparia`,`kontakia`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of the canon of the holy great-martyr, and 4 from ODE VI of the canon of the venerable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Wounded by the love of Thee, her Bridegroom, O Master, the passion-bearer Barbara rejected all the ungodliness of her father with unrestrained vehemence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Neither the sweet beauty and comeliness of flowers, nor riches, nor yet the sweetness of youth satisfied thee, O goodly virgin, glorious Barbara, who had become the bride of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Neither the hindrance of a feminine nature or youthful stature impeded the martyr's perfect struggles, O Christ; for she was fortified by Thine invisible power.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined by the grace of the Spirit, and clearly enriched by the knowledge of secular things, thou didst generously give thy wealth to the needy, O John.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Like the choirs of heaven didst thou adorn the Church in Orthodox manner, intoning divine harmonious hymns to the Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou gavest birth without knowing a man, O Virgin, and remainest eternally virgin, revealing the true Godhead of thy Son and God in images.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],troparia:[{text:`Let us honor the holy Barbara; for the most honored one * broke the snares of the enemy and was delivered from them like a bird, ** with the help and aid of the Cross.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Troparion of the holy great-martyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy great-martyr, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Teacher of Orthodoxy, instructor of piety and chastity, * luminary of the Church, God-inspired nourishment of monastics, * O supremely wise John, thou spiritual flute illumining all, ** entreat Christ God that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Troparion of the venerable one at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],kontakia:[{text:`Let us hymn John, the honored and divinely eloquent speaker and hymnographer, * the instructor and teacher of the Church, * the opponent of the enemy; * for taking up the Cross of the Lord as a sword, * he hath cut down all the falsehood of heresies, * and as a fervent intercessor before God ** he bestoweth forgiveness of transgressions upon all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Kontakion of the venerable one at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`John of Damascus`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Following God Who is piously hymned in Trinity, * thou didst dim the pagan temples O spiritual athlete; * and suffering amid thy contest, * O Barbara of manly mind, * thou wast not afraid of the threats of the tyrants, * ever chanting aloud: ** “I worship the Trinity, the one God!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Kontakion of the holy great-martyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Barbara`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy great-martyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],prokeimenon:{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`In congregations bless ye God, the Lord from the well-springs of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p12 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE GALATIANS,`,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p13 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§208 (3: 23-29)`,citation:{book:`Galatians`,chapter:3,verses:`23-29`,pericope_number:208},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`With patience I waited patiently for the Lord, and He was attentive unto me, and He hearkened unto my supplication.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p13 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone I`,label_inline:!0,tone:1},alleluia_verse:{text:`And He brought me up out of the pit of misery, and from the mire of clay.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p13 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. MARK,`,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p13 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§21 (5:24-34)`,citation:{book:`Mark`,chapter:5,verses:`24-34`,pericope_number:21},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-04.pdf`,locus:`p13 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-05":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.little_vespers`,`c0.great_vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our venerable and God-bearing father Sabbas the Sanctified`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR VENERABLE AND GOD-BEARING FATHER, SABBAS THE SANCTIFIED`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 5th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`vigil`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-05.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 2: the Menaion prints a LITTLE VESPERS for the saint, so Vigil, Fekula 2F. ODS vol. III has no 12-05 entry. Great Vespers with "Blessed is the man", 8 stichera (three printed, marked Thrice, Thrice, Twice), three lessons with printed references, a Litiya, the blessing of the Loaves, and "But if a vigil is not served" with a dismissal Theotokion. Matins: Polyeleos with a Magnification and a Selected Psalm verse, a Gospel, the sticheron after Psalm 50 (the same hymn as the Praises Glory). Two canons, the Theotokos (two or three troparia to the ode, no Theotokion marked) and the venerable one, by Theophanes; a katavasia is printed after every ode, the first headed "Katavasia, in Tone I". The page ends Matins at the Praises Theotokion: NO "Great Doxology" line is printed. The melody line at Lord I have cried is printed "Spec Mel.:". The Matins prokeimenon is printed in Tone IV and the same words at Liturgy in Tone VII.`,troparion:{text:`With the streams of thy tears thou didst irrigate the barren desert, * and with sighs from the depths of thy soul thou didst render thy labors fruitful an hundredfold, * becoming a beacon for the whole world, resplendent with miracles. ** O Sabbas our father, entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Little Vespers`,tone:8},{locus:`p7 blessing of the Loaves`,tone:8,repeat:2},{locus:`p8 God is the Lord`,tone:8,repeat:2},{locus:`p20 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},kontakion:{text:`In thy virtue didst thou offer thyself from childhood unto God * as an unblemished sacrifice, O blessed Sabbas, * becoming a gardener in the garden of piety. * Therefore, thou wast an adornment for the venerable and a right praiseworthy citizen of the desert. ** Wherefore, we cry to thee: Rejoice, O most noetically rich Sabbas!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Kontakion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p15 after Ode VI`,tone:8},{locus:`p20 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`To thee the champion leader ...`,tone:8},ikos:{text:`O leader of the fathers, beauty of the venerable, boldness of fasters before Christ, citizen and gardener of the desert: how can I hymn thy life, O venerable one? for thou dost shine forth in brilliance unto the ends of the earth, like the sun. Wherefore, I cry unto thee: Rejoice, beauteous glory of the Cappadocians! Rejoice, honored standard of the whole world! Rejoice, most good offspring of the desert! Rejoice, godly delight of the righteous! Rejoice, for thou didst disdain that which is fleeting and corruptible! Rejoice, for thou dost dwell with the angels in the heavens! Rejoice, correction and rule of monastics! Rejoice, rousing of the slothful toward God! Rejoice, divinely flowing fountain of miracles! Rejoice, honored instrument of the Spirit! Rejoice, thou with whom the East is adorned! Rejoice, thou through whom the Western lands shine forth! Rejoice, O most noetically rich Sabbas!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`With thy mind wast thou a beholder of the noetic powers, as one that followed the divine words, laying them up in thy heart; and therein establishing thine ascents as a ladder, O Sabbas, our venerable father. Pray thou now that our souls be granted peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`O Sabbas most venerable, from thy childhood thou didst offer thy life to Christ our God. Strengthened by Him, thou didst subject thy carnal passions to thy mind, subjugating that which is worse to that which is better. Wherefore, pray thou that our souls be granted peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`O our God-bearing father, thou didst show thyself to be a beacon most great, enlightening all the earth with the splendors of thy miracles and with divine works. Wherefore, after thy repose the unwaning Light received thee. Pray thou now that our souls be granted peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`O venerable father, having earnestly taught thyself the virtues from thy childhood, thou didst become an instrument of the Holy Spirit; and having received from Him the ability to work miracles, thou didst urge all to disdain the delights of life. And now, enlightened most purely with divine light, illumine our thoughts, O Sabbas, our father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone II`,tone:2},lic_closer:{text:`All of my hope do I place on thee, * O Mother of God; ** keep me under thy protection.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`From thy swaddling clothes * thou wast revealed to be * a sanctified vessel * and abode of the most holy Spirit, ** O our God-bearing father.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Bearing upon thy shoulders * the cross of the Lord, * O Sabbas, our father, * thou didst utterly lay waste ** to demonic fantasies.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord; * in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Having renounced the deception of the evil demons * by the power of the Cross, * thou didst shine forth * with the glory of Christ, ** O Sabbas, our father.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`O good Lady, * stretch forth thy holy hands * unto thy Son, * the soul-loving Creator, ** that He spare thy servants.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`theotokion`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in the same melody`},troparion_closer:{text:`O good One, Who for our sake wast born of the Virgin * and, having endured crucifixion, cast down death by death, * and as God revealed the Resurrection: * disdain not that which Thou hast fashioned with Thine own hand. * Show forth Thy love for mankind, O merciful One; * Accept the supplications of the Theotokos who bore Thee, ** and save Thy despairing people, O our Savior!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers dismissal Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`dogmatikon`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya_rubric`,`litiya`,`litiya_glory`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`,`virgin_theotokos_rubric`,`no_vigil_rubric`,`troparion_closer`],rubric:{text:`We chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O divinely wise Sabbas, as one who standest together with the angels, abiding in union with the venerable, conversing with the prophets, O coheir to the kingdom with the martyrs and apostles, thou dost now dwell in unwaning Light, shining with His divine rays, and with extreme desire thou dost ever stand before Him with boldness, unceasingly enlightened, and delighting in His beauties. Entreat Christ, O venerable father, and beseech Him to grant to the Church oneness of mind, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`O venerable father ...`,repeat:3,provenance_note:`The melody line is printed "Spec Mel.:" without the full stop after "Spec" (p3).`},{text:`O divinely wise Sabbas, inextinguishable lamp of abstinence, most radiant beacon for monastics, ever illumined with rays of love, an immovable pillar of patience, confirmation and strength to those who honor thee with faith, treasury of healings, and a desert-dweller in truth, having shown it to be a divine paradise bearing the divine fruit of the saved. O venerable one. Entreat Christ, O venerable father, and beseech Him to grant to the Church oneness of mind, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O venerable father ...`,repeat:3},{text:`O divinely wise Sabbas, fiery pillar of the virtues, beacon guiding men from the sea of life to the divine harbor, who hast set at naught deceptions of the spirit, pure abode of the Holy Spirit, instructor of monastics, sure measure of abstinence, radiant summit of humility, wellspring which poureth forth an abyss of healings. Entreat Christ, O venerable father, and beseech Him to grant to the Church oneness of mind, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O venerable father ...`,repeat:2}],lic_glory:{text:`Having preserved that which was fashioned according to the image of God and through fasting, made thy mind master over the pernicious passions, thou didst ascend as one mighty, unto that which is according to the likeness of God. For, having manfully compelled thy nature, thou didst strive to subject that which was worse to the better, and to enslave the flesh to the spirit. Wherefore, thou hast been revealed to be the lofty summit of monastics, a desert-dweller, an admonisher of those who run the course of life well, and a most sure rule of virtue. And now, when the shadows have been set aside, O Sabbas, our father, in a pure manner thou dost behold the Holy Trinity in the heavens, praying directly on behalf of those who honor thee with faith and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},dogmatikon:{text:`Who doth not call thee blessed, O most holy Virgin? * Who will not hymn thy most pure birthgiving? * For the only-begotten Son Who hath shone forth timelessly from the Father, * came forth, ineffably incarnate, from thee, O pure one; * By nature He is God, by nature for our sakes, He hath become a man * not divided into two Hypostases, * but known in two natures without commingling. * Him do thou beseech, O pure and most blessed one, ** that our souls find mercy!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Both now, Dogmatic Theotokion`},type:`dogmatic_theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., the Dogmatic Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the Day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 1`},citation_verbatim:`(3:1-9).`,citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:3,verses:`1-9`},citation_basis:`printed`},{heading:`READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 2`},citation_verbatim:`(5:15-6:3).`,citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:5,verses:`5:15-6:3`},citation_basis:`printed`},{heading:`READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 3`},citation_verbatim:`(4:7-15).`,citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:4,verses:`7-15`},citation_basis:`printed`}],litiya_rubric:{text:`At the Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya rubric`}},litiya:[{text:`O venerable Sabbas, having trained upon earth in the school of fasting, thou didst blunt all the assaults of the passions with the flow of thy tears. O divine and honored ladder which leadest to heaven, thy God-pleasing life hath been made known unto all; for, having shown forth the fruits of piety therein, thou dost thereby heal the weaknesses of the passions of those who faithfully cry out to thee: Rejoice, O most golden star of the East, radiant lamp of monastics, our pastor! Rejoice, O ever-hymned one, thou exceedingly good nourishment of the desert and unshaken confirmation of the Church! Rejoice, O great guide of those who stray! Rejoice, O our boast, thou radiant joy of the whole world!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`And these Stichera to the saint, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`Let us honor Sabbas, an angel on earth, a man of God in the heavens, the good adornment of the world, the delight of the good, the boast of the virtues of fasting; for, planted in the house of God, he flourished righteously like a cedar in the desert, and he increased Christ's flock of rational sheep, in holiness and righteousness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`God, Who alone resteth in His saints, acquiring thy sanctified soul as a pure dwelling-place, made His abode therein and filled it with divine graces, whereby thou dost lead to the Light those who hymn thee, O blessed and sanctified Sabbas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 3`},label:`plain`}],litiya_glory:{text:`Receiving a desire for good things which transcend understanding, thou didst disdain all the beautiful things in the world, O thou who art pleasing unto God; for, thus thou wast not entrapped by the fruit as was Adam. And having repulsed the serpent by abstinence, thou didst live an angelic life and now dost dwell in the heavens, nurtured by the Tree of Life, entreating God on behalf of us, who faithfully celebrate thy memory, O sanctified Sabbas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone II`,tone:2},litiya_closer:{text:`O new wonder greater than all the wonders of old! * For who hath ever known a mother to give birth without having known a man, * and to bear on her arm Him Who sustaineth all creation? * Yet it was the will of God to be born. * O most pure one, who carried Him as an infant in thine embrace * and before Whom thou hast a mother's boldness: * cease not to pray on behalf of those who honor thee, ** that He have compassion and save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Rejoice, truly fragrant vessel of the struggles of fasting; for, having taken thy cross upon thy shoulder and offered thyself to Christ the Master, O all-blessed one, thou didst trample down the base understanding of the flesh, and didst illumine thy soul with the virtues, and didst take flight to divine desire. Wherefore, surrounding thy most holy shrine, O all-praised Sabbas, we ask that, by thy prayers, we receive God's love for mankind, and that the world be granted great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O God-bearing Sabbas, having drawn nigh unto the fire of the Spirit, thou hast shown thyself forth in the world as a divinely radiant ember enlightening the souls of those who faithfully have recourse to thee, O godly-wise and venerable father, leading them to the unwaning Light. And, bedewed from on high with divine grace, thou didst quench the burning coal of the desert. Wherefore, Christ, the Helmsman of divine righteousness, hath manifestly bestowed upon thee a crown of victory, O blessed one. Entreat Him, that He grant our souls great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord; * in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thy life was clearly a ladder spanning the gulf between the earth and the heavens, O divinely wise one, whereby thou didst ascend to the heights and wast deemed worthy to converse with Christ the Master, O all-blessed one. Having enlightened thy mind with the radiance there, with the rays thereof thou didst receive splendor equal to that of the angels. Standing now before Him, pray thou, O venerable one, that we who celebrate thy divine and wholly sanctified memory may stand with thee, and that He grant the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`We honor thee as the instructor of a multitude of monks, O Sabbas, our father; for we have truly learned to walk aright in thy steps. Blessed art thou, who didst labor for Christ and didst renounce the power of the adversary, O converser with the angels. With them do thou entreat the Lord, that He have mercy on our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_closer:{text:`O unwedded Virgin! * thou who ineffably conceived God in the flesh, * Mother of God Most High: * accept the supplications of thy servants, O all-immaculate one, * granting unto all cleansing of transgressions; * and, accepting now our supplications, ** pray thou that we all be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the Loaves, the Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Blessing of the Loaves rubric`}},virgin_theotokos_rubric:{text:`And “Virgin Theotokos, rejoice! ...,” (Once).`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Virgin Theotokos rejoice rubric`}},no_vigil_rubric:{text:`But if a vigil is not served, then after the Troparion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 If a vigil is not served`}},troparion_closer:{text:`O good One, Who for our sake wast born of the Virgin * and, having endured crucifixion, cast down death by death, * and as God revealed the Resurrection: * disdain not that which Thou hast fashioned with Thine own hand. * Show forth Thy love for mankind, O merciful One; * Accept the supplications of the Theotokos who bore Thee, ** and save Thy despairing people, O our Savior!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p7 Dismissal Theotokion (no vigil)`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.troparion_closer.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord rubric`}},troparion_closer:{text:`O good One, Who for our sake wast born of the Virgin * and, having endured crucifixion, cast down death by death, * and as God revealed the Resurrection: * disdain not that which Thou hast fashioned with Thine own hand. * Show forth Thy love for mankind, O merciful One; * Accept the supplications of the Theotokos who bore Thee, ** and save Thy despairing people, O our Savior!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},sessional_1:[{text:`Having piously finished thy life on earth, thou wast revealed to be a pure dwelling-place of the Spirit, enlightening those who have recourse unto thee in faith, O blessed one: Wherefore, beseech thy Master, that He enlighten the souls of us who hymn thee, O divinely wise Sabbas, our father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the first chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`The choir of angels ...`,tone:1},{text:`Through the Holy Spirit didst thou conceive in thy womb God, the Creator and Fashioner of all, O pure and all-immaculate one, and gave birth to Him without corruption. Glorifying Him, we hymn thee, O Virgin, as the palace of the King of all, the protection of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1}],sessional_2:[{text:`Having shone forth like the sun, thou dost emit splendid rays upon the earth, O venerable one, through the far-reaching effulgence of thy teaching, O wondrous and light-bearing Sabbas, thou boast of the venerable.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the second chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared today ...`,tone:4},{text:`Accepting the entreaty of us * who have recourse to thy protection, O all-holy Virgin, * cease thou never to make supplication to Him * Who is the Lover of mankind, ** that He save thy servants.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`After the Polyeleos, this Magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We bless thee, O our venerable father Sabbas, and we honor thy holy memory, instructor of monks and converser with angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Selected Psalm rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`With patience I waited patiently for the Lord, and He was attentive unto me, and He hearkened unto my supplication.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p8 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God! (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`Truly thou wast sanctified from thy mother's womb, O most sacred Sabbas, and on earth thou didst live like an angel; for thou didst slay the flesh by abstinence, rightly emulating the demeanor of the great Euthymius, and revealed to be a favorite of the Trinity, O blessed one. Wherefore, having brought together a multitude of monastics emulating thy godly life, O our ever-memorable and God-bearing father, entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who honor thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`And the following Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8,provenance_note:`The extraction displaces one comma (printed slightly below the line after "womb") onto a line of its own; it is restored to its printed place, checked against a render of p9.`},{text:`Let us hymn the heavenly gate and ark, * the all-holy mountain, the cloud of light, the heavenly ladder, * the spiritual Paradise, the redemption of Eve, * the great treasure of the world; * because salvation for the world and forgiveness of ancient offences were wrought in her. * Therefore we cry unto her: * Intercede with thine own Son and God to grant forgiveness of offences ** to those who devoutly worship thine all-holy Offspring.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p9 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(6:17-23)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:6,verses:`17-23`},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`O venerable father, the sound of thy corrections hath gone forth into all the earth. Wherefore, thou hast found thy reward in the heavens, having destroyed legions of demons, thou hast attained unto the ranks of the angels, whose life thou didst blamelessly emulate. Having boldness before Christ God, beg peace for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone VI`,tone:6},canon_rubric:{text:`The canon of the most holy Theotokos, with 6 Troparia; and the canon of the venerable one, with 8 Troparia:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the most holy Theotokos, the acrostic whereof is: “I chant praise unto the Life-bearing maiden”, in Tone I:`,acrostic:`I chant praise unto the Life-bearing maiden`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Traversing dryshod the impassible, peculiar path in the sea, * Israel the chosen cried aloud: * Let us chant unto the Lord, * for He hath been glorified!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The immaterial ladder of old and the path of the sea made strangely firm revealed thy birthgiving, O pure one. Her do we all hymn, for she hath been glorified!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The power of the Most High, the perfect Hypostasis, the Wisdom of God incarnate from thee, O most pure one, hath conversed with mankind, for He hath been glorified!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Sun of thy righteousness hath passed through the impassible door of thy locked womb, O pure one, and shone forth upon the world, for He hath been glorified!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The bow of the mighty hath been broken * by Thy might, O Christ, * and the enfeebled * have girded themselves with power.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He that, as the Creator of time, is outside all time, O Virgin, willingly made Himself a Child through thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us hymn the womb which is far more spacious than the heavens, through which Adam hath made his abode in the heavens, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard report O Lord, * of Thy glorious dispensation, * and I have glorified, Thine unapproachable power, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Behold! the supremely revealed Mother of God, the divine mountain of the house of the Lord, is exalted far above the heavenly powers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin, who, alone outside the laws of nature, hast given birth unto the Ruler of creation: thou hast been deemed worthy of a divine calling.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`The burning Ember was revealed to Isaiah, * and the Sun hath shone forth from the Virgin's womb, * granting the enlightenment of the knowledge of God * to those who in darkness have gone astray.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Clouds of darkness rain down delight upon those who are on earth, for unto us hath a Child been given, Who hath existed from before all ages: our God, incarnate from the Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Light hath shone forth upon my life and my flesh, and hath destroyed the gloom of sin: the most Exalted One, Who in the latter days became incarnate without seed from the Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`O Master, hearkening unto the sound of entreaties * from a soul in pain, * do Thou deliver me from my grievous sins, * for Thou alone art the Cause of our salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Human nature, enslaved to sin, hath obtained freedom through thee, O pure Lady; for thy Son hath been sacrificed like a lamb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`We all cry out to thee, the true Mother of God: Save thou thy wrathful servants, for thou alone hast boldness before thy Son.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Of old the youths revealed themselves to be rhetors * with a supreme love for wisdom, * for from the depths of their God-pleasing souls, * they theologized with their lips as they sang: * O supremely divine God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`At night Jacob beheld God as in a dream, and He Who became incarnate from thee hath revealed Himself in splendor unto those who chant: Most divine and supremely glorified is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He that wrestled with Jacob, prefiguring the ineffable union in thee, O pure one, whereby He willingly united Himself to mankind: He is the most divine and supremely glorified God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The vile one who did not proclaim Thee, the Son of the Virgin, to be One of the all-hymned Trinity, cried out with steadfast thought and with his tongue: Most divine and supremely glorified is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Disdaining the golden image, the thrice-blessed children, * beholding the immutable and living image of God, * chanted in the midst of the flame: * Let all existing creation hymn the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He Who is incomparable in grace and might became visible on earth and dwelt with mankind through thee. Chanting unto Him, O all ye faithful, let us cry out: Let all existing creation hymn the Lord and exalt Him supremely throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Truly proclaiming thee the pure one, we glorify thee, O Theotokos, for thou didst give birth to the One of the Trinity Who became incarnate. And to Him, with the Father and the Spirit, do we sing: Let all existing creation hymn the Lord and exalt Him supremely throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thou art all desire, Thou art all sweetness, * O Word of God, Son of the Virgin, * God of gods, most holy Lord of the saints. * Wherefore, we magnify Thee * and her who hath given birth to Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`In thy womb, O pure one, the Word of God was given to corruptible nature as a staff of strength. And He restored what had been dragged down to Hades. Wherefore, we magnify thee, O most pure one, as the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Master, mercifully accept Thy mother as an intercessor on our behalf, as Thou hast willed, and all things shall be filled with Thy goodness, that we all may magnify Thee as our Benefactor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon of the Venerable One, the acrostic whereof is: “Lovingly I hymn Sabbas, most eminent among fasters,” the composition of Theophanes, in Tone VIII:`,acrostic:`Lovingly I hymn Sabbas, most eminent among fasters`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`The wonderworking staff of Moses, * striking and dividing the sea in the figure of a cross, * once drowned pharaoh the pursuing charioteer, * while it saved the fleeing people of Israel * as they fled on foot, * chanting a hymn unto God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With the splendor of the Holy Spirit, O Sabbas, illumine us who with devout love praise thee with hymns as the boast of fasters, the glory of monastics, the adorner of the desert and teacher of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having offered all thy love to God from thy youth and made Him the object of all thy desire, rejoicing, thou didst mortify the movements of the flesh and the assaults of the passions, O all-praised God-bearer Sabbas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Conquering the serpent hidden in the fruit, thou didst trample it down and easily pass over his snares, taking flight on wings of piety, O father; and, rejoicing, thou didst partake of life in the garden of the Cross.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined with the light of grace, thou didst enter into the fire and, like the three youths, remained unconsumed, for God preserved thee, revealing to all thine ultimate future progress and perfection, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Death hath laid hold upon us with irresistible assaults; but, drawing nigh to thine Offspring, it perished and, rushing against Him, it was destroyed. For thou didst truly give birth unto everlasting Life incarnate, O Virgin Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The Master saved His people by working a wonder, * making solid the watery waves of the sea of old; * and having willingly been born of the Virgin, * He hath set before us a path leading to heaven. * Let us glorify Him Who is by nature equal to both the Father and mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 katavasia`},tone:1,sourceLabel:`Katavasia, in Tone I`,label_inline:!0}},3:{irmos:{text:`O Christ fortify me on the rock of Thy commandments, * Thou who in the beginning didst establish the heavens with understanding * and didst establish the earth upon the waters, * for there is none holy save Thee, O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having set thy mind as master over the passions, O spiritually rich father, showing thyself to be a dispenser of justice; for thou didst manifestly subject what is worse to that which is better. Wherefore, thou didst flourish in the desert like a palm tree, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having resolved to follow in the steps of the Master, thou didst forsake thy homeland; and, making thine abode in the desert, thou didst win a victory over the adversaries, strengthened by the power of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by steadfastness of mind, O all-blessed one, thou didst denounce the divers wiles of the enemy, unmasking them in the sight of all, and setting at naught his conceited audacity, O wise one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Perceiving thee to be sacred of soul and adorned with simplicity of intent and with the virtues, Euthymius, the most radiant star, received thee, prophetically proclaiming thy splendor, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Mother, thou hast truly been known to be the splendid portal of the dispensation of the Word, Who hath saved us; for thou hast brought forth upon us the noetic Ray of the supremely divine Godhead.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Look upon the hymns of Thy servants, O Benefactor, * and humble the vaunted pride of the enemy; * bearing far above sin those who hymn Thee * making them unshakably firm by the foundation of faith, * O Thou good One Who seest all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},4:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, art my strength and Thou art my power, * Thou art my God and Thou art my joy, * Thou Who, while never leaving the bosom of Thy Father, * hast visited our poverty. * Therefore with the prophet Habbakuk I cry unto Thee, * “Glory to Thy power, O Lover of mankind!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Cleansing and expanding the state of thy soul with divine visions, thou didst truly fashion it into a dwelling-place of divine gifts, O divinely blessed one; and by the laying on of thy hands thou didst heal the afflicted, being an emulator of the Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He that waxed arrogant against thee, O father, was swallowed up like the wretched Dathan, and like Abiram was destroyed; for the grace of God invisibly preserved thee, intending the salvation of many, O all-blessed, glorious and divinely wise Sabbas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely eloquent one, having chastised thy senses with the Law of God, thou didst direct thy skillful thought to the knowledge of incorporeal and noetic things, passing inexorably from glory to glory and from strength to strength, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Proposing to do good unto thy compatriots, thou didst found magnificent and spiritually profitable cities in the desert, bringing springs of water to the parched land, and most gloriously bringing down rains from heaven upon the waterless fields.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`A beauteous paradise newly sprung forth hast thou been shown to be, O thou who most divinely bore within thy womb and gave birth to, the Tree of Life planted therein, Which poureth forth the hope of salvation upon all who with faith know thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The renewal of the human race was hymned of old * and proclaimed beforehand by the prophet Habbakuk, * who having ineffably been deemed worthy to behold in image; * the Word coming forth from the mountain, * the Virgin, as a little Babe, * for the restoration of the people.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},5:{irmos:{text:`O Light never-waning, * why hast Thou turned Thy face from me * and why hath the alien darkness surrounded me, * wretched though I be? * But do Thou guide my steps I implore Thee * and turn me back towards the light of Thy commandments.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Stretching forth unwavering thought toward Him Whom thou didst desire, from Him thou didst receive the sure grace of most wondrous miracles, O father; compassionately healing those who have recourse to thee in faith, O venerable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Putting away the coarseness of the heaviness of the flesh, thou didst become a divinely wrought and chosen vessel of the Holy Spirit, O wondrous one, adorned with abstinence from foods, patience and chastity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast appointed the most resounding herald of the divine dogmas of the Councils, O father, and wast a partaker with the saints, enlightening emperors, to whom, O blessed one, thou wast clearly revealed to be protected by divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely inspired one, the grace given thee by God sounded forth, for it hath been distributed unto all, unto the ends of the earth, manifestly bringing about the divine activity of wondrous revelation in a most godly manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, intercessor for the faithful, indestructible rampart of those who praise thee, O thou who hast given birth in the flesh unto God, the Salvation revealed to the whole human race: save thou my soul!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`O Christ Who art our cleansing, come unto us, * who out of the night of the deeds of gloomy delusion, * valiantly hymn Thee as a Benefactor, * granting us an expeditious path, * ascending upon which we find glory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 5 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},6:{irmos:{text:`Cleanse me, O Savior, * for many are mine iniquities; * lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee, * for unto Thee have I cried, * and Thou hast hearkened unto me, * O God of my salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having acquired love for God and neighbor, fulfilling the chief precepts of the Law and the prophets; thou didst achieve unattainable virtue, surpassing all others, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst attain on earth a life equal to that of the angels, and Christ hath given thee honor equal to that of the angels, sending thy soul to accompany the ranks of the holy ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having been shown to be a child of wisdom, thou didst desire the beginning of wisdom, the fear of God; and, strengthened thereby, O father, thou didst attain unto perfection as far is permitted.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure Lady, who hast given birth unto God, the Savior and Redeemer of all, Who took our flesh upon Himself: from misfortune save those who call upon thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Dwelling in the uttermost depths of the sea, * Jonah besought Thee to come and still the tempest; * and I, pierced by the arrow of the tyrant, * chant unto Thee, O Christ * Thou Destroyer of evil, * do Thou come quickly unto my slothfulness!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 6 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},7:{irmos:{text:`Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe * of God's condescension; * for which sake the youths in the furnace, * dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst put away transitory things, being rewarded with eternal things; and with the angels dost thou join chorus as one that led an angelic life. And with them hast thou chanted: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thanksgiving thy great and most honorable Lavra crieth out to the Lord, putting thee forward as its inhabitant, founder and citizen, O wise one, and crying out in praise: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Sabbas most wise, entreat the Lord unceasingly on behalf of thy flock, and earnestly pray that thy labors be preserved forever for those who bear fruit and cry out with love: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Reasoning rightly, we call thee the bridal chamber, the banquet hall and throne of the incarnation of the Word, most pure beyond telling; and, rejoicing, we cry out to thy Son: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Captured by the love of the King of all, * the children reviled the uncontrollable rage and ungodly blasphemies of the tyrant, * and the great fire submitted to them as they spake unto the Master saying: * Blessed art Thou throughout the ages`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 7 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},8:{irmos:{text:`In his wrath the Chaldean tyrant made the furnace blaze, * with heat fanned sevenfold for the servants of God; * but when he perceived that they had been saved by a greater power * he cried aloud to the Creator and Redeemer; * “Ye children bless, ye priests praise, * ye people, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages”.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With gladness the ranks of the saints preceded thy most pure soul to the place of delight among the splendid mansions, where the choirs of the righteous rejoice, O venerable one. With them dost thou now chant: Ye priests, hymn; ye people su-premely exalt Christ throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strange are thy wonders, for thou didst tame wild beasts, having quelled the waves of the passions; and with thy prophetic gift thou dost foretell things to come; and, expelling legions of demons, thou dost wound them with thy right powerful vigils, prayers and fasts, and by the invincible power of the Cross, O God-bearer.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`He, that of old spake to Moses from the pillar of cloud and fire, showed thee to be a most magnificent pillar reaching from the earth, where now thy patient and much-suffering body doth lie, unto heaven. Standing before it in faith, we piously chant: Ye people, exalt Christ supremely forever!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Joyously is thy memory celebrated, O all-praised one; for thou didst robe thyself in the virtue which bringeth joy, the true garment of salvation, the pure and radiant garment of gladness, wherein adorned, thou dost now chant unceasingly: Ye priests, hymn; ye people supremely exalt Christ throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Remaining virgin, thou didst give birth without knowing wedlock, and by thy strange birthgiving thou hast brought all together, abolishing the strife of time and great distance, bearing in thy womb Christ, the Bestower of peace. Him do we faithfully hymn and supremely exalt throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The children who in the time of the Old Covenant * were cast into the fire, * prefigured the unconsumed womb of the maiden, * which hath supra-naturally given birth yet remaineth sealed; * and both wondrously working as a single miracle * moveth the people to hymn the Grace of each.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 8 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},9:{irmos:{text:`Heaven was stricken with awe, * and the ends of the earth were filled with amazement, * for God hath appeared in the flesh, * and thy womb was rendered more spacious than the heavens. * Wherefore, the ranks of men and of angels * magnify thee as the Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy shrine issueth forth a sweet spiritual fragrance, richly making glad thy children who fervently surround thee, commemorating thine angelic sojourn on earth, O venerable one, and the radiance, glory and everlasting beauty bestowed upon thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Water broke forth in the desert, and the parched earth became a marsh, transformed by thy prayers, O father; for legions of fasters inhabit it as it were a river valley, and the land of Jordan hath blossomed forth like a lily, watered by thy tears.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The splendor of the saints in the heavens shone forth upon thee, in that thou wast a righteous man, O father; for thou didst manifestly love the true righteousness of Christ. Following His manner of life, O all-blessed one, thou didst emulate His life-imparting sanctity as far as thou wast able.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shining with rich light, O God-bearer, beholding now the choirs of angels standing in splendor around the light of the Trinity, and receiving rays of divine knowledge through grace, pray thou unceasingly that remission of sins be granted to those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, thou art more highly exalted than all mortal mankind in thine incomparable preeminence; for in thy womb thou didst contain God, the Creator of all creation. Him do thou beseech, in that He is merciful, that He grant to His Churches oneness of mind, peace and serene prosperity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`From fear it may be easier, * for us to prefer silence, * for though not fraught with danger, O Virgin, * it is difficult to fashion hymns fittingly wrought for thee. * Yet, O Mother, grant us the power to chant in such a way, * insofar as it is our will.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 9 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having forsaken all earthly things, while on earth in the body thou wast a companion of the angels in spirit; for, having mortified the passions present in thy body, thou wast shown to be a servant of the Trinity, O blessed one. Wherefore, thou dost cure the sufferings of the afflicted and, at thy word, dost drive away evil spirits through grace, O our God-bearing father. Pray thou to Christ God, that remission of sins be granted unto those who celebrate thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`Abandoning the tumults of life and taking thy cross upon thy shoulders, thou didst offer thyself wholly unto God; and, being beyond the flesh and the world, thou didst become a converser with the Holy Spirit. Wherefore, raising men up to zealous deeds, thou didst empty the cities and didst make cities of desert places, O our God-bearing father. Entreat Christ God, that remission of transgressions be granted to those who celebrate thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode III sessional, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., and another Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`As the all-immaculate Bride of the Creator, * Mother of the Redeemer, who knewest not a man, * and as the receptacle of the Comforter O all-hymned one, * hasten thou to deliver me, * the vile abode of iniquity and noetic plaything of the demons, * from their evil machinations; * and make me the bright dwelling-place of the virtues, * O thou incorrupt light-bearing one. * Drive away the clouds of the pas-sions and grant that, * by thy supplications, * I may receive a portion on high ** and share in the never-waning light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],exapostilarion:{text:`With thy wisdom-loving ways thou didst make the desert a city, O divinely wise father Sabbas, adornment of the fathers, and thou didst make of it a perfect noetic paradise blossoming with the divine flowers of a multitude of those who share thy ways, fittingly celebrating thine honored memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p18 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the venerable one`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`As one who hast compassion and great mercy, O all-hymned Virgin Theotokos, look upon my lowliness and quell the turmoil of the passions and the temptations of life that assail me, O maiden, and by thy prayers deliver me from the fire of Gehenna.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`The divinely wise Sabbas, * disdainer of things below, * and sojourner and lover of things above, * dweller in the desert, * doth command us all to celebrate with faith ** the saving day of his departure unto God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Being in thy virtues apart from the flesh and from the world, * thou didst thereby glorify the Lord of glory * on earth in thy life, O wise father. * And as is fitting thou hast been glorified by Him * and shown to be a divine wellspring of healings, ** O God-pleasing Sabbas.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`O father, thou wast truly humble, guileless, meek, simple * and more quiet than other men, * and while material * thou wast shown to be a most worthy immaterial house of God, * mercifully imparting unto us ** the gifts given thee by Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`O venerable father, the sound of thy corrections hath gone forth into all the earth. Wherefore, thou hast found thy reward in the heavens, having destroyed legions of demons, thou hast attained unto the ranks of the angels, whose life thou didst blamelessly emulate. Having boldness before Christ God, beg peace for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},praises_closer:{text:`O Theotokos, thou art the true vine * that hast budded forth for us the Fruit of life. * Thee do we entreat: ** Pray thou, O Lady, with the holy apostles, that He have mercy upon our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p19 Praises Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III and 4 from ODE VI of the canon of the venerable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Having set thy mind as master over the passions, O spiritually rich father, showing thyself to be a dispenser of justice; for thou didst manifestly subject what is worse to that which is better. Wherefore, thou didst flourish in the desert like a palm tree, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having resolved to follow in the steps of the Master, thou didst forsake thy homeland; and, making thine abode in the desert, thou didst win a victory over the adversaries, strengthened by the power of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by steadfastness of mind, O all-blessed one, thou didst denounce the divers wiles of the enemy, unmasking them in the sight of all, and setting at naught his conceited audacity, O wise one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Perceiving thee to be sacred of soul and adorned with simplicity of intent and with the virtues, Euthymius, the most radiant star, received thee, prophetically proclaiming thy splendor, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having acquired love for God and neighbor, fulfilling the chief precepts of the Law and the prophets; thou didst achieve unattainable virtue, surpassing all others, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst attain on earth a life equal to that of the angels, and Christ hath given thee honor equal to that of the angels, sending thy soul to accompany the ranks of the holy ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having been shown to be a child of wisdom, thou didst desire the beginning of wisdom, the fear of God; and, strengthened thereby, O father, thou didst attain unto perfection as far is permitted.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude 7`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure Lady, who hast given birth unto God, the Savior and Redeemer of all, Who took our flesh upon Himself: from misfortune save those who call upon thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p20 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`READING FROM THE EPISTLE TO THE GALATIANS`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(5:22-6:2).`,citation:{book:`Galatians`,chapter:5,verses:`5:22-6:2`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord, in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VIII`,label_inline:!0,tone:8},alleluia_verse:{text:`His seed shall be mighty upon the earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`READING FROM THE GOSPEL OF ST. MATTHEW`,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(11 :27-30)`,citation:{book:`Matthew`,chapter:11,verses:`27-30`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-05.pdf`,locus:`p21 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-06":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.little_vespers`,`c0.great_vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our father among the saints Nicholas, Archbishop of Myra in Lycia, the Wonderworker`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR FATHER AMONG THE SAINTS NICHOLAS, ARCHBISHOP OF MYRA`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 6th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`vigil`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-06.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 2: the Menaion prints a LITTLE VESPERS for the saint, so Vigil, Fekula 2F. ODS vol. III has no 12-06 entry. Great Vespers with "Blessed is the man", 8 stichera in two sets of four (seven printed, one marked Twice), three lessons with NO reference printed (citations are identifications), a Litiya of six stichera, the blessing of the Loaves; no "if a vigil is not served" line. THE FOREFEAST OF THE NATIVITY ALREADY SOUNDS: the Both now at Lord I have cried and at the Litiya are labelled "of the forefeast", the aposticha Both now (labelled only "the composition of Byzantius") is of the same matter and is typed with them by its content, and Canon II of the hierarch is set on the irmoi of the Nativity canon, each printed again after its ode as the katavasia. Matins: two sessional hymns of the saint at each kathisma and after the Polyeleos; a Magnification and Selected Psalm verse; a Gospel; THREE canons (the Theotokos, with no Theotokion marked; Canon I by Theophanes; Canon II, whose acrostic is the Greek alphabet, with a Triadicon and a Theotokion in every ode); two exapostilaria; six stichera on the Praises printed in two sets; Great Doxology. The Praises Both now names its composer as "German us the Patriarch" (a broken word). At Liturgy the Beatitude troparia are from Ode III of Canon I and Ode VI of Canon II, six printed, one marked Twice.`,troparion:{text:`The truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, * icon of meekness, and teacher of temperance; * wherefore, thou hast attained the heights through humility and riches through poverty; * O hierarch Nicholas our father, ** entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Little Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 blessing of the Loaves`,tone:4,repeat:2},{locus:`p8 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:2},{locus:`p24 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`In Myra thou wast shown to be a performer of the sacred mysteries, O holy one, * for, fulfilling the Gospel of Christ, * thou didst lay down thy life for thy people, O venerable one, * saving the innocent from death. ** Wherefore, thou hast been sanctified as a great initiate of the grace of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Kontakion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p17 after Ode VI`,tone:3},{locus:`p24 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hierarch, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},ikos:{text:`With songs let us now hymn the holy hierarch, the pastor and teacher of the people of Myra, that we may be enlightened by his prayers. For, lo! he hath been shown to be wholly pure, incorrupt of spirit, offering to Christ the immaculate and pure sacrifice which is right acceptable to God, as a hierarch pure in soul and body. Wherefore; as a true intercessor and champion of the Church, he is a great initiate of the grace of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17-p18 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`The grace of God the Spirit * having anointed thee with divine myrrh * set thee to preside as bishop for the people of Myra, * and perfumed with the myrrh of thy virtues * the ends of the world, O most sacred one, * for by thy sweetly spiritual prayers * thou dost ever drive away the fetid passions. * Wherefore, we praise thee with faith ** and celebrate thy most sacred memory, O Nicholas.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Fittingly do we bless thee, O Nicholas, * as a never-waning luminary, * a universal beacon * shining forth brightly * in the firmament of the Church, * illumining the world, * driving away the darkness of grievous misfortunes, * dispelling the winter of grief ** and instilling profound tranquility.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Being here, and appearing in dreams, O Nicholas, * thou didst save those who were about to be unjustly put to death, * in that thou art compassionate, * as one right loving, * as a most fervent deliverer, as a true intercessor * for those who with faith ask of thee defense, * O most sacred father, * thou fellow citizen with the angels, ** peer of the apostles and prophets.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Thy most glorious life * hath ever shown thee to be most wondrous, * O divinely wise and most sacred father, * thou majesty of holy hierarchs, * adornment of the venerable. * And, spreading forth thy rays upon the earth, * like the sun thou hast illumined the hearts of the faithful * who celebrate thy radiant and divine memorial, ** O all-blessed Nicholas.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Thy memory, O holy hierarch, hath shone forth like the sun, noetically illumining the hearts of the faithful; and celebrating it today with splendor, we cry out to thee in prayer: Rejoice, O might of chastity who, armed with the shield of abstinence, didst preserve the estate of thy soul intact! Rejoice, O pastor and teacher of thy Christian people! Rejoice, adornment of the Church, beauty of hierarchs, boast of monastics! O all-blessed and most sacred father Nicholas, unceasingly entreat Christ God, that He grant peace to the whole world and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer:{text:`No one that fleeth unto thee, O most pure Virgin Theotokos, * departeth from thee ashamed; * for those that asketh grace of thee, ** ever receiveth a gift for their profitable petition.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`O blessed Nicholas, have pity on me who fall down before thee, I pray, and enlighten the eyes of my soul, O most wise one, that in purity I may gaze upon the compassionate Bestower of light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:6,spec_mel:`On the third day ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`As thou hast boldness before God, O blessed hierarch Nicholas, rescue me from the enemies who seek to do me evil, and save me from men of blood, O holy one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`On the third day ...`},{text:`Thy priests shall be clothed with righteousness, * and Thy righteous shall rejoice.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O hierarch, we, the faithful, have acquired thee as a calm haven, an impregnable rampart, a tower of confirmation and a portal of repentance, a guide and champion of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`On the third day ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Zealous in his opposition to thy flock, O most pure one, every day the wicked adversary seeketh to devour it. But rescue us from his harm, O Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory/Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers dismissal Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya_rubric`,`litiya`,`litiya_glory`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`,`virgin_theotokos_rubric`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera of the holy hierarch: 4 in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Dwelling bodily in Myra, * thou wast truly shown to be myrrh, * having been anointed with noetic chrism, * O holy Nicholas, hierarch of Christ, * thou dost perfume the faces of those * who with faith and love ever celebrate * thine all-glorious memory, * freeing them from misfortunes, perils and sorrows ** by thy prayers to God, O father.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`As a true namesake of victory, * to the faithful people * thou hast been revealed to be mighty amid perils, * O holy Nicholas, hierarch of Christ; * for whenever thou art invoked, * thou dost quickly hasten to those who with love * have recourse to thy protection. * For, appearing to the faithful by day and at night, ** thou dost save them from dangers and evil circumstances.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`In a dream thou didst appear * to the Emperor Constantine and to Ablavius, * and instilling fear in them, * thou didst speak to them thus: * “Quickly release those whom ye hold bound in prison, * for they are undeserving of a lawless execution. * But if thou wilt disobey me, * I will petition the Lord and King against thee ** when I pray!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`For those of us who find ourselves * amid misfortunes as we journey * by land or sail the seas, * for those of us who are nearby or afar off, * thou art a great and fervent advocate, * an exceeding merciful and mighty intercessor, * O holy Nicholas, sacred preacher of Christ. * Wherefore, assembling, we cry: ** Entreat the Lord, that we may be delivered from every evil circumstance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`With what wreaths of praise shall we crown the holy hierarch who, while bodily in Myra, doth spiritually reach out to all who love him in purity, the advocate and helper of all, the comforter of all the sorrowful, the refuge for all amid misfortunes, the pillar of piety, the champion of the people? For his sake hath Christ, Who hath great mercy, cast down the arrogance of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`And 4 in Tone II`,spec_mel:`With what wreaths of praise ...`,tone:2},{text:`With what songs of hymnody shall we praise the holy hierarch, the opponent of impiety and champion of piety, the leader, great ally and teacher, who putteth to shame all the infamous, the destroyer of Arius and his followers? For his sake hath Christ, Who hath great mercy, cast down the arrogance of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`With what wreaths of praise ...`},{text:`With what hymns of prophecy shall we praise the holy hierarch, who foresaw things far distant and unerringly prophesied things afar off as though they were near, who watches over the whole world and delivers all the oppressed, who of old appeared to the divinely wise emperor in a dream and delivered from execution those unjustly arrested, bestowing upon us great mercy?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 7`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`With what wreaths of praise ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Assembling, O ye who love the feasts of the Church, let us hymn the adornment of hierarchs, the glory of the fathers, the well-spring of miracles and great defender of the faithful, saying: Rejoice, O protector of Myra, honored primate and steadfast pillar of its Church! Rejoice, O most radiant beacon, illumining the ends of the earth with wonders! Rejoice, divine joy of the sorrowful and fervent intercessor for the oppressed! And now, O blessed Nicholas, cease not to entreat Christ God on behalf of those who honor thine ever-gladsome and most illustrious memory with faith and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer:{text:`Adorn thyself well, O cave, for the ewe-lamb approacheth, bearing Christ in her womb! O manger, receive Him Who by His word hath loosed us mortals from irrational activity! Ye shepherds, piping, bear witness to the awesome wonder! O magi from Persia, bring ye gold, frankincense and myrrh to the King, for the Lord hath re-vealed Himself through the Virgin Mother! And, gazing down upon Him, His Mother made obeisance to Him as though she were His handmaiden, and greeted Him as she held Him in her embrace, saying: “How wast Thou sown within me, and how didst Thou spring forth within me, O my Redeemer and God?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Both now, of the forefeast`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., of the forefeast, in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM PROVERBS`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:10,verses:`10:7, 3:13-16, 8:6`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. The body opens "The memory of the just is praised" (Proverbs 10:7) and moves to "Blessed is the man who hath found wisdom" (3:13-16), then the Wisdom-speech of chapter 8: the composite hierarch lesson, as 11-14A Lesson 1. The body runs on past 8:6. Identified by correspondence; confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM PROVERBS`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:10,verses:`10:31-32, 11:1-12`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "The mouth of the righteous droppeth wisdom" (Proverbs 10:31) and closes "a sensible man is quiet" (11:12), as 11-14A Lesson 2. Identified; confirm against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:4,verses:`7-15`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "Though the righteous be prevented with death", closes "that He doth visit His chosen": Wisdom 4:7-15. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`}],litiya_rubric:{text:`At Litiya, these Stichera, the composition of Byzantius:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya rubric`}},litiya:[{text:`Christ God hath revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith and a model of meekness, O holy hierarch Nicholas. For which cause, as one who emitteth sweet fragrance in Myra, and whose divine corrections shine forth in the joy of the Lord, ever intercede for us, O holy Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,composer:`Byzantius`,sourceLabel:`In Tone II`,label_inline:!0,tone:2},{text:`O father Nicholas, the shrine of thy relics, like a phial, doth enrich Myra with fragrant myrrh. And, appearing to the emperor in a vision during sleep, thou didst thereby free from death, fetters and prison those unjustly held condemned. And now, as then, do thou ever appear in visions, praying for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O father Nicholas, even though the land of Myra hath fallen silent, yet the whole world, which hath been enlightened by thee with the sweet fragrance of thy myrrh and the multitudes of thy miracles, crieth out in hymns of goodly praises; and we, saved by thee from condemnation cry out with those in Myra, chanting: Pray thou, that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O father Nicholas, as the phial of the most holy Spirit, thou pourest forth the sweet fragrance of divine perfume in Myra; for, having emulated the apostles of Christ, thou dost traverse the world over in the report of thy miracles. Wherefore, appearing during sleep to those afar off and to those nearby, thou didst deliver from death those who were to be executed through an unjust sentence, and most gloriously savest from misfortunes many who call upon thee. Wherefore, by thy supplications, from besetting evils free us also, who ever praise thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya 4`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`In Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},{text:`The fruit of thy valiant deeds hath illumined the hearts of the faithful, O venerable father. For who, hearing of thy boundless humility, hath not marveled at thy patience, thy solicitude toward the poor, thy consolation of the sorrowful? Thou hast taught all in a godly manner, O holy hierarch Nicholas, and hast now been crowned with a never-fading wreath. Pray thou on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya 5`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`In Tone VIII`,label_inline:!0,tone:8},{text:`Throughout this fleeting life thou didst hasten to praise the Lord, O Nicholas, and He hath therefore glorified thee in the true life in heaven. Wherefore, having acquired boldness before Him, pray that He save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya 6`},label:`plain`}],litiya_glory:{text:`O good and faithful servant, husbandman of the vineyard of Christ: thou didst bear the burden of the day and didst increase the talant entrusted to thee; and thou didst not envy those who came after thee. Wherefore, as the portals of heaven have been opened to thee, enter thou into the splendor, O intercessor for the orphans and widows. Wherefore, pray thou unceasingly, that He save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},litiya_closer:{text:`Hold festival, O Sion! Be glad, O Jerusalem, thou city of Christ! Receive the Creator Who is contained in the cave and the manger! Open unto me thy gates, and, entering therein, I shall behold Him Who holdeth all creation in His hand, wrapped as a babe in swaddling-clothes: the Lord and Bestower of life, Whom the angels hymn with unceasing voices, and Who saveth our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Both now, of the forefeast`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., of the forefeast, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the holy hierarch, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Rejoice, O sacred one, pure abode of the virtues, standard of the most divine priesthood, great shepherd, most radiant beacon, who bearest victory in thy name, who dost ever incline mercifully to those who entreat thee, bending thine ear to the pleas of the infirm, ready deliverer, saving preserver of all who with faith honor thine all-glorious memory! O most blessed one, beseech Christ, that He send down great mercy upon the world!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Rejoice, O most sacred mind, pure habitation of the Trinity, pillar of the Church, confirmation of the faithful, help of the vanquished, star who, by the splendors of thy right acceptable supplications, dost ever dispel the darkness of perils and sorrows, calm haven to which those beset by the threefold waves of life hasten and find salvation. O holy hierarch Nicholas, entreat Christ, that He grant great mercy to our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Thy priests shall be clothed with righteousness, * and Thy righteous shall rejoice.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Rejoice, O thou who wast filled with divine zeal, and who, by thy dread confrontation and warnings, didst deliver from a wicked sentence those who were unjustly condemned to be executed, O wellspring in Myra, pouring forth myrrh in abundance, giving drink to our souls and driving away the fetor of the passions, O sword mowing down the tares of delusion, O winnowing-fan scattering the teachings of Arius like chaff! O Nicholas, pray thou, that He send down great mercy upon our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`O man of God, faithful servant and minister of the Lord, man of divine desires, chosen vessel, pillar and foundation of the Church, heir of the kingdom: cease thou never to cry unto the Lord on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Glory`},composer:`John the Monk`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of John the Monk, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_closer:{text:`O Virgin who knewest not wedlock, from whence hast thou come? Who begat thee? Who is thy mother? How is it that thou bearest the Creator in thine arms? How is it that thy womb was not subject to corruption? O the great, most glorious and awesome mysteries which we see wrought in thee on earth, O all-holy one! We make ready fitting recompense for thee on earth: the cave; and we ask that the star be given from heaven, and that magi come from the lands of the East to the West, to behold the Salvation of men, Who is wrapped in swaddling-bands in the manger.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Both now`},composer:`Byzantius`,type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., the composition of Byzantius, in Tone VI`,tone:6},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the Loaves, the Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Blessing of the Loaves rubric`}},virgin_theotokos_rubric:{text:`And “Virgin Theotokos, rejoice! ...,” (Once).`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p7 Virgin Theotokos rejoice rubric`}}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.troparion_closer.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_glory.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord rubric`}},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},sessional_1:[{text:`Dwelling bodily in Myra, O hierarch, thou wast shown to be noetically anointed with the myrrh of the Spirit, O father Nicholas. Wherefore, thou hast perfumed the world with the myrrh of thy wonders, pouring forth ever-flowing myrrh through thy memory and thy discourses, which are fragrant of myrrh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Thy tomb, O Savior ...`,tone:1},{text:`Thou shinest forth upon the earth with rays of miracles, O wise Nicholas, moving every tongue to the glorification and praise of Him Who hath glorified thee on earth. Him do thou beseech, that we who with faith and love honor thy memory may be delivered from all want, O thou who art chosen among the fathers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., another Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,tone:1},{text:`Through the Holy Spirit didst thou conceive in thy womb God, the Creator and Fashioner of all, O pure and all-immaculate one, and gave birth to Him without corruption. Glorifying Him, we hymn thee, O Virgin, as the palace of the King of all, the protection of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1}],sessional_2:[{text:`Thou intercedest for the faithful, protecting and preserving them, O blessed one, and manifestly delivering them from all sorrow, O most comely glory and boast of hierarchs, venerable Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared today ...`,tone:4},{text:`Receiving from God a well-spring of miracles, O wise father, thou pourest forth honeyed waters upon all the faithful, O blessed one; for as a pastor and preacher of the Faith, thou didst carry out the words of the true Shepherd. Wherefore, as thou hast boldness before Him, thou didst save men from death, O blessed hierarch Nicholas. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who honor thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p8-p9 Sessional 2, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., another Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`I have fallen into the mire of sins, and there is no firm place for me. The tempest of transgressions hath cruelly engulfed me. Yet as thou hast given birth to the Word Who alone is the Lover of mankind, look upon me, thy servant, and deliver me from every sin and the soul-destroying passions, and from every wicked affliction of the murderer, O Theotokos who knewest not a man. Entreat Christ God, that He grant me remission of sins, for thee do I, thy servant, have as my hope.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify thee, O holy hierarch Nicholas, and we honor thy holy memory; for thou dost entreat Christ God on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Hear this, all ye nations; give ear, all ye that inhabit the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God. (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`O ye faithful, let us all piously praise the God-bearing Nicholas, the most wise hierarch, as a fervent ally and defender amid misfortunes and sorrows, sent by God; for he prayeth to the Lord on behalf of those who with faith celebrate and hymn his divine memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone V`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word ...`,tone:5},{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a most ardent intercessor for the Church of Christ, O Nicholas, boldly refuting the ungodly teachings of heresies, and thou hast been revealed to all as a standard of Orthodoxy, praying for all who follow thy divine teachings and instructions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., another Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Go thou quickly before ...`,tone:4},{text:`Quickly receive our prayers, O Lady, and bring them to thy Son and God, O all-blameless Sovereign Lady; extinguish the blasphemies of the evil-tongued heretics; bring to naught their devices, and cast down the impudence of the ungodly who make war against thy servants, O most pure One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon in Tone IV`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p9 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. JOHN`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§36 (10:9-16)`,citation:{book:`John`,chapter:10,verses:`9-16`,pericope_number:36},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`O heir of God, fellow communicant of Christ, minister of the Lord, holy Nicholas: as was thy name, so also was thy life. For the radiance of thy countenance bore witness to thine intellect, shining forth in thine innocence of spirit, and thy serenity proclaimed thy meekness. Thy life was glorious, and thy repose is with the saints. Pray thou on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone VI`,tone:6},canon_rubric:{text:`Canon of the Theotokos, with 6 Troparia, including the Irmos; and two canons of the holy hierarch, with a total of 8 Troparia;`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the Theotokos, in Tone I:`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us all chant a triumphant hymn unto God * Who wrought wondrous miracles * with His upraised arm, * and saved Israel, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O pure one who hast given birth to the Abyss of wisdom, by thy grace send down upon me a wellspring which poureth forth drops of wisdom, that I may hymn the abyss of thy grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`I hymn thee, O all-hymned one, whom the ranks of angels hymn as the one who gave birth to the supremely hymned God, Whom all creation doth hymn, for He hath been glorified.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Let my heart be established in Thy will O Christ God, * Who hath established a second heaven over the waters, * and founded the earth upon the waters, * O all-powerful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`I herald the Theotokos as the abode of the King, more pure than the heavens, the truly fragrant garden of paradise emitting the sweet odor of grace, the hope of Christians.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`At the word of the archangel thou hast given birth to the Word Who by His word hath brought all nature, rational and irrational, into existence, and Who delivereth mankind from irrationality, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Foreseeing in the Spirit O prophet Habbakuk, * the incarnation of the Word, * thou didst proclaim, crying aloud: * When the years draw nigh, Thou shalt be known; * when the season cometh, Thou shalt be shown forth! * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Eve became the cause of death for mortals through the counsel of the serpent; but thou, O pure Virgin who at the angel's word gave birth to the Word, hast been revealed to be the mediatress of immortality and life. Wherefore, we hymn thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Foreseeing thee in the Spirit as the mountain, the gate, the table, the holy ark, the lampstand, the throne of Life, the jar and couch, O pure one, the prophets revealed thee beforehand in indistinct images, the fulfillment of which we behold.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Shine forth thy radiant and everlasting light * upon us who rise early at dawn, * unto the judgments of Thy commandments, * O Master, Lover of mankind, * Christ our God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O honored Lady, thou didst contain God Almighty like the ark of sanctity, like the holy throne of fire, like a sanctified palace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O only most pure one, among virgins thou hast been revealed to be a Mother who knew not a man, and among mothers a virgin; for thou didst ineffably give birth to God Who animateth nature.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Emulating the prophet Jonah, I cry aloud: * Free Thou my life from corruption, O good One; * and save me who crieth out: * O Savior of the world, Glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O help of the faithful and joyful gladness of the grieving, with spiritual joy enrich thy servants, who desire thine aid.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let the noetic heaven, the most pure temple, the holy ark, the most beautiful paradise of God, wherein the Tree of my life doth stand, be hymned!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The furnace became bedewed, O Savior, * and the children dancing, chanted: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The Most High hath shown thee, O pure one, to be an animate heaven, a bridal-chamber surrounded with grace, a royal robe in-woven with gold, a garden of paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Make steadfast the inconstancy of my mind, and by thy protection establish my turbulent thoughts upon the immovable Rock, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Him of whom the angels and all the hosts of heaven are in awe * as their Lord and Creator, * ye priests hymn, ye children praise, * ye peoples bless and supremely exalt * throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Virgin, thou hast been revealed to be an animate bridal-chamber and an inspired mantle of scarlet, the embroidered cloak of the King of all, and the purple robe, from whom the flesh of the Word and God-man shone forth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ineffably, and beyond all understanding, thou didst conceive God the Creator, Who holdeth all creation in the palm of His hand, Who for our sake became a man like us, without forsaking that which He was.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The ever-flowing wellspring of life, * light-bearing candlestick of grace, * the animate temple, and most pure cloud, * wider than the heavens and the earth, * the Theotokos do we the faithful magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`A stream of thy grace do thou pour forth upon me who am consumed by the flame of afflictions, and am grievously wasting away, O wellspring who pourest forth in abundance and hast given birth to the River of grace, which, drinking thereof, we thirst no more.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lady of all, save me who entreat thee as the beautiful chamber of the Bridegroom, the animate palace of the Master, the golden robe, the most comely habitation of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon I of the holy hierarch, the acrostic whereof is: “I chant divine hymnody unto thee, O Nicholas”, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone II:`,acrostic:`I chant divine hymnody unto thee, O Nicholas`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`In the deep of old the infinite Power overwhelmed Pharaoh's whole army. * But the Incarnate Word annihilated pernicious sin. * Exceedingly glorious is the Lord, * for gloriously hath He been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Standing, crowned, before the throne of Christ with the angelic armies, O most wise Nicholas, grant me the enlightenment which illumineth the darkness of my soul, that, rejoicing, I may praise thy memory, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord Who glorifieth all who glorify Him hath given thee to the faithful as a refuge delivering from perils those who have recourse to thy protection, who call upon thee with faith and love, O Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The all-wicked serpent, instilling in me the desire to make myself equal with the Creator, took me captive; but through thee, O all-pure one, I have been restored and truly deified, for thou hast given birth to Him Who hath deified me, O Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The desert of the barren Church of the nations * blossomed like a lily * at Thy coming, O Lord, * therein hath my heart been established.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O blessed Nicholas, as thou art the true disciple of the Master thou savest from grievous misfortunes and bitter death, those who have recourse to thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Cleanse thy servants, granting them remission of sins, in that Thou art good, through the mediations before Thee of Nicholas, Thy favorite, O greatly Merciful One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Quell thou the turmoil of my soul, O all-pure one, and guide thou my life, O most holy one who hast given birth to God, in Whom my heart hath been established.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`From a Virgin didst Thou come forth, not as an ambassador, * nor as an angel, * but the very Lord himself incarnate, * and didst save me, the whole man; * wherefore I cry unto Thee: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having in purity drawn nigh to the rays of the Spirit, thou didst become a light-bearer, illumining the ends of the world, interceding for all, and saving all who have recourse to thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As of old thou didst appear, delivering the young men from death, O venerable Nicholas, so now save me from every evil circumstance, from perils and misfortunes, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst shine forth with the effulgence of the virtues, O all-blessed one, as a most excellent emulator of thy Master; saving those who invoke and glorify thee with reverence and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Incarnate, the Master of creation came upon thee, wholly saving me, in that He is compassionate. Wherefore, we, the faithful, glorify thee as Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ my Savior, the enlightenment of those lying in the darkness of sin. * I rise early to hymn Thee O King of Peace, * enlighten me with Thy radiance, * for I know no other God than Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Enlightened by a godly life, O thrice blessed one, standing forth thou didst deliver those condemned by an unjust sentence to death, and who cried to Christ God: We know none other God than Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Now beholding everlasting glory in the heavens, and delighting in the most splendid effulgence of ineffable and divine radiance, protect me by thine intercessions, O venerable and most honorable favorite of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`That Thou mightest seek out Thine image, which had been buried by the passions, O Savior, hiding from the heavenly hosts, Thou didst appear, incarnate of the Virgin, to those who cry to Thee: We know none other God than Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Whirled about in the abyss of sin, * I appeal to the unfathomable abyss of Thy compassion: * Raise me up from corruption, O God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The crown of victory hath fittingly been placed upon thy head, O Nicholas. As thou art a most excellent victor, save those who call upon thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Appearing, O blessed one, save me who am slain by transgressions and engulfed by the threefold billows of the passions, and lead me to the harbor of the will of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thee, O Ever-virgin Mother, have I placed my hope of salvation, and thee do I set forth as the steadfast and unshakable intercessor for my life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`When the golden image was worshipped on the plain of Dura, * Thy three children spurned the impious command, * and, cast into the midst of the flame, * they were bedewed, and sang: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Into precipitous temptation have I fallen, and am grievously pierced; I have drawn nigh unto the gates of Hades and am wounded by sorrows. Save me by thy supplications, O blessed one, and raise me up who chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined with the immaterial rays of the never-waning Light, rescue the afflicted who find themselves in the darkness of tribulations, and guide to the light of gladness those who chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ask Christ, thy Son and God, O Virgin Birthgiver of God, for those sold under grievous transgressions and the deceptions of the serpent, that by His pre-cious Blood they may be delivered who chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`God Who descended into the fiery furnace * with the Hebrew children, * and transformed the flame into dew, * do ye works hymn, * and supremely exalt as Lord throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As thou art good and compassionate, O blessed Nicholas, free those who are grievously mired in the abyss of perils, granting them release from the evils which hold them, by thy supplications to Christ the Savior, O initiate of the sacred mysteries.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art an initiate of things which pass understanding, the minister of things holy and celestial, and a faithful hierarch, O divinely wise one, ask our Savior for remission of transgressions, O thou who art manifest in sanctity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`My mind now faileth, having fallen into the abyss of impiety, for I am beset on every side by divers evils; yet do thou heal me, O Virgin, clothing me in the light of dispassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Son of the beginningless Father, God and Lord, * hath appeared to us incarnate of a virgin, * to enlighten those in darkness, * and to gather the dispersed; * therefore the all-hymned Theotokos do we magnify`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Enlightened by lamps of grace, O divinely wise one, thou didst manifestly become a lamp of piety: saving those in danger, delivering those out upon the deep of the sea, and most gloriously feeding the hungry, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Dwelling now in the sweetness of paradise, and clearly beholding ineffable glory, thou lookest down from the circles of heaven upon those who hymn thee, delivering them from sufferings, O all-blessed God-bearer.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure Mother of God, thou hast given birth to the Wisdom, Power and hypostatic Word of the Father, Who built the temple of His body from thy most pure blood, and inseparably joined Himself to it through unification.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}},{title:`Canon II of the holy hierarch, the acrostic whereof, excluding the Triadica and Theotokia, is the (Greek) alphabet, in Tone I:`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ is born, render ye glory. * Christ cometh from heaven, meet ye Him. * Christ is on earth, be ye exalted. * O all the earth, sing unto the Lord, * and sing praises in gladness, O ye people, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Though my tongue and lips are at a loss, O Nicholas, I have come to bring this meager praise and entreaty to thy godly excellence; but, as thou art a bestower of riches, render God the Savior merciful to me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a heavenly man thou wast shown to be angelic upon the earth, a ready defender of widows, an avenger of the oppressed, and a helper amid misfortunes for all who are sorrowful, O father Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`All who are under the heavens speak of the abyss of the wonders of thy virtues, O thrice blessed Nicholas: the poor call thee their intercessor, the orphans and widows their nurturer, the blind their guide, and all mankind their champion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I honor the uncreated Trinity the Father, the Son and the Spirit - the simple Being, the Godhead, the indivisible Essence, which existeth essentially in three Hypostases, distinguished as to Person and Hypostasis.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Without seed thou didst conceive the Word Who is One of the Trinity, O all-immaculate one, giving birth to Him in the flesh, yet remaining a virgin after birthgiving, as thou wast before. Ever entreat Him on our behalf, in that He is thy Son and God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Christ is born, render ye glory. * Christ cometh from heaven, meet ye Him. * Christ is on earth, be ye exalted. * O all the earth, sing unto the Lord, * and sing praises in gladness, O ye people, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 1 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},3:{irmos:{text:`To the Son who was begotten of the Father * without change before all ages, * and in the last times, without seed, was made flesh of the Virgin, * to Christ our God let us cry aloud: * Thou hast raised up our horn, holy art Thou, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having acquired in thy heart tablets inscribed with many virtues by the immortal and most pure finger of Christ God, O Nicholas, sweetness’s greater than that of honey or the honey-comb poureth forth from thy lips.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Grace most gloriously showed forth miracles in thee, O Nicholas, for thy pure life, truly more lustrous than gold, illumines darkened souls with the radiance of the divine Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou livest even after death, manifestly appearing in dreams, and most gloriously delivering the young men from death, crying aloud to the emperor: “Do no harm to these men, who have been slandered by vainglorious jealousy!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Be merciful, O all-holy Trinity our God, unto me who have defiled my life with immeasurable transgressions, O Father, Son and living Spirit, Who preservest me wholly and ever unwounded by sorrow.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O Theotokos, thou givest thy servants hope of salvation. Stand forth in thy speedy supplications to preserve and help us amid wants and perils, for thou art the boast of us, the faithful, O Ever-virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`To the Son who was begotten of the Father * without change before all ages, * and in the last times, without seed, was made flesh of the Virgin, * to Christ our God let us cry aloud: * Thou hast raised up our horn, holy art Thou, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 3 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},4:{irmos:{text:`Rod of the root of Jesse, * and flower that blossomed from his stem, * O Christ, Thou hast sprung from the Virgin. * From the Mountain overshadowed by the forest * Thou hast come, made flesh from her that knew not wedlock, * O God who art not formed from matter. * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`When thy name alone is invoked, with all speed it truly delivereth those who fervently call upon thee from all the counsels of the enemy, O sacred Nicholas. As of old thou didst deliver the soldiers, so also save us from every grievous circumstance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Standing before the throne of God, cease thou never to make earnest supplication on behalf of all of us, thy faithful servants, O wise and wondrous Nicholas, that we may be delivered from everlasting fire, from the enemy, from the wicked tongue, and from affliction.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou dost everywhere pour forth healings upon those who have recourse to thee, delivering all from bondage. Wherefore, by thy supplications which are acceptable to God, transform our grief into joy, O most radiant Nicholas, casting down the proud haughtiness of our enemies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I honor and venerate the principality of the beginningless Godhead-the Father, the Son, and the all-holy Spirit, which accomplisheth all things, and is one, indivisible, and ever distinguished in three sets of characteristics and Hypostases: the single undivided Kingship.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 4 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Thou alone art truly more honorable than those on earth and those in heaven, O Birthgiver of God, for thou didst conceive in thy womb the Creator of all, clothed in material flesh, giving birth to Him without seed. O what a new wondrous sight!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Rod of the root of Jesse, * and flower that blossomed from his stem, * O Christ, Thou hast sprung from the Virgin. * From the Mountain overshadowed by the forest * Thou hast come, made flesh from her that knew not wedlock, * O God who art not formed from matter. * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 4 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},5:{irmos:{text:`As Thou art the God of peace and Father of compassions, * Thou hast sent unto us Thine angel of great counsel, * granting us peace. * Wherefore guided towards the light of the knowledge of God, * and watching by night we glorify Thee, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The great metropolis of Myra, the province of Lycia, and all the parts of thy homeland, proclaim thy wonders and miracles, whereby thou dost deliver all from pain and sorrow, O divinely blessed father Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As the feeder of wisdom and father of orphans, the most excellent help of those in sorrow, the consolation of the grieving, the shepherd and guide of all the lost, O Nicholas, by thy supplications deliver us from misfortunes.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast passed over from earth to the immaterial mansions, where thou dost gaze upon the ineffable beauty of Christ, and hast been revealed to be a converser with the angelic armies. Wherefore, joining chorus with the apostles and martyrs, earnestly pray for us to the Master of all, O father Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I manifestly glorify the three independent Hypostases of the one, indivisible Godhead, co-beginningless and co-enthroned, by Whom I have been brought out of nothingness into existence; and with the angels I cry; Holy, Holy, Holy art Thou, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O pure one, who alone settest salvation and hope before all mankind and savest them, help us now who cry aloud to thee and ever call upon thee amid grievous circumstances; for after God, we have none other intercessor than thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`As Thou art the God of peace and Father of compassions, * Thou hast sent unto us Thine angel of great counsel, * granting us peace. * Wherefore guided towards the light of the knowledge of God, * and watching by night we glorify Thee, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p16 Ode 5 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},6:{irmos:{text:`The sea monster spat forth Jonah as it had received him, * like a babe from the womb: * while the Word, having dwelt in the Virgin and taken flesh, * came forth from her yet kept her incorrupt. * For being Himself not subject to decay. * He preserved His Mother free from all harm.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a new Abraham, O Nicholas, for, ever offering up the un-bloody sacrifice, thou didst bring thy mind to thy Master as if it were thine only-begotten son; wherefore, thou wast blessed as a lover of strangers, O father, and became a divine and immaculate habitation of the Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou workest strange and awesome miracles, O Nicholas, interceding in thy speedy supplications for those in peril throughout the earth and far out at sea, showing thyself to the faithful as a physician of the sick, a feeder of the poor, and the namesake of victory over the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Foreseeing things yet to come with the eye of thy mind, thou didst fill all the ends of the earth with right doctrines, and, declaring to us that the Son is consubstantial with the Father, thou didst set at naught the savagery of Arius, O pillar of the Orthodox Faith, setting forth thine honored corrections.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I venerate and honor the indivisible Trinity, which is ever distinguished in three Hypostases, and united in essence and nature, as a single Principal: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit, Who with might hath dominion over all and preserveth all things as He so desires.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Wholly incarnate within thy womb, O most pure one, Christ God was born without seed; for, unable to endure the sight of the work of His hands tormented by the deceiver, He came in the guise of a servant to deliver the race of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The sea monster spat forth Jonah as it had received him, * like a babe from the womb: * while the Word, having dwelt in the Virgin and taken flesh, * came forth from her yet kept her incorrupt. * For being Himself not subject to decay. * He preserved His Mother free from all harm.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p17 Ode 6 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},7:{irmos:{text:`Scorning the impious decree of the godless one, * the children brought up together in godliness * feared not the threat of fire, * but standing in the midst of the flames, they sang: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having been shown to be a most excellent physician of all manner of grievous ailments, and having healed the infirmity of my soul, O father Nicholas, grant me goodly health, that I may cry: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having of old delivered the warriors from death, O holy one, thou didst raise them up to hymn and glorify Christ with ardent faith; and they cried aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p18 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having mystically approached the cup of wisdom, O father Nicholas, from thy lips thou didst let fall rain-drops sweeter than honey or the honey-comb, commanding the people to cry aloud: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We hymn Thee, O Trinity, Thou thrice-effulgent consubstantial Unity: Father, Son and Holy Spirit. And having been baptized there-into, we chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 7 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`As thou art more exalted than all other creatures, O Theotokos, entreat thy Son and God, that those who truly honor and glorify thee may be delivered from torments, crying: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`Scorning the impious decree of the godless one, * the children brought up together in godliness * feared not the threat of fire, * but standing in the midst of the flames, they sang: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p19 Ode 7 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},8:{irmos:{text:`The furnace moist with dew * was an image and prefiguring of a wonder past nature, * burning not the children whom it had received, * so the fire of the Godhead consumed not the Virgin's womb * into which it had descended. * Therefore in song let us sing: * Let the whole creation bless the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The ranks of the patriarchs and apostles, the assemblies of the hieromartyrs, the company of prophets and the whole council of fasters bless thy godly life; and with them we also cry aloud: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Most High, O Word, Thou King of all great in might! Through the supplications of the venerable pastor grant peace to the life of all Christians, aiding our Orthodox hierarchs in the struggle against heresy, that with him we may cry out to Christ: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined with light unapproachable, O father, thou shinest upon the souls of those in tribulation, dispelling all the gloomy darkness of perils, and enlightening our hearts with gladness. And enlightened thereby from afar, we cry aloud: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Following the truly divine teachings of the fathers, with faith we hymn the Trinity - the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit - the Life and Lives, the One and Three Lights. And with them we piously chant: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Of old on Mount Sinai, the bush prefigured a strange mystery, O pure maiden, burning without being consumed, depicting the mystery of thy birthgiving; for the fire of the Godhead which dwelt within thee preserved thee unharmed. Him do we magnify throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`The furnace moist with dew * was an image and prefiguring of a wonder past nature, * burning not the children whom it had received, * so the fire of the Godhead consumed not the Virgin's womb * into which it had descended. * Therefore in song let us sing: * Let the whole creation bless the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p20 Ode 8 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},9:{irmos:{text:`A strange and most wondrous mystery do I see: * the cave is heaven; * the Virgin the throne of the cherubim; * the manger a room, in which Christ God, * whom nothing can contain, is laid. * Whom we praise and magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ye who love the feasts of the Church, let us all join chorus in spirit. Ye heavens, ye mountains and hills, ye choirs of virgins and of the Church, ye splendor of fasters: rejoice at the memorial of the all-blessed one; and, assembling together thereon, let us magnify the Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With hymns let all the ends of the earth chant unceasingly, manifestly adorning Nicholas, the favorite of Christ God, with wreaths of praise. Through his supplica-tions may we be delivered from sufferings and misfortunes.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Nicholas, accept this meager effort as fitting hymnody, as Christ accepted the widow's two mites. Disdain not one accursed with passions, for it is not out of pride that I presumed to do so, O thrice-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Trinity is united in a consubstantial will, yet it is indivisibly distinguished in Hypostases - the Father, the Son and the living Spirit - the one God in three Hypostases, ever preserving His might. Him do we magnify.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p21-p22 Ode 9 Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`All grief hath been abolished by thy birthgiving, and the Lord hath taken away lamentation, weeping, and every tear from the face of mortals, O pure Theotokos who knewest not wedlock. In thee do we also fulfill our debt.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia:{text:`A strange and most wondrous mystery do I see: * the cave is heaven; * the Virgin the throne of the cherubim; * the manger a room, in which Christ God, * whom nothing can contain, is laid. * Whom we praise and magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Ode 9 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having ascended to the summit of the virtues and been illumined by the divine splendors of miracles O father, thou wast truly revealed to be a most radiant pastor for the world, and an invincible intercessor for us amid perils. Wherefore, having most gloriously vanquished the enemy, thou didst drive falsehood away and save many from sin. O Nicholas, entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love honor thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy hierarch, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`The Abyss of mercy hath shown thee to be a river pouring forth healings in abundance and an inexhaustible well-spring of miracles, O Nicholas; for those who are bitterly afflicted with grievous ailments and cruelly tormented by the vexations of life truly find the curative healing of all suffering in thy fervent defense. Wherefore, we cry aloud to thee: Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of transgressions unto those who with love celebrate thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode III sessional, Glory`},label:`glory`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Another Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`All we, the generations of mankind, * call thee blessed, * in that thou art the Virgin who alone among women * hast given birth without seed unto God in the flesh; * for the fire of the Godhead made its abode within thee, * and thou didst feed the Creator and Lord * with milk as an infant. * Wherefore, we, the race of mankind and of angels, * glorify thy birthgiving, * and together we cry out to thee: * Entreat Christ God to grant forgiveness of sins ** unto those who with faith worship thy most holy Offspring.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],exapostilarion:{text:`Let us all praise Nicholas, the great arch-pastor, hierarch and prelate of Myra; for he saved those who were unjustly condemned to be executed, appearing to the emperor and to Ablavius in a dream, annulling the unjust verdict.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy hierarch`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_glory:{text:`The Lord glorified thee greatly in miracles, both during thy life and after thine end, O hierarch Nicholas; for whenever anyone, out of love for the Faith, doth but call upon thy holy name, he is straightway heard, and findeth thee to be a fervent intercessor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Another Exapostilarion`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Another Exapostilarion`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Having given birth to Christ, the hypostatic Wisdom, the transcendent Word, the Physician of all, O Virgin, heal thou the grievous and longstanding wounds of my soul, and slay thou the passionate thoughts of my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 6 Stichera: 2 Stichera, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Lifting thine eyes unwaveringly toward the heights of understanding, and gazing mystically into the abyss of wisdom, O father, thou hast enriched the world with thy teachings. Pray thou ever to Christ on our behalf, O holy hierarch Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1},{text:`O man of God, faithful favorite, performer of His mysteries, man of divine desires, animate pillar and inspired image: the Church of Myra, marveling, received thee as a divine treasure, and an advocate for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Praises 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Soaring above the flowers of the Church, * like a fledgling of the angelic nest of the Most High, * O thrice-blessed Nicholas, * thou ever criest out to God * on behalf of us who find ourselves amid violent misfortunes and temptations, ** delivering us by thy supplications.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`And 4 Stichera, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`,tone:1},{text:`Thou didst make the beauty of thy priestly vesture * yet more splendid through active virtues, * O God-bearing father; * wherefore, as a hierarch thou dost accomplish wondrous things for us, * delivering us from evils, ** O sacred minister of glorious miracles.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p22-p23 Praises 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Passing through the beauties of the invisible ones, * thou didst comprehend the awesome glory of the saints, * O holy one; * wherefore, O most sacred father, * thou hast revealed to us in heavenly words ** the visions of those who live eternally.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p23 Praises 5`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Thou didst stand before the pious emperor in a dream, * and didst deliver the prisoners from death, O father. * Pray thou unceasingly, * that, by thy supplications, * we also, who praise thee well, * may be delivered from temptations, ** misfortunes and pain.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p23 Praises 6`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`Rejoicing, let us sound the trumpet of festal hymns, let us leap up and join chorus on this the God-bearing father's prayerful celebration. Let kings and princes come together, and let them hymn him who by his dread appearance in a dream prevailed upon the king to release the three warriors who were unjustly imprisoned. O ye teachers and pastors of the good Shepherd, assembling, let us praise the pastor who showed forth love like His. And lauding the great hierarch, the physician of the infirm, the redeemer of those in misfortune, the helper of sinners, the treasure of the poor, the consoler of the sorrowful, the companion of those who travel, the helmsman of those at sea, who fervently anticipateth the needs of all in every place, let us say thus: O most holy Nicholas, come forth and deliver us from these present tribulations, and save thy flock by thy supplications!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p23 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone V`,tone:5},praises_closer:{text:`Let us sound the trumpet of hymnody! For the Queen of all, who is both Mother and Virgin, hath been revealed from on high, and with blessings crowneth those who hymn her. Let those who exercise dominion assemble and in hymns praise the Queen who hath given birth unto the King Who before was well-pleased, in His love for mankind, to deliver those held fast by death. Ye pastors and teachers, assembling, let us praise the most pure Mother of the good Shepherd, the golden lamp-stand, the Light-bearing cloud, her who is more spacious than the heavens, the animate ark, the fiery throne of the Master, the golden jar which received the Manna, the gate of the Word which was shut, the refuge of all Christians; and praising her with divinely eloquent hymns, let us say thus: O palace of the Word, vouchsafe the kingdom of heaven unto us, the lowly, for naught is impossible for thy mediation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p23 Praises Both now`},composer:`Germanus the Patriarch`,type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., the composition of German us the Patriarch, in Tone V`,tone:5},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p23 Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of Canon I, and 4 from ODE VI of Canon II of the holy hierarch.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`O blessed Nicholas, as thou art the true disciple of the Master thou savest from grievous misfortunes and bitter death, those who have recourse to thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Cleanse thy servants, granting them remission of sins, in that Thou art good, through the mediations before Thee of Nicholas, Thy favorite, O greatly Merciful One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a new Abraham, O Nicholas, for, ever offering up the un-bloody sacrifice, thou didst bring thy mind to thy Master as if it were thine only-begotten son; wherefore, thou wast blessed as a lover of strangers, O father, and became a divine and immaculate habitation of the Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou workest strange and awesome miracles, O Nicholas, interceding in thy speedy supplications for those in peril throughout the earth and far out at sea, showing thyself to the faithful as a physician of the sick, a feeder of the poor, and the namesake of victory over the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`I venerate and honor the indivisible Trinity, which is ever distinguished in three Hypostases, and united in essence and nature, as a single Principal: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit, Who with might hath dominion over all and preserveth all things as He so desires.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude Triadicon`},label:`trinitarion`,sourceLabel:`Triadicon`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Wholly incarnate within thy womb, O most pure one, Christ God was born without seed; for, unable to endure the sight of the work of His hands tormented by the deceiver, He came in the guise of a servant to deliver the race of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`The righteous man shall be glad in the Lord, * and shall hope in Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O God, unto my prayer, when I make supplication unto Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p24 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE HEBREWS,`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p25 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§ 335 (13: 17-21)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:13,verses:`17-21`,pericope_number:335},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Thy priests shall be clothed with righteousness, and Thy righteous shall rejoice.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p25 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},alleluia_verse:{text:`For the Lord hath elected Sion, He hath chosen her to be a habitation for Himself.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p25 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE,`,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p25 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 24 (6: 17-23).`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:6,verses:`17-23`,pericope_number:24},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-06.pdf`,locus:`p25 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-07":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our father among the saints Ambrose, Bishop of Milan`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR FATHER AMONG THE SAINTS, AMBROSE, BISHOP OF MILAN`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 7th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-07.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the hierarch at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-07 entry. The page prints three stichera of the Theotokos to be sung first "if Alleluia be chanted at Matins", and "The Aposticha from the Oktoechos" with no Glory. At Matins one canon, with five troparia in Odes I and IX and four elsewhere (the rubric says "with 4 Troparia"); the sessional hymn after Ode III; the kontakion after Ode VI with NO ikos; no exapostilarion. The troparion is the general one of a hierarch with the name written in. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`The truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, * icon of meekness, and teacher of temperance; * wherefore, thou hast attained the heights through humility and riches through poverty; * O hierarch Ambrose our father, ** entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Shining with divine dogmas, thou didst darken the deception of Arius, * O Ambrose, pastor and teacher of the mysteries. * And working wonders through the power of the Spirit, * thou didst manifestly heal divers passions, O venerable father. ** Entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:3},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hierarch, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Of the divine faith ...`,tone:3},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_rubric`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy hierarch, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Adorning the seat of government with thy virtues, * thou didst likewise receive the hierarchal office * through divine inspiration, * wherefore, having been a faithful steward * of grace in both, O Ambrose, ** thou didst inherit a twofold crown.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`In abstinence and sorrow, * in many vigils and in lengthy prayers, * thou didst cleanse soul and body, O divinely wise one; * henceforth manifest as a chosen vessel of Christ God, * equal to the apostles, ** thou didst receive heavenly gifts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`As Nathan reproved David, * so didst thou boldly reprove the pious emperor who once had sinned, * O all-blessed Ambrose, * and thou didst openly cut him off from the Church; * and having chastised him in godly manner with a penance, ** thou didst number him again amongst thy flock.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`O pure Birthgiver of God, * with the staff of thine intercession * drive thou the bestial passions * from my wretched soul; * and, peacefully guiding me to life, ** number me among the holy flock of thy chosen sheep.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art the helper of helpless men, * as thou art the hope of all the hopeless, * O Theotokos, be thou my release and aid amid evils, * O most pure one, * delivering me from sins and tribulations, ** in that thou art merciful.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With divine dew and by the rain of thy will, * quench the fiery urgings * of my most pernicious passions O Virgin, * that even I, like the youths, * may render thanks unto God Who was born from thee, ** and glorify and bless thy grace, O Lady.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`Having stumbled headlong through my corrupt character, * I lay prostrate, O Virgin, yet I flee to thy serenity. * Deliver me from the storm of the adversary * and from multifarious temptations, * that I may unceasingly hymn thy grace, ** O ever-virgin Mother and Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Standing at the foot of the Cross of thy Son and God, * and looking upon His long-suffering, * O pure Mother, weeping, thou didst say: * “Woe is me, O my sweetest Child! * How is it that Thou sufferest these things unjustly, O Word of God, ** that Thou mayest save mankind?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},aposticha_rubric:{text:`The Aposticha from the Oktoechos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and the canon of the saint, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I praise Ambrose most great,” in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and the canon of the saint, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I praise Ambrose most great,” in Tone IV:`,acrostic:`I praise Ambrose most great`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Through the deep of the Red Sea, * marched dry shod Israel of old, * and by Moses’ outstretched hands, * raised in the form of a cross, * the power of Amalek was routed in the wilderness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O venerable one, radiant with divine splendors, by thy prayers illumine those who piously honor thy radiant, light-bearing and holy repose.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Word of God gave thee the discourse of wisdom adorned with true knowledge, O hierarch Ambrose, dispelling the irrational and malicious thought of the heretics.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having cleansed the vision of thy mind of the darkness of the passions, most noetically rich hierarch, thou didst render it receptive to the pure effulgence of the most holy Spirit, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having by thine all-wise and sacred dogmas, as a pastor fended off the destruction of those who were of like mind with Arias, O all-wise one, with faith thou didst shepherd thy rational sheep in the meadows of Orthodoxy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`By the Father's will and through the divine Spirit of God, thou didst, seedlessly conceive and give birth in the flesh unto the Son Who, for our sake, was begotten of the Father without mother and was born of thee without father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Not in wisdom, nor in power do we glory, * but we glory in Thee O Christ, * the Hypostatic Wisdom of the Father, * for there is none more holy than Thee, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having received of God an abundance of grace and power, O father Ambrose, by thy tangible touch thou didst heal the divers passions of those who had recourse to thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O venerable one, having learned all the knowledge of the Scriptures, in that thou wast a godly hierarch, thou didst manifestly make plain to the ignorant things difficult to understand, O father Ambrose.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the sentence of God thou didst instantly strike dead the vile woman who audaciously and senselessly strove to draw nigh unto thee, who shone forth with spiritual wisdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou alone hast renewed the human race, having given birth unto the Creator and Lord of our nature. Wherefore, we glorify thee, O divinely joyous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`For the sake of love for Thine image, * O compassionate One, * Thou didst ascend the cross * and the nations melted away. * For Thou, O Lover of mankind, * art my strength and my praise.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having been anointed with the chrism of the priesthood, thou wast shown forth as a hierarch, ordaining priests and granting the cleansing of salvation unto all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst protect thy flock from all the harm of the adversaries, O blessed one, and didst blind the delusion of Arius with the radiance of thy words.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Invested with the power of the Spirit, thou didst dispel the evil spirits of malice, who could not endure thy rebuke, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`He that wrought all things by His will is Himself wrought of thy pure blood, saving those who acknowledge thee to be the pure Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, who camest into the world, * art my light, * a holy Light turning from the darkness of ignorance * those who sing Thy praises in faith.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having attained a mind resplendent with immaterial light, O blessed Ambrose, thou hast emitted rays of healing and miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst raise thyself up as a sacred dwelling place of the Spirit, O divinely inspired Ambrose, destroying the temples of idolatry.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emperors were put to shame by thee, shining with the effulgence of the greatest of virtues, and their restrictions did not cause thy tongue to falter.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`He that wrought all things in wisdom through His will, desiring to renew mankind, O Virgin, made His abode within thy womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The Church crieth out unto Thee O Lord, * ‘I will sacrifice unto Thee with a voice of praise * having been cleansed of the blood of the demons' * by the blood that for mercy's sake flowed from Thy side.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Amazed, Rome faithfully praiseth thine honored deeds; for, like a radiant star, O hierarch, thou dost shed the rays of thy wonders everywhere.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having risen at dawn for Christ, thou hast been richly illumined with splendors and filled with divine light; enlightening those who ever faithfully honor thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having sanctified body and soul, O father, thou didst render thy heart, which ever attendeth unto sweet desire, receptive to the gifts of grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Heal thou the wounds of my soul, O Virgin, by thy divine overshadowing, and enlighten my mind, which hath been darkened by slothfulness and by the malice of the adverse foe.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`In the Persian furnace the youths and descendants of Abraham, * burning with a love of piety * rather than by a flame of fire, * cried aloud saying: * Blessed art Thou in the temple of Thy glory, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Like lightning, the divine proclamations of thy dogmas have flashed throughout all the earth, O all-wise father; shoning forth as light with the revelations of miracles, and enlightening hearts that were in darkness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Following the command of the Savior, O father, thou didst, like a blessed servant, diligently increase manifold the talent given thee, and hast been deemed worthy of the Master's joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having deepened thy theological mind, like a river thou didst put forth streams of sacred dogmas, giving drink unto the fullness of the faithful, O father Ambrose, teacher of the mysteries.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Behold, O Virgin, thou didst conceive within thy womb the Word Who is co-beginningless with the Father, and hast given birth in the flesh unto Him Who granteth restoration unto all who from Adam have fallen, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Having spread his hands, Daniel closed the lions’ jaws * in their den; * while the zealously pious youths, * girded with virtue, * quenched the power of the fire and cried aloud: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having mortified thy members and slain the wisdom of the flesh, thou didst impart life unto thy soul and poured forth a fountain of miracles upon those who had been slain by the passions, O venerable one, granting life unto those who cry: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast informed of thine approaching repose in the body by the Spirit of God, O wise one; for thou didst say so prophetically unto those who were with thee, and didst pass over to the heavens crying out with joy: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having rid thy body, mind and heart of the turbulence of the passions, O Ambrose, thou didst receive a fiery ray of light from on high, crying out like the divine disciples: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast been revealed to be more exalted than the heavens, O most pure one, having given birth unto the God of heaven, Who hath united those of earth with those of the heavens, and Who granteth knowledge of Himself unto all who cry aloud: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`A cornerstone not cut by hand O Virgin, * was cut from thee the unhewn mountain: * even Christ, Who hath joined together the disparate natures; * therefore rejoicing we magnify thee, * O Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`In ecstasy thou didst behold the everlasting honors which are being laid up for the saints, O father; and having passed over to them, rejoicing, thou hast received the reward of thy labors, O glorious one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like a ripe cluster of grapes wast thou gathered into the vats of heaven, pouring forth the wine of immortality and gifts of healing upon those who piously have recourse to thee, as is meet, O divinely wise Ambrose.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With a mighty voice we bless thee, O father, the golden candlestick of the divine Spirit, which putteth forth the light of pious teachings and the radiance of healings, enlightening the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Church, O all-blessed one, having acquired thee as a daystar, doth escape all the deception of darkness, and, illumined with the splendors of thy sacred dogmas, she doth bless thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`With joy we utter unto thee the salutation of the archangel, O Virgin: Rejoice, thou abolition of the curse! Rejoice, deliverance from all evils, O thou who, in a manner beyond understanding, hath deified mortals by thy birthgiving!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Zealously emulating Elijah the prophet, and likewise John the Baptist, thou didst manfully denounce the iniquitous emperor, O hierarch; in a godly manner adorning thy see, and enriching the world with a multitude of miracles. Wherefore, learned in the divine Scriptures, thou didst establish the faithful therein, and convert the unbe-lieving. O hierarch Ambrose, entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of transgressions unto those who, with love, celebrate thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy hierarch, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`Having fallen with wicked thoughts, * I have sunk into the abyss of sin, * and, groaning, I cry to thee with all my heart, O all-pure one: * Show forth upon me the wonder of thy rich mercy, * the unfathomable depth of thy tender compassion * and the immeasurable wealth of thy compassions, * and grant me repentance and forgiveness of transgressions, * that I may cry unto thee with love: * Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto me, ** for thee do I, thy servant, have as my hope.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Upon beholding the Lamb, Shepherd and Redeemer * upon the Cross, * the ewe-lamb exclaimed weeping, bitterly lamenting, and crying aloud: * “The world rejoiceth, having received deliverance through Thee, * but my womb doth burn, beholding Thy crucifixion, * which Thou hast endured in Thy merciful loving-kindness. * O long-suffering Lord, * Thou abyss and inexhaustible well-spring of mercy, * take pity, and grant forgiveness of sins ** unto those who hymn Thy divine sufferings with faith!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-07.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-08":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our venerable father Patapius of Thebes`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR VENERABLE FATHER PATAPIUS OF THEBES`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 8th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-08.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the venerable one at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-08 entry. The page prints three stichera of the Theotokos to be sung first "if Alleluia be chanted at Matins". No Glory of the saint, no aposticha and no aposticha rubric are printed at Vespers. At Matins one canon, no acrostic printed; the sessional hymn after Ode III; the kontakion after Ode VI with NO ikos; no exapostilarion. The ODE VII heading is printed with every glyph doubled. The troparion is the general one of a venerable father with the name written in. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`In thee, O father, the image of God was preserved, * for taking up thy cross, thou didst follow after Christ; * by activity thou didst learn to disdain the flesh, as something transient, * but to care for thy soul as something immortal. ** Wherefore, with the angels thy spirit doth rejoice, O venerable Patapius.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:8},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},kontakion:{text:`Those who find thy temple to be a place of spiritual healing, O holy one, * and have recourse thereto with zeal, * ask to receive the healing of their infirmities * and forgiveness of the transgressions committed by them in their lives; ** for thou art seen to be an intercessor for all that are in need, O venerable Patapius.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:3},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer_rubric`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O father Patapius, * having quenched the burning * of the assaults of the flesh by abstinence, * like Elijah of old thou didst make thine abode in the desert, * purifying thy mind with unceasing prayers unto God. * And pray thou now, * that He grant our souls ** peace and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`O father Patapius, * thou didst enroll thyself in the choirs of fasters, * adorning thyself with dispassion; * and making thine abode in the mansions of the venerable, * where the light is unwaning * and the Tree of Life doth stand. * And pray thou now that peace and great mercy ** be granted our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`O father Patapius, * thou didst shine forth as a beacon from Egypt, * enlightening the world * with the splendors of thy miracles, * and dispelling the gloom of soul-destroying infirmities, * driving off the darkness of the demons. * And pray thou now, ** that peace and great mercy be granted our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`Incorruptibly didst thou give birth unto God * Who hath destroyed corruption and poured forth incorruption, * O incorrupt and undefiled one. * Wherefore, I beseech thee: * By thy prayers, O pure one, * renew me who have become corrupt through wicked deeds, * that with love I may glorify and magnify thee ** who hast exalted our race.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-hymned Lady, * thou hope and confirmation, * refuge and help of the faithful, * thee do we entreat: * From all misfortune preserve thy servants * who worship thy birthgiving with faith, * and pray thou unto Christ, ** that He grant our souls peace and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Alas! What shall become of me * who by transgressing have defiled mind, soul and body? * What shall I do? * How will I be able to avoid the unquenchable flame * and the everlasting and unbreakable bonds? * But before the end * entreat thy Son, O all-immaculate one, ** to grant me forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`In thy womb * thou didst bear Christ, * the Fire of the divinity, * O all-pure one. * Him do thou now beseech, * that He quench the easily kindled matter of my passions, * deliver me from everlasting fire, * and grant me the splendor of the righteous ** when He cometh to judge all things.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The Sovereign Lady, the unblemished ewe-lamb, * beholding her Lamb upon the Cross, * bereft of form and comeliness, * lamenting, said: “Woe is me! * Whither hath Thy comeliness gone, O most Sweet One? * Where is Thy splendor? Where is the brilliant grace * of Thine image, ** O my Son most beloved?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},troparion_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion Theotokion rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and this canon of the venerable one, with 4 Troparia, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and this canon of the venerable one, with 4 Troparia, in Tone II:`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`In the deep of old the infinite Power overwhelmed Pharaoh's whole army. * But the Incarnate Word annihilated pernicious sin. * Exceedingly glorious is the Lord, * for gloriously hath He been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`I pray thee, O venerable Patapius: Beseech the Lord Who driveth away the clouds of ignorance, that He grant a ray of grace from heaven unto me who desires to praise the splendid achievements of thy radiant life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He Who of old covered the Egyptians with the deep by divine command, having drawn thee forth as from the abyss of the world's turmoil, illumined thee with divine splendors and showed thee forth as a most radiant star, O venerable father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Burning with the fervor of the Spirit like a noetic ember, O venerable one, thou didst drive away the gloom of the demons and quenched the fiery darts of sin; and being most pure thou wast led to the summit of dispassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Granting the world deliverance from the ancient curse, the Redeemer was born from thee, O Virgin, He Who hath shown the venerable Patapius to be a wellspring of healing for all who have recourse to him in faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`The desert of the barren Church of the nations * blossomed like a lily * at Thy coming, O Lord, * therein hath my heart been established.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having thoroughly watered the field of thy soul with streams of tears, thou didst bring forth the divine grain of good works which is stored in the granaries on high.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Armed with love as with a sword, and protected thereby as with a shield, O venerable one, thou didst destroy legions of demons by thy divine humility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like a lily thou didst sprout the blossom of abstinence, O venerable one, perfuming the hearts of those who hymn thee and celebrate thy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Borne upon the arms of her who gave birth to Thee, O Lord, by Thy might Thou didst destroy the idols of Egypt, from whence a multitude of the venerable sprang forth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`From a Virgin didst Thou come forth, not as an ambassador, * nor as an angel, * but the very Lord himself incarnate, * and didst save me, the whole man; * wherefore I cry unto Thee: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The sea of thy fervent fears drowned the armies of the demons and the uprisings of sin; and thou didst show thyself to be a sea of miracles unto those who are in the midst of the seas of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having acquired humility, vigilance and intense prayer, unfeigned love, faith and hope, O venerable father, thou didst become a converser with the angels of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With divine ascents and unceasing purification thou didst lay to rest the tumult of divers passions. Wherefore, after thy repose thou didst depart unto the unwaning light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like the sun through a cloud didst Thou shine forth from the Virgin, O compassionate One, showing Thy venerable ones to shine like stars, having crucified themselves to the world and the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ my Savior, the enlightenment of those lying in the darkness of sin. * I rise early to hymn Thee O King of Peace, * enlighten me with Thy radiance, * for I know no other God than Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Enlightenment of those who lie in darkness, shine Thy radiance upon me through the divine prayers of Thy venerable one, drive away the clouds of despair which hang over my soul, and rain down upon me the dew of forgiveness, for I know none other God than Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having purged thy noetic eye of the defilement of the passions by abstinence, O God-bearing father, thou didst open the eyes of the blind with divine prayer and dispelled the gloom of evil with the effulgence of healing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come ye, let us all draw forth health of body and soul, and abundant grace from the divine shrine of the wise Patapius, as from a wellspring, for it poureth forth miracles like water upon those who have recourse to it with pure faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thine ineffable birth giving, O maiden, thou didst give birth to the Giver of life Who created all things, to Him Who is glorious in the saints and resteth in the venerable. Him do thou entreat, O Bride of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Whirled about in the abyss of sin, * I appeal to the unfathomable abyss of Thy compassion: * Raise me up from corruption, O God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Illumining thy mind with most radiant ascents, O father, thou didst live in the flesh as one of the bodiless ones, unsullied by sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating Elijah the Tishbite and following John the Forerunner, of old thou didst make thine abode in the desert, having cleansed thy mind with stillness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A beacon of most godly splendor from Egypt, O most radiant father Patapius, thou didst shine forth in the city of Constantinople with the effulgence of healings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ Who sitteth upon a light cloud came of old into Egypt, and, having cast down the idols, He hath brought together choirs of the venerable.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`When the golden image was worshipped on the plain of Dura, * Thy three children spurned the impious command, * and, cast into the midst of the flame, * they were bedewed, and sang: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With noetic fire thou didst inflame the senses of thy soul; reducing the fire of sin to ashes by the activity of the Spirit, and wast thereby revealed to be radiant, O Patapius, chanting: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely blessed one, who opened the eyes of the blind with divine assistance, O divinely blessed one, thou didst heal divers passions and by the invocation of God drove away the wicked legions of the demons, chanting: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O father, thy tomb hath been shown to be an abyss of wonders, a river of healing, and an ever-flowing wellspring, a stream which is never exhausted, for those who approach it with faith and cry out fervently: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The supremely divine God Who was born from thee, O Virgin, hath deified me, having Himself taken on the guise of a servant; and He hath restored the paths of knowledge within the bounds of His nature, leading aloft a multitude of monks and the venerable one, who chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`God Who descended into the fiery furnace * with the Hebrew children, * and transformed the flame into dew, * do ye works hymn, * and supremely exalt as Lord throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having cleansed thyself of the filth of the passions with care, O father, thou wast revealed to be a most splendid tabernacle of God, crying aloud: Hymn the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having ordered thy life in a godly manner, O venerable father, thou wast shown to be a good steward serving the needs of the saints, O venerable one; and with them thou hast been deemed worthy of a heavenly inheritance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy prayers to the Lord cleanse us of every impurity, and by thy fervent supplication, O Patapius, do thou deliver from the threefold waves of passions, infirmities and tribulations us who honor thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one who rendered our earthly and corruptible nature celestial, glory of the angels and joy of the venerable, thou that alone art the Sovereign Lady of creation, forever hymned as she who gave birth unto God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Son of the beginningless Father, God and Lord, * hath appeared to us incarnate of a virgin, * to enlighten those in darkness, * and to gather the dispersed; * therefore the all-hymned Theotokos do we magnify`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy commemoration hath dawned as a day of salvation enlightening those who are in the murky darkness, dispelleth the gloom of the passions and showeth forth as children of the light those who now honor thee as a favorite of the Lord, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Patapius, who was shown to be an angel on earth, the offspring of Thebes, the boast of the desert, the glory and splendor of monastics, the beacon of Byzantium, let us now bless him as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Being a converser with the angels, the peer and fellow heir of the prophets and apostles, the martyrs and hierarchs, thou didst serve the honored Trinity with purity of mind, O venerable one. Pray thou on behalf of us all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The great mystery of thy birthgiving, which surpasseth understanding, doth astound the angels, O divinely joyous one, delighting the assemblies of the venerable, and gladdening the sacred fathers who hymn thee in a godly manner, O pure Theotokos who knewest not wedlock.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`The flame of the passions didst thou quench with streams of fasting and abstinence, pouring forth an abyss of wonders upon all, and like another Moses, thou didst thereby subdue the deceitful assaults of legions of demons. Wherefore, assembling, we honor thy most worthy and prayerful commemoration, O venerable and God-bearing Patapius. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who honor thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`As thou hast given birth unto the merciful and loving Word, O Lady of all, have mercy upon all who have recourse to thee and free us from temptations and illness, from all afflictions and from the everlasting flame, that in thanksgiving we may glorify the wealth of thy many compassions and thine infinite mercy, and that we may ever cry out to thee: Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who worship thy birthgiving with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`The Virgin and Mother of the Redeemer, standing before the Cross and lamenting with tears of anguish, cried out maternally: What strange and most glorious thing is this that I behold, O my Son? Thou Who pourest forth dispassion upon all mankind art crucified upon a Cross between two condemned malefactors, Thy side pierced, and given gall to drink by hands which Thou Thyself hast made; but arise and grant remission of sins unto those who hymn Thy divine Passion with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-08.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-09":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.little_vespers`,`c1.great_vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`feast`,name:null,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE CONCEPTION OF THE MOST HOLY THEOTOKOS BY SAINT ANNA`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 9th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`doxology`,fekula_section:`2C`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-09.pdf`,note:`Rank: \`doxology\`. ODS vol. III has this date (ods3-1209-sun, ods3-1209-wkd; rank "doxology" by its explicit rubric), and the page agrees with the 1.1 waterfall: "Great Doxology" is printed after the Praises, with no Polyeleos, no lessons, no Litiya. Six stichera at Lord I have cried (three printed, each marked Twice); the aposticha are the feast's own, with verses; "This Troparion is chanted without a Theotokion"; the troparion is marked Thrice at God is the Lord. The sessional hymns and the exapostilarion are each followed by "Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated." Two canons "of the righteous Anna": Canon I by Andrew, Canon II (acrostic the alphabet) on the irmoi of the Nativity canon, with "Katavasia: Christ is born" printed after Ode I only. The troparion's Liturgy printing moves one phrase mark and is stored at its own position. At Liturgy six Beatitude troparia printed (two marked Twice, for the eight of the rubric), and two communion verses.`,troparion:{text:`Today, the bonds of barrenness are loosed, * for God, hearkening unto Joachim and Anna, * doth manifestly promise unto them who, beyond all expectation, * will give birth to the divine maiden, * from whom the Infinite One Himself, becoming a man, shall be born. * And He commandeth the angels to cry unto her: ** Rejoice, thou who art full of grace, the Lord is with thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the conception`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p3 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:3}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the conception, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Today the whole world doth celebrate Anna's conceiving, * which was brought about by God; ** for she gave birth unto her who ineffably gave birth unto the Word.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Kontakion of the conception`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p8 after Ode VI`,tone:4},{locus:`p12 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the conception, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Thou hast appeared today ...`,tone:4},ikos:{text:`The wondrous Joachim and the divinely wise Anna, living together in all piety according to the law of Moses, were childless; and they prayed to God with all their heart, saying: “O supremely good Lord of hosts, Thou help of all: Thou knowest the pain, reproach and grief of childlessness. Wherefore, grant us fruit of the womb, and Ye will bring to Thy temple as a; sacred gift and perfect offering her who ineffably giveth birth unto the Word!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer_rubric`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera of the conception, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`The barren woman who, * in a manner past hope, beareth as fruit * her who will give birth to God in the flesh, * is made radiant with joy * and danceth, rejoicing * and crying aloud: * Let all the tribes of Israel rejoice with me! * For, lo! I have conceived in my womb * and put away the disgrace of barrenness: * for thus hath the Creator been well pleased, * and, hearkening unto my prayer * in those things which I have desired, ** He hath healed the pain of my heart.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`},{text:`He Who poured forth water * from the dry stone, * granteth fruit to thy womb, O Anna: * the Ever-virgin Theotokos, * from whom the water of salvation will issue forth. * No longer shalt thou remain on earth * like barren ground; * thou hast put away thy disgrace. * For, thou givest rise to the fertile ground * which will bear the Grain of life Who taketh away the disgrace of all men, * for He hath been well pleased in the loving-kindness of His mercy ** to form Himself in what is alien to Him.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`},{text:`The sayings of the prophets * are now fulfilled: * for the holy mountain * is rooted in Anna's womb; * the divine ladder is set up; * the great throne of the King is made ready; * the place wherein God will enter is adorned; * the unburnt bush * beginneth to sprout forth; * the phial of holiness already poureth forth, * spreading abroad in rivers the fruitfulness * of the divinely wise Anna, ** whom with faith we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Called from on high ...`}],lic_closer:{text:`The most glorious great mystery hidden from the beginning of time, which was unknown to angels and mortals, is manifest today: Mary, the divine maiden, becometh a child in the womb of the chaste Anna, and is prepared as a dwelling-place for the King of all ages, unto the restoration of our race. Her do we entreat with pure conscience, crying out to her: Beseech thy Son and God, in that thou art the intercessor of us Christians, that He save our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now`},composer:`Germanus`,type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of Germanus, in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Once Anna, the divinely favored one, praying for a child, cried out to God the Creator of all: “O Adonai Sabaoth, Thou knowest the disgrace of my barrenness! Do Thou Thyself relieve the pain of my heart: open the flood-gates of my womb and show me forth, who am barren, to be fertile; that, in thanksgiving, we may offer Thee the gift which is born, chanting and glorifying with oneness of mind Thy compassion, whereby great mercy is given to the world.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`The Lord hath sworn in truth unto David, * and He will not annul it.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Of old, the chaste-minded Anna, entreating and beseeching God, heard an angelic voice which announced to her the divine fulfillment of her petitions. With her one of the incorporeal ones manifestly conversed, saying: “Thy supplication hath come before the Lord. Be not downcast, neither weep, for thou shalt be a fruitful olive-tree, putting forth as a branch the comely Virgin Who shall give rise in the flesh to a Flower: Christ Who granteth great mercy to the world!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Of the fruit of thy loins * will I set upon thy throne.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The honorable couple beareth as fruit the divine heifer, from whom the Bullock will come forth, Who is truly fattened by His ineffable word and Who will be slaughtered for the whole world. Therefore, rejoicing, in compunction they offer unceasing confession to the Lord and will conceive her who will benefit all things. Wherefore, let us call them blessed and let us dance with faith at their divine conceiving of the Mother who will give birth to our God, and through whom great mercy is richly given.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Today the mystic flower beginneth to grow out of Jesse, the robe of royal purple sprouteth forth from the root of David, wherein Christ our God shall spring forth, saving our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone II`,tone:2},troparion_closer_rubric:{text:`This Troparion is chanted without a Theotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p2 The troparion is chanted without a Theotokion`}}},matins:{order:[`god_is_lord_rubric`,`troparion`,`sessional_1`,`sessional_2`,`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer_rubric`,`praises_rubric`,`praises`,`praises_closer`,`great_doxology_rubric`],god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the conception, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 God is the Lord rubric`}},sessional_1:[{text:`A new heaven is fashioned in the womb of Anna by the command of God the Creator of all, from which the never-setting Sun shall shine forth, illumining the whole world with rays of divinity in the superabundance of His tender compassion, in that He alone is the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`The choir of angels ...`,tone:1},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 1 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],sessional_2:[{text:`Of old, the choir of prophets proclaimed the pure and immaculate divine maiden and Virgin, whom Anna doth conceive, being barren and childless. Her do we bless today with gladness of heart, having been saved for her sake, who alone is pure and immaculate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,tone:1,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in the same melody`},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Sessional 2 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],canon_rubric:{text:`Two canons of the righteous Anna: the first with 8 Troparia, including its Irmos; and the second with 6 Troparia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon I, composition of Andrew, in Tone I:`,composer:`Andrew`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us all chant a triumphant hymn unto God * Who wrought wondrous miracles * with His upraised arm, * and saved Israel, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O divinely wise Anna, we celebrate thy conception today, for, loosed of the bonds of barrenness, thou didst conceive her who contained Him Who is in nowise contained.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst hearken to the supplication of the righteous ones, didst fulfill the vow of Thy holy forebears, O Lord, and didst give them a fruit: the pure one who gave Thee birth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The glorious Anna now conceiveth the pure one who conceived the supremely good, incorporeal Lord, and who will give birth in the flesh unto Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`From a corruptible womb didst thou shine forth, O Virgin, for in thine incorrupt womb thou didst bear the Sun of glory Who became as we are, save for change and confusion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Let my heart be established in Thy will O Christ God, * Who hath established a second heaven over the waters, * and founded the earth upon the waters, * O all-powerful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Anna cried to the Lord: “If Thou wilt grant fruit to my womb, I shall be magnified, and will offer it to Thee.” Therefore, she conceived the pure Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having observed the provisions of the law and served God blamelessly, O most honorable Anna, thou truly bearest in thy womb her who wilt give birth unto the Giver of the law. Wherefore, we, the faithful, call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`When thou didst pray in the garden, thou didst hear the voice of the Most High, O divinely wise Anna; and He gaveth fruit to thy womb: the portal which by grace shall open paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Dispel all the barrenness of my fruitless mind, and show forth my soul to be fruitful in the virtues, O all-holy Theotokos, thou help of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Foreseeing in the Spirit O prophet Habbakuk, * the incarnation of the Word, * thou didst proclaim, crying aloud: * When the years draw nigh, Thou shalt be known; * when the season cometh, Thou shalt be shown forth! * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“O the divine proclamation! O the strange report, if I shall conceive!” Anna cried out, amazed, to the angel who was sent to her. “Glory be to my God, Who hath wrought marvelous things!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Rejoice with me, all ye tribes of Israel! I have conceived in my womb a new heaven, from which Jesus, the Bestower of life, shall in time shine forth!” Anna cried, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`God hearkened to the sighs of Anna; the Lord attended to her supplication and, dispelling the cloud of her childlessness, He most gloriously illumineth her with the light of fertility. Wherefore, she conceiveth her who alone is pure.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Theotokos, undefiled tabernacle, with the most pure sprinkling of the compassions cleanse me now who have been defiled by transgressions, and grant me a helping hand, that I may cry: glory to thee, O pure and divinely glorious one!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Grant us Thy peace, O Son of God, * for we know no other God than Thee, * and we call upon Thy Name, * for Thou art the God of the living and the dead.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Springing forth from the root of Jesse and David, Anna now beginneth to put forth the divine shoot which shall give rise to Christ, the mystic Flower, the Creator of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“The people look upon me who am become a mother, and marvel;” Anna cried, “for, lo! I shall give birth, as is the good pleasure of Him Who loosed the bonds of my barrenness!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“The voices of the prophets proclaimed from afar the maiden whom I have conceived, to be the mountain and the impassable gate!” Anna cried out most joyfully to those who came to her.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure Virgin Mother, we know thee to be the cloud, paradise and portal of light, the fleece, the jar bearing Manna within, the sweetness of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Emulating the prophet Jonah, I cry aloud: * Free Thou my life from corruption, O good One; * and save me who crieth out: * O Savior of the world, Glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`How can she who contained God in her womb be contained? How can she who gave birth unto Christ in the flesh be born? How can she who nourished the Creator with milk take nourishment at a woman's breast?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hearkening unto your entreaty, O all-praised Joachim and Anna, God this day doth now grant you fertile fruit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having conceived the pure dove in her womb, Anna was truly filled with spiritual joy, offering hymns of thanksgiving unto God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The threefold waves of wicked thoughts, the assaults of the passions and the abyss of sins bestorm my wretched soul. Help me, O holy Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Thy children who were in the furnace O Savior, * were neither touched nor troubled by The fire. * Whereupon the three sang, as with a single mouth * Thy praises and blessed Thee, saying: * 'O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou.'`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Anna entreated the Master of all, that she might escape the reproach of childlessness; and, hearkening unto her pitiful cry, He granted her as fruit her who gave birth to Him, as was His good pleasure.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Anna, the weaving of a robe of royal purple beginneth in thy womb, wherewith God, the King of all, having clothed Himself, appeareth unto men and layeth low the enemies which war against us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In thy womb, O Anna, didst thou conceive the fragrant myrrh who, in a manner transcending nature, received the Master, the Myrrh of life, Who perfumeth our thoughts with the wafted scents of grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We glorify Thee as One of the Trinity, O Christ; for, incarnate of the Virgin without change, Thou didst assume full humanity, without separation from the Father's nature, though Thou didst unite Thyself to us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Him of whom the angels and all the hosts of heaven are in awe * as their Lord and Creator, * ye priests hymn, ye children praise, * ye peoples bless and supremely exalt * throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“Behold! I receive in my womb the Queen whom David foretold,” cried Anna; “and I shall give birth unto the intercessor for all the faithful, who will give birth unto Christ the King!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The land in which the Creator of earth made His abode, the holy scepter, the new ark, the jar of Manna who gave birth to Him, beginneth to bud forth in her mother's womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The unburnt bush, the golden candle-stand, the animate bridal-chamber of the Lord God, the precious staff who gave birth to Him, beginneth to bud forth in her mother's womb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Raise me up who lie in the abyss of evils, and vanquish the enemies that now engage me in battle. Disdain me not who am wounded by countless pleasures, O good and pure one, but take pity and save me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The ever-flowing wellspring of life, * light-bearing candlestick of grace, * the animate temple, and most pure cloud, * wider than the heavens and the earth, * the Theotokos do we the faithful magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Conceiving the Life-receiving well-spring, O divinely wise Anna, receive joy now, taking the holy temple into thy womb, magnifying her who is radiant with the light of the Creator's righteousness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let Joachim and Anna be honored: the honorable and most glorious twain, the forebears of the pre-eternal Son, the renowned observers of the law, who gave birth to the first-fruits of joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us hymn the Virgin Theotokos, whom Daniel beheld as a great mountain, whom Joel saw as a holy land, whom Isaiah perceived as an impassable gate, and another prophet foretold as a sealed fountain and divine fleece.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let the Virgin Theotokos be glorified: the purple which dyed the fleece of the ineffable incarnation of the Word, the golden lamp-stand, the table on which Christ, the Bread of life, was set forth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}},{title:`Canon II, the acrostic whereof is the alphabet, in Tone I:`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ is born, render ye glory. * Christ cometh from heaven, meet ye Him. * Christ is on earth, be ye exalted. * O all the earth, sing unto the Lord, * and sing praises in gladness, O ye people, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Anna, receiving in her womb the pure Virgin and divine maiden who will become the Mother of the Creator, cried out with joy: “All ye tribes of Israel, rejoice with me! For, behold! I have conceived!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Anna, holding in her womb the book which the prophet foretold, which was sealed by the divine Spirit, cried out to all: “All the scriptures proclaim her! I am magnified, putting her forth this day!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The temple of the divine Savior is contained and formed in her mother's womb. The ladder is set up which leadeth all men on high, whose conception we celebrate with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}],katavasia:{text:`Christ is born ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 1 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},3:{irmos:{text:`To the Son who was begotten of the Father * without change before all ages, * and in the last times, without seed, was made flesh of the Virgin, * to Christ our God let us cry aloud: * Thou hast raised up our horn, holy art Thou, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Entreating the Lord, Joachim receiveth from on high the message he desired when an angel appeared before him and said: “Depart, O righteous man, for the God of all hath fulfilled thy petitions.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Calling upon the God of all, Anna once, standing in the garden, beheld an angel, who appeared before her, saying: “Be thou not downcast, for thou shalt become the mother of the Mother of God!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`When thou, O Anna, full of zeal, didst offer up supplications to God, thou didst conceive in thy womb the pure one who without seed hast received the infinite Word, and thou hast imparted grace to us all in thy fertility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Rod of the root of Jesse, * and flower that blossomed from his stem, * O Christ, Thou hast sprung from the Virgin. * From the Mountain overshadowed by the forest * Thou hast come, made flesh from her that knew not wedlock, * O God who art not formed from matter. * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy womb, which before bore no children, hath been opened, O Anna, and receiveth the heavenly cloud, from whence the radiant Sun, shining forth upon us, hath illumined all with the light of truth and driven away the profound darkness of ungodliness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The fiery throne of God hath been set up in thy womb, O blessed Anna, acceptable to God, and, seated thereon, He hath rested and taken away the labors of all the pious; and He hath planted the pure knowledge of God on earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Behold, thou hast received in thy womb the bower which Solomon described beforehand, most truly preserved for the true King, for the divine restoration and conversion of the human race. Wherefore, O Anna, we bless thee with joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`As Thou art the God of peace and Father of compassions, * Thou hast sent unto us Thine angel of great counsel, * granting us peace. * Wherefore guided towards the light of the knowledge of God, * and watching by night we glorify Thee, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Joachim descended from the mountain, not receiving tablets of the law, but her whom the law prefigured and whom all the sayings of the prophets revealed the Mother of God. And, dancing, he cried aloud: “My heart hath been magnified!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When Anna felt in her womb the divinely fruitful branch which had been planted there, from whom the ripe Cluster would blossom forth which abundantly poureth forth upon us the wine of immortality, she exclaimed: “What shall I render unto Thee, O compassionate Lord?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Joachim, unable to endure the sight of creation bereft of piety, prayed that the barrenness of Anna might pass, and that she would conceive that maiden to whom a Son would be given; the Most Exalted One Who bringeth about the adoption of all to His Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The sea monster spat forth Jonah as it had received him, * like a babe from the womb: * while the Word, having dwelt in the Virgin and taken flesh, * came forth from her yet kept her incorrupt. * For being Himself not subject to decay. * He preserved His Mother free from all harm.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“The shadows of the law are manifestly transcended; for, lo! the ray of divine grace is shown forth: the cloud who is the Virgin, from whence the radiant Sun of the Godhead shall truly shine forth!” Anna cried out, rejoicing and magnifying the God of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“A strange sight will it be if I, who before was barren and childless, conceive,” Anna said when she heard the angel announce that she would give birth to a child; and she cried aloud: “Better than any good report will be the fulfillment of thy words!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let the mountains and hills, the fields and the sea, the multitude of the angels and all human nature be glad; for Anna received the divine temple of the Master, the beginning of our reconciliation. And when she sensed that she had conceived, she cried aloud.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Scorning the impious decree of the godless one, * the children brought up together in godliness * feared not the threat of fire, * but standing in the midst of the flames, they sang: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The fire-bearing bush of old, which Moses beheld upon Sinai, hath Anna conceived in her childless womb, and it consumeth the fire as impiety, for those who chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`A drop, O Anna, hath now been most gloriously poured into thy womb, which hath contained all the Water of life within it, bedewing those who cry out with faith thereto: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou didst behold the bird's nest, thou wast furnished with wings by the Spirit and prayer; and thou didst receive the unblemished turtle-dove who beareth Christ, the olive branch Who freeth us from the noetic deluge, O Anna.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The furnace moist with dew showed forth an image * of a wonder past nature, * for it burned not the youths whom it had received; * neither did the fire of the Godhead consume the Virgin * when it descended into her womb. * Wherefore, chanting, we sing: * Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As Thou didst foretell through the prophets, O Master, Anna once cried out: “What hast Thou done for my childless womb and my withered breasts? Loose Thou the disgrace of my childlessness and grant me a fruit with whom I may cry aloud: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Anna, the lamp-stand hath entered thy womb, she who mystically contained the divine Lamp Who illumineth every creature with the effulgence of the knowledge of God. Wherefore, rejoicing, thou didst cry aloud: “Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Joachim and Anna, as a most comely husband and wife, bring forth the divine heifer, from whom the beautiful Bullock will shine forth, Who was slaughtered for all, and they chant: “Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`A strange and most wondrous mystery do I see: * the cave is heaven; * the Virgin the throne of the cherubim; * the manger a room, in which Christ God, * whom nothing can contain, is laid. * Whom we praise and magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Dance ye all and leap up! Now hath the earth been prepared which, without being ploughed, will produce the life-bearing Grain, eating of which those who magnify His goodness will hunger no more.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O David, take up thy psaltery and harp and chant! Behold, the ark of God hath appeared which thou didst foretell would be for our edification. Thereby have we arisen from our fall into sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like two magnificent stars ye bore forth the most radiant beam who shineth forth the great Sun upon the world. Wherefore, we praise and glorify you, O Joachim and Anna, as divinely wise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`The sacred Joachim and Anna offered a gift to the priests of old, but it was not accepted, for they were barren; but they made entreaty to the Giver of all things, and, hearkening to their prayer, He granteth them the Tree of Life, whose holy conception we honor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`O Thou Who wast lifted up upon the Cross ...`,tone:4},{text:`The divinely adorned Mary, the unblemished ewe-lamb and most pure bridal-chamber, now most gloriously beginneth to issue forth from the righteous ones, O ye faithful. Be glad henceforth, O heaven and earth; and all ye born on earth, exult! For this day hath God wrought most glorious things, showing forth in the womb the one Virgin, the fruit of a barren woman. Her do we hymn with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional, Glory/Both now`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ...,`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`}],exapostilarion:{text:`Her who gave birth unto the Light which illumineth all creation doth Anna begin to bring forth today from her barren womb. Wherefore, let us all make haste, for our redemption from the condemnation of Eve hath come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p10 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the conception`,spec_mel:`O Light immutable ...`},exapostilarion_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., The foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Glory, Both now: the foregoing is repeated`}},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Human nature, which before was sterile, * trusting in God, * putteth forth the Virgin, the first-fruits of piety, * in whom the fertility of the good is proclaimed * in her conception on earth, ** to serve for the advent of Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`The impassable gate of Christ the King, * by the counsel of God, * receiveth conception in a barren womb. * When she appeareth on earth, * the portals of heaven are opened ** and permit the entry of mortals.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`The conception of the pure and godly maiden, * the first-fruits of faith, hath ap-peared, * which before the ages * was ineffably proclaimed by God * in His divine and dread mysteries. ** Through her are the works of darkness and the passions brought to an end.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],praises_closer:{text:`Come, ye of every rank and age, and together with the choirs of angels let us joy-ously celebrate today with splendor, the most glorious conception of the Theotokos. Ye patriarchs, praise the Mother of the King of all! Ye prophets, praise her whom ye preached! Ye forefathers, honor the Mother of God who is descended from you! Ye elders, acclaim the forebears of God! Ye ancestors of God, bless the divine maiden! Ye virgins, honor the Ever virgin! Ye faithful, exalt the root of faith! Ye priests, magnify the most sacred temple of God! Ye choirs of all the saints, acknowledge the cause of your assembling! Ye armies of angels, pay homage to her who gave birth to the Master of all creation, the Savior of our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Praises Glory/Both now`},composer:`Malax`,type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the composition of Malax, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology. The Troparion, once. Litanies and dismissal.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p11 Great Doxology. The Troparion. Litanies and dismissal.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`liturgy_troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verses`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of the first canon, and 4 from ODE VI of the second canon of the righteous Anna.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Anna cried to the Lord: “If Thou wilt grant fruit to my womb, I shall be magnified, and will offer it to Thee.” Therefore, she conceived the pure Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Having observed the provisions of the law and served God blamelessly, O most honorable Anna, thou truly bearest in thy womb her who wilt give birth unto the Giver of the law. Wherefore, we, the faithful, call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`When thou didst pray in the garden, thou didst hear the voice of the Most High, O divinely wise Anna; and He gaveth fruit to thy womb: the portal which by grace shall open paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“The shadows of the law are manifestly transcended; for, lo! the ray of divine grace is shown forth: the cloud who is the Virgin, from whence the radiant Sun of the Godhead shall truly shine forth!” Anna cried out, rejoicing and magnifying the God of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`“A strange sight will it be if I, who before was barren and childless, conceive,” Anna said when she heard the angel announce that she would give birth to a child; and she cried aloud: “Better than any good report will be the fulfillment of thy words!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let the mountains and hills, the fields and the sea, the multitude of the angels and all human nature be glad; for Anna received the divine temple of the Master, the beginning of our reconciliation. And when she sensed that she had conceived, she cried aloud.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`}],liturgy_troparion:{text:`Today, the bonds of barrenness are loosed, * for God, hearkening unto Joachim and Anna, * doth manifestly promise unto them who, * beyond all expectation, will give birth to the divine maiden, * from whom the Infinite One Himself, becoming a man, shall be born. * And He commandeth the angels to cry unto her: ** Rejoice, thou who art full of grace, the Lord is with thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Troparion of the conception at Liturgy`},sourceLabel:`Troparion of the conception, in Tone IV`,tone:4},prokeimenon:{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`In congregations bless ye God, the Lord from the well-springs of Israel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p12 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE GALATIANS,`,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§ 210 (4: 22-31)`,citation:{book:`Galatians`,chapter:4,verses:`22-31`,pericope_number:210},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The salvation of the righteous is from the Lord, and He is their defender in a time of affliction.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone I`,label_inline:!0,tone:1},alleluia_verse:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE,`,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 36 (8: 16-21)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:8,verses:`16-21`,pericope_number:36},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verses:[{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Communion Verse`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`I will take the cup of salvation, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09.pdf`,locus:`p13 Another Communion Verse`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Another`,label_inline:!0}]}},{kind:`feast`,name:null,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE MIRACULOUS ICON OF THE MOTHER OF GOD KNOWN AS “UNEXPECTED JOY”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 9th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`vigil`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-09A.pdf`,note:`Second file of 9 December: a feast of an icon of the Theotokos ("Unexpected Joy"), beside the Conception of the Theotokos (12-09), which ODS vol. III and the OCA keep on this date. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 2: the file prints a LITTLE VESPERS, so Vigil, Fekula 2F, PROVISIONAL under Q-0002 (which service of the date a parish serves; ODS vol. III has no entry for this service). Great Vespers with "Blessed is the man", 6 stichera (three printed, each Twice), three lessons whose headings name the book and print no reference (citations identified), a Litiya with one sticheron, the blessing of the Loaves. Matins: troparion Thrice; every sessional hymn is followed by "the foregoing is repeated"; a Magnification; a Gospel; two canons of the Theotokos with no title line, no tone and no acrostic printed ("Canon I", "Canon II"), "Katavasia: Christ is born" after Ode I only; Great Doxology, after which the troparion is printed again. One hymn, "All the noetic ranks", is the Glory at Lord I have cried, the sticheron after Psalm 50 and the Glory at the Praises; the Vespers printing differs from the other two in two places. The label of the Polyeleos sessional hymn is printed "in Tone Il-", a misprint for Tone II (Bill, 16 Nov 2026).`,troparion:{text:`O ye faithful people, let us celebrate in spirit today, * glorifying the fervent helper of the Christian race; * and, hastening to her most pure image, let us cry aloud: * O most merciful Lady Theotokos, * grant unexpected joy * unto us who are weighed down by sins and many sorrows, * and deliver us from all evil, * entreating thy Son, Christ our God, ** that He save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy icon`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Little Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p5 blessing of the Loaves`,tone:4,repeat:2},{locus:`p6 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:3},{locus:`p15 after the Great Doxology`,tone:4},{locus:`p16 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy icon, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`We have none other help, we have none other hope but thee, O Lady. * Do thou help us! * In thee do we trust, and in thee do we boast; ** for we are thy servants. Let us not be put to shame.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Kontakion of the holy icon`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p11 after Ode VI`,tone:6},{locus:`p16 AT LITURGY`,tone:6}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy icon, in Tone VI`,tone:6},ikos:{text:`Entrust me not to the intercession of men, O most holy Lady, but accept the prayer of thy servant; for I am held fast by sorrow and cannot endure the arrows of the demons. I have no protection, neither have I any place to flee, wretched as I am. Ever vanquished, I have no consolation save thee, O Lady of the world. O hope and intercession of the faithful, disdain not mine entreaty, but render it profitable.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera of the Theotokos, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O Lady, thou dost intercede for all who with faith flee to thy mighty protection; for, weighed down by many sins we sinners have no other sure deliverance amid misfortunes mid tribulations. O most pure one, Mother of God Most High, hasten thou to help thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,repeat:2},{text:`When a certain iniquitous man fell down before thy most wondrous image, offering the angelic salutation unto thee, who alone art most pure and most blessed, thou didst turn him away from the path of destruction and gave him the unexpected joy of salvation, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring to pour forth the abundant riches of grace upon His faithful, the Savior scattered the icons of His Mother like stars shining among the Orthodox lands, pouring forth the grace of miracles and bestowing healings, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`The most glorious and most pure Theotokos, * the true Mother of God, * Let us piously venerate with praises rejoicing, * greeting her as did the angel: * Rejoice! holy Mother of the incarnate Son of God; * Rejoice! habitation of the Holy Spirit, ** ever interceding on our behalf that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Let heaven and earth join chorus; for, lo! the Mother standeth before her Son, earnestly entreating forgiveness of sins for a great sinner. The angels rejoice over this; and with them let us also join chorus, magnifying the Theotokos with hymns.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5},{text:`I shall commemorate thy name * in every generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`With the priestly ranks let all of us, the generations of the faithful, rejoice, celebrating the festival of the Mother of God, who in her wonder-working image hath been revealed to us as an ever-flowing well-:spring, granting unto all the abundant gifts of goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The angels of heaven and men on earth bless thee as the one who gave birth to the God of all, for thou prayest for the faithful people, protecting by thy mercy those who celebrate thy festival.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`O Sovereign lady, * accept the supplications of thy servants, ** and deliver us from all want and grief.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`,`virgin_theotokos_rubric`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Come, let us sing unto the Lord Who hath given us great joy in the miraculous icon of His Mother; and, gazing thereat, let us all sing: O all-wondrous Lady and Theotokos, save this city and thy people, who with faith and love bow down before thy most precious icon!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,repeat:2},{text:`He who speaketh of Thy power, O Lord, maketh all Thy praises heard; for Thou hast given Thy most pure Mother to the Christian race as a bold mediatress who leadeth sinners to Thee, who granteth unexpected joy to them, and asketh peace and great mercy for us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O most pure Mother of God Most High, thou art the helper of all the sorrowful and oppressed, the feeder of the starving, the comfort of travelers, the haven of the tempest-tossed, the visitation of the sick, the protection of the weak, the support of the elderly: hasten thou to help thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,repeat:2}],lic_closer:{text:`All the noetic ranks rejoice with us beholding the Queen and Lady of all glorified with many names by the faithful; and the souls of the righteous rejoice also, seeing the Mother of God extending her most honored hands toward her Son on behalf of the sinful people, and asking for them remission of sins, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM GENESIS`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Genesis`,chapter:28,verses:`10-17`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`The heading names the book and prints no reference. The body opens "Jacob went forth from the well of the oath" and closes "this is the gate of heaven": Genesis 28:10-17, Jacob's ladder, as 11-27A Lesson 1. Identified by first and last words; confirm.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE PROPHECY OF EZEKIEL`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Ezekiel`,chapter:43,verses:`43:27-44:4`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`The heading names the book and prints no reference. Opens "Thus saith the Lord: It shall come to pass from the eighth day and onward", closes "I fell upon my face": Ezekiel 43:27-44:4, the shut gate, as 11-27A Lesson 2. Identified by first and last words; confirm.`},{heading:`A READING FROM PROVERBS`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:9,verses:`1-11`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`The heading names the book and prints no reference. Opens "Wisdom hath built a house for herself", closes "years of life shall be added to thee": Proverbs 9:1-11, which 11-27A prints with its reference. Identified by first and last words; confirm.`}],litiya:[{text:`Having cleansed our mind and understanding, we hold festival with the angels, chanting with splendor the hymn of David to the Bride and maiden, the Mother of Christ our God the King of all, saying: Arise, O Lord, into Thy rest, Thou and the ark of Thy holiness! For Thou hast adorned her like a beautiful palace, O Master, to protect and save the faithful by Thy mighty power.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`At Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple, and this Sticheron, in Tone II`,tone:2}],litiya_closer:{text:`Come, ye faithful, let us hymn the helper of the Christian race, who brought herself to make supplication unto her Son and God on behalf of an iniquitous man who had angered the Son of God by his sinful life, and thereby crucified Him anew; and let us cry out to her from the depths of our souls: O most merciful mediatress, forsake us not, making right acceptable supplications to thy Son on our behalf!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Litiya Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Thy miraculous icon hath shone forth upon us like the most radiant sun, O Lady, pouring forth the rays of thy goodness in abundance: health for the sick, consolation for the sorrowful, and for our souls deliverance from misfortunes, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4},{text:`I shall commemorate thy name * in every generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O ye people, let us chant the hymn of David to the maiden Bride of God, the Mother of Christ, the King of all: The Queen stood at Thy right hand, O Master, arrayed in a vesture of gold and adorned with divine majesty; for, having adorned her, as chosen from all women, and above all the earth, He was well-pleased to be born of her in His great mercy, and hath given her, who alone is blessed, as a helper for His people, and a protector of His servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, * and incline thine ear.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Inclining thine ear to the glad tidings of the archangel, O pure one, thou didst take into thy womb Him Who bowed down the heavens and descended to earth for our salvation, Who now inclineth His ear to thy right acceptable supplications on behalf of all who honor thee with faith and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Having recourse unto thy protection, O Lady, * all we born of earth cry aloud to thee: * O Theotokos, our hope, deliver us * from our countless transgressions, ** and save thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Aposticha Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VII`,tone:7},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the Loaves, the Troparion of the holy icon, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Blessing of the Loaves rubric`}},virgin_theotokos_rubric:{text:`And “Virgin Theotokos, rejoice! ...,” (Once)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Virgin Theotokos rejoice rubric`}}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer_rubric.praises_rubric.praises.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric.closing_rubric`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the holy icon, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 God is the Lord rubric`}},sessional_1:[{text:`Surrounded by the divine effulgence of the angelic armies, and graciously receiving, as the Mother of God, the ministry of the ranks of the prophets and apostles, visit us, thy servants, entreating Christ our God to grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone III`,tone:3},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 1 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],sessional_2:[{text:`O Mother of God, thou art truly the strength of the helpless, the protection of all, and our mediatress before God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone VI`,tone:6},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Sessional 2 repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify thee, O most holy Virgin, divinely elect maiden, and we honor thy holy image, whereby thou pourest forth healings upon all who have recourse to it.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm Verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Remember, O Lord, David and all his meekness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God. (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`A great and most glorious mountain art thou, greater than Mount Sinai; for then, unable to bear the descent of the glory of God in images and shadows, it burned with fire, and thunder and lightning smote it; but, having received within thee the divine Fire, the Word of God, without being consumed thou didst bear Him Who beareth all things in His hand. As thou hast maternal boldness before Him, O Lady, help those who honor thee with faith, for thou hast received from God the gift of ordering and protecting the Christian flock, thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone Il-`,provenance_note:`The label is printed "in Tone Il-" (p6; both extractions and the page image): a misprint for "in Tone II:" (Bill, 16 Nov 2026). Tone II is set by hand.`},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Polyeleos sessional repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`I shall commemorate thy name * in every generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hearken, O daughter, and see, and incline thine ear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE,`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 4 (LK. 1: 39-49, 56)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:1,verses:`39-49, 56`,pericope_number:4},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`All the noetic ranks rejoice with us, beholding the Queen and Lady of all glorified with many names by the faithful; and the souls of the righteous rejoice also, seeing the Mother of God extending her all-honored hands toward her Son on behalf of the sinful people, and asking for them remission of sins, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone VI`,tone:6},canon_rubric:{text:`Two canons of the Theotokos: Canon I, with 6 Troparia, including its Irmos, and Canon II, with 8 Troparia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon I`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`I shall open my mouth, * and be filled with the Spirit, * and utter discourse to the Queen and Mother; * and be seen radiantly keeping festival, * joyfully praising her wonders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O thou who opened the portals of God's tender compassion when the archangel offered thee his salutation, close not off His love for mankind from us who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Wondrous was thy life on earth, O most glorious Virgin Mother, yet even more wondrous is thy dwelling in heaven; for thou dost unceasingly reveal the wonders of thy maternal loving-kindness toward those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Son, Who was timelessly begotten of the Father before all ages, didst thou in latter times conceive through the overshadowing of the Holy Spirit, giving birth to eternal joy for the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O sea which drowned the devil, the noetic pharaoh! Rejoice, O stone which gave drink to those thirsting for the life of the Spirit! For thou hast given to the human race the Redeemer of those held captive and the Guide of those who are lost.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Theotokos, thou living and plentiful fount, * establish in spiritual fellowship those who sing hymns to thee, * and in thy divine glory * grant them crowns of glory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Confirm in the virtuous life those who fervently hymn thee, and earnestly entreat Him Who was born from thee, that we not be deprived of crowns of glory due to our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In our life we have angered thy Son by our sins more than any of the iniquitous; yet be thou our mediatress, O loving Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`May Jesus Who is the Lover of mankind, Who was born of thee and hast the authority to forgive men their sins, grant unto us crowns of glory in His divine glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O virgin who contained the infinite God within thy womb, who carried Him as a babe and fed Him at thy breast!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`He who sitteth in glory upon the throne of the Godhead, * Jesus the true God, * is come in a swift cloud * and with His sinless hands he hath saved those who cry: * Glory to Thy power, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Mother who hast given birth to the Savior, do thou thyself save from the misfortunes and the grief of life those who confess thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Mother of the Son and Redeemer Who lifted up our sins upon the Cross, heal all our grievous and incurable sicknesses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`God the Word, the hypostatic Wisdom, chose thee to be His dwelling-place. Him do thou earnestly entreat, that He save us by the judgments which He knoweth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O all-comely, beauteous Bride! Rejoice, O pure turtledove! Rejoice, O Mother of Emmanuel, ever-virgin Theotokos!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`All creation stands in awe of thy divine glory; * for thou, O Virgin who hast not known wedlock, * didst contain within thy womb the God of all, * and gave birth to the timeless Son, * bestowing peace, upon all who hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Heaven and earth are amazed, beholding thy tender compassion toward the Christian race, O most glorious Virgin Mother, for thou dost condescend even to those sinners who have fallen the most, O most good one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Save thy servants from evils and tribulations, O Theotokos, and grant unto those who hymn thee the peace of God which transcendeth any earthly peace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast given birth unto Him Who hath reconciled those above with those below, Who descended to earth for this purpose, yet hath not separated Himself from the Father and the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O Queen of heaven and earth! Rejoice, thou who dost surpass the angels and archangels! Rejoice, for through thee the Reconciler foretold to us by Jacob hath come down!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Celebrating the divine and solemn feast * of the Mother of God * O ye divinely wise, * let us come, clapping our hands, * and glorify God who was born of her.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Spiritually celebrating a sacred festival now, O ye who love the feasts of the Church, come, let us hymn the Mother of God with songs, glorifying her Son, Who hath bestowed such grace upon His Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Look upon the hymnody of thy servants, O Birthgiver of God, casting down the conceited pride of our enemies, visible and invisible, and pouring forth thine exalted mercies upon the humble.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art the root from whence Christ, the Rod of Jesse, sprang forth: a Man from the house of David, and God Who is co-eternal with the Father and the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O joyous Mother! Rejoice, O thou who dost surpass all the daughters of mankind in beauty! Rejoice, O noble scion of the divinely chosen race of David!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Refusing to worship created things * in place of the Creator, * the divinely wise youths bravely trampled down the threatening fire * and rejoicing they sang aloud: * O supremely hymned Lord and God of our Fathers, Blessed art Thou.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst spurn all the beautiful things of this world, O pure one, desiring to serve God alone; and to Him thou didst chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lady, to the one God do thou guide us who have failed utterly to follow the pious children, but have instead cleaved unto creation instead of the Creator; and teach us to chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With noetic eyes, O Christ, Daniel foresaw Thee as the Stone uncut by human hands, destroying the vain kingdoms of mankind, for the salvation of those who hymn Thee, and the Father and the Spirit: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O mountain overshadowed by the grace of God, from whence Christ was quarried, the Stone set by God the Father as the Cornerstone of His Church, to Whom we chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Offspring of the Theotokos * saved the holy children in the furnace. * He who was then prefigured hath now been born on earth, * and He gathereth all creation to hymn thee: * all ye works praise ye the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Hearken, O pure Virgin maiden, unto the words announced to thee by Gabriel: Thou shalt bear a Son Who doth save those who chant: Hymn the Lord, O ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`He Who issued forth from thee in the flesh saved from fire the children who gazed upon Him with faith. Him do thou beg, that He save us also who burn with the flame of the passions and sing to Him, thy Son: Hymn the Lord, O ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ, Thou wast seen in the Babylonian furnace as a radiant angel like in appearance unto the Son of God. Unto Thee, with the Father and the Spirit, do we chant: Hymn the Lord, O ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O bush seen by Moses, who in latter times sprang forth from the root of David and hast given birth ineffably to the Savior of all, to Whom we chant: Hymn the Lord, O ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Let every mortal born on earth, * radiant with light, in spirit leap for joy; * and let the host of the angelic powers * celebrate and honor the holy feast of the Mother of God, * and let them cry aloud: * Rejoice! O all-blessed Theotokos, * thou pure Ever-virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`God, Who became incarnate from thee and hath come unto us, rendered thy womb more spacious than the heavens. O wondrous marvel! The Infinite is contained in the Virgin's womb, that we may hymn her throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Entreat Him Who was ineffably conceived by thee in latter times, O Virgin Theotokos, that He transform all our grief into joy and grant us His never-waning light, that we may hymn thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art the throne of the glory of God which Ezekiel mystically beheld, for thou didst receive into thy most pure womb the Son of God Who is co-enthroned with the Father and the Spirit, and didst hold Him in thy maternal arms.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O animate temple wherein God dwelt in the flesh! Rejoice, O ark overshadowed by the glory of the Son of God! Rejoice, O all-blessed and pure Ever-virgin Theotokos!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]}}},{title:`Canon II`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Taking up the Song of Moses, O my soul, * cry aloud: * 'A helper and a protector hath become unto me salvation. * My God, * whom I will glorify'.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast delivered the whole human race from slavery to the enemy, having given birth to the Savior of all the world. Him do thou beseech, that He save us from the assaults of the evil one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most holy Virgin, in the midst of our perils be thou a mediatress and intercessor for us before thy Son, that, delivered from them, we may glorify Him with the Father and the Holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who art more exalted than the angels and archangels, and higher in honor than all creation, thou art the great intercessor of the Christian race.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`}],katavasia:{text:`Christ is born ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 1 katavasia`},sourceLabel:`Katavasia`,label_inline:!0}},3:{irmos:{text:`Establish me, O Lord my God, * that mine enemy may not boast concerning me; * for Thou, O Lord, art my confirmation, * my refuge and my power.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Hearken unto our prayers, O Virgin Mother, and give ear unto our sighs; and make supplication to thy Son on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In that thou art full of tender compassion, give ear to our supplications, and grant us deliverance from grievous and evil circumstances and sorrows.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Still thou the tempest of the threefold waves of life, and drive away our evil passions, O most pure one, that we may glorify thee in peace and dispassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, ye people of God, let us now praise the Queen of heaven, who gazeth down upon us from her holy heaven and leadeth us up to the heavens.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I hymn Thee, O Lord, for I have heard report of Thee, * and I was afraid; * for Thou comest to me, seeking me who am lost. * Wherefore, I glorify Thy great condescension towards me, * O greatly merciful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Even though our tongue is at a loss how to praise thee worthily, yet, moved by love for thee, with all our heart and all our mind we glorify and praise thee, the mediatress of all good things.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Who can plumb the depths of the sea? And who is “able to number the great mercies and compassions which thou hast for us?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Father and Lord of heaven and earth, what thanks shall we offer Thee? For thou hast given to the Christian race a good and powerful mediatress.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Stretching forth thy hands toward Him Who was born of thee, O all-loving Mother, cease not to make supplication for us, that by thine entreaties we may be counted worthy of earthly and heavenly gifts.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ my Savior, the enlightenment of those lying in the darkness of sin. * I rise early to hymn Thee O King of Peace, * enlighten me with Thy radiance, * for I know no other God than Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`From the spheres of the celestial lights the Archangel Gabriel brought to thee the joy of the annunciation; and obeying that ineffable counsel of God, O thou who art wondrous among women, thou thyself dost bring joy unto all who hymn thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast truly given unexpected joy to the whole universe - the world below and the world above, for He Who issued forth from thee hath brought peace and united those above with those below. Him do thou now beseech, that we be delivered from malice and misfortunes.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The poison of sin hath penetrated the whole human race through our ancient forefather, but He Who was born of thee hath cleansed, hallowed and saved all. Him do thou now beseech, that we be delivered from sinful and unseemly passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy compassions are beyond number and are like unto the goodness of the Word thy Son. This we know, and know well. Yet what shall we render unto thee for them, O supremely compassionate Virgin Mother?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`I am held fast in the depths of sin O Savior, * and am overwhelmed by the sea of life, * but as Jonah was delivered from the sea-monster, * so also deliver me from the passions, * and save me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`By thy birthgiving thou hast saved the human race from Hades, death and corruption; wherefore, as is meet, all the ranks of heaven and earth bless thee as the Mother of the Destroyer of Hades, and our Liberator from death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Turn not away from us because of our sins, O most holy Virgin, but by thy supplications mediate for us liberation from Hades and everlasting death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O the slothfulness, O the indifference toward our salvation, wherein we have wasted our whole life! What torment, what flames lie before us! Yet by the grace given thee, O Mother, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst bear Christ, the divine Fire, in thine arms without being consumed; wherefore, standing now before the fiery throne of His glory, pray thou, that He enflame us with the desire to do good.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The bush which burned with fire on the mountain * and the dew-bearing furnace of the Chaldeans * clearly prefigured thee, O Bride of God; * for, without being consumed, * thou didst receive the divine and immaterial Fire * within thy material womb. * Wherefore, we chant unto Him Who was born of thee: * O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`God the Word, the Creator and Fashioner of all, in latter times made His abode within thy womb, O most glorious divine maiden, and hath taught all to chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sorrows, tribulations, and sicknesses have, because of the great multitude of our sins, brought our souls down in the abyss like the waves of the sea; yet setting our hope on thine aid, O Mother of God, we do not despair, but cry aloud to thy Son: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Who in heaven can describe thy power, which He Who issued forth from thee hath given thee? And who on earth can render audible all the praises made to thy great protection and thine assistance to mortals, who chant: “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!”?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure maiden who knewest not wedlock, cleanse our minds of vain thoughts and our hearts of wicked lusts, that with pure souls and undefiled lips we may chant unto thy Son: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The three holy children were not obedient * to the decree of the tyrant; * and cast into the furnace they confessed God, singing: * O all ye Works of the Lord, bless ye the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The fleece wet with dew, which Gideon beheld, mystically prefigured thee, the Virgin Mother, who without knowing a man hast given birth to God the Word by the overshadowing of the Holy Spirit. To Him do we chant: Bless the Lord, O ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The mindless rage of the tyrant cast the pious children into the furnace kindled with fire, but thy Son quenched the power of the flame with mystic dew. Him do thou entreat, O most holy one, that He deliver us from everlasting fire and deprive us not of the dew-bearing kingdom, that we may chant there: Bless the Lord, O ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst serve the ineffable mystery of the incarnation of Christ, loving Him with all a mother's love, and didst maternally lament Him as He hung upon the Cross. Him do thou entreat, that He not reject even the most hardened of sinners, that they may chant: Bless the Lord, O ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We glorify and hymn thee as is meet, O most compassionately merciful Mother; for thou art the great helper of the Christian race, our supremely good and speedy aid.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst contain within thy Womb * the God whom nothing can contain, * and hast brought forth joy to the world, * wherefore we sing thy praises, * O Virgin Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast given to the world the good Shepherd Who sought the lost sheep, and with Him thou dost now reign. Lead unto Him all the sheep that have gone astray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Father, Who passeth all understanding in His love for those who have fallen in Adam, hath through thee revealed the Lamb Who taketh away the sins of the whole world. Cease thou never to make supplication before Him, that by the Blood of His Son we may be sanctified and cleansed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Son of God Who art equally glorified with the Father and the Spirit, by the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee forsake us not who are perishing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`He Who was incarnate and became a man through thee hath set thee higher than all the angelic ranks. Standing there, lead us also up to the heights of heaven, taking away our every sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`O fervent and invincible intercessor, * diligent and unashamed hope, * rampart, protection and haven * of those who have recourse to thee, * O pure Ever-virgin do thou, together with the angels, * entreat thy Son and God, ** that He grant peace, salvation and great mercy to the world.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone V`,tone:5},{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode III sessional repeat device`},label:[`glory`,`both_now`]}],exapostilarion:{text:`The Dayspring from on high hath visited us, O Theotokos, and amid sorrowful circumstances hath given thee to us as a beam of surpassing radiance, a Mediatress for sinners, imparting unexpected joy unto us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy icon`,spec_mel:`Having fallen asleep in the flesh ...`},exapostilarion_closer_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., the foregoing is repeated.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Glory, Both now: the foregoing is repeated`}},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Let heaven and earth join chorus; for, lo! the Mother standeth before her Son, earnestly entreating forgiveness of sins for a certain sinful man. At this the angels rejoice. With them let us also spiritually rejoice, magnifying the Theotokos with hymns.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,repeat:2},{text:`O ye people, let us chant the hymn of David to the maiden Bride of God, the Mother of Christ, the King of all: The Queen stood at Thy right hand, O Master, arrayed in vesture of gold and adorned with divine majesty; for, having adorned her, chosen from all women, above all the earth, He was well-pleased to be born of her in His great mercy, and hath given her, who alone is blessed, as a helper to His people, and a protector of His servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2}],praises_closer:{text:`All the noetic ranks rejoice with us, beholding the Queen and Lady of all glorified with many names by the faithful; and the souls of the righteous rejoice also, seeing the Mother of God extending her all-honored hands toward her Son on behalf of the sinful people, and asking for them remission of sins, peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises Glory/Both now`},type:`of_the_feast`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology and the Troparion, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Great Doxology and the Troparion`}},closing_rubric:{text:`Litanies and dismissal. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Litanies and dismissal. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of Canon I, and 4 from ODE VI of Canon II.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Confirm in the virtuous life those who fervently hymn thee, and earnestly entreat Him Who was born from thee, that we not be deprived of crowns of glory on account of our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`In our life we have angered thy Son by our sins more than any of the iniquitous; yet be thou our mediatress, O loving Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`May Jesus Who is the Lover of mankind, Who was born of thee and hast the authority to forgive men their sins, grant unto us crowns of glory in His divine glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O virgin who contained the infinite God within thy womb, who carried Him as a babe and fed Him at thy breast!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy birthgiving thou hast saved the human race from Hades, death and corruption; wherefore, as is meet, all the ranks of heaven and earth bless thee as the Mother of the Destroyer of Hades, and our Liberator from death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Turn not away from us because of our sins, O most holy Virgin, but by thy supplications mediate for us liberation from Hades and everlasting death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`O the slothfulness, O the indifference toward our salvation, wherein we have wasted our whole life! What torment, what flames lie before us! Yet by the grace given thee, O Mother, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 7`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst bear Christ, the divine Fire, in thine arms without being consumed; wherefore, standing now before the fiery throne of His glory, pray thou, that He enflame us with the desire to do good.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 8`},label:`plain`}],prokeimenon:{text:`the Song of the Theotokos: My soul doth magnify the Lord, * and my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Savior.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone III`,label_inline:!0,tone:3},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`For He hath looked upon the lowliness of His handmaiden; for behold, from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE HEBREWS,`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§ 320 (HEB. 9: 1-7)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:9,verses:`1-7`,pericope_number:320},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Arise, O Lord, into Thy rest, Thou and the ark of thy holiness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone II`,label_inline:!0,tone:2},alleluia_verse:{text:`The Lord hath sworn in truth unto David, and He will not annul it.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE,`,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 54 (LK. 10: 38-42,11: 27-28)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:10,verses:`10:38-42, 11:27-28`,pericope_number:54},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`I will take the cup of salvation, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-09A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-10":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.little_vespers`,`c1.great_vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Martyrs Menas, Hermogenes and Eugraphus of Alexandria`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYRS MENAS, HERMOGENES AND EUGRAPHUS OF ALEXANDRIA`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 10th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-10.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the martyrs at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-10 entry. NO stichera of the Theotokos for Alleluia days are printed here (unlike 1, 2, 3, 7, 8 and 11 December). "Aposticha Stichera from the Octoechos" with no Glory. One canon by Joseph. TWO kontakia: one in Tone I after Ode III, before the sessional hymn, and the kontakion with its ikos in Tone IV after Ode VI, which is the one printed at Liturgy. An exapostilarion with its Theotokion. At Liturgy a prokeimenon, Epistle, Alleluia, Gospel and communion verse are printed, and no Beatitudes rubric. The melody lines are printed "Spec. Mel:" throughout this file.`,troparion:{text:`Having mortified the fiery movements of the passions by abstinence, O martyrs of Christ, * ye received the grace to dispel the ailments of the infirm, * and living even after your death, ye work miracles. * O truly most glorious wonder! Bare bones pour forth healing! ** Glory be to Thee the only God and Creator!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 Troparion of the holy martyrs`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p1 end of Vespers`,tone:8},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyrs, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},kontakion:{text:`The right harmonious sound of thy words, * leading Hermogenes up from the abyss of perdition, * set him on the rock of life; * and Eugraphus, having denounced the emperor, * hath his glorious head severed, rejoicing. * And do thou earnestly pray, O Menas, ** that all who honor thee with love be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy martyrs`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:4},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Having been lifted up ...`,tone:4},ikos:{text:`Thy life was godly, thy discourse sweet, thy boldness and teaching great, thy courage wondrous in the face of the iniquitous, O Menas, who showed thyself forth with steadfastness of mind to be in no wise afraid. And with instruction thou didst teach all to worship the one God in three Hypostases and to serve Him with unwavering intent. And confessing the Son of God Who for our sake assumed flesh in these latter days, thou didst pursue Hermogenes. Wherefore, with him do thou pray, that all who honor you with love be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_rubric`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy martyrs, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O most glorious martyr Menas, * when thou wast smitten on thy heels, * thine eyes putout, * and thy divinely eloquent tongue cut off; * thou didst endure steadfastly, * looking for divine rewards. * Wherefore, pray thou, * that God grant to our souls ** peace and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`The glorious Hermogenes * loved the severing of his hands * and the removal of his feet; * and, gazing at the fire * he showed forth a mightier ardor of heart, * cleaving unto God. * To Him doth he now pray, * that He grant our souls ** peace and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`},{text:`Your members broken, O wise saints, * ye were cast into the depths of the sea; * and by the hand of the Most High * ye were guided * to the calm haven of sweetness, * having drowned the malice of the serpent. * Wherefore, pray ye, * that God grant our souls ** peace and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`}],lic_closer:{text:`Without corruption didst thou give birth unto God * Who hath destroyed corruption and poured forth incorruption, * O incorrupt and blameless one. * Wherefore, I pray thee: * By thy supplications renew me * who am become corrupt through evil, O pure one, * that I may glorify thee * and magnify thee with love ** who hast magnified our race.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Once, when the unblemished Virgin * beheld on the Tree * Him to Whom she had given birth from her seedless womb, * unable to endure the wounding of her womb, * she said, rending her hair: * “O Thou Who sustainest all creation, * how hast Thou been uplifted upon the Cross * as one condemned, ** desiring to save mankind in every way?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},aposticha_rubric:{text:`Aposticha Stichera from the Octoechos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`kontakia_ode3`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Octoechos; and this canon for the holy martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn the steadfast crown-bearing martyrs,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Octoechos; and this canon for the holy martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “I hymn the steadfast crown-bearing martyrs,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone I:`,composer:`Joseph`,acrostic:`I hymn the steadfast crown-bearing martyrs`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Having been delivered from bitter slavery, * Israel traversed the impassable as though dry land; * and beholding the enemy drowned, * they chanted unto God as to their Redeemer, * Who worketh wonders with His upraised arm, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ye martyrs adorned with crowns of glory, who stand before the throne of God, filled with divine light: From the darkness of the passions deliver those who with love keep your splendid memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Loving divine glory and desiring the beauty of God, ye most manifestly spurned the beautiful things of life and all power, O martyrs, and by your death obtained never-ending life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Burning with divine zeal, the exceeding wise Hermogenes and Menas quenched the fire of ungodliness; and shining the light of piety upon all, by faith they were all radiantly shown forth as beacons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`That thy servants may be delivered from possession by the passions, O all-immaculate maiden, do thou earnestly entreat thy Lord and Master, to Whom thou gavest flesh from thy most pure blood, and Who hath entered into fellowship with us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`To the Son who was begotten of the Father * without change before all ages, * and in the last times, without seed, was made flesh of the Virgin, * to Christ our God let us cry aloud: * Thou hast raised up our horn, holy art Thou, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Clearly illumined with heavenly light, the martyrs dispersed the darkness of the delusion of idolatry, and have emitted the radiance of healings for us who chant unto the God of all: Holy art Thou, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Following the living Master of mortality, O wondrous Menas, thou wast broken underfoot and thus broke the head of the tyrannical enemy, setting thy feet firmly upon the hard path of torment, O most manly martyr.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`His hands cut off, Hermogenes hymneth the Savior, having manifestly made the vesture of the priesthood most bright with the moistening of his blood, being revealed through grace as an emulator of Him Who suffered in the flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ the comely, finding thee alone to be comely among women, issued forth incarnate from thy womb, O maiden, enlightening our race with divine beauty. Wherefore, we honor thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p2 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Rod of the root of Jesse, * and flower that blossomed from his stem, * O Christ, Thou hast sprung from the Virgin. * From the Mountain overshadowed by the forest * Thou hast come, made flesh from her that knew not wedlock, * O God who art not formed from matter. * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Proclaiming the brilliant laws of God, O Menas, thou didst endure the putting out of thine eyes by the iniquitous, lifting up the eyes of thy heart unto the never-waning Light, and chanting with joy: Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When it was cut out, thy tongue was found to be honed by the fire of the Spirit, O most wise one; for it spake, hymning the wonders of God and manifestly brought to the glory of piety the tyrant who had caused thy muteness, O Menas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Enduring great suffering, Hermogenes was deprived of his feet, yet he trampled upon the head of the serpent, preparing with unwavering demeanor the path of witness which leadeth to the life of heavenly splendor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`When thou wast preserving thy soul unwounded, O Menas, Christ appeared to thee, healing thy wounds and commanding thee to endure manfully, that for thy sake He Who desireth mercy might work salvation for all who beheld thy torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst put forth the Rod from the root of Jesse, O pure and all-hymned Virgin who budded forth the Husbandman of all creation, Who hath caused the gardens of fruitless knowledge to wither and hath piously rooted the most true Faith within us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`As Thou art the God of peace and Father of compassions, * Thou hast sent unto us Thine angel of great counsel, * granting us peace. * Wherefore guided towards the light of the knowledge of God, * and watching by night we glorify Thee, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Wherefore trouble ye yourselves in vain? The martyrs cried out together to the most iniquitous judge. He Who giveth power standeth before us, He Who alone is invincible in might, for Whose sake we most mightily endure wounds!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sudden was the conversion of the wondrous Hermogenes to the Lord; for he was cleansed in the laver of baptism, and received the light of the hierarchal office by the judgment of God, illumining with his teachings those who were in the night of evil.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Abandoning the worthless mentality of the rhetors, ye were caught in the snares of the unlettered apostles when the Spirit rendered you truly wise as martyrs and through faith rendered you mighty in strength against every storm of torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast shown to surpass the holy angels, O pure Virgin who hast given birth unto the angel of Great Counsel, Emmanuel, Who by His condescension united mankind to the heavenly, in His unutterable compassion, O maiden.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The sea monster spat forth Jonah as it had received him, * like a babe from the womb: * while the Word, having dwelt in the Virgin and taken flesh, * came forth from her yet kept her incorrupt. * For being Himself not subject to decay. * He preserved His Mother free from all harm.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O Almighty God, after three days Thou didst save from the monster Jonah, who foreshadowed Thy burial; and the bodies of the martyrs which were cast into the deep Thou didst guide to the most tranquil haven of burial, where Thy divine will is the safekeeping of us, the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O invincible martyrs, upon dry land and unharmed did the deep give up your bodies, which were guided by the angels of heaven who proclaimed to all your spiritual state, which poureth forth healings and delivereth all from the passions of the soul, O blessed ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The ranks of the angels marveled at your endurance, and how in the body ye vanquished the incorporeal serpent, and were crowned with wreaths of victory, O martyrs, who stand before the throne of God, illumined with the effulgence of divine light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through thee, O Virgin, hath death ceased to be, for thou hast given birth unto those who believe in Him with pure faith. To Him do thou pray, O all-holy one, that He deliver thy servants from misfortune.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Scorning the impious decree of the godless one, * the children brought up together in godliness * feared not the threat of fire, * but standing in the midst of the flames, they sang: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O spiritual athletes, ye have made your abode with the souls of the joyous, where the sound of the voices of those who keep festival in a pure manner is heard, full of gladness, and chanting: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sweet to me is the death whereby I die, cried Hermogenes, for me to live is Christ, and to die is immeasurable gain. Let my members be cut off as I chant with love: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With steadfast wisdom thou didst inscribe thyself in the Book of Life, O wise Eugraphus; for when thy head was severed, thou wast transported to the never-waning Light on thy blood, as upon a chariot.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The incarnate Word issued forth from thee, O maiden, without burning thy womb or disturbing the seal of thy virginity, granting incorruption and life to us who chant: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The furnace moist with dew * was an image and prefiguring of a wonder past nature, * burning not the children whom it had received, * so the fire of the Godhead consumed not the Virgin's womb * into which it had descended. * Therefore in song let us sing: * Let the whole creation bless the Lord * and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`He whose wisdom was vain fell at thy feet, beaten, O divinely wise Menas; for, having deprived thee of eyes and tongue, he was yet unable to shake thy thought of the dwelling-place on high. Wherefore, thou didst cry out with joy: Let all creation bless the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`When the most irrational tyrant deprived thee of both thy hands and feet by his most savage will, then, O wise Hermogenes, desiring the prize, and rejoicing, thou didst chant unto Christ: Let all creation bless the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I hymn thy divine suffering, O Menas; I honor the struggles of Hermogenes; I venerate your relics, sing of the wounds, bonds, persecutions and death whereby ye were taken up into life, crying: Let all creation bless the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We have known thee to be the jar which contained the Manna of the Godhead, O maiden, the ark, the table, the candlestick, the throne of God, the palace, and the bridge which doth lead to divine life those who chant: Let all creation bless the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Bush, which burnt without being consumed, * prefigured thy pure birthgiving, O Theotokos. * Wherefore we now entreat Thee: * quench the raging furnace of temptations that beset us, * that we may unceasingly magnify Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Lo! the brilliant celebration of the radiant martyrs hath shone forth upon all, illumining the ends of the world and removing the blindness of men's souls. Let us make haste with all diligence, and draw forth sanctity there-from.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As ye ever stand before God, O great martyrs, we entreat you: Pray ye that those who honor your radiant memory with faith, may receive the blessings of heavenly glory whereof ye have been deemed worthy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Immolated in the fire of torment, and illumined with the most pure light, O all-praised ones, ye brought body and soul to the Creator of all as an unblemished sacrifice, and have been numbered among the choirs of the martyrs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The splendid and divine choir of the martyrs, the divinely wise Menas, Hermogenes and Eugraphus, were taken up to the mansions of heaven and stand before the Father, the Son and the Holy Ghost, manifestly delighting in deification.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`The effulgence of the splendor of thy birthgiving hath our rejected nature seen, O all-immaculate one, and it hath been delivered from the night of unbelief and the dark tumult of the passions. Wherefore, we honor thee as the cause of our salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`Together let us all honor with sacred and sweet hymnody * the wondrous Menas, the godly Hermogenes and Eugraphus, * as ones who rendered honor unto the Lord, * and who suffered for Him, * and attained unto the choirs of the incorporeal in the heavens, ** and pour forth miracles.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Kontakion of the holy martyrs (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`The choir of the angels ...`,tone:1}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Disdaining the glory of the world and furnishing themselves with wings through divine glory, Menas, Hermogenes and the glorious Eugraphus endured the weight of cruel tortures with zealous purpose, sparing not their flesh. Wherefore, cast into the depths of the sea after their end, they were guided to the will of God. To them let us cry aloud with faith: Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love honor your holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`From the snares of enemies visible and invisible, * we have been overcome by the storms of our uncountable sins, * and fleeing unto the safe harbor of thy goodness O pure one, * we have thee as our rampart and sure protection. * Wherefore we thy servants beseech thee * to ceaselessly make fervent supplication, O most pure one, * unto Him who seedlessly became incarnate from thee, * that those who worthily hymn thee ** may be granted the remission of their sins.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`Upon beholding the Lamb, Shepherd and Redeemer * upon the Cross, * the ewe-lamb exclaimed weeping, bitterly lamenting, and crying aloud: * “The world rejoiceth, having received deliverance through Thee, * but my womb doth burn, beholding Thy crucifixion, * which Thou hast endured in Thy merciful loving-kindness. * O long-suffering Lord, * Thou abyss and inexhaustible well-spring of mercy, * take pity, and grant forgiveness of sins ** unto those who hymn Thy divine sufferings with faith!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`By thy rhetoric and divine miracles, O Menas, thou didst draw the sacred Hermo-genes to suffer with thee; and together with him and the holy Eugraphus, we now most joyfully praise you.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy martyrs,`,spec_mel:`The heavens with stars ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`The mountain overshadowed and densely wooded which the divine Habbakuk foresaw of old hast thou been shown to be, O Virgin; and thee doth David call God's hill, even an high hill, as the hill of Bashan.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],prokeimenon:{text:`In the saints that are in His earth hath the Lord been wondrous; * He hath wrought all His desires in them.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`I beheld the Lord ever before me, for He is at my right hand, that I might not be shaken.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`THE EPISTLE TO THE EPHESIANS`,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(6:10-17).`,citation:{book:`Ephesians`,chapter:6,verses:`10-17`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The righteous cried, and the Lord heard them, and He delivered them out of all their tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},alleluia_verse:{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, and the Lord shall deliver them out of them all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`READING FROM THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p8 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(21 :12-19).`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:21,verses:`12-19`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10.pdf`,locus:`p9 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}},{kind:`saint`,name:`our father among the saints Joasaph, Bishop of Belgorod`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY HIERARCH JOASAPH`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 10th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`vigil`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-10A.pdf`,note:`Second file of 10 December, a separate service (Bill, 15 Nov 2026, on the lettered files). Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 2: the Menaion prints a LITTLE VESPERS for the saint, so Vigil, Fekula 2F. ODS vol. III has no 12-10 entry. Which of the two services of the day a parish keeps is Q-0002. Great Vespers with "Blessed is the man", 8 stichera in two sets of four (three printed in each, the first marked Twice), three lessons with NO reference printed (citations are identifications), a Litiya ("the Sticheron of the temple, and this Sticheron"), the blessing of the Loaves. The Both now at Lord I have cried is labelled "of the forefeast" (10 December, as at 6 December), and the katavasia "Christ is born" is named after Ode I and not printed. TWO troparia: Tone III and "Or this Troparion, in Tone II", the second printed at Little Vespers (with its own Theotokion), at the blessing of the Loaves and at Liturgy. Matins: a sessional hymn and Theotokion at each kathisma and after the Polyeleos; a Magnification and Selected Psalm verse; a Gospel; "Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia" is appointed and NOT printed; the canon of the hierarch, with 8, is printed, its acrostic naming "the Tsar and the people"; Great Doxology. The label of the sticheron after the Gospel is printed "in Tone VI-". At Liturgy the rubric appoints 8 Beatitude troparia, 4 from Ode III and 4 from Ode VI; four, three and the Theotokion of Ode VI are printed.`,troparion:{text:`O holy hierarch, beloved of Christ God, * thou wast a rule of faith and model of tender compassion for all; * thou didst shine forth like a beacon in vigil, fasting and prayer, * and hast been revealed to be glorified by God. * Wherefore, abiding in, incorruption in thy body, * whilst standing in spirit before the throne of God, * thou pourest forth most glorious wonders. * Entreat Christ God, * that He establish our homeland in Orthodoxy and piety, ** and save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Little Vespers`,tone:3},{locus:`p7 blessing of the Loaves`,tone:3,repeat:2},{locus:`p8 God is the Lord`,tone:3,repeat:2},{locus:`p17 AT LITURGY`,tone:3}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone III`,tone:3},kontakion:{text:`Who can describe the divers struggles of thy life? * Who can reckon the many and varied mercies of God made manifest through thee? * Knowing well thy boldness before the most pure Theotokos and our most compassionate God, * in compunc-tion of heart we cry out to thee: * Deprive us not of thy help and assistance, O Joasaph, ** holy hierarch of Christ and wonderworker.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Kontakion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p13 after Ode VI`,tone:8},{locus:`p18 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hierarch, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},ikos:{text:`O holy hierarch, who from thy youth wast chosen by the most pure Mother of God as a vessel of grace, by the piety of thy life thou wast revealed to be a truly good shepherd of the reason-endowed sheep; wherefore, thou hast received the gift of healing from Christ our God Who loved thee. For this cause we cry out to thee: Deprive us not of thy help and assistance, O Joasaph, holy hierarch of Christ and wonderworker.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`,`troparion_alternate_rubric`,`troparion_alternate`,`troparion_alternate_closer`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera of the holy hierarch, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Let us chant a hymn of radiant festivity, O brethren, blessing the newly manifest favorite of God and offering supplication to him, that he cleanse the eyes of our hearts and enlighten our souls with the memory of his wonders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1},{text:`O Joasaph, thou favorite of Christ, thou wast a struggler for all the virtues; therefore, having endured tribulations on earth and received everlasting joy from God in heaven, hearken to the entreaty of thy children, and beseech Him to save and enlighten our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O holy hierarch Joasaph, who didst love the poor and sorrowful and ever offered up prayer for sinful people, thou thyself wast beloved of Christ. Be thou mindful of us who honor thy struggles, and make supplication to the Lord, that He save and enlighten our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Who can count the multitude of healings which flow forth from thy wonderworking relics, O favored one of Christ? Who will not marvel at thy great assistance? What human heart is not moved to compunction by thy love? Wondrously hath the word, Who enlighteneth and saveth our souls, been glorified in thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 4`},label:`plain`}],lic_glory:{text:`When thou didst study as a child, O venerable one, thou wast taken under the protection of the Lady Theotokos, as thy father was assured in a vision; and when thou didst finish thine earthly life, another vision assured the people that thy spirit is glorified by God. Pray thou on our behalf, O holy hierarch of Christ, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer:{text:`O Theotokos, thou art the true vine * that hast budded forth for us the Fruit of life. * Thee do we entreat: ** Pray thou, O Lady, with the holy apostles, that He have mercy upon our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`O holy hierarch Joasaph, * censer of unceasing prayer * and most fervent intercessor for the people: * Reject us not who hymn thee, ** but be thou our faithful helper.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord; * in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Let us hymn Joasaph, * the favorite of Christ, O brethren, * moving him to pray for us, * that we be delivered from misfortunes ** and given repentance before the end.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Thy priests shall be clothed with righteousness, * and Thy righteous shall rejoice.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The praise of mankind was not sufficient for thee, * O holy hierarch of Christ; * for at an early age * thou wast borne witness to by the most pure Theotokos ** as one chosen of God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`O venerable father, report of thy corrections hath gone forth into all the earth. Wherefore, thou hast found the reward of thy labors in the heavens, having routed legions of demons and attained unto the ranks of the angels whose life thou didst blamelessly emulate. As thou dost possess boldness before Christ God, ask thou peace for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_closer:{text:`Great gifts hast thou been deemed worthy of, O pure Virgin Mother of God; for thou hast given birth in the flesh unto One of the Trinity, Christ the Bestower of life, unto the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Now and ever ..., Theotokion`},troparion_closer:{text:`We hymn thee who hast mediated the salvation of our race, * O Virgin Theotokos; * for thy Son and our God, * accepting suffering on the Cross in the flesh * He had received of thee, * hath delivered us from corruption, ** in that He is the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers dismissal Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3},troparion_alternate_rubric:{text:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Or this Troparion rubric`}},troparion_alternate:{text:`O Joasaph, most excellent man of prayer from thy childhood, divinely elect and holy hierarch of Christ, by thy pious life thou providest all with a rule of faith and model of tender compassion, and abundantly pourest forth healings upon those who have recourse to thee with faith. Entreat Christ God, that He establish the right Faith, peace and piety in our homeland, and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Or this Troparion`},sourceLabel:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II`,tone:2},troparion_alternate_closer:{text:`All of thy most glorious mysteries are beyond comprehension, * O Theotokos; * for, thy purity sealed and thy virginity intact, * thou art known to be a true Mother, having given birth unto God. ** Him do thou entreat, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Theotokion after the alternate troparion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya_rubric`,`litiya`,`litiya_glory`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`,`virgin_theotokos_rubric`,`troparion_alternate_rubric`,`troparion_alternate`],rubric:{text:`After the introductory psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,”:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera of the holy hierarch; 4 in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, Who worketh miracles among the generations of Christians and revealeth His new chosen ones; for we now see the favored one Joasaph glorified by Christ, illumining the Russian land with the beauty of his virtues, and possessing great boldness, to grant peace to the whole world and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,repeat:2},{text:`The choir of Thy saints, O Lord, hath been augmented by the repose of Thy holy hierarch Joasaph, whom the Church hymneth on earth; accept Thou his prayers on our behalf, O Lover of mankind, as Thou hast great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As the darkness of the night doth thicken, the radiance of the stars increaseth, and the eyes of those who are astray are lifted thereto; thus also as the darkness of sin increaseth on earth, let us lift up our eyes, O brethren, and, catching sight of the splendor of the virtues of the holy hierarch, let us make haste to the heavenly homeland, whereof may the Lord, Who hath great mercy, not deprive us sinners.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O sacred one, Joasaph, holy hierarch of God, divinely wise standard of pastors and supremely good instructor of monks! Rejoice, most glorious healer of the sick and merciful consoler of the sorrowful. Pray thou ever to the Lord, that we may be emulators of thee and, having disdained all things sinful, may labor for God alone.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`And 4 Stichera, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`Rejoice, thou who didst oppose the passions and laborer of spiritual activity! Rejoice, O righteous one, full of humbleness of mind, reprover of the prideful of this world, and terrible punisher of the slothful! Cease thou never to pray to the Lord for us, that we may be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, dweller in heaven, who regardest the earth with a merciful eye and acceptest the supplications of those who hymn thee! Rejoice, thou who didst ever lift thine eyes unto heaven and spurned earthly possessions! Teach us, therefore, O holy hierarch of Christ, to acquire treasure in heaven and to behold thy glory clearly there.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 6`},label:`plain`}],lic_glory:{text:`With what hymns of praise shall we crown the holy hierarch of Christ, who unceasingly declared the glory of the Lord and everywhere planted true piety, the living tablet of the commandments of Christ, who gazed not upon the faces of men, but led the souls of all to salvation? For with imperishable crowns doth Christ our God, Who hath great mercy, crown him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer:{text:`Adorn thyself well, O cave, for the ewe-lamb cometh, bearing Christ in her womb! O manger, receive Him Who by His word hath loosed us mortals from irrational activity! Ye shepherds, piping, bear witness to the awesome wonder! O magi from Persia, bring ye gold, frankincense and myrrh to the King, for the Lord hath revealed Himself through the Virgin Mother! And, gazing down upon Him, His Mother made obeisance to Him as though she were His handmaid, and greeted Him as she held Him in her embrace, saying: “How wast Thou sown within me, and how didst Thou spring forth within me, O my Redeemer and God?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Both now, of the forefeast`},type:`of_the_feast`,saint:`forefeast`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., of the forefeast, in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`READING FROM THE PROVERBS.`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:10,verses:`10:7, 3:13-16, 8:6`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. The body opens "The memory of the righteous man calleth forth praises" (Proverbs 10:7) and moves to "Happy is the man that findeth wisdom" (3:13-16), then the Wisdom-speech of chapter 8: the composite hierarch lesson, as 11-14A and 12-06 Lesson 1, in another translation. The body runs on past 8:6. Identified by correspondence; confirm the span against the page.`},{heading:`READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON.`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Proverbs`,chapter:10,verses:`10:31-32`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Headed "READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON." No reference printed. Opens "The mouth of the righteous droppeth wisdom" (Proverbs 10:31) and, unlike the 11-14A and 12-06 printing, runs on into the Wisdom of Solomon ("O God of my fathers ... Give me wisdom"), closing "their devices are but uncertain" (Wisdom 9:14): the long composite form of the hierarch lesson. The citation names its opening verses only; the span is NOT settled. Confirm against the page.`},{heading:`READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON.`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:4,verses:`4:1, 6:11-12, 17-21`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`Headed "READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON." No reference printed. Opens "When the righteous is praised, the people will rejoice", as 11-14A Lesson 3; composite, running through the "let us condemn him" material of Wisdom 2 to "opposest the prideful with thine own arm". Identified by correspondence only; the span is NOT settled. Confirm against the page.`}],litiya_rubric:{text:`At the Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple, and this Sticheron, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya rubric`}},litiya:[{text:`It is fitting that He Who kept the virginal body of the holy hierarch intact through everlasting incorruption be glorified; for, purified by the virtues of the venerable one while he was yet alive, his body became a temple of the Holy Spirit, and after his repose it hath been revealed to be a wellspring of miraculous gifts, marveling at which, let us send up compunctionate supplication to the favorite of God for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1}],litiya_glory:{text:`The Lord, Who is wondrous in His saints, was glorified in the life of the holy hierarch Joasaph, and after his repose He worketh wonders through his incorrupt relics, teaching countless people to believe and trust in the help of heaven. Let us therefore make haste, O brethren, to seek the one thing needful, and to cleanse our souls with repentance, invoking the aid of the holy hierarch, and to glorify God Who is hymned in Trinity, throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},litiya_closer:{text:`Christ the Lord, my Creator and Redeemer, * Who came forth from thy womb, O most pure one, * and clothed Himself in my nature, * hath freed Adam from the primal curse. * Wherefore, like the angel * we unceasingly cry out to thee, * O most pure one, * who art truly the Mother of God and Virgin: * Rejoice!, O Sovereign Lady, ** the intercession, protection and salvation of our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone VII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Be ye adorned, O mansions of heaven! Throw yourselves wide, O portals of the house of God. For, lo! the righteous soul of the holy hierarch is borne up from the earth and given a dwelling place with the angels whom he had emulated in his life. By his prayers, O Christ God, spare and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:7},{text:`My mouth shall speak wisdom, * and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The souls of the righteous are in the hands of God, and no torment shall touch them; thus the dead body of the righteous Joasaph remained untouched by corruption and hath been shown to be a wellspring of grace for souls corrupted by sins, granting health to the sick when they ask the prayers of the favorite of God and have recourse with faith to his relics.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The mouth of the righteous shall meditate wisdom, * and his tongue shall speak of judgment.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Let us excel in piety, a brethren, for we see it crowned with everlasting glory; let us despise pride and avarice, for the holy hierarch of Christ, spurning them, hath received everlasting glory in heaven and on earth, and obtained a treasure which cannot be taken away; wherefore, having acquired from God the boldness to pray for sinful people and the grace of healings, he teacheth the iniquitous the ways of God thereby turning the impious to the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`}],aposticha_closer:{text:`Hold festival, O Sion! Be glad, O Jerusalem, thou city of Christ! Receive the Creator Who is contained in the cave and the manger! Open unto me thy gates, and, entering therein, I shall behold Him Who holdeth all creation in His hand, wrapped as a babe in swaddling-clothes: the Lord and Bestower of life, Whom the angels hymn with unceasing voices, and Who saveth our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Glory/Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VII`,tone:7},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the Loaves, the Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Blessing of the Loaves rubric`}},virgin_theotokos_rubric:{text:`Rejoice O Virgin Theotokos (Once).`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Virgin Theotokos rejoice rubric`}},troparion_alternate_rubric:{text:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Or this Troparion rubric`}},troparion_alternate:{text:`O Joasaph, most excellent man of prayer from thy childhood, divinely elect and holy hierarch of Christ, by thy pious life thou providest all with a rule of faith and model of tender compassion, and abundantly pourest forth healings upon those who have recourse to thee with faith. Entreat Christ God, that He establish the right Faith, peace and piety in our homeland, and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Or this Troparion`},sourceLabel:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II`,tone:2}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.troparion_closer.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord rubric`}},troparion_closer:{text:`We hymn thee who hast mediated the salvation of our race, * O Virgin Theotokos; * for thy Son and our God, * accepting suffering on the Cross in the flesh * He had received of thee, * hath delivered us from corruption, * in that He is the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3},sessional_1:[{text:`Let Joasaph, the holy hierarch of Christ, be magnified, and let him inherit the everlasting kingdom prepared for him; for he served Christ faithfully, taking care for the least of his brethren, and took the repentant into his love; and now he prayeth for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`O ye faithful, let us bless the Theotokos, * our helper, the fervent aid of those amid misfortune, ** by whom we have been delivered from foreign bondage.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],sessional_2:[{text:`During thy life, O favored one of Christ, thou didst lay waste to thy body with fasting and labors; wherefore, after thy death it blossomed with incorruption and is become a wellspring of healings for the faithful. Earnestly entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`As the all-immaculate Bride of the Creator, * Mother of the Redeemer, who knewest not a man, * and as the receptacle of the Comforter O all-hymned one, * hasten thou to deliver me, * the vile abode of iniquity and noetic plaything of the demons, * from their evil machinations; * and make me the bright dwelling-place of the virtues, * O thou incorrupt light-bearing one. * Drive away the clouds of the pas-sions and grant that, * by thy supplications, * I may receive a portion on high ** and share in the never-waning light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`At the Polyeleos, this Magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify thee, O holy hierarch father Joasaph, and we honor thy holy memory; for thou dost entreat Christ our God on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p8 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Hear this, all ye nations; give ear, all ye that inhabit the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God. (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`Come all ye faithful, and standing round the much-healing relics of the holy hierarch, let us pour out our hearts in prayer, that he may remain with us in spirit, may instruct us in good works, and teach us to vanquish the temptations of the flesh and please God alone.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`Without separating Himself from the divine Essence, * when taking flesh in thy womb, * He remained God though He had became a man; * and even after thy birthgiving, preserved thee, His Virgin Mother, * as immaculate as thou wast before giving birth. * Him do thou earnestly beseech, ** that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone II`,tone:2}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`My mouth shall speak wisdom, * and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hear this, all ye nations; give ear, all ye that inhabit the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. JOHN`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(10:9-16).`,citation:{book:`John`,chapter:10,verses:`9-16`},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`By unceasing prayer, instructive discourse, great loving-kindness and a virtuous life thou wast a model for the faithful, O divinely wise Joasaph, leading all to Christ and guiding them to the path of salvation. Deprive not of thy chief shepherd-ship, us who with faith honor thy memory, O great and holy hierarch of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 After the Gospel sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After the Gospel, this Sticheron, in Tone VI-`,tone:6,provenance_note:`The label is printed "in Tone VI-", a hyphen for the colon (p9).`},canon_rubric:{text:`Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia; and that of the holy hierarch, with 8 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “O holy hierarch Joasaph, pray thou for the Tsar and the people.” in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p9 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia; and that of the holy hierarch, with 8 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “O holy hierarch Joasaph, pray thou for the Tsar and the people.” in Tone IV:`,acrostic:`O holy hierarch Joasaph, pray thou for the Tsar and the people.`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`O Thou who wast born of the Virgin, * drown I implore Thee, in the depth of dispassion * the triune nature of my soul, * as Thou didst the mighty strongholds of the warriors, * that in the mortality of my flesh * as on a timbrel * I may chant a hymn of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Hymning the struggles of the holy hierarch Joasaph, let us cleanse the thoughts of our mind, O brethren, moving him to prayer for the forgiveness of our sins and the gift of grace-filled compunction.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy parents, having diligently striven to instill in thee piety from thine infancy, O favored one of Christ, acquired the worthy reward of their labors in thee; for from thy childhood thou wast a joy to them in thy pious behavior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy father emulated the righteous Anna, O holy hierarch; for she saw her daughter led into the Holy of Holies, and he was deemed worthy of beholding in a vision, the most holy Theotokos crowning thee with hierarchical glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`I weep for myself, wretch that I am, having enslaved myself to the passions from my youth. Have mercy on me in thine intercession, O holy hierarch, who enslaved the passions to thy soul from thy youth and served God alone until thy death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us hymn the holy mountain, the transcendent chariot, the Mother of God who remained a true virgin after giving birth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia_rubric:{text:`Katavasia: Christ is born ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Katavasia: Christ is born`}}},3:{irmos:{text:`From on high didst Thou willingly descend to earth, * O Thou Who art more exalted than every noetic principality, * and from the uttermost depths of Hades * thou didst raise up lowly human nature; * for there is none more holy than Thee, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast a child obedient to thy parents, O Joasaph, yet, loving God more than them, thou didst depart from thy father's home for the sake of thy salvation; and having received an education, didst confine thyself to a monastic community.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst show thyself to be a stranger to pharisaical pride, O venerable father; and loving monastic humility from thy youth, thou didst humble thy flesh with secret struggles, illumining thy soul by prayer before the heavenly Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`For me to live is Christ, and to die is gain, thou didst say to thyself, O favorite of Christ; and when pangs wracked thy flesh thou didst add labors upon labors for the sake of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having received holy obedience and been arrayed in priestly vesture, Joasaph the favorite of Christ became a good instructor of children, teaching them piety by word and life, manifesting a mature mind in his early years.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who knewest not wedlock, who hast given birth unto God in the flesh, make me steadfast who am bowed down under the assaults of the passions; for I have no helper save thee, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`He who sitteth in glory upon the throne of the Godhead, * Jesus the true God, * is come in a swift cloud * and with His sinless hands he hath saved those who cry: * Glory to Thy power, O Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`I know the path which leadeth to salvation, but, woe is me, I do not overcome my slothfulness! Wherefore, O holy hierarch, I invoke thee in prayer, that thou mayest establish in me the desire for salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Trusting in the Lord, the Anchor of salvation, thou didst accept the Abbotship; and was thereby compelled to deal with the cares of domestic order, at the same time thou didst not cease to order the affairs of thy soul to be conducive to salvation. O venerable father, teach this also to me who am exceedingly vainglorious.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adding labors upon labors, raising the Monastery of Lubensk up from lack of use, and traveling about the land of Russia for alms, the holy hierarch Joasaph established the Empress in piety and taught all the people of the salvation of souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Possessing genuine love for the poor in his heart, Joasaph, the favorite of Christ, exhibited paternal care for the monastery's laborers and showed his compassion to his neighbors from the sufficiency thereof.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-praised Sovereign Lady Theotokos, thou who hast cleansed my thought by thy supplications, show me forth as right fruitful, O Mother of the God of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Now I shall arise said God prophetically, * now I shall be glorified, now I shall be exalted, * elevating fallen human nature, * which I received from the Virgin, * to the noetic light of My divinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thee do I entreat in contrition of heart, O holy hierarch of Christ; for as during thy lifetime thou didst forgive the penitent, so also, beholding the contrition of my heart, entreat Christ to grant me forgiveness of my sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The hart maketh haste unto springs of water; and thou, O favored one, didst ever direct all thy deeds and thoughts to the glory of the Church of Christ, and thus adorned the monasteries of the holy hierarch Athanasius and the venerable Sergius as much with the piety of the brethren as with the erection of churches.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hearken, ye people, and marvel at the humility of mind of the favorite of God; for he beheld the holy Athanasius in a vision and when asked, answered him, saying: I wish thee to punish me as a sinner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Most High praised the young Solomon who asked not for riches, but for wisdom from the Lord Who appeared to him, and the whole world glorified him; but more wise even than him did Joasaph show himself to be, asking punishment for his sins from the holy hierarch who appeared to him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`God became hypostatically incarnate, O pure one, united to the flesh He received from thee; yet He remained immutable, being incorporeal in His divine essence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Prefiguring Thy three-day burial * prophet Jonah praying in the belly of the sea-monster cried aloud: * Deliver me from corruption * O Jesus Thou King of hosts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Through the prayers of the venerable Sergius, and by thy labors for the glory of the saints of God, and more through the purity of thy heart, thou wast magnified by the Lord while yet on earth, O favorite of God, and invested with the hierarchical rank unto the salvation of thy flock.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst show fiery zeal in the ordering of the Church in the region of Belgorod, O holy hierarch Joasaph; wherefore, grant thou confirmation to the Church and victory to our hierarchs over heresies and schisms.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst not shirk filial love whilst thou wast in the heights of the hierarchy, and didst make a prostration to the ground to thy father, as if Christ was in thy midst; therefore, humble thou my most prideful heart, and by thy supplications admonish me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst remain an un-acquisitive monk on thy hierarchical throne, O holy hierarch, increasing thy struggles of fasting and prayer, sending up good entreaty for thyself and the people, and teaching the priests and all mankind the commandments of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`The incarnate Word of God, Who transcendeth all nature, didst thou bear for us; wherefore, with lips and soul we proclaim thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The three youths in Babylon, * regarded the tyrant's command as foolishness, * and cried aloud in the midst of the flame: * Blessed art Thou, O Lord God of our fathers!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Let us marvel at the holy hierarch Joasaph , O ye people, knowing him to be like the wonderworker Nicholas, visiting the hovels of the poor in secret, or preparing firewood for them with his own hands, and even receiving beatings from the gatekeeper.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst perceive the wounds of sin upon the souls of all, O holy hierarch, and didst reprove their secret transgressions with love and longsuffering; wherefore, by thy supplication lead us also to repentance and correction of life, and have mercy on our souls through thine intercession.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Wretch that I am, I have likened myself to the governor who, being himself iniquitous, showed himself to be exceedingly cruel to prisoners; but as thou didst set him aright by thine instruction, O father Joasaph, holy hierarch of Christ, so also teach me to be merciful to my neighbor and to be severe with myself.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O good warrior of the heavenly King and faithful shepherd of the flock of Christ, make supplication for the Orthodox hierarchs and people, that, having lived a peaceful life on earth, we may be deemed worthy of everlasting life in heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`We all bless thee as the Mother who in thy womb conceived in the flesh the God of all: God the Word, Who hath shone forth pre-eternally from the Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O almighty Redeemer of all, * having descended and bedewed the children * in the midst of the flame, * Thou didst teach them to sing: * All ye works bless and hymn the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As thou wast an emulator of that Athanasius who was beloved of thee, O holy hierarch, thou didst strive to finish thine earthly life in the struggle of wandering; and, foreseeing thine end, thou didst fearlessly undertake a lengthy journey.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Taking leave of thy flock, thou didst say to the people: Ye shall not see me alive again. Wherefore, thou didst command that a coffin be fashioned for thee there as a token of fellowship. Teach us also to be mindful of the hour of death and to unceasingly take care for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As great as was thy zeal for the monastic life, so was thy love for thy household; for thine own were not only thine according to the flesh, but in spirit they were shown to be with thee in God. Wherefore, thou didst desire to visit thy parents before thine end and to impart to them the blessing of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The abbot who struggled in asceticism near the place of thy righteous end was informed in a vision of the hour of thy repose, and straightway became a faithful witness to thy glorification by God. Show forth, then, the power of thy prayer upon me, O favorite of Christ, and free me thereby from the tyranny of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most holy virgin, who hast given birth to God the Word in the flesh, driving away the darkness of my soul by thy prayers, enlighten me who cry out: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thy birthgiving was revealed to be incorrupt, * God came forth from thy womb, * and He appeared upon earth in mortal flesh * and dwelt among mankind; * Wherefore we all magnify thee, O Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Love never faileth, saith the divine Spirit, and this truth was proclaimed in the wonders of thy love, O holy hierarch of Christ, for from thine incorrupt relics thou pourest forth healing upon the sick and consolation upon the sorrowful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`From of old the southern borderland of Russia hath been filled with thanksgiving for thy miracles; and in our times we have seen people hastening thither from the remote lands of the north, and the suffering being healed, rejoice in thine aid.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Suffering children didst thou love more than others, O holy hierarch of Christ, increasing healing and gracious help for them and changing the sorrow of their parents into joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The dead man arose on touching the bones of Elisha; and countless people have been cured upon venerating thy relics. Heal me also, who fall down before thee, of sinful passions, and strengthen the faith of my greatly sinful soul, O venerable father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ God, through the prayers of Joasaph thy favorite, grant peace to the Church and prosperity to Orthodox Christians, deliverance from famine and plague, and the forgiveness of our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 9 troparion 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who hast given birth unto joy, the Fruit of thy womb hath made him who sang aloud the hymn to thee: Rejoice! a member of the heavenly choir.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`What virtue did not find a dwelling place in thy soul? In what struggle wast thou not a champion? For poverty of spirit, weeping for the kingdom of heaven, meekness of demeanor, the pursuit of righteousness, tender compassion toward thy neighbor, and purity of heart shone forth in thy blameless life. Ever interceding for our souls O Joasaph, grant that we who pray to thee may also have a share in these gifts, O thou chosen one of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy hierarch, in Tone VI`,tone:6},{text:`O Thou Who didst call Thy Mother blessed, of Thine own will Thou didst go to voluntary suffering, shining forth on the Cross, desiring to rescue Adam, saying to the angels: Rejoice with Me, for I have found the lost coin! a our God Who hast ordered all things with wisdom, glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6}],exapostilarion:{text:`Let the radiant luminary Joasaph be hymned in the midst of the Church, as a venerable monk and an honorable hierarch, a reprover of the foolish and a teacher of the Faith, a physician of the ailing who workest wonders, an expeller of demons and a most fervent intercessor for the whole world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy hierarch`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`The great and most glorious mystery of thy birthgiving, O divinely joyous maiden, Mother of God and Virgin, have the prophets proclaimed, the apostles taught, the martyrs confessed, and the angels and mankind hymn and worship.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Venerating the relics of the holy hierarch of the Lord, O ye faithful, let us cleanse ourselves of defilement of flesh and spirit, and let us move our hearts to compunction with the memory of his wonders, crying out fervently to Christ in repentance: By the prayers of Thy favorite, O Lord, set within us the desire to emulate him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,repeat:2,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`No one departeth from thee empty-handed, O Joasaph, holy hierarch of God; for everyone receiveth healing of body and sanctification of souls if he invoke thine aid with faith, and offering up repentance for his sins doth strive to correct his life. This do thou teach us also, O holy one, and make supplication for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Bedewing our faces with tears of compunction, O ye faithful let us venerate the incorrupt relics of the favored one as a river of miracles and an inexhaustible wellspring of healings; for this most clear sign of divine power increaseth faith in the hearts of all, in our age of little faith, bringing the unbelieving to the Faith and teaching all to honor the holy hierarch of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`O most glorious wonder! O, the longsuffering of God for us sinners! For when temptations have multiplied on earth and faith hath decreased exceedingly, wondrous healings have increased through the relics of the hierarch. Behold, therefore, ye people of Russia and all ye faithful children of the Church of Christ, how much the prayer of a righteous man can accomplish, and how the likeness of the wonders of old hath been made manifest to us today. Glory to Thee, O Christ God, for Thou art He Who worketh wonders through the saints! Make worthy of such grace us who have heard of and witnessed the miracles of the holy Joasaph, deliver us from countless sins, and grant us the joy of Thy salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p15-p16 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},praises_closer:{text:`Let us sound the trumpet of hymns; for, bowing down from on high, the Virgin Mother, the Queen of all, crowneth with blessings those who hymn her. Let kings and princes come together, and let them clap their hands in hymns before the Queen who gave birth to the King Who, in His love for mankind, hath been well-pleased to loose those held fast by death from of old. Ye pastors and teachers, assembling, let us praise the most pure Mother of the good Shepherd. And with divinely voiced hymns praising the golden lampstand, the Light-bearing cloud, the animate ark more spa-cious than the heavens, the fiery throne of the Master, the golden jar which held the Manna, the portal of the Word which is shut, the refuge of all Christians, let us say thus: O palace of the Word, grant the kingdom of heaven unto us, the lowly; for naught is impossible to thy mediation!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Praises Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology and Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p16 Great Doxology and Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`troparion_alternate_rubric`,`troparion_alternate`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III and 4 from ODE VI of the canon of the holy hierarch.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Thou wast a child obedient to thy parents, O Joasaph, yet, loving God more than them, thou didst depart from thy father's home for the sake of thy salvation; and having received an education, didst confine thyself to a monastic community.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst show thyself to be a stranger to pharisaical pride, O venerable father; and loving monastic humility from thy youth, thou didst humble thy flesh with secret struggles, illumining thy soul by prayer before the heavenly Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`For me to live is Christ, and to die is gain, thou didst say to thyself, O favorite of Christ; and when pangs wracked thy flesh thou didst add labors upon labors for the sake of the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having received holy obedience and been arrayed in priestly vesture, Joasaph the favorite of Christ became a good instructor of children, teaching them piety by word and life, manifesting a mature mind in his early years.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through the prayers of the venerable Sergius, and by thy labors for the glory of the saints of God, and more through the purity of thy heart, thou wast magnified by the Lord while yet on earth, O favorite of God, and invested with the hierarchical rank unto the salvation of thy flock.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst show fiery zeal in the ordering of the Church in the region of Belgorod, O holy hierarch Joasaph; wherefore, grant thou confirmation to the Church and victory to our hierarchs over heresies and schisms.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst not shirk filial love whilst thou wast in the heights of the hierarchy, and didst make a prostration to the ground to thy father, as if Christ was in thy midst; therefore, humble thou my most prideful heart, and by thy supplications admonish me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude 7`},label:`plain`},{text:`The incarnate Word of God, Who transcendeth all nature, didst thou bear for us; wherefore, with lips and soul we proclaim thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p17 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],troparion_alternate_rubric:{text:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Or this Troparion rubric (Liturgy)`}},troparion_alternate:{text:`O Joasaph, most excellent man of prayer from thy childhood, divinely elect and holy hierarch of Christ, by thy pious life thou providest all with a rule of faith and model of tender compassion, and abundantly pourest forth healings upon those who have recourse to thee with faith. Entreat Christ God, that He establish the right Faith, peace and piety in our homeland, and save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Or this Troparion (Liturgy)`},sourceLabel:`Or this Troparion, in Tone II`,tone:2},prokeimenon:{text:`My mouth shall speak wisdom, * and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone I`,label_inline:!0,tone:1},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hear this, all ye nations; give ear, all ye that inhabit the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`THE EPISTLE OF ST. PAUL TO THE HEBREWS`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(7:26-8:2)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:7,verses:`7:26-8:2`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The mouth of the righteous shall meditate wisdom and his tongue shall speak judgment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone II`,label_inline:!0,tone:2},alleluia_verse:{text:`The law of God is in his heart, and his steps shall not be tripped.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. JOHN`,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p18 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(10:9-16)`,citation:{book:`John`,chapter:10,verses:`9-16`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-10A.pdf`,locus:`p19 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-11":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our venerable father Daniel the Stylite`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR VENERABLE FATHER DANIEL THE STYLITE OF CONSTANTINOPLE`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 11th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},preface_rubric:{text:`Alleluia, or “God is the Lord ...,”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 Alleluia, or God is the Lord`}},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-11.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the venerable one at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-11 entry (its Sunday of the Forefathers entries are for the movable Sunday, 12-11B). Under the title the page prints "Alleluia, or God is the Lord" and then gives BOTH forms at Lord I have cried: three stichera of the Theotokos, a Theotokion and a Stavrotheotokion "if Alleluia be chanted", and "If God is the Lord is to be chanted at Matins, then we chant" a Glory of the saint in Tone V, with no Both now printed after it. Aposticha from the Oktoechos at Vespers and at Matins. One canon by Joseph (Ode VI has two troparia and a Theotokion); kontakion and ikos; the saint's exapostilarion is appointed at Glory after that of the Oktoechos. At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`Thou wast a pillar of patience, O venerable one, * emulating the forefathers: * Job in sufferings, Joseph in temptations, * and the life of the bodiless ones while yet in the body. * O Daniel, our father, ** entreat Christ God that our souls be saved!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:1},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:1}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone I`,tone:1},kontakion:{text:`Having ascended thy pillar like a star of great radiance, * thou didst illumine the world with thy venerable deeds, * and didst dispel the gloom of deception O father, * wherefore, we beseech thee: Shine forth even now in the hearts of thy servants ** the unwaning light of knowledge.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:8},{locus:`p8 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII,`,spec_mel:`As first fruits ...`,tone:8},ikos:{text:`Flawed is the hymn which I now offer in praise of thy struggles, O father; for my heart is impure, in that I have shamefully defiled it. But grant me the words, O holy one, to hymn in a pure manner thy life at which even the angels marveled, for thou wast like an incorporeal one, having received the unwaning light of knowledge.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`lic_glory_rubric`,`lic_glory`,`aposticha_rubric`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`What shall we proclaim thee to be, O Daniel? * An uprooter of the passions * and planter of the virtues, * a true wonderworker, an intercessor for sinners, * a most valiant exorcist of demons, * a beacon radiant with piety, * a dwelling place of the Spirit and champion of the Church. ** Pray thou that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,spec_mel:`What shall we call you ...`},{text:`What shall we name thee, O Daniel? * A faster, * for thou didst subject the passions to thy mind; * a sufferer, * for thou didst endure all manner of discomfort, * lifted high above the ground on thy pillar; * a most diligent spiritual athlete and a most skilled physician. ** Pray thou that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`What shall we call you ...`},{text:`What shall we now call thee, O Daniel? * A model for monastics and teacher of abstinence, * an adornment of the faithful * and worker of healings, * a beacon shining forth light upon those who are in darkness, * a fellow citizen of the angels, equal in honor to them, * and an inhabitant of paradise and a heavenly man. ** Pray thou that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`What shall we call you ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`Strange and awesome is the mystery * of thy seedless birthgiving, * surpassing all of man's thought in majesty, O pure Virgin. * For thou hast given birth in the flesh * unto Him Who is ever of the Father's essence, * upon Whom the many-eyed cherubim dare not gaze * and before Whom all the ranks of angels tremble. * We glorify thee who gavest Him birth, ** O Bride of God!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`To whom hast thou likened thyself, * in no wise rousing thyself to repentance, * O my wretched soul, * neither fearing the fire * which awaiteth the wicked? * Arise, and call upon her who alone is quick to help, and cry aloud: * O Virgin Mother, entreat thy Son and our God, ** that He deliver me from the snares of the deceiver!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure and undefiled one, * who hast given birth unto the unbearable Fire * which utterly consumeth sins * and bedeweth the faithful: * By thy supplications burn up the tinder of my countless offenses, * and with dew cool thou my soul * which withereth because of the passions, ** that I, thy servant, may magnify thy mercy and power.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`O Lady, help of all, * send down a drop of the oil of thy mercy upon me * who am tempest-tossed upon the sea of darkness * and ever compassed about by the billows and waves * of the evils of this life; * and give me a helping hand, * and grant unto me the portion of the elect and the righteous, ** for thou hast given birth unto the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:8,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in the same melody`},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The ewe-lamb, as she beheld the Lamb * stretched out of His own will upon the Tree of the Cross, * cried out maternally, in pain with her weeping: * O my Son, what is this strange sight? * O Longsuffering One, how is it that Thou art slain, * Who, as Lord, bestoweth life upon all, * granting resurrection to mortals? ** I glorify Thy great condescension, O my God!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},lic_glory_rubric:{text:`If “God is the Lord ...” is to be chanted at Matins, then we chant:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 If God is the Lord is chanted at Matins`}},lic_glory:{text:`Having made good the talent entrusted thee by Christ, O venerable father, even after death thou hast been revealed to be an exorcist of demons and a physician for those suffering from divers ailments, a pillar and foundation, and a holy mountain of the Church of Christ. Wherefore, we beseech thee, O wonderworker Daniel: Ask thou that our souls find peace and great mercy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory (God is the Lord days)`},composer:`the Studite`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone V, the composition of the Studite`,tone:5},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha rubric`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion_glory`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and that of the venerable one, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “With hymns I honor Daniel the Stylite,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and that of the venerable one, with 4 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “With hymns I honor Daniel the Stylite,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone VIII:`,composer:`Joseph`,acrostic:`With hymns I honor Daniel the Stylite`,tone:8,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us sing unto the Lord, * who led His people through the Red Sea: * for He alone hath gloriously been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O blessed Daniel, send down a luminous ray of light from heaven upon me who with hymns desire to praise thy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a truly great sun, O father, thou didst shine forth to the ends of the earth, illumining the assemblies of the faithful with the splendor of thy virtues.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Submitting to the laws of the Master, O father, thou didst mortify the flesh with abstinence, and subject it to the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The immutable Lord Who was born from thee, O Theotokos, appeared as a whole man, even though after incarnation He remained as He had been.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Lord, Creator of the vault of heaven * and Builder of the Church, * do Thou strengthen me in Thy love, O Summit of desire, * O Support of the faithful, * O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having parted the sea of the passions with the rod of abstinence, O father, thou didst traverse it without drowning, and attained unto the mountain of true dispassion, conversing with God in purity of mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having ascended to the heights of the virtues, thou didst become known to the world; for thou didst stand lifted aloft upon thy pillar, illumining those who came to thee with faith with the splendor of most glorious wonders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Founded upon the rock of the knowledge of God, thou wast revealed to be unmoved by all the wiles of the demons; wherefore, thou didst raise up thy body on a pillar above the earth, and didst let thy soul soar to the heavens.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Deliver me from the assault of the passions, O Lady, and do thou now vanquish the enemies that war against me; establish me upon the rock of the will of God, and enlighten my soul, O portal of the Light divine.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, art my strength and Thou art my power, * Thou art my God and Thou art my joy, * Thou Who, while never leaving the bosom of Thy Father, * hast visited our poverty. * Therefore with the prophet Habbakuk I cry unto Thee, * “Glory to Thy power, O Lover of mankind!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O ever-memorable father, thou didst behold Simeon, the servant of God, shining forth like the radiant sun upon his pillar; and divinely illumined by the divine splendors which issued forth from him, O Daniel, thou didst follow his manner of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst vanquish the demonic legions with the sword of faith and drown them in the torrents of thy prayers, causing the destruction they wrought upon those at sea to cease; and thereby save those who chanted with faith unto God: Glory to Thy power, O Lover of mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having ascended thy pillar, O all-blessed father, thou didst stand whole nights like one of the bodiless ones, having acquired an humble spiritual eye; and, as a shining mirror of the Spirit, received radiance and divine manifestations with a pure mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The laws of nature are renewed in thee, O most pure one, for thou hast given birth, in a manner truly beyond cause and telling, unto the Word, the Giver of the Law, Who hath delivered from ignorance the race of mankind which faithfully chants: Glory to Thy power, O Lover of mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Light never-waning, * why hast Thou turned Thy face from me * and why hath the alien darkness surrounded me, * wretched though I be? * But do Thou guide my steps I implore Thee * and turn me back towards the light of Thy commandments.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`That thou O father mightest receive immortal glory, thou didst slay the desires of thy flesh, and bridle the urgings of the passions with the labors of abstinence; and hast thereby been revealed to be a river of miracles and a wellspring of healings. O ever-memorable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The wondrous Simeon appeared to thee who wast struck with fear, O blessed father, and with two angels he pointed out the path which thou wast to tread upon the earth, crying aloud: Come and stand by me, borne aloft to God by grace!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined by unwaning radiance and divine effulgence, O father, thou didst dispel the gloom of the passions and wast revealed to be a pillar of light and a stairway truly leading the faithful up to God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O maiden Bride of God, who hast given birth unto the Master, thou hast been revealed to be more exalted than the heavenly hosts, and hast deified the nature of the earthly; wherefore, with soul and tongue, O Virgin, we the faithful glorify thee as her who is most truly the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Cleanse me, O Savior, * for many are mine iniquities; * lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee, * for unto Thee have I cried, * and Thou hast hearkened unto me, * O God of my salvation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy mind, O father, illumined through drawing nigh unto God, remained unconsumed by the fire of pleasures and above the passions, and higher than passionate attachments to the flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy soul was filled with the Spirit's gifts of life-creating waters, O divinely wise and all-blessed one; and thou didst truly pour forth rivers of healing which quench the torrents of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`All we, the faithful, have acquired thee as an intercessor and a helper in the deep of evil and the billows and waves of tribulation which ever pass over us, O Theotokos, for thou alone art the refuge of mortals.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The Hebrew children in the furnace * boldly trampled upon the flames, * changing the fire into dew, they cried aloud: * 'Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God, throughout the ages'.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The ranks of angels marveled at thy standing upon thy pillar, O all-blessed God-bearer; for having assumed their manner of life while yet in the body, thou didst cry aloud: Blessed art Thou, O Lord God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Luminous with the loftiness of an immaterial way of life and with the splendor of prophecy, thou hast shone forth rays of healing upon us who piously honor thee, O wondrous Daniel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the radiance of thy prayers disperse thou the gloom of my passions, O all-blessed one, and guide me to the path of life who chant: Blessed art Thou, O Lord God, throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Be thou merciful unto me, O Virgin, and with the healing power of thy prayers cure me who have been wounded by the sting of sin and who cry aloud: Blessed is the Fruit of thy womb!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In his wrath the Chaldean tyrant made the furnace blaze, * with heat fanned sevenfold for the servants of God; * but when he perceived that they had been saved by a greater power * he cried aloud to the Creator and Redeemer; * “Ye children bless, ye priests praise, * ye people, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages”.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O God-bearing father, in renowned manner thou didst attain unto the ultimate desire, the greatest good, soaring aloft on the wings of thy virtuous deeds; and with the bodiless ones, O Daniel, thou dost cry aloud: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The power of God manifestly strengthened thee and enabled thee to endure the bitter cold of winter, the burning heat of the sun, the decay of thy flesh and the discomfort caused by the worms which issued forth therefrom; and thou didst cry: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast revealed to be a new Job, O right wondrous Daniel, beset by a multitude of temptations and tribulations; and emulating the meekness of David, the guilelessness of Jacob and the chastity of Joseph, thou didst cry aloud in thanksgiving: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-hymned and all-holy Lady, fulfilling thy words by acknowledging thee to be the Theotokos, we now bless thee, in that thou hast given birth unto God for us. And hymning Him in two natures and one Hypostasis, we cry aloud: Ye children bless; ye priests hymn; ye people supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Every ear is awestruck at hearing of God's ineffable condescension, * for the Most High voluntarily descended and assumed flesh, * becoming man in the Virgin's womb; * wherefore we the faithful magnify the most pure Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Lo! when thou didst repose, having finished thy course, the gates of heaven were opened unto thee, and the ranks of angels received thee; and Christ, the Bestower of crowns, crowned thee with the glory of righteousness. We, the faithful, magnify Him in song.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like a lily of the valley didst thou blossom in the paradise of abstinence, and like a cypress didst thou rise to the heights of perfection; like the olive tree of the Psalms hast thou been shown to be, anointing our faces and hearts with the oil of thine asceticism.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Creation knoweth thee to be a pillar firmly grounded upon the rock of the virtues, an unbreachable rampart, a foundation of miracles, a right calm haven, a treasury of healing and the dwelling place of the Spirit. Wherefore, we celebrate thy memory today, O Daniel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Today thy divine memory hath shone forth upon us more brightly than the sun, illumining the hearts of the faithful with the light of righteousness, and dispelling the darkness of the soul-destroying passions. And celebrating it, we piously hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Thou that wast born of her whom Thou didst preserve incorrupt even after birthgiving, have pity upon me when Thou sittest to judge my deeds, and overlook mine iniquities and my sins; for Thou, Who only art without sin, a merciful God and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having lifted thyself up upon a pillar, thou didst lay waste to thy flesh through abstinence, O father Daniel. Wherefore, thou wast deemed worthy to become a vessel of the Spirit, and having received divine grace, O thrice-blessed one, thou dost drive away every ailment from those who with faith honor thy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Thy tomb, O Savior ...`,tone:1},{text:`O most holy Virgin, hope of Christians, with the hosts on high do thou unceasingly beseech God to Whom, in a manner surpassing understanding and all telling, thou hast given birth, that He grant forgiveness of all our sins and correction of life unto those who with faith and love ever glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},{text:`Upon seeing the Lamb and Shepherd hanging dead upon the Tree, * the unblemished ewe-lamb, cried aloud, weeping * and exclaiming maternally: * “How is it that Thou dost willingly endure abasement and sufferings * which surpass all telling, ** O my Son, and supremely good God?”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion_glory:{text:`With wordless utterance, thy pillar proclaimeth the ascetic feats of thee who suffered, standing unprotected at the mercy of the adverse elements. Wherefore, thou didst shine forth as a luminous beacon, enlightening all creation, O father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion of the venerable one, at Glory`},sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion from the Oktoechos, and Glory ...,`,spec_mel:`O immutable Light ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`With unceasing hymns we bless thee, O Virgin, for thou hast given birth unto One of the Trinity and didst bear in thy divine arms the transcendent Word, immutably and without change.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`},aposticha_rubric:{text:`Aposticha from the Oktoechos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Aposticha rubric`}}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}},{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Martyr Myrax`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYR MYRAX`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 11th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-11A.pdf`,note:`Second file of 11 December, a separate service (Bill, 15 Nov 2026, on the lettered files). Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the martyr at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no 12-11 entry for it. A Glory at Lord I have cried and a Glory at the aposticha, each followed by "Both now, Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion" with the Stavrotheotokion printed. One canon by Valeria, written in the martyr's own voice; kontakion and ikos; an exapostilarion with its Theotokion. The troparion is the general one of a martyr, with no name in it. The ODE VIII heading is printed "OODE VIII". At Liturgy only the troparion and kontakion.`,troparion:{text:`In his sufferings, Thy martyr Myrax O Lord, * received an imperishable crown from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * he set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By his supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy martyr`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Overcome by the fear of cruel tortures, Myrax denied Christ; * but, repenting, he confessed Him again with a loud voice, * and, having suffered manfully, * he received the crown of martyrdom. ** Wherefore, he dwelleth in the mansions of heaven.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy martyr`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},ikos:{text:`Coming to his senses and receiving boldness through repentance, the martyr Myrax cried aloud: “The Lord is my light! Whom shall I fear? The Lord is the Defender of my life! Of whom shall I be afraid?” And he was condemned to death for confessing Christ. Wherefore, he now dwelleth in the mansions of heaven with the other passion-bearers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy martyr, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Lo! the martyr Myrax crieth aloud: “I hear that my God and Savior hath said: 'Whosoever rejecteth me shall I also reject on the last day!' Yet let it not be so with me, thrice wretched as I am, O Lord. For even though I apostatized from Thee, yet I know Thee to be merciful and loving: for Thou didst not spurn the tears of Peter who had denied Thee, nor didst thou reject the repentance of Paul who had persecuted Thee, but didst make both of them steadfast in Thy love. Wherefore, I pray: accept also my fervent repentance, and, overlooking mine apostasy, restore and save me, for Thou canst do all things whatsoever Thou dost desire.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:6},{text:`“Judas, who betrayed Thee by a kiss, refusing to embrace repentance, devoid of fervent love for Thee, neither understanding that thou hast mercy on all who approach Thee in penitence, departed and hanged himself; but do Thou, O Lord, deliver me from such insane hardness of heart: accept my bitter groaning, raising me up from my fall, and save me who repent, in that Thou art good and full of loving-kindness.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Peter, the preeminent apostle, who once denied Thee thrice, O Christ, wept bitterly, and Paul, the teacher of the nations, who had persecuted Thee, called himself the least of the apostles; yet both afterwards served Thee, performing great deeds. But what shall I, who have rejected Thee, offer unto Thee besides tearful repentance? Yet let my blood, which is shed for Thee, cry out for me. Thou inclinest thy loving-kindness toward me, O Lord, for thou hast mercy upon all, in that Thou art mighty.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_glory:{text:`Let him not boast who hath acquired the riches of the world, and power and glory which passeth quickly away, for in an instant he will be deprived of them all, and will find himself suddenly standing before the judgment-seat, naked, poor and bereft of glory, having only his trust in Thy boundless compassion, whereby do Thou also save me, O good Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Of old, when the unblemished ewe-lamb, * the immaculate Lady, * beheld her Lamb * uplifted upon the Cross, * she exclaimed maternally * and, marveling, cried aloud: * “O my Child most sweet, * what is this new and most glorious sight? * How is it that the ungrateful assembly hath betrayed Thee to the judgment of Pilate * and condemneth Thee, the Life of all, to death? * Yet do I hymn, O Word, ** Thine ineffable condescension.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos, then:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p1 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha_glory:{text:`The martyr Myrax crieth aloud: “I have foolishly apostatized from Christ, buying a transitory life and vain benefits! And, lo! I see myself poor and naked, devoured by spiritual hunger, tormented by a thirst for forgiveness! For I received the royal coin from God, but have cast it to the swine, and have found naught to exchange for it. Yet I beg Thee, praying: Take this my transitory life, O Lord, giving me in exchange life everlasting! Accept my blood, which is shed for Thee, and grant that I may share in Thine immortal banquet! Receive my repentance as Thou didst that of the thief, and save me!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`“I cannot bear, O my Child, * to behold Thee * dying upon the Tree, * Thou Who givest courage unto all, * that Thou mightest give divine and saving courage * unto those who of old fell into the sleep of perdition * through the fruit of disobedience!” ** weeping, said the Virgin, whom we magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`,tone:8}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion`,`exapostilarion_closer`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and that of the holy martyr, the acrostic whereof is: “Have mercy on me who have fallen away from Thee, O my God!” the composition of Valeria, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, and that of the holy martyr, the acrostic whereof is: “Have mercy on me who have fallen away from Thee, O my God!” the composition of Valeria, in Tone II:`,composer:`Valeria`,acrostic:`Have mercy on me who have fallen away from Thee, O my God!`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Taking up the Song of Moses, O my soul, * cry aloud: * 'A helper and a protector hath become unto me salvation. * My God, * whom I will glorify'.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“O Christ, Who accepted the repentance of the preeminent. Peter who had denied Thee, and made him a great shepherd of Thy sheep; receive me like a lost sheep!” the martyr Myrax cried.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I have fallen away from Thee Who didst become incarnate for my sake! I have rejected Thee Who wast nailed to the Cross for me! Yet I now confess that Thou art my God, and I glorify Thee!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“O most radiant choir of martyrs, even though I denied Christ for a time, accept me now who have endured cruel tortures for Him, that I may glorify God with you!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I confess to thee my great sin, O Lady; for I shamelessly denied thy divine Son!” Myrax cried out to the Theotokos in lamentation, begging her aid.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`My mind hath not brought forth good fruit, * but do Thou show me to be fruitful * in Thy compassion O God, * Thou husbandman of all good things.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“Lovest thou Me, O Simon? “, Thou didst ask the disciple who had denied Thee, O Lord. And 'Lovest thou Me, O Myrax?', Thou hast now asked me as well, O all-merciful Savior. And I give Thee mine answer in deeds instead of words, accepting death for Thee.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I denied Thee with my mouth, O my Savior, when my heart was filled with terror and grew weak amid the struggle; yet grant me strength now, O Master, to live my life for Thee.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Whosoever confesseth Me before men, him will I also confess before the heavenly Father; but if any man deny Me, him will I also deny!', Thou didst proclaim, O Lord. Yet let not these latter words apply to me!” the martyr Myrax prayed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Pray for me who have fallen, O Mother of God!” the martyr Myrax cried out in repentance; “and remain with me, the thrice-accursed, during my sufferings!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`The prophet foreseeing Thy birth from a virgin, * prophesied crying aloud: * ‘I have heard report of Thee, and I was afraid; * For from the South, from the Overshadowed mountain * shalt thou come forth O Christ’`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“Having eaten Thy bread, Thy most pure Body, and drunk Thy divine Blood, like Judas I rose up against Thee. Wherefore, I fear Thine everlasting condemnation, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Fearing to commit my body to tortures, I surrendered my soul instead to endless torment. O most merciful Savior, permit me now to change; for, lo! I give my body and all its members over to suffering. Wherefore, free Thou my soul from captivity to sin.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Wretch that I am, I loved the flesh-pots of Egypt and mindlessly rejected the promised land, but lead me now thereto, O Thou Who knowest the hearts of men, for I now cross not the streams of the Jordan, by the river of my blood which I have shed for Thee.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“O blessed Theotokos, merciful surety of sinners: speak to thy divine Son on behalf of me, the thrice-accursed!” the martyr Myrax prayed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`The night is far spent, the day is at hand: * Thy light hath shone upon the world! * Therefore the ranks of angels sing Thy praises, * and all things glorify Thee, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“Dare I make my dwelling with the martyrs? Can I wash away the sin of apostasy with my blood? O all-merciful Master, illumine me with repentance, and save me!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I have no wedding garment; for I have sullied the vesture of my soul with apostasy. Yet cleanse and make it white through repentance, as Thou didst promise, O Savior!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I now endure bodily tortures with gladness, having endured bitter torment of soul when I denied Thee, O Lord; yet do I glorify Thy long-suffering, for Thou hast been well-pleased to illumine me with repentance.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Lead me up to the eternal mansions, O Lady; for even though I sinned, denying thy divine Son, yet in repentance do I lay down my life for Him. Wherefore, be thou well-pleased to have mercy upon me!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`I am held fast in the depths of sin O Savior, * and am overwhelmed by the sea of life, * but as Jonah was delivered from the sea-monster, * so also deliver me from the passions, * and save me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“Fettered with the chains of a weak nature, as Jonah was stuck fast in the belly of the sea monster, I sinned; yet, calling me up from the depths of the darkness of sin, Thou hast freed my soul, O Merciful One!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I am a useless and unfaithful servant!” the martyr Myrax cried aloud; “yet receive me who come to Thee in repentance like the prodigal son, O heavenly Father, and cause me to dwell with the thief who confessed Christ God at the eleventh hour!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Who can describe the depth of my fall? Yet who can fathom the depths of the tender compassion? Wherefore, I cry out to Him out of the pit of destruction: With Thy mighty arm raise me up from the abyss of sin!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Wide is the path that leadeth to destruction, but narrow is the way of salvation which the martyr Myrax found in suffering, praising thine aid, O Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Like unto the cherubim, the children rejoicing in the furnace sang: * 'Blessed art Thou O God, * for in truth Thou hast brought this judgment upon us * because of our sins, * Thou art supremely praised and glorified throughout all ages'.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“The apostles preached Thee throughout the whole world, O Christ; but out of fear I remained silent. The martyrs boldly proclaimed Thee, O God Whom I denied!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Let not Thy righteous wrath fall upon me!” the martyr Myrax said; “for even though I have sinned, yet purify me with the fire of repentance, and from the furnace of torments call me forth into the coolness of never-ending life, O all-hymned and supremely glorious God, throughout all ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I have denied Thee, yet turn not Thy face away from me, lest the fiery sword of the cherubim bar mine entry through the gates of paradise! For, lo! having washed my garments in the blood of martyrdom, I have come; and with confession I have hallowed my mouth, which was defiled by apostasy. Wherefore, I chant unto Thee, my God, throughout all ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Thy luminous grace hath turned me, who have fallen into grievous temptation, O most pure Virgin, and hath strengthened me for the struggle of martyrdom; wherefore, I hymn thee, the most glorious Mother of my God!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`God Who descended into the fiery furnace * with the Hebrew children, * and transformed the flame into dew, * do ye works hymn, * and supremely exalt as Lord throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“O God Who appeared to Moses in the fire of the bush, deliver me from eternal fire and burn up my guilt with the dew of my tears, that I may hymn Thee throughout the ages.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Having quelled the throes of my conscience and acquired boldness through fiery repentance, rejoicing I endure tortures!” the martyr Myrax cried aloud, hymning Christ the Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Remit my sins and have mercy on me; and accept the shedding of my martyr's blood as a redeeming sacrifice, that I may hymn and bless Thee, 'O Christ, throughout the ages!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I offer my life as a pleasing sacrifice to thy Son and my Savior, O Lady. Him do thou entreat on behalf of me, the thrice-accursed, that I may bless thee throughout the ages.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Who born on Earth hath ever heard of, or beheld, * a Virgin miraculously conceiving in her womb, * and painlessly giving birth to a child, * wherefore we magnify thee O pure Virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`“When Thou shalt sit to judge the whole world, O impartial Judge and King of all creation, number me among the sheep at Thy right hand, that with them I may magnify Thy loving-kindness, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Enduring cruel tortures, the martyr Myrax prayed: “Strengthen, forgive and have mercy on me, O Savior of the-world, that I may magnify Thee in Thy kingdom!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having redeemed his apostasy by voluntary confession, the martyr Myrax offered up the repentance of the thief at the eleventh hour, and, dwelling now with Christ God, He magnifieth the Trinity of one Dominion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`“I confess thine ineffable mercy, O Lady; for thou didst not leave me to perish, O surety of sinners!” the martyr Myrax crieth out, rejoicing, magnifying the aid of the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`“I stretch forth my hands to Thee, O my God; for I am ashamed to lift up mine eyes to heaven. Account the fountains of my tears, for I know that they cannot wash away my sin. Wherefore, I hasten to wash in my blood. Turn not Thy face away from me, but, pouring forth upon me the depths of Thy loving-kindness, save me, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy martyr, in Tone V`,tone:5},{text:`O pure Ever-virgin, thou fervent and invincible intercessor, excellent and unashamed hope, rampart, protection and refuge of those who have recourse unto thee: with the angels entreat thy Son and God, that He grant peace, salvation and great mercy to the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word ...`},{text:`Beholding Thee hanging of Thine own will upon the Cross between the thieves, O Christ, Thy Mother said maternally, her womb rent with pain: “O my sinless Son, how is it that Thou art unjustly nailed as a malefactor to the Cross, desiring to bring life to the human race, in that Thou art compassionate?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion:{text:`As the martyr Myrax was proceeding to suffering of his own will, the Lord said to him: “Fear not those who slay the body, yet cannot slay the soul, O My child! Be not afraid of torture, for I shall give thee the strength to endure torment; wherefore, trust no longer in thyself, for thou hast come to know the weakness of man; for without Me ye can truly accomplish naught!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the holy martyr`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`He Who on high is glorified as God by the angels, O pure one, ineffably dwelt with those below without leaving the bosom of the Father; and thou wast the cause of His salvation, inexpressibly lending flesh to Him of thy pure blood, O pure one. Him do thou beseech, that He grant deliverance from transgressions to thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-11A.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}},liturgy:{order:[`troparion`,`kontakion`]}}]},"12-12":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`,`c1.identity`,`c1.little_vespers`,`c1.great_vespers`,`c1.matins`,`c1.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`our father among the saints Spyridon the Wonderworker, Bishop of Tremithus`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR VENERABLE FATHER SPYRIDON THE WONDERWORKER, BISHOP OF TREMITHUS`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 12th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`six_stichera`,fekula_section:`2C`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-12.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: SIX stichera of one saint at Lord I have cried (three printed, each marked Twice), a Matins aposticha with a Glory, and no Great Doxology in the service as the Slavonic Menaion has it: six-stichera, Fekula 2C. ODS vol. III has no 12-12 entry. THE PAGE ITSELF NOTES (p8): "In Greek usage, the service to St. Spyridon is of Doxology rank, rather than of six-Stichera rank, as in the Slavonic Menaion", and prints Praises stichera for that usage, with the same Glory (one word differs between the two printings: "all-praised", "most praised") and Stavrotheotokion as the Matins aposticha. Both are stored; the rank follows the Slavonic service. Two troparia: the general one of a hierarch with the name written in (Tone IV), and "Or this Troparion, in Tone I", printed at Vespers and at Liturgy. The canon by Theophanes is appointed "with 6 Troparia" (three and a Theotokion are printed in each ode), the Oktoechos canons "without their martyria". At Liturgy four Beatitude troparia from Ode III, readings printed.`,troparion:{text:`The truth of things revealed thee to thy flock as a rule of faith, * icon of meekness, and teacher of temperance; * wherefore, thou hast attained the heights through humility and riches through poverty; * O hierarch Spyridon our father, ** entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p9 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hierarch, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`O most sacred one, wounded with love for Christ, * and giving wings to thy mind through the radiance of the Spirit, * thou didst find thy work fulfilled in the activity of divine vision. * O thou who art pleasing to God, thou divine oblation, ** beseech Him that divine illumination be granted unto all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy hierarch`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p5 after Ode VI`,tone:2},{locus:`p9 AT LITURGY`,tone:2}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hierarch, in Tone II`,spec_mel:`Seeking the Highest ...`,tone:2},ikos:{text:`Let us now praise Spyridon, the hierarch of the Lord, sanctified from his mother's womb, who received the tablets of the grace of divine glory, as one most glorious in miracles from all of creation, as a fervent witness of the divine radiance, intercessor for the poor, and spiritual guide for the sinful; for he hath become a divine oblation for the throne of Christ, asking divine illumination for all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer_rubric`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`troparion`,`troparion_alternate_rubric`,`troparion_alternate`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera of the holy hierarch, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Rejoice, thou rule of hierarchs, unshaken confirmation of the Church, glory of the Orthodox, wellspring of miracles, inexhaustible stream of love, most radiant beacon, organ of the Spirit, intellect divine, meek and guileless, adorned with true simplicity, heavenly man and earthly angel, laborer in the vineyard, true friend of Christ! Beseech Him to grant great mercy to those who honor thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`O Spyridon, glory of the fathers, thou wast truly shown to be meek and an heir to the land of the meek. By the sinews of thy wise and simple words thou didst strangle Arius, the most wicked and demented enemy, by divine grace. And, having clarified the divine dogma for all, and extolled by the Spirit that which leadeth to salvation, and enlightened all the Orthodox most manifestly, thou didst indicate to all the faithful to glorify the One Word as truly the Only Begotten of the beginningless Father, Who granteth the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Having slain the carnal passions, thou didst raise the dead by the grace of God, and didst change a serpent into gold, and didst restrain the raging of the river by thy prayer, O father, Appearing to the afflicted emperor by night, thou didst heal him by drawing nigh unto his heart when the Lord glorified thee most gloriously. Wherefore, we honor thy memory with a mighty voice and reverence the divine and sacred shrine of thy relics, whence floweth forth a divine stream of healings and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`O venerable father Spyridon, blessed and wise, for the sake of the love of God thou didst question the dead woman as though she were alive, and didst transform a serpent into gold for him that was beset by poverty, and didst restrain the flow of the river, taking pity on the people, and didst stand before the emperor as physician through the providence of God; and, as His disciple, thou didst raise up the dead, and amongst many fathers didst make clear the Faith. Wherefore, enabled to do all things by Christ, Who strengtheneth thee, do thou now entreat Him that our souls be saved!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone I`,tone:1},lic_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion; or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Both now rubric`}},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The Virgin, beholding Thine unjust sacrifice, weeping, cried out to Thee, O Christ: O my Child most sweet, how is it that Thou diest unjustly? How is it that Thou, Who suspended all the earth upon the waters, art Thyself suspended upon a Tree? O greatly merciful Benefactor, I pray Thee, leave me not alone who am Thy Mother and handmaid!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion; or this Stavrotheotokion, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`O all-praised martyrs ...`,tone:1},aposticha_glory:{text:`O father Spyridon, venerable and wise, by thy virtues hast thou been shown to be a divine treasure of hierarchs. Wherefore, being an intercessor of the Church, thou didst cast out the chief of the heretics and, in council, didst crush the blasphemy of Arius to the earth. Therefore, working wonders in word and deed, do thou beseech Christ that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`The Aposticha from the Oktoechos; Glory ..., to the saint, in Tone II`,tone:2},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon beholding Thine unjust slaying, O Christ, * the Virgin, cried out to Thee, weeping: * “O my sweetest Child! * How is it that Thou diest unjustly? * How is it that Thee Who hast suspended the whole earth upon the waters * dost hang upon the Tree *? * Leave me not alone * who am Thy Mother and handmaiden, ** I pray, O greatly merciful Benefactor!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},troparion_alternate_rubric:{text:`Or this Troparion, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Or this Troparion rubric`}},troparion_alternate:{text:`Thou wast shown forth as a champion of the First Council * and a wonderworker, O Spyridon, our God-bearing father. * Wherefore, thou didst speak to one dead in the grave, * and didst change a serpent into gold. * And, whilst chanting thy holy prayers, * thou didst have angels serving with thee, O most sacred one. * Glory to Him that hath given thee strength! * Glory to Him that hath crowned thee! ** Glory to Him that worketh healings for all through thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p2 Or this Troparion`},sourceLabel:`Or this Troparion, in Tone I`,tone:1}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`,`ikos`,`exapostilarion_glory`,`exapostilarion_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer_rubric`,`aposticha_stavrotheotokion`,`usage_rubric`,`praises_rubric`,`praises`,`praises_glory`,`praises_closer_rubric`,`praises_stavrotheotokion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without their martyria; and the canon of the holy hierarch, with 6 Troparia, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos, without their martyria; and the canon of the holy hierarch, with 6 Troparia, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone II:`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:2,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`In the deep of old the infinite Power overwhelmed Pharaoh's whole army. * But the Incarnate Word annihilated pernicious sin. * Exceedingly glorious is the Lord, * for gloriously hath He been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having attained unto the land of the meek, being thyself meek, merciful and pure, O father, calm thou the present tempest of my heart, that, in divine tranquility, I may hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having cleared thy soul of the overgrowth of the passions through godly cultivation, O father Spyridon, thou didst become god-like and wast enriched by the most radiant splendor of the divine Spirit. Wherefore, thou dost illumine those who sincerely bless thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Taking thee from a flock as He had David, the Creator appointed thee as a most eminent shepherd of the rational sheep, shining forth in simplicity and meekness, and adorned with guilelessness, O venerable pastor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most holy and pure Virgin, enlighten and hallow my thoughts and soul, I pray thee, dispelling the clouds of mine ignorance, and removing the darkness of sin, that I may bless thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Thou hast established me on the rock of faith, * and my mouth hath been emboldened against mine enemies. * For my spirit rejoiceth when I sing: * There is none as holy as our God * and none more righteous than Thee, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having illumined thy mind with dispassion and adorned thyself with divine humility, thou didst receive the gifts of the Spirit to cast out evil spirits and to loose the infirmities of those who faithfully honor thee, O most sacred one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having slain the serpent, the author of evil, and trampled down the inclination towards avarice, O holy hierarch, taking pity on him who was in need, thou didst transform a serpent into a golden ornament by thy sacred prayers, O venerable father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst ascend the mountain of dispassion; thou didst enter the darkness of the vision of God, and didst receive the law of salvation on the tablets of thy heart, in that thou art a most sacred and faithful favorite of thy Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Heal thou the wounds of my soul, O Bride of God, and illumine my mind which hath been darkened by neglect, that I may chant: There is none blameless save thee, O immaculate one, and none pure but thee, O Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`From a Virgin didst Thou come forth, not as an ambassador, * nor as an angel, * but the very Lord himself incarnate, * and didst save me, the whole man; * wherefore I cry unto Thee: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Set afire by the burning coal of the honored Spirit, thou didst burn up all the readily kindled fuel of the passions, O all-blessed one, enlightening the world with the fiery rays of thy virtues.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having slain the movements of thy flesh, O divinely inspired one, thou didst raise up the dead by thy life-imparting call. Wherefore, I beseech thee: Enliven my slain soul, O father!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O father, the dead woman, obeying thee, spake, and by thy commands the raging of the river was restrained. For thou wast revealed as a worker of wonders endowed with divine grace, O blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The prophets foretold the incomprehensible abyss of thy mystery, for thou alone, O pure one, didst give birth unto the Unknowable One, Who, in His unutterable tender compassion, became incarnate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ my Savior, the enlightenment of those lying in the darkness of sin. * I rise early to hymn Thee O King of Peace, * enlighten me with Thy radiance, * for I know no other God than Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The river of the gifts which are within thee doth water every heart, O venerable one, and richly granteth health unto all, moving all to glorify God, Who hath glorified thee and honored thee with all manner of wonders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The earthly emperor clearly recognized thee as a true servant of the heavenly King, full of divine gifts, O blessed one, when thou didst come to him, proclaiming the great Physician, Who is God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating the hospitable character of Abraham, thou didst open the doors of thy house unto all, and wast all things to all people, mindful of those who were in evil straits, O blessed Spyridon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`For us hast thou given birth unto a newborn Babe, Who before the ages was begotten of the beginningless Father, O maiden. Him do thou entreat as thy Son and God, that He spare those who, with a pure soul, proclaim thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Whirled about in the abyss of sin, * I appeal to the unfathomable abyss of Thy compassion: * Raise me up from corruption, O God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Gold was as mire to thee who shone forth in dispassion more brightly than gold, and wast enriched by thy most golden gifts of the Spirit, O venerable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Serving thy Master in purity, O venerable one, thou didst have a multitude of the angelic hosts serving thee with unseen voices, O most sacred one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most glorious and all-wise father, thy life hath made thee most glorious to the world. Wherefore, rejoicing, we that hymn thee celebrate thy divine memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`More spacious than the heavens was thy womb, which contained God Whom no place can contain, O all-holy virgin Bride of God, who knewest not a man.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The godless order of the lawless tyrant * fanned the roaring flame; * but Christ bedewed the God-fearing children with the Spirit, * therefore He is blessed and supremely exalted.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having acquired the guilelessness of Moses, the meekness of David and the blamelessness of Job of Uz, thou didst become a dwelling-place of the Spirit, chanting most sacredly: Blessed and supremely glorious art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The showers of heaven rained down upon thy head during the harvest and prefigured the future; for, as thou didst say, God glorified thy divine memory, sanctifying the faithful by thy mediation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`In the council of the fathers God glorified thee, who guarded thy words in judgment, O blessed one. Thou didst bring them forth with faith, openly disclosing the follies of the most irrational Arius and destroying his opposition.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through the ineffable Word, O Virgin, thou didst put forth the Cluster of grapes as the Branch which alone was uncultivated and which poureth forth the wine gladdening all mankind, sanctifying mortals and dispelling all the drunkenness of the wicked.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`In Babylon, the activity of the fire was once divided, * for, by the command of God it consumed the Chaldeans, * but bedewed the faithful, who chant: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou didst extinguish the furnace of the passions with divine outpourings of the divine Spirit, O father, pouring forth a dew which taketh away the fever of the ailing who ever have recourse unto thee in faith, O blessed and most noetically rich Spyridon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Guileless, upright, meek, merciful, not mindful of the wrongs done thee, loving and hospitable wast thou, O most sacred hierarch, adorned with the wisdom of Orthodoxy, O venerable one. Wherefore, we honor thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Of old, the dead woman when questioned by thee O father, replied as though alive. Oh what a most marvelous wonder! Oh what a most glorious mystery! Oh, the grace which thou hast received, having adorned thyself with an angelic life, O right wondrous one!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Heal thou the passions of my heart with thy mercy, O all-hymned one; calm thou my mind, enlighten my soul, and guide me to walk the paths of salvation, that I may ever hymn thee, O all-hymned one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The Son of the beginningless Father, God and Lord, * hath appeared to us incarnate of a virgin, * to enlighten those in darkness, * and to gather the dispersed; * therefore the all-hymned Theotokos do we magnify`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Exalted among the God-bearing fathers, thou didst openly proclaim the Son of the beginningless Father to be of one essence and equally everlasting with the Father, and didst stop the mouths of the iniquitous, O all-blessed and holy hierarch.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-radiant sun, adornment of the fathers, glory of priests, converser with angels: By thy prayers grant the unwaning Light unto those who now joyously celebrate thy light-bearing memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With a voice of rejoicing have the divine mansions, the heavenly city and the beauteous choir of those who hold festival received thy soul, which hath been hallowed and adorned with the virtues, O all-blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The great mystery of thy birthgiving, which passeth understanding doth astound the angels, O divinely joyous one, delighting the assembly of the venerable and making glad the sacred fathers who hymn thee, the hope of our souls, in a godly manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Thou didst shine forth as a divinely appointed pastor, O Spyridon, raised from the tending of sheep by God, Who entrusted thee to preside over the Church of Christ. Thou didst drive away the wolves of false teaching by thy words, grazing thy flock on the pasture of piety. Wherefore, thou didst affirm the Faith by the wisdom of the Spirit in the midst of the God-bearing fathers, O blessed hierarch. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who celebrate thy holy memory with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy hierarch, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`As the all-immaculate Bride of the Creator, * Mother of the Redeemer, who knewest not a man, * and as the receptacle of the Comforter O all-hymned one, * hasten thou to deliver me, * the vile abode of iniquity and noetic plaything of the demons, * from their evil machinations; * and make me the bright dwelling-place of the virtues, * O thou incorrupt light-bearing one. * Drive away the clouds of the passions and grant that, * by thy supplications, * I may receive a portion on high ** and share in the never-waning light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:8,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in the same melody`},{text:`The ewe-lamb, beholding her Lamb, Shepherd and Redeemer upon the Cross, weeping, exclaimed, and bitterly lamenting, cried out: The world doth. rejoice, receiving deliverance through Thee, but my womb doth burn, beholding Thy crucifixion, which Thou dost endure in the tender compassion of Thy mercy. O longsuffering Lord, Thou abyss and inexhaustible wellspring of mercy, have pity and grant remission of sins unto those who hymn Thy divine Pas-sion with faith!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion_glory:{text:`O God-bearing Spyridon, thou light of the world, like Moses and David, whose calling thou didst follow, the Spirit led thee up from an irrational flock unto the rational one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion of the holy hierarch, at Glory`},sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion from the Oktoechos; Glory ..., that of the holy hierarch`,spec_mel:`He, Who as God hath adorned heaven with stars ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`Thou wast the cause of the blessings bestowed by God upon the world, O Theotokos. And, even now, for the salvation of all, do thou move to pity God, Who is readily appeased.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, the Stichera from the Oktoechos, then:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha_glory:{text:`O venerable father, all-praised and holy hierarch, filled with the teaching of the apostles, and manifest as the habitation of the divine Spirit by thy virtuous life, with thy teachings thou didst drive off the wolves that beset the Church, and didst make clear the Faith of the Orthodox, and wast a pillar and champion of piety. Wherefore, working wonders in days past, thou didst transform a serpent into gold, and didst raise up a dead woman to question her. Yet, O thou that art right wondrous among the fathers, converser with teachers, entreat the Savior, that He save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone IV`,tone:4},aposticha_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Aposticha Both now rubric`}},aposticha_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The most pure Lady, beholding Christ dying, Who doth slay the deceiver, bitterly cried out to Him that had come forth from her womb, and marveling at His longsuffering, exclaimed: O my most beloved Child, forget not Thy handmaid! O Lover of mankind, delay not my consolation!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p7 Matins Aposticha Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},usage_rubric:{text:`N.B. In Greek usage, the service to St. Spyridon is of Doxology rank, rather than of six-Stichera rank, as in the Slavonic Menaion. Therefore, if Greek usage is followed, On the Praises:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 N.B. Greek usage: Doxology rank`}},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Illumined with the radiance of the Spirit, thou didst dispel the darkness of the foolish prating of Arius, O wise hierarch. Wherefore, in simplicity, faithfully teaching the Trinity, thou wast glorified by the wise and learned, and didst confirm the Council.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`Illumined with heavenly rays and with the power of Christ, thou dost bestow healing of both soul and body upon those who even now celebrate thy memory with faith, O divinely blessed father and wonderworker. Cease thou never to intercede for us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`In thy faithfulness to the commandments, thou wast shown to be a husbandman of Christ, the True Vine, O God-bearer. Wherefore, having mystically received the talent of the kingdom from on high, pray thou without ceasing for us that honor thee, O wise Spyridon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`O venerable father, most praised and holy hierarch, filled with the teaching of the apostles, and manifest as the habitation of the divine Spirit by thy virtuous life, with thy teachings thou didst drive off the wolves that beset the Church, and didst make clear the Faith of the Orthodox, and wast a pillar and champion of piety. Wherefore, working wonders in days past, thou didst transform a serpent into gold, and didst raise up a dead woman to question her. Yet, O thou that art right wondrous among the fathers, converser with teachers, entreat the Savior, that He save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone IV`,tone:4},praises_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises Both now rubric`}},praises_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The most pure Lady, beholding Christ dying, Who doth slay the deceiver, bitterly cried out to Him that had come forth from her womb, and marveling at His longsuffering, exclaimed: O my most beloved Child, forget not Thy handmaid! O Lover of mankind, delay not my consolation!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p8 Praises Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or this Stavrotheotokion`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`troparion_alternate_rubric`,`troparion_alternate`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from the Oktoechos, and 4 from ODE III of the canon of the holy hierarch.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`Having illumined thy mind with dispassion and adorned thyself with divine humility, thou didst receive the gifts of the Spirit to cast out evil spirits and to loose the infirmities of those who faithfully honor thee, O most sacred one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having slain the serpent, the author of evil, and trampled down the inclination towards avarice, O holy hierarch, taking pity on him who was in need, thou didst transform a serpent into a golden ornament by thy sacred prayers, O venerable father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst ascend the mountain of dispassion; thou didst enter the darkness of the vision of God, and didst receive the law of salvation on the tablets of thy heart, in that thou art a most sacred and faithful favorite of thy Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Heal thou the wounds of my soul, O Bride of God, and illumine my mind which hath been darkened by neglect, that I may chant: There is none blameless save thee, O immaculate one, and none pure but thee, O Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],troparion_alternate_rubric:{text:`Or this Troparion, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Or this Troparion rubric (Liturgy)`}},troparion_alternate:{text:`Thou wast shown forth as a champion of the First Council * and a wonderworker, O Spyridon, our God-bearing father. * Wherefore, thou didst speak to one dead in the grave, * and didst change a serpent into gold. * And, whilst chanting thy holy prayers, * thou didst have angels serving with thee, O most sacred one. * Glory to Him that hath given thee strength! * Glory to Him that hath crowned thee! ** Glory to Him that worketh healings for all through thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Or this Troparion (Liturgy)`},sourceLabel:`Or this Troparion, in Tone I`,tone:1},prokeimenon:{text:`My mouth shall speak wisdom, * and the medita-tion of my heart shall be of understanding.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone I`,label_inline:!0,tone:1},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Hear this, all ye nations; give ear, all ye that inhabit the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p9 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`THE EPISTLE TO THE HEBREWS`,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p10 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`(13:17-21)`,citation:{book:`Hebrews`,chapter:13,verses:`17-21`},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The mouth of the righteous shall meditate wisdom, and his tongue shall speak of judgment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p10 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone II`,label_inline:!0,tone:2},alleluia_verse:{text:`The law of his God is in his heart, and his steps shall not be tripped.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p10 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. LUKE`,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p10 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`(6:17-23)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:6,verses:`17-23`},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12.pdf`,locus:`p10 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}},{kind:`saint`,name:`our venerable father Herman, Wonderworker of Alaska`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF OUR VENERABLE FATHER HERMAN, WONDERWORKER OF ALASKA`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 12th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`vigil`,fekula_section:`2F`,oca_primary:!1,source_file:`12-12C.pdf`,note:`Second file of 12 December, a separate service (Bill, 15 Nov 2026, on the lettered files). THE DATE: the page is headed "THE 12th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER" and the file stands under 12 December; the OCA calendar keeps the Repose of Venerable Herman of Alaska on 13 DECEMBER (oca.org, checked 16 Nov 2026). Captured where it is printed; where the tool serves it is Q-0018. Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 2: the Menaion prints a LITTLE VESPERS for the saint, so Vigil, Fekula 2F. ODS vol. III has no 12-12 or 12-13 entry for him. Great Vespers with "Blessed is the man", 8 stichera all printed (3 in Tone III, 5 in Tone VI), the Dogmatic Theotokion, three lessons with NO reference printed (citations are identifications), a Litiya, the blessing of the Loaves, and "if a vigil is not served" a Theotokion after the troparion. Matins: a sessional hymn and Theotokion at each kathisma and after the Polyeleos; a Magnification and Selected Psalm verse; a Gospel; "Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia, including the Irmos" is appointed and NOT printed; the canon of the venerable one, with 8, is printed; Great Doxology. FAULTS IN PRINT: the last sticheron at Lord I have cried breaks off ("wherefore, teach us"); the Tone VI Glory is printed three times and the printing after Psalm 50 opens with its first two phrases in the other order. At Liturgy the rubric appoints 8 Beatitude troparia, 4 from Ode III and 4 from Ode VI; three (the first Twice), three and the Theotokion of Ode VI are printed.`,troparion:{text:`O venerable Herman, * ascetic of the northern wilderness * and gracious advocate for all the world, * teacher of the Orthodox Faith, * good instructor of piety, * adornment of Alaska and joy of all America: ** Entreat Christ God, that He save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p2 end of Little Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p7 blessing of the Loaves`,tone:4,repeat:2},{locus:`p8 God is the Lord`,tone:4,repeat:2},{locus:`p16 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`O beloved of the Mother of God, who received the tonsure at Valaam, * new zealot of the struggles of the desert-dwellers of old: * wielding prayer as a spear and shield, * thou didst show thyself to be terrible to demons and pagan darkness. * Wherefore, we cry out to thee: O venerable Herman, ** entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Kontakion of the venerable one`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p12 after Ode VI`,tone:8},{locus:`p17 AT LITURGY`,tone:8}],sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},ikos:{text:`Being of our race, and having fled to the Lord in thy youth, like unto Herman of Valaam in name and struggle, this Herman grew to the stature of the fathers of old, who brought forth fruits in patience. And the meek one was sent to the Aleut people, who had not yet been enlightened. Hard was his life among those simple people, but harder yet was the opposition of his compatriots to his goodly ad-monitions. Yet showing kindness to them all, the meekness of Herman instructed them. Glorifying thy memory for all these things, O venerable Herman, we cry out to thee: Entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},little_vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`lic_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone I:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`O joy of the Church of Christ, * having proclaimed the glory of God, * thou hast inherited glorious things in heaven. * Accept glory from us also on earth, * and entreat the King of glory, O venerable one, ** that He grant us a share in His glory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:1,repeat:2,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`O joy of the Church of Christ, * by thine evangelical life in the wilderness * thou didst dispel the darkness of idolatry, * uniting the heathen to the life of Christ. * O venerable Herman, ** make us also to share in the grace thereof.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`},{text:`We who are held fast in the gloom of life * have straightway received illumination for our minds * through thy heavenly visitation, * O venerable father Herman. * Wherefore, we have set our hope ** on thine intercession before God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Joy of the ranks of heaven ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`When the time of departure drew nigh for the venerable one, and the candles were lit and the Acts of the apostles were read by his bier, the holy Herman shone forth wondrously, saying: “Glory to Thee, O Lord!” And, mystically receiving from the Savior seven more days of life, he awaited the day which was foretold. Then, when the candles were again lit and the Acts were being read, he reposed in the sweet savor of his asceticism, having lived a most fruitful and venerable life, and he liveth eternally, ever entreating the Lord of glory on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},lic_closer:{text:`O Virgin Theotokos and Sovereign Lady, * as thou didst heal the venerable Herman, * ever heeding his supplications ** have mercy on us who hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers LIC Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone II:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`The Lord hath shown thee * to be the abode of the grace * of the divine Spirit. * Teach us, O father, ** those things which we ought to do.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:2,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The storms of the sea * were as naught unto thee * when Christ shone upon thee * like the sun from on high. ** Wherefore, we glorify thee, O venerable one.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`},{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord * for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O lover of the Faith, * defender of orphans, * glory of monks: * make steadfast those ** who offer thee their praises, O father.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p1 Little Vespers Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O house of Ephratha ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`Have the fleeting years or the bosom of the earth been able to conceal thy glory, which is in the heavens, O venerable Herman? Wherefore, glorifying thee now, we, the children of thy people, fall down before thee, having thee as a mediator before the Lord. Him do thou entreat, that He grant salvation to the suffering land of Russia, prosperity to this land, and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_closer:{text:`O Theotokos, thou art the true vine * that hast budded forth for us the Fruit of life. * Thee do we entreat: ** Pray thou, O Lady, with the holy apostles, that He have mercy upon our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p2 Little Vespers dismissal Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`}},great_vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`dogmatikon`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`litiya_rubric`,`litiya`,`litiya_glory`,`litiya_closer`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion_rubric`,`troparion`,`virgin_theotokos_rubric`,`no_vigil_rubric`,`troparion_closer`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 Great Vespers rubric`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 8 Stichera: 3 Stichera, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Leap up, ye waters of Valaam! Join chorus, ye islands of Alaska! Sing, ye people of a new land! Let heaven and earth rejoice; for the converser with the angels is glorified, and the Orthodox Faith is proclaimed to the ends of the world. Let us cry aloud to Christ God: Through the supplications of our father Herman, save Thou our souls, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:3},{text:`Come ye all, and in hymns let us proclaim the victory of honorable abstinence; for, having broken asunder the serpent, the author of evil, the meek Herman tasteth triumph in the choir of the angels. Wherefore, O brethren, let us praise him who doth adorn the company of fasters, and, joining chorus, let us cry out with splendor: Rejoice, O venerable Herman, thou angelic boast of monks!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O venerable Herman, ascetic of savage Alaska and dweller in the mansions of heaven, with what praises shall we honor thee, with what names shall we magnify thee? What is our glorification compared to the glory of heaven? Rejoice, O our compatriot, who sharest in heavenly glory! Fill thou with joy the hearts of us who fall down before thee in humility!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having now assembled, * let us glorify the wondrous one, * who, even while among mortals, * attained heavenly things, * who by his deeds and words * did carry the light of Christ * unto the ends of the world * for the unenlightened people * who were crushed beneath the darkness of idolatry. ** By his supplications may Christ save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`And 5 Stichera, in Tone VI`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`,tone:6},{text:`Rejoice, O Valaam, * thou dwelling-place of God, * for thou didst nurture * the wondrous ascetic of Christ, * who, like a lamp upon a lampstand, * shone forth among the islands of Alaska, * a new and unknown land, * and brought an unbelieving people to the Orthodox Faith. * With them let us glorify God, ** Who is wondrous in His saints!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`},{text:`Having but one desire, * to bring the unbelieving people * to the one God, * thou didst become all things to all people: * teaching them the sacred Scriptures * and how to live in accordance therewith; * training them in handicrafts; * acting as intercessor for them before the authorities, * teaching them in every way, * as though they were children, * that thou mightest lead the people to God. ** Forsake us not also, who hymn thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p3 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`},{text:`Following the words of the apostle, * to give place to the wrath of God, * thou didst withdraw to Spruce Island, * turning away from the hardheartedness * of the lovers of this world; * and, finding there a new Valaam, * preferring life there * with the birds and wild beasts, * and conversing with God and the angels, * illumined by visions from on high, * thou now dwellest in the highest. ** Pray thou on behalf of our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC 7`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`},{text:`What is above all, * if not the Lord, our Creator? * The Adorner of majesty, * the Bestower of life, * the Sustainer and Nurturer of all things. * Ought we not to love Him * as the One most worthy of love, * and place our own happiness in Him?” * Thus didst thou teach, O venerable one; ** wherefore, teach us`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC 8`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Having set aside ...`,provenance_note:`The sticheron breaks off in print: it ends "wherefore, teach us", with no close (p4; confirmed by a second extraction). Stored as printed.`}],lic_glory:{text:`Have the fleeting years or the bosom of the earth been able to conceal thy glory, which is in the heavens, O venerable Herman? Wherefore, glorifying thee now, we, the children of thy people, fall down before thee, having thee as a mediator before the Lord. Him do thou entreat, that He grant salvation to the suffering land of Russia, prosperity to this land, and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},dogmatikon:{text:`Who doth not call thee blessed, O most holy Virgin? * Who will not hymn thy most pure birthgiving? * For the only-begotten Son Who hath shone forth timelessly from the Father, * came forth, ineffably incarnate, from thee, O pure one; * By nature He is God, by nature for our sakes, He hath become a man * not divided into two Hypostases, * but known in two natures without commingling. * Him do thou beseech, O pure and most blessed one, ** that our souls find mercy!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 LIC Both now, Dogmatic Theotokion`},type:`dogmatic_theotokion`,tone:6,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Dogmatic Theotokion, in the same tone`},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 Entrance`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p4 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:3,verses:`1-9`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "The souls of the righteous are in the hand of God", closes "and He hath care for His elect": Wisdom 3:1-9. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:5,verses:`5:15-6:3`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "The righteous live for evermore", closes "sovereignty from the Most High": Wisdom 5:15-6:3. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p5 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:4,verses:`7-15`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "Though the righteous be prevented with death", closes "unto His chosen": Wisdom 4:7-15, as 12-06 Lesson 3. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`}],litiya_rubric:{text:`At Litiya, the Sticheron of the temple, and this of the venerable one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya rubric`}},litiya:[{text:`O ascetic of New Valaam, thy brethren were dear to thee, and with them thou didst live in the Valaam of thy homeland. Yet thou didst desire a hundred times more thine incorporeal friends, who caught thy soul up to the vision of God, and with whom thou now makest thine abode. Rejoice, O father, for us who glorify thy memory, invisibly guiding us to goodly repentance! O Herman, thou favorite of God, scion of the Russian land, offspring of the waters of Ladoga, and blessing of the Church for Alaska and the Aleutian Islands, goodly hope of America, gracious witness to Orthodoxy: Ask for us great mercy and the peace of God which passeth all understanding.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p5 Litiya 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8}],litiya_glory:{text:`When the time of departure drew nigh for the venerable one, and the candles were lit and the Acts of the apostles were read by his bier, the holy Herman shone forth wondrously, saying: “Glory to Thee, O Lord!” And, mystically receiving from the Savior seven more days of life, he awaited the day which was foretold. Then, when the candles were again lit and the Acts were being read, he reposed in the sweet savor of his asceticism, having lived a most fruitful and venerable life, and he liveth eternally, ever entreating the Lord of glory on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},litiya_closer:{text:`O Virgin Theotokos and Sovereign Lady, * as thou didst heal the venerable Herman, * ever heeding his supplications ** have mercy on us who hymn thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Litiya Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`Rejoice, O Life-bearing Cross, * invincible victory of piety; * for through thee hath the gate of paradise been opened, * enlightenment been given to new lands, * the darkness of idolatry been abolished, * the dominion of death been trampled down, * and mortals are borne up to the heavens! * Rejoice. O ye faithful, and be glad, * for the glory of the Life-bearing Cross, * the hope of the new martyrs * and of the vener-able Herman, * is proclaimed in a new land, * imparting to all the faithful ** great and rich mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Rejoice, O venerable guide * of the newly-chosen flock of Christ, * who didst enlighten the hearts of the unbelieving * with the grace of the word of God, * didst teach them with the spirit of meekness * and the piety of humility, * and didst root within them the truth of the Faith * by brotherly love and charity. * O wondrous elder Herman, * herald of the light of Christ * and dispeller of the darkness of the demons, * illumine also our hearts. * driving away the darkness of unbelief, ** that we may find great mercy with the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord * for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Rejoice. O defender of the newly-enlightened people, * most simple and lowly, * before the mighty of this world: * for by thy life's blood thou didst become * a mediator for them, * an instructor and most lowly servant of their race; * and likewise, thou wast a friend to those afflicted with an incurable disease, * listening to their cries and groaning day and night; * and, comforting them, thou didst lead them to the healing of heaven, * O fearless shepherd of thy flock, even though thou didst decline priestly ordination. * Rejoice, O thou who didst take pity on the wild beasts, * as didst the venerable seraphim! ** Rejoice, thou who with the flame of faith didst subdue the conflagration of material fire!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p6 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`O venerable father, the sound of thy corrections hath gone forth into all the earth; wherefore, thou hast found the reward of thy labors in the heavens having routed the hordes of the demons, and attained unto the ranks of the angels, whose life thou didst blamelessly emulate. As thou hast boldness before Christ God, ask thou peace for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},aposticha_closer:{text:`Christ the Lord, my Creator and Redeemer, * Who came forth from thy womb, O most pure one, * and clothed Himself in my nature, * hath freed Adam from the primal curse. * Wherefore, like the angel * we unceasingly cry out to thee, * O most pure one, * who art truly the Mother of God and Virgin: * Rejoice!, O Lady, ** the intercession, protection and salvation of our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:6,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in the same tone`},troparion_rubric:{text:`At the blessing of the loaves, the Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 Blessing of the Loaves rubric`}},virgin_theotokos_rubric:{text:`And “Virgin Theotokos, rejoice! ...” (Once).`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 Virgin Theotokos rejoice rubric`}},no_vigil_rubric:{text:`But if a vigil is not served, then after the Troparion:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 If a vigil is not served`}},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p7 Dismissal Theotokion (no vigil)`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}},matins:{order:`god_is_lord_rubric.troparion.troparion_closer.sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric`.split(`.`),god_is_lord_rubric:{text:`On “God is the Lord ...,” the Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord rubric`}},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 God is the Lord Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:4,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},sessional_1:[{text:`Heeding the call of the Lord, and reckoning all the beauties of this world as but dung, thou didst attain unto the most beautiful wilderness in a remote and savage land, where, manfully putting to flight hordes of the demons, thou didst converse with the angels, thy companions. Wherefore, we praise thee as a wondrous adornment of the wilderness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Awed by the beauty of thy virginity ...`,tone:3},{text:`O Lady, as the only hope of Christians and their intercessor before God, with the venerable Herman entreat thy Son on behalf of thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3}],sessional_2:[{text:`Teaching illiterate peoples and converting the unbelieving, thou didst plant the true Faith among them, laboring in every way and edifying them with thy piety. Wherefore, O venerable Herman, teach us also to cleave unto the Truth and to do works of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Thy tomb, O Savior ...`,tone:1},{text:`Having thee as our sure hope and protection, O most pure Mother, trusting in thee we fear not the assault of the enemy, for thou savest our souls from all evils.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone I`,tone:1}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We bless thee, O our venerable father Herman, and we honor thy holy memory, O instructor of monks and converser with the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verse:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Selected Psalm verse rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`With patience I waited patiently for the Lord, and He was attentive unto me, and He hearkened unto my supplication.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God! (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p8 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`In a fragile ship didst thou traverse the stormy abyss of the sea, O venerable one, until thou didst reach a far-away land. There Spruce Island became for thee a spiritual vessel, upon which thou didst reach the heavenly harbor through the preaching of the Gospel and thy works of piety, ever rejoicing in the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Awed by the beauty of thy virginity ...`,tone:3},{text:`O Theotokos our Lady, who hast revealed to us the pre-eternal Word in the flesh: to thee do we flee as to our protection and help. Shield us with the omophorion of thy prayers from all the assaults of the enemy, that undistracted we may worship thy Son.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO MATTHEW,`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§43 (MT. 11: 27-30)`,citation:{book:`Matthew`,chapter:11,verses:`27-30`,pericope_number:43},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`Hath the bosom of the earth or the fleeting years been able to conceal thy glory, which is in the heavens, O venerable Herman? Wherefore, glorifying thee now, we, the children of thy people, fall down before thee, having thee as a mediator before the Lord. Him do thou entreat, that He grant salvation to the suffering land of Russia, prosperity to this land, and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone VI`,tone:6},canon_rubric:{text:`Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia, including the Irmos; and that of the venerable one, with 8 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “Let us love God more than all, and Herman let us hymn”, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraklisis), with 6 Troparia, including the Irmos; and that of the venerable one, with 8 Troparia, the acrostic whereof is: “Let us love God more than all, and Herman let us hymn”, in Tone III:`,acrostic:`Let us love God more than all, and Herman let us hymn`,tone:3,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`He who of old gathered the waters * into one by His divine decree, * divided the sea for the people of Israel. * For He is our God and supremely glorious, * to Him alone let us sing, for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O most merciful Savior, help me to hymn Herman, Thy favorite, illumining the eyes of my darkened soul, that he who is glorious among Thy saints may be glorified to the ends of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring from thy youth to seek out the heavenly homeland and to labor for God alone, O venerable Herman, thou didst entrust thyself to the protection of heaven, having Sergius and Herman of Valaam as thy constant helpers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having the commandments of the Lord continually in thy heart, thou didst never give thy body over to the ways of slothfulness, every laboring, and enlightening thy soul with divine effulgence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Loving God above all else, thou didst commit thy whole life to Him, cherishing most of all thy conversation with the choirs on high. Yet thou didst not neglect love for thy brethren, O venerable one, praying and crying out with them: O Jesus most sweet, save us sinners!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst cure the young Herman of a deadly ailment, O Theotokos, hearkening to his ardent entreaty; wherefore, disdain us not, who fall down before thee and call upon him to supplicate thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`O Most High, Ruler of all, * who out of nothing hath established all things, * fashioned by Thy Word, * perfected by the Spirit, * confirm me in Thy love.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The divinely wise Nazarius, having come to Valaam from Sarov, planted there love for interior spiritual activity; wherefore, partaking of this grace, O venerable one, with spiritual enlightenment thou didst prepare thy soul for the struggle of evangelism.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As fruitful branches of the vine of Christ, O Sergius and Herman of Valaam, who nourished the new Herman with the grapes of the virtues, fill ye our hearts with the wine of divine gladness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With prayer and activity thou didst prepare thy soul for a new task; wherefore, thou didst reach a far-away country with thy brother evangelists, leading the inhabitants of Alaska to Jesus most sweet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O good Mother of the good King, who ever pourest forth thy benefactions upon thy servants: guide us to every good deed, protecting us from all the actions of the evil ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Thou hast shown us steadfast love, O Lord, * for Thou gavest Thine only-begotten Son over to death for our sake. * Wherefore with thanksgiving we cry unto Thee, * ‘Glory to Thy power, O Lord!’`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou hast provided us an example of a good shepherd and a solicitous father, O venerable one, for thou wast the fervent help and healing of the sick and infirm, and protection and teaching of the orphaned. Wherefore, deprive us not, as orphans, of the protection of thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O venerable Herman, the people marveled at how thou wast able to live alone in the forest. “I am not alone,” thou didst say; “for God, Who is everywhere present, is with me, as are His angels. How then can I be despondent, when I have such companions?” And now, O thou who dwellest with the inhabitants of heaven, depart not from us who are on earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O guardian of Alaska, who didst call thyself the servant and teacher of new peoples, even after thy death thou didst extend thy care to them. And lo! with thy words we now cry out to thee: Be thou for us a father and protector; wipe away the tears of defenseless orphans; cool the hearts of those who are melting under the heat of grief; and grant that they may come to know the consolation of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, let us hymn the most pure Virgin, who by her humility hath corrected the deception of Eve and hath revealed to us the new Adam, that, receiving a new adoption, we may become heirs to life everlasting.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`I rise at dawn unto Thee, * the Creator of all, * surpassing all worldly understanding; * for Thy commandments are light, * wherein do Thou guide me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thou wast like unto Adam the first-formed when thou didst purify thy soul by many sorrows, vigils and prayers, and arrayed it in man's primal beauty. And the wild beasts submitted themselves to thee, sensing in thee the odor of paradise and the kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Restraining the passions of the senses with the reins of abstinence and with constant prayer, thou didst reach the summit of dispassion; wherefore, we fall down before thee, as before O gracious physician, crying aloud: Cure us of the passions and move us to do good works!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring to mystically labor for God alone, thou didst make thine abode in a cave, striving to bury the passions of the flesh, that thou mightest resurrect thy soul, illumined with the effulgence of heaven, receiving a foretaste of the eternal Pascha.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst enter the noetic paradise of the virtues, where thou didst produce multifarious flowers of good works, whereby thou dost emit sweet fragrance in the world even to this day, O father Herman.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`The choir of holy angels hymn thy majesty, O all-immaculate one, and I, a sinner, entreat thee: Drive far from me the ugly fantasies of the demons, preserving my heart in tranquility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The uttermost depths of sin have surrounded me, * and my spirit perisheth, * but do Thou, O Master, stretch forth Thy lofty arm * and like Peter save me, * O my Helmsman.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`To proclaim the glad tidings of the Gospel thou didst travel to the ends of the world, to a new place, Spruce Island, which thou didst call New Valaam, showing thy love for the Valaam of thy homeland; and therein thou didst acquire new brethren, the newly-enlightened people, through the discourse of thy preaching and thy works of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord glorified thy brethren, O venerable one, for their works were truly like unto the struggles of the apostles: Juvenal chanteth in the choir of the martyrs, Joasaph and Innocent, and those with them, sing in the ranks of hierarchs, and together we chant unto God: Glory to Thee Who hast shown us the light!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy works and those of thy fellow evangelists have received their sanctification and crowning through the confession and martyr's blood of Peter the Aleut, at whose mighty faith and endurance thou didst marvel. Wherefore, following thee, we cry aloud: O holy new-martyr Peter, pray to God for us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy life thou didst show forth the justification of the true Faith, O venerable one; wherefore, the teaching of the discourse which thou didst make hath been shown forth in deed, drawing thirsting hearts to correction when thou didst cry aloud: Glory to the holy judgments of our merciful God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, ye people, that we may see how the stormy waters which were about to engulf the island submitted to the meek Herman. Before the icon of the Mother of God they humble themselves and turn back to the ocean's depths. And let us, who are tempest tossed by the waves of life, cry out with the chosen of the Mother of God: O most holy Theotokos, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`As of old Thou didst bedew * the three pious children in the Chaldean flames, * so also with the radiant fire of Thy divinity * illumine us who cry to Thee, * ‘Blessed art Thou, the God of our fathers!’`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The order of nature is altered when the Spirit of God worketh. And having illumined the eyes of thy soul with His effulgence, O venerable one, thou didst see things afar off as though they were near at hand, and things yet to come as though they were of the present, declaring the judgments of God for the edification and correction of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Zealous concerning celestial things, thou didst lay up for thyself treasure in heaven; wherefore, those who sought earthly treasures in thy cell found nothing. Teach us now, O unmercenary father, to lay up heavenly treasures, and to set our heart on Him Who alone is beyond price.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, and the Lord delivered thee from them all, filling thy heart with heavenly joy, which thou dost now enjoy in the never-waning day of the kingdom of Christ. Pray for us, O venerable one, that the Lord may transform our tribulations into joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come ye all, and let us honor the joy of the angels, the instructor of the monastic ranks, and the protectress of the Christian race, and let us pay homage to her as the Queen of heaven, the constant intercessor for mortals before God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`United together in the unbearable fire, * yet not harmed by the flame, * the children, champions of godliness, sang a divine hymn: * O all ye works of the Lord, * bless ye the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Neither thy weakness, thine advanced age, nor the blindness of thine eyes; was able to hinder thy mediation for the people before those in authority, whom thou didst beseech to deal mercifully with them, rather than make them victims, that they themselves might find mercy with the Lord. And now, as thou art in heaven, deprive us not also of thy mediation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy forest cell rang with angelic hymnody when thou didst chant alone, so that the people marveled exceedingly. And an angel likewise served thee, sanctifying the waters with the blessing of the Jordan, when thou didst cry: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p13-p14 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Arrayed in the robe of salvation and the vesture of gladness which was woven of thy manifold labors and tribulations, thou didst enter into the bridal-chamber of Christ the King, where, with the choirs of the angels and the apostles, thou dost partake eternally of the banquet of joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Our sins consume the good intentions of our soul with the likeness of unbearable fire; wherefore, we fall down before thee, as to the Sovereign Lady of heaven and earth, crying: Bedew thou our hearts, that every good work may spring forth!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`New is the wonder and befitting of God: * for the Lord clearly passes through the closed gate of the Virgin: * naked at His going in and God bearing flesh at His coming out, * while the gate remaineth closed. * As ineffably the Theotokos and Mother of our God we magnify her.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Glory to Thee, O God, Who hast revealed to us Thy wondrous favorite, by whose prayers do Thou preserve us from every assault of the enemy and from the soul-destroying passions; and guide us to every good thing, that, having escaped everlasting torment, we may attain unto Thy kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The evening of thy life arrived, O venerable one and the book of thine apostolic works was brought to an end in the never-waning effulgence of thy countenance, shining forth thy glory in the mansions of heaven, do thou also help us attain thereto by thy holy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A pillar of fire was seen, marking the departure of the venerable one from earth to heaven, so that the people were greatly astonished. Wherefore, we cry out to him: Be thou ever for us a pillar of tire, lighting and showing us the path to the heavens.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`To Thy true disciple, O Lord, have we offered praises with our unworthy mouths, glorifying Thee Who art wondrous in Thy saints; by their prayerful intercession preserve this land and its cities from misfortunes and plague, granting us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Mary, thou dwelling-place of God and instructor of purity, by thine aid show me forth as pure, who have become the abode of sinful defilements and impurity, and have fallen into the snares of the unclean spirits; and make me again a habitation of God, that I may magnify thee with piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`The day of thy commemoration hath arrived, O all-praised father Herman, gladdening thy chosen flock. Illumine us with the splendors of thy miracles, which issue forth from thy precious relics, quench thou the flame of our passions, and bedew the minds of the faithful who ever glorify thee with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Awed by the beauty of thy virginity ...`,tone:3},{text:`Rejoice, O Virgin who art full of grace, for thou revealest to us thy new chosen one, who sprang forth in the northern wilderness and hath made the newly-enlightened region fragrant with heavenly gifts! Wherefore, with gifts of thanksgiving we honor thee, the Sovereign Lady of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone III`,tone:3}],exapostilarion:{text:`O Lord, Bestower of life, by the supplications of our beacon of piety, the venerable Herman, shine forth Thy never-waning light upon this land and upon us who with faith serve Thee and piously celebrate his luminous memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p14 Exapostilarion`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion of the venerable one`,spec_mel:`Hearken, ye women ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`O Bride of God, mystic lamp, who by the activity of the divine Spirit hast revealed the pre-eternal Light to the world: upon us who are in the darkness of ignorance do thou shine forth the light of the truth, and save all who piously magnify thee as the Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone VIII:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`Herman, the meek and humble, * as a lover of the glory of God * is sent forth to announce the glad tidings of Christ: * and he preached the Gospel with his mouth * and confirmed It with piety. * Wherefore, he hath inherited glorious things in heaven. * Let us then glorify him also on earth. * By his supplications, O Christ God, ** save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:8,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O herald of the words of the Lord * and pious doer of them, * as one mighty in the grace of the Holy Spirit * thou didst bear the weakness of the infirm * caring for the infants as a teacher * and for the children as a father, * Instructing them in every way by thy deeds and words. * Wherefore, visit us also, ** healing our infirmities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O venerable Herman, thou didst say * “From this day and from this hour * let us love God above all, * and let us do His holy will, * that we may inherit good things!” * O thou wondrous teacher * and confirmation of Orthodoxy, * preaching of the glory of God, ** and the teaching of us sinners!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`},{text:`O most glorious wonder! * A new land hath been sanctified! * For the wonder-worker Herman appeareth today, * borne up to the heights. * Wondrous is God in His saints! * God is with us! Understand, O ye nations! * Be ye instructed by Herman in Orthodoxy! * By his supplications, O Christ God, ** save Thou our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 4`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O most glorious wonder ...`}],praises_glory:{text:`Thou didst wondrously ascend the ladder of the virtues, O venerable one; for, receiving prayer, fervor of heart and tears, thou didst purify thy mind of vainglorious thoughts and thy heart of multifarious sensations, and didst attain unto the dispassion of paradise, illumined by visions of the mysteries on high, which lead us up to the heavens, that we may know God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VIII`,tone:8},praises_closer:{text:`O Sovereign lady, * accept the supplications of thy servants, ** and deliver us from all want and grief.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p15 Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. Dismissal. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakion`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III and 4 from ODE VI, of the canon of the venerable one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`The divinely wise Nazarius, having come to Valaam from Sarov, planted there love for interior spiritual activity; wherefore, partaking of this grace, O venerable one, with spiritual enlightenment thou didst prepare thy soul for the struggle of evangelism.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`As fruitful branches of the vine of Christ, O Sergius and Herman of Valaam, who nourished the new Herman with the grapes of the virtues, fill ye our hearts with the wine of divine gladness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With prayer and activity thou didst prepare thy soul for a new task; wherefore, thou didst reach a far-away country with thy brother evangelists, leading the inhabitants of Alaska to Jesus most sweet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`To proclaim the glad tidings of the Gospel thou didst travel to the ends of the world, to a new place, Spruce Island, which thou didst call New Valaam, showing thy love for the Valaam of thy homeland; and therein thou didst acquire new brethren, the newly-enlightened people, through the discourse of thy preaching and thy works of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord glorified thy brethren, O venerable one, for their works were truly like unto the struggles of the apostles: Juvenal chanteth in the choir of the martyrs, Joasaph and Innocent, and those with them, sing in the ranks of hierarchs, and together we chant unto God: Glory to Thee Who hast shown us the light!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy works and those of thy fellow evangelists have received their sanctification and crowning through the confession and martyr's blood of Peter the Aleut, at whose mighty faith and endurance thou didst marvel. Wherefore, following thee, we cry aloud: O holy new-martyr Peter, pray to God for us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, ye people, that we may see how the stormy waters which were about to engulf the island submitted to the meek Herman. Before the icon of the Mother of God they humble themselves and turn back to the ocean's depths. And let us, who are tempest tossed by the waves of life, cry out with the chosen of the Mother of God: O most holy Theotokos, save us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],prokeimenon:{text:`Precious in the sight of the Lord * is the death of His saints.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone VII`,label_inline:!0,tone:7},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`What shall I render unto the Lord for all that He hath rendered unto me?`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE GALATIANS,`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§213 (5: 22-6: 2)`,citation:{book:`Galatians`,chapter:5,verses:`5:22-6:2`,pericope_number:213},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`Blessed is the man that feareth the Lord; in His commandments shall he greatly delight.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone VI`,label_inline:!0,tone:6},alleluia_verse:{text:`His seed shall be mighty upon the earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE:`,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§ 24 (LK. 6: 17-23)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:6,verses:`17-23`,pericope_number:24},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be; he shall not be afraid of evil tidings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-12C.pdf`,locus:`p17 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-13":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Martyrs Eustratius, Auxentius, Eugene, Mardarius and Orestes, and the holy Martyr Lucia`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYRS EUSTRATIUS, AUXENTIUS, EUGENE, MARDARIUS & ORESTES COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYR LUCIA`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 13th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`polyeleos`,fekula_section:`2E`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-13.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: no Little Vespers; "Blessed is the man", three lessons, a Polyeleos with a Magnification and a Gospel, a Great Doxology: Polyeleos, Fekula 2E. ODS vol. III has no fixed 12-13 entry (its 11 to 17 December entries are the movable Sunday of the Forefathers, Q-0019; in 2026 that Sunday IS 13 December). THE OCA KEEPS ST. HERMAN OF ALASKA ON THIS DAY; this Menaion prints him under 12 December (12-12C, Q-0018). The title also names the holy Martyr Lucia: NO hymn of hers is printed apart; three theotokia of Canon I name her. Six stichera of the martyrs in two sets of three, both Tone IV; the Dogmatic Theotokion; three lessons with NO reference printed (citations are identifications); no Litiya and no blessing of the Loaves. Matins: no God is the Lord rubric; a sessional hymn (Twice) and Theotokion at each kathisma and after the Polyeleos; "Canon of the supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraclysis), with 6 Troparia" appointed and NOT printed; two canons of the martyrs "with a total of 8", Canon I by John the Monk in Tone IV, Canon II in Tone VI with no composer named; the katavasia "Christ is born" named after Ode I. TWO kontakia: Tone II after Ode III, Tone III with the ikos after Ode VI; both are printed at Liturgy, headed "ODE III" and "ODE VI". Four stichera on the Praises by Germanus, John the Monk and Cassia the nun. The ODE III heading is printed doubled. At Liturgy the rubric appoints 8 Beatitude troparia; three (the first Twice), three and a Theotokion are printed.`,troparion:{text:`In their sufferings, Thy martyrs O Lord, * received imperishable crowns from Thee, our God; * for, possessed of Thy might, * they set at naught the tyrants and crushed the feeble audacity of the demons. ** By their supplications save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p4 Troparion of the holy martyrs`},verified_sites:[{locus:`p4 end of Vespers`,tone:4},{locus:`p16 AT LITURGY`,tone:4}],sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,tone:4},kontakion:{text:`Eloquently speaking of divine things before the iniquitous, O all-wondrous one, * thou didst endure beatings with a most courageous heart, * shining forth with godly signs, * and extinguishing the towering flame of delusion. ** Wherefore, we honor thee, O all-blessed Eustratius, martyr of Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Kontakion of the holy martyrs (after Ode VI)`},sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone III`,spec_mel:`Today the Virgin ...`,tone:3},ikos:{text:`Today the Church doth mystically celebrate a sacred feast, radiantly proclaiming thy valor, pangs and labors, thy divine struggles surpassing nature, and the wounds which covered thy body, whereby thou didst cast down the greatly crafty one, O thou great glory and boast of spiritual athletes, pillar of courage, beacon for all who piously honor thee, treasury of healings, enricher of the poor, first champion of honorable martyrs, all-blessed Eustratius, martyr of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ikos`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0},vespers:{order:[`rubric`,`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_glory`,`dogmatikon`,`entrance_rubric`,`readings`,`aposticha_rubric`,`aposticha`,`aposticha_glory`,`aposticha_closer`,`troparion`,`troparion_closer`],rubric:{text:`After the Introductory Psalm, we chant “Blessed is the Man ...,” the first antiphon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 Blessed is the man`}},lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera of the holy martyrs, 3 in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Like the sun, in splendor, O Lord, * shineth forth the memory * of Thy passion-bearer Eustratius, * who eclipsed polytheism with his invincible discourses, * rendering it, through his faith, as useless as a dark shadow, * and who inspired four others * to be his companions and fellow sufferers. * For their sake grant us cleansing, ** in that Thou lovest mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`Eustratius compelled the stones * to acknowledge the noetic mastery * of him who in the flesh * prevailed upon them to experience his power, * which suddenly caused the wounds inflicted by dreadful, tortures to disappear, * and who destroyed delusion, * that he might theologize concerning Thee with his mouth, * O Almighty Jesus, ** Thou, Savior of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`By their discourses and sufferings, * and the divers ways * in which they were deprived of life, * the holy ones showed perfect and constant love * for Thee, O Lord: * the glorious Orestes and Mardarius, * who struggled together with the wise Eustratius, * Auxentius and Eugene. ** By their supplications, save Thou our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`Serving well the King of hosts as a warrior, * thou didst voluntarily give thyself over * to torture and a violent death, * O blessed Eustratius, * bringing with thee a choir of martyrs. * And with them thou didst suffer * and hast received crowns of victory. * With them make supplication ** on our behalf, O all-glorious one.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`And 3 Stichera, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`,tone:4},{text:`The divine wise Eustratius, * the valiant Auxentius, * the glorious Eugene and Mardarius, * who, with the brave Orestes, * vanquished the enemy * and shone forth brightly like stars of great radiance, * have illumined the hearts of the faithful * and dispelled the darkness of delusion ** by the effulgence of the Spirit.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`},{text:`Unremittingly beaten, * consumed by fire, * thy feet pierced with the nails of iron sandals, O all-wise one, * in which thou wast forced to walk the roads, * imprisoned in a dungeon, * and baked in an oven like a pure sacrifice, * thou didst offer thyself to Him Who was sacrificed for thy sake, * as an immolation of sweet savor for the banquet on high, ** O martyr Eustratius.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`As one valiant among the martyrs ...`}],lic_glory:{text:`Come, ye who love the martyrs, and in hymns let us honor the spiritual athletes of Christ: Eustratius, the invincible martyr, Auxentius and Eugene, Mardarius and Orestes, the five-membered choir of martyrs who fought the good fight against the invisible foe and have been crowned with wreaths of victory. For they pray to Christ for those who celebrate their memory with faith and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone VI`,tone:6},dogmatikon:{text:`Who doth not call thee blessed, O most holy Virgin? * Who will not hymn thy most pure birthgiving? * For the only-begotten Son Who hath shone forth timelessly from the Father, * came forth, ineffably incarnate, from thee, O pure one; * By nature He is God, by nature for our sakes, He hath become a man * not divided into two Hypostases, * but known in two natures without commingling. * Him do thou beseech, O pure and most blessed one, ** that our souls find mercy!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Both now, Dogmatic Theotokion`},type:`dogmatic_theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Dogmatic Theotokion, in Tone VI`,tone:6},entrance_rubric:{text:`Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p2 Entrance. Prokeimenon of the day. Three Lessons`}},readings:[{heading:`A READING FROM THE PROPHESY OF ISAIAH`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p2 Lesson 1`},citation:{book:`Isaiah`,chapter:43,verses:`9-14`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "Thus saith the Lord: Let all the nations be gathered together", closes "the Holy One of Israel": Isaiah 43:9-14, the first lesson of martyrs. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p2 Lesson 2`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:3,verses:`1-9`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "The souls of the righteous are in the hand of God", closes "and He hath care for His elect": Wisdom 3:1-9. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`},{heading:`A READING FROM THE WISDOM OF SOLOMON`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Lesson 3`},citation:{book:`Wisdom of Solomon`,chapter:5,verses:`5:15-6:3`},citation_basis:`identified`,provenance_note:`No reference printed. Opens "The righteous live for evermore", closes "sovereignty from the Most High": Wisdom 5:15-6:3. Identified by first and last words; confirm against the page.`}],aposticha_rubric:{text:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha rubric`}},aposticha:[{text:`A radiant pillar of light, emitting the effulgence of wisdom, O wise and glorious spiritual athlete, thou wast raised up to the heights of endurance, and wast guided to the light of understanding, illumining with thy divine splendors and wise discourses us who are given wings by thy love, O blessed Eustratius. Wherefore, honoring thy memory with praises, we lovingly pray, that by thy supplications we may receive God's love for mankind, and that He may grant the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha 1`},label:`plain`,tone:5,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`The righteous cried, * and the Lord heard them.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha verse 1`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`The cup of thy wisdom filled to overflowing with goodness and true sweetness, poured forth the wine of piety in thine exceedingly sweet and abundant discourses, O wise one; and delighted thereby, we are in truth mystically carried up to the calm and sweet divine knowledge of the Master, O Eustratius. Wherefore, honoring thy sufferings in praises with faith and love, we ask, that through thy supplications we may receive God's love for mankind, and that He may grant the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`},{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, * and the Lord shall deliver them out of them all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha verse 2`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},{text:`Let us honor with praises the victorious, radiant and splendid five-membered company of the martyrs, which truly had Eustratius as its brilliant commander, who zealously denounced the sacrifices of the heathen, and made the God-proclaiming Christians steadfast by his discourse. Wherefore, let us praise him who hath filled the cup of wisdom and brought us spiritual gladness, ever entreating Christ, Who granteth the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p3 Aposticha 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice ...`}],aposticha_glory:{text:`Undaunted by the savagery of the torturers, and openly preaching the Christian Faith all the more, ye endured many lacerations and torments, O Eustratius and Auxentius, Eugene Orestes, and glorious Mardarius. Wherefore, entreat ye God the King on behalf of us who celebrate your memory with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha Glory`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., in Tone V`,tone:5},aposticha_closer:{text:`We, the faithful bless thee, O Virgin Theotokos, and we glorify thee as is meet, for thou art the impregnable city, the impassable rampart, the steadfast intercessor and refuge of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p4 Aposticha Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone V`,tone:5},troparion_closer:{text:`The mystery hidden from all ages * and unknown to the ranks of angels, * hath been revealed to those on earth through thee, O Theotokos: * God incarnate in an uncommingled union, * Who willingly accepted the Cross for our sake, * and through it hath raised up the first-formed man, ** and saved our souls from death.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p4 Dismissal Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}},matins:{order:`sessional_1.sessional_2.megalynarion_rubric.megalynarion.megalynarion_verse_rubric.megalynarion_verse.megalynarion_closing_rubric.sessional_polyeleos.anabathmoi_rubric.prokeimenon.prokeimenon_verse.gospel_rubric.gospel.psalm50_sticheron.canon_rubric.canons.kontakia_ode3.sessional_ode3.kontakion.ikos.exapostilarion.exapostilarion_closer.praises_rubric.praises.praises_glory.praises_closer.great_doxology_rubric`.split(`.`),sessional_1:[{text:`Manfully arrayed in the breastplate of faith, and piously armed with divine wisdom, O glorious Eustratius, thou didst vanquish all the hordes of the devil, and denounced the feeble audacity of the ungodly. As thou hast boldness before God, pray that we be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Sessional 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Go thou quickly before ...`,tone:4},{text:`Darkened in mind by many transgressions, I, the prodigal, cry out to thy mighty aid, O Theotokos: Enlighten the eyes of my soul, shine upon me a radiant beam of repentance, and clothe me in the armor of light, O pure Virgin Birthgiver of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Sessional 1 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],sessional_2:[{text:`With the sword of thy discourses thou didst wound the tyrant, as a commander of the Christ-bearing people, O divinely wise Eustratius. Thou didst shine forth, upon the world with rays of miracles, and a crown was fashioned for thee from on high. Wherefore, we glorify Christ on the day of thy commemoration.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Sessional 2`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`We hymn thee, O Bride of God, Mother of Christ God, glorifying thine unap-proachable Offspring, by Whom we have been delivered from the deceit of the devil and from all misfortune, O Sovereign Lady Theotokos; and we faithfully cry out: Have mercy on thy flock, O thou who alone art all-hymned!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Sessional 2 Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],megalynarion_rubric:{text:`Polyeleos, and this magnification:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 magnification rubric`}},megalynarion:{text:`We magnify you, O holy passion-bearers and martyrs, and we reverence your noble sufferings, which ye endured for Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Magnification`},label_inline:!0},megalynarion_verse_rubric:{text:`Selected Psalm verses:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Selected Psalm verses rubric`}},megalynarion_verse:{text:`Our God is refuge and strength, a helper in afflictions which mightily befall us:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Selected Psalm verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`A`,label_inline:!0},megalynarion_closing_rubric:{text:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Alleluia ..., Glory to Thee, O God. (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 after the selected verses`}},sessional_polyeleos:[{text:`Made steadfast by thy faith in the Trinity, and armed with the sling of truth, thou didst bring down the alien audacity of falsehood, and take up the sword of discourse, therewith cutting down the lying opposition of the enemy. Wherefore, having set falsehood at naught by thy victories, thou didst die in the body, yet live in spirit, O passion-bearer Eustratius. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love celebrate thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p5 Polyeleos sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`After the Polyeleos, the Sessional Hymn, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`From the snares of enemies visible and invisible, * we have been overcome by the storms of our uncountable sins, * and fleeing unto the safe harbor of thy goodness O pure one, * we have thee as our rampart and sure protection. * Wherefore we thy servants beseech thee * to ceaselessly make fervent supplication, O most pure one, * unto Him who seedlessly became incarnate from thee, * that those who worthily hymn thee ** may be granted the remission of their sins.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Polyeleos sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}],anabathmoi_rubric:{text:`Song of Ascents, the first antiphon of Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Song of Ascents rubric`}},prokeimenon:{text:`The righteous cried, * and the Lord heard them.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, and the Lord shall deliver them out of them all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel_rubric:{text:`Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Let every breath`}},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO MATTHEW,`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Matins Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§36 (10:16-22)`,citation:{book:`Matthew`,chapter:10,verses:`16-22`,pericope_number:36},citation_basis:`printed`},psalm50_sticheron:{text:`O ye people, hymning Christ the Savior, let us praise the five-membered choir of the saints: Eustratius the passion-bearer, patient of soul and steadfast, and with him Auxentius, Eugene, Mardarius and Orestes; for, having suffered for the Faith, they trampled underfoot the threefold waves of the enemy, and pray to Christ, that He grant cleansing and remission of sins unto those who with faith celebrate their memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 After Psalm 50 sticheron`},sourceLabel:`After Psalm 50, this Sticheron, in Tone I`,tone:1},canon_rubric:{text:`Canon of the supplication to the Theotokos (the Paraclysis), with 6 Troparia, including the Irmos; and two canons of the martyrs, with a total of 8 Troparia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon I of the holy martyrs, the composition of John the Monk, in Tone IV:`,composer:`John the Monk`,tone:4,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Through the deep of the Red Sea, * marched dry shod Israel of old, * and by Moses’ outstretched hands, * raised in the form of a cross, * the power of Amalek was routed in the wilderness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Distributing gifts in the heavens to the spiritual athletes on earth with His almighty right hand, Christ the Judge of the contest sitteth and extendeth divine crowns to Eustratius and those with him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, let us behold the five-membered choir of martyrs, which emmiteth the most radiant light, and hath Eustratius as its desired leader, who is crowned with divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Casting off the vesture of an earthly army, thou didst enlist for the true King, receiving the token of suffering from Christ through Auxentius, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast the edifice which contained the divine Essence, O pure Birthgiver of God. Wherefore Lucia, desiring thee, was as a virgin led to thy Son in thine entourage.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Thy Church, O Christ, rejoiceth in Thee crying aloud: * Thou, O Lord, art my strength, * my refuge and foundation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O all-blessed Eustratius, by the hope of torments wast thou supra-naturally filled with all manner of joy, like an immaterial treasury.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With spiritual wisdom and the endurance of perils thou didst denounce the ungodliness of the tyrant, O Auxentius, martyr of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like most splendid adornments, like flowers, ye were arrayed in the wounds of Christ, O martyrs of the Church of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`We, the faithful, truly honor thee, the Theotokos, as our Sovereign Lady; for thou hast given birth to God, Who became flesh, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`For the sake of love for Thine image, * O compassionate One, * Thou didst ascend the cross * and the nations melted away. * For Thou, O Lover of mankind, * art my strength and my praise.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With the wounds of thy flesh thou didst set aside the defilements of thy soul, and by faith thou didst shatter the arrows of the wicked serpent, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy wounds was the King of glory glorified, O passion-bearer Eustratius, and He hath filled thee with ineffable glory by the power of miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Emulating the boldness of the fishermen, fishing with the net of martyrdom thou didst bring the wise Eugene to the Master, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-immaculate one, who alone hast been revealed to be more holy than the cherubim: from every evil circumstance save the souls of us who hymn thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Thou, O Lord, who camest into the world, * art my light, * a holy Light turning from the darkness of ignorance * those who sing Thy praises in faith.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Like a radiant star thou didst shine forth like a light from afar among the company of martyrs, O victorious Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O the goodly fate! O the divinely given portion! O the most beauteous woman, who by light overcame the deception of our first mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst consider all things of beauty to be as dung, O Mardarius, superseding the laws of nature in thy suffering.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The earthly mind cannot comprehend thy conceiving, which passeth understanding, O Virgin maiden and Mother; for thou hast given birth unto God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The Church crieth out unto Thee O Lord, * ‘I will sacrifice unto Thee with a voice of praise * having been cleansed of the blood of the demons' * by the blood that for mercy's sake flowed from Thy side.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Mardarius cried aloud “Christ is more to me than everything: home, land, honor and fame”; for he was thus taught by thee, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Though cut out, thy tongue hath not ceased to sing, and thy severed hands have lifted themselves up to God, O Eugene, asking salvation for those who hymn thy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Suspended upside-down by thy feet, thy shoulders burned with heated irons, thou didst surrender thy spirit to the Master, O Mardarius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Finding thee to be her steadfast might, O Virgin the passion-bearer valiantly endured wounds, and rejoicing, was brought to the Master of all in thine entourage.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`In the Persian furnace the youths and descendants of Abraham, * burning with a love of piety * rather than by a flame of fire, * cried aloud saying: * Blessed art Thou in the temple of Thy glory, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Possessed of the immutable wisdom of confession to worship the one God in Trinity, thou didst prevail over torments, crying aloud: Blessed art Thou in the temple of Thy glory, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As one blessed, thou didst walk in the path of the blameless and didst right wisely bow the knee to the Redeemer, committing thy soul into the hands of the Master as a most fragrant sacrifice, O Auxentius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The same God Who sent food to Elijah by a raven, O Auxentius, working a miracle with thy precious head, revealed it to those who desired it, as a cherished object greatly desired by the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Mother, the pure Word loved thee as one pure and incorrupt, and, becoming incarnate of thee, He refashioned all of mankind, and hath glorified Lucia with miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Having spread his hands, Daniel closed the lions’ jaws * in their den; * while the zealously pious youths, * girded with virtue, * quenched the power of the fire and cried aloud: * Bless ye the Lord, all ye works of the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Opening thy lips in purity, thou didst draw in the divine Spirit, O Eustratius; wherefore, having denounced the feebleness of soul-destroying worship, thou didst cry out that mankind should worship God in the Trinity: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`His resolve strengthened by thy wise instructions, O martyr Eustratius, the invincible Orestes, stretched out upon a bed of iron, cried out like the children to those who would destroy him by flame: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy body stretched forth patiently upon a heated bed, O glorious Orestes, thou wast numbered among the martyrs, rejoicing in the Lord, and hast found rest in the tabernacles of heaven, crying aloud: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast been revealed to be more exalted than the heavens, having given birth to the God of heaven Who hath rendered heavenly the whole essence of mortals, O all-pure one, and illumined the memory of the honorable Lucia. To Him do we ever cry: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`A cornerstone not cut by hand O Virgin, * was cut from thee the unhewn mountain: * even Christ, Who hath joined together the disparate natures; * therefore rejoicing we magnify thee, * O Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Desiring to partake of the divine mysteries, O blessed passion-bearer Eustratius, and to be deemed worthy of the radiant manifestation of God, thou didst hasten to Christ Whom thou desired, and Who called thee to the heavens.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing exceedingly in the gladsome condemnation of the full mindlessness of the tyrant, O passion-bearer Eustratius, chanting hymns thou didst magnify Christ, the Destroyer of death, the Judge of thy contest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Come, all ye who love the martyrs, and with sacred hymnody let us magnify Eugene, the destroyer of falsehood, and with him the wise Orestes and Mardarius, Auxentius and Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Light hath now shone forth upon us from thy womb which knew not a man, O Virgin; and the wondrous Lucia, divinely illumined by His effulgence, became light, O Virgin Mother and Birthgiver of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}},{title:`Canon II, in Tone VI:`,tone:6,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`When Israel walked on foot in the sea as on dry land, * on seeing their pursuer Pharaoh drowned, * they cried: * Let us sing to God * a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Christ, the King of the circles of heaven and Bestower of gifts, setteth forth his seat, extending crowns of victory to Eustratius and those who suffered with him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O ye faithful, let us praise the chanting and divinely crowned choir of the five passion-bearers, which had the wise Eustratius to lead them faithfully and divinely to Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring to enlist in the army of the Most High, O Eustratius, thou didst shun honors; and, leading thy life to God, O wise one, thou wast purified in sanctity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing, the choir of the right victorious martyrs, who have received crowns of victory, hymneth thee, O pure one; for through thee hath heaven been rendered accessible to us, in that thou hast given birth past understanding to the Creator of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],katavasia_rubric:{text:`Katavasia: Christ is born ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p7 Katavasia: Christ is born`}}},3:{irmos:{text:`There is none as holy as Thou, * O Lord my God, * who hast exalted the horn of Thy faithful O good One, * and strengthened us upon the rock * of Thy confession.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having set all thy hope on God Most High with firmness of mind, O blessed one, thou wast wholly filled with consolation by the expectation of wounds.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through divine wisdom thou didst flourish in the love of Christ; and by enduring wounds, O Auxentius, thou didst denounce the mindlessness of the persecutors, their insolence and vainglory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The unrestrained rage of Lysius and the fire of mighty tortures didst thou account as but a dream, O wise one; for, made steadfast in Christ, thou didst prevail, as though it were another who was suffering.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Chanting, we, the faithful, bless thee in a godly manner with voices of sacred discourse, O Virgin Mother of God, as the one who brought about our Author, Who became like unto us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Christ is my power, * my God and my Lord, * the holy Church divinely singeth, * crying with a pure mind, * keeping festival in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The Almighty, enkindling divine desire in thy soul, showed thee to be eminently wondrous, making the wounds of thy flesh whole.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Fishing with the spiritual net of the fishermen, O wise Eustratius, thou didst bring to Christ the King the wise Eugene.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy feet pierced by the nails of iron sandals during thy torture, O all-wise one, thou didst wholly stain thyself with thy blood, emulating the suffering of Jesus the King.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The infinite and immutable Word of God the Father, having been transformed by an outward appearance in becoming incarnate through thee, O all-immaculate one, hath deified me in His love for mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Illumine with Thy divine light, I pray, O good One, * the souls of those who with love rise early to pray to Thee, * that they may know Thee, O Word of God, * as the true God, * Who recalleth us from the darkness of sin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Wondrous like a star for the Church, thou didst shine forth among the martyrs, with martyric rays illumining the world more than the sun, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The divinely eloquent Mardarius, seeing thee emitting radiance in brilliant splendors, in the simplicity of his heart followed thee like an innocent lamb.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The intelligent and Christ-loving woman who loved her husband achieved supremacy over her kindred nature and eminently vanquished it completely, anointing her husband for martyrdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O good one, save those who confess thee with all their soul to be the Theotokos and Sovereign Lady of the world; for thee, who art the Theotokos, have we acquired as an invincible intercessor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Beholding the sea of life surging with the tempest of temptations, * I run to Thy calm haven, and cry to Thee: * Raise up my life from corruption, * O greatly merciful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Crying aloud: “Christ is more to me than all the things of my fathers”, O Mardarius, thy heels wholly burned away by heated irons, and thy breast pierced by arrows, thou didst repose, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Cut out, thy tongue did not cease to hymn Christ, O Eugene; and severed, thy hands elevated themselves to God, O blessed one, asking deliverance for those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy manly soul was right wondrous, O most noble Eugene, for when thy legs were violently broken thou didst surrender thy spirit into the hands of the Master of all, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure Lady who hast given birth to the Lord, and Helmsman of mortals, calm thou the constant and grievous turbulence of my passions, and grant serenity to my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`An angel made the furnace bedew the holy children. * But the command of God consumed the Chaldeans * and prevailed upon the tyrant to cry: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As a victor thou didst hasten to the kingdom of heaven, O Auxentius; for after many and varied trials and torments, thou didst die, beheaded, for Christ God, confessing Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Most wondrous is thy right wise courage, O Orestes, for thou didst show forth understanding at the tribunal, binding the soul of Lysius by the Cross, and chanting: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having Orestes as thy companion on the path of martyrdom, walking with thee as a fellow prisoner, O Eustratius, thou didst enrich him chanting: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The furnace did not consume the three youths, prefiguring thy birthgiving; for the divine Fire, dwelling within thee, did not consume thee, illumining all to cry aloud: Blessed is the God of our fathers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p12 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst make flame bedew the holy children, * and didst burn the sacrifice of a righteous man with water. * For Thou alone, O Christ, dost do all as Thou willest, * Thee do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Boldly preaching the infinite power of the one Essence of the Trinity, thou didst theologize, and denounced the vain worship of idols, O most divinely wise Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Ignorant of thy patience, the persecutor strove to terrify thee by the sight of the flames; but, spitting upon his savagery, thou didst chant, rejoicing in the Lord, O Eustratius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The divinely wise Orestes, instructed by thy divine words, leapt up, dancing upon the bed, wholly consumed like an innocent lamb, crying out to God, the Bestower of crowns: Bless the Lord, all ye works of the Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure Virgin, save me and be thou the help of my weakness. Deliver me from many tribulations and evils, that I may glorify thee, who alone art the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`It is impossible for mankind to see God * upon Whom the orders of angels dare not gaze; * but through thee, O all-pure one, * did the Word Incarnate become a man * and with the heavenly Hosts * Him we magnify and thee we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p13 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Hymning Him Whom thou didst desire, O blessed Eustratius, and becoming a participant in the sacred mysteries, in prison thou wast deemed worthy of a divine vision of Him, Who called thee to the heavenly life of His kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by the power of Christ, O glorious Eustratius, thou didst mock the blandishments of the persecutors, magnifying Christ with hymns; for, like the youths of old, thou didst enter the furnace rejoicing, as if it were a beautiful garden, O blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all ye people, with songs and hymns let us praise the divine warriors Auxentius and Eugene, together with Mardarius, the glorious Orestes and the wise Eustratius, their leader, fellow sufferer and guide.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin, thou wast the temple of Christ, Who reigneth with the Father and the Spirit; for thy sake, O pure one, we have been deemed worthy of adoption by Him through baptism, becoming temples through grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a most splendid luminary * for those who sit in the darkness of ignorance, * O passion-bearer; * for, armed with faith as with a spear, * thou wast undaunted by the arrogance of the enemy, * O Eustratius, ** who art far more eloquent than any orator.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Kontakion of the holy martyrs (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone II`,spec_mel:`The tomb and mortality ...`,tone:2}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Neither the sword, nor wild beasts, nor fire, nor any other thing that filleth material beings with fear was able to dissuade thy steadfastness; for, having trampled underfoot the power of the enemy by thy contest, as one impervious to fear thou didst pass over to the life of the incorporeal ones. Wherefore, thou bestowest healings upon the faithful who hasten to thy memorial with love, O holy passion-bearer Eustratius. Entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love celebrate thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,repeat:2,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy martyrs, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`When the Master and Fashioner of all * shall come to judge the whole world, * do thou number me, the condemned, * at His right hand with the sheep; * and deliver me, thine unprofitable servant, * from the outermost darkness and torment, * I pray, that with thanksgiving I may magnify the richness of thy goodness, * O all-immacu-late one, * and cry out to thee, rejoicing: * Pray to Christ God, that He grant me remission of sins, ** for thee do I, thy servant, have as my hope.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`}],exapostilarion:{text:`Thou didst complete the wondrous course of suffering, O blessed Eustratius, bringing with thee the honorable Eugene and the wise Auxentius, Mardarius and Orestes, at whose faith and boldness the assemblies of angels and mortals have marveled.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Exapostilarion`},sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion`,spec_mel:`By the Spirit in the sanctuary ...`,label:`plain`,repeat:2},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`As a most honorable temple, O all-immaculate Bride and Theotokos, thy birthgiving was ineffable; for thou hast given birth to God the pre-eternal Word, Who made His abode within thee. Wherefore, chanting, we magnify thy birthgiving, O all-immaculate maiden.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion`},praises_rubric:{text:`On the Praises, 4 Stichera: The composition of Germanus, in Tone III:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises rubric`}},praises:[{text:`With discourse of eloquent rhetoric the warrior of Christ filled the iniquitous with awe; with the wounds of his suffering the glorious Eustratius, the steadfast spiritual athlete, manfully triumphed over the powers of the enemy: and, having trodden the narrow path which is full of sorrow, he hath attained the land of life everlasting, wherein he entreateth Christ, that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises 1`},label:`plain`,tone:3,composer:`Germanus`},{text:`With martyric hymns let us crown Eustratius, great among witnesses, who was revealed to be a philosopher of divine wisdom and shown to be an orator in the beauty of his discourses; for this warrior of Christ, having gathered together a pious company, and arrayed himself for the struggles of martyrdom in the time of battle, seized the sword of the enemy and wounded him therewith. To him let us cry aloud: O most excellent of martyrs, with those who suffered with thee entreat Christ God on behalf of those who celebrate thy most honored memory with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p14 Praises 2`},label:`plain`,composer:`Germanus`},{text:`Let the right victorious witnesses to the Truth be crowned by us with praises: Eustratius, the denouncer of the myth-devising pagans, the preacher of the divine knowledge of Christ; Auxentius, who by the wisdom of his words and the patience of his acts denounced the ungodliness of the tyrants; and with him Eugene, who was right profitable for God, but useless for the tormenters because of his saving confession, and Orestes, the true and wondrous warrior of the King of all; and with them also Mardarius, the innocent dove who put the crafty serpent to shame by the grace of Christ God, the Savior of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 3`},tone:4,composer:`John the Monk`,label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`The composition of John the Monk, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0},{text:`O holy martyrs, ye preferred the wisdom of the apostles to the teachings of the heathen, forsaking books of rhetoric and em-bracing the wisdom of the fishermen; for ye learned eloquence of discourse and the divine knowledge of the Trinity among the unlettered and divinely eloquent. Therein pray ye, that our souls be preserved in peace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises 4`},composer:`Cassia the nun`,label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`The composition of Cassia the nun`,label_inline:!0}],praises_glory:{text:`Let us hymn and piously praise the God-bearing martyrs-the five-stringed harp and five-branched lamp-stand of the Church of God; in accordance with their names: Rejoice, O divinely wise Eustratius, O rhetor of rhetors, who wast well enrolled by God in the army of heaven, and who pleased Him Who enlisted thee! Rejoice, O blessed Auxentius, Who increased greatly the talant entrusted to thee by God! Rejoice, O divinely wise Eugene, most comely scion of divine nobility! Rejoice, O all-blessed Orestes, beauteous in aspect and supremely good of character, twice eminent, who abidest wholly in the mountains of God! Rejoice, O invincible Mardarius, thou pearl resplendent of luster, who joyfully endured bitter tortures! Rejoice, O choir of wise virgins equal in number to the martyrs! We beseech you to deliver from all wrath and tribulations those who honor your annual memorial, and to make us partakers of your ineffable glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises Glory`},composer:`Cassia the nun`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., the composition of Cassia the nun, in Tone IV`,tone:4},praises_closer:{text:`Having thee O Theotokos as our hope and intercession, * we fear not the assaults of the adversary, ** for thou dost save our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p15 Praises Both now, Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},great_doxology_rubric:{text:`Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. First Hour.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p15 Great Doxology. Troparion. Litanies. First Hour.`}}},liturgy:{order:[`beatitudes_rubric`,`beatitudes`,`troparion`,`kontakia`,`prokeimenon`,`prokeimenon_verse`,`epistle`,`alleluia`,`alleluia_verse`,`gospel`,`communion_verse`],beatitudes_rubric:{text:`On the Beatitudes, 8 Troparia: 4 from ODE III of Canon I, and 4 from ODE VI of Canon II of the canons of the holy martyrs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitudes rubric`}},beatitudes:[{text:`O all-blessed Eustratius, by the hope of torments wast thou supra-naturally filled with all manner of joy, like an immaterial treasury.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`With spiritual wisdom and the endurance of perils thou didst denounce the ungodliness of the tyrant, O Auxentius, martyr of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like most splendid adornments, like flowers, ye were arrayed in the wounds of Christ, O martyrs of the Church of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Crying aloud: “Christ is more to me than all the things of my fathers”, O Mardarius, thy heels wholly burned away by heated irons, and thy breast pierced by arrows, thou didst repose, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`Cut out, thy tongue did not cease to hymn Christ, O Eugene; and severed, thy hands elevated themselves to God, O blessed one, asking deliverance for those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 5`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy manly soul was right wondrous, O most noble Eugene, for when thy legs were violently broken thou didst surrender thy spirit into the hands of the Master of all, rejoicing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude 6`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure Lady who hast given birth to the Lord, and Helmsman of mortals, calm thou the constant and grievous turbulence of my passions, and grant serenity to my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Beatitude Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}],kontakia:[{text:`Thou hast been shown to be a most splendid luminary * for those who sit in the darkness of ignorance, * O passion-bearer; * for, armed with faith as with a spear, * thou wast undaunted by the arrogance of the enemy, * O Eustratius, ** who art far more eloquent than any orator.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Kontakion after Ode III, at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`ODE III, Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`Eloquently speaking of divine things before the iniquitous, O all-wondrous one, * thou didst endure beatings with a most courageous heart, * shining forth with godly signs, * and extinguishing the towering flame of delusion. ** Wherefore, we honor thee, O all-blessed Eustratius, martyr of Christ.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p16 Kontakion after Ode VI, at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`ODE VI, Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone III`,tone:3}],prokeimenon:{text:`In the saints that are in His earth hath the Lord been wondrous; * He hath wrought all His desires in them`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Liturgy Prokeimenon`},sourceLabel:`Prokeimenon, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},prokeimenon_verse:{text:`I beheld the Lord ever before me, for He is at my right hand, that I might not be shaken.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Liturgy Prokeimenon verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},epistle:{heading:`EPISTLE TO THE EPHESIANS,`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Epistle`},citation_verbatim:`§233 (6: 10-17)`,citation:{book:`Ephesians`,chapter:6,verses:`10-17`,pericope_number:233},citation_basis:`printed`},alleluia:{text:`The righteous cried, and the Lord heard them, and He delivered them out of all their tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia`},sourceLabel:`Alleluia, in Tone IV`,label_inline:!0,tone:4},alleluia_verse:{text:`Many are the tribulations of the righteous, and the Lord shall deliver them out of them all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Alleluia verse`},label:`refrain`,sourceLabel:`Verse`,label_inline:!0},gospel:{heading:`GOSPEL ACCORDING TO LUKE,`,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Gospel`},citation_verbatim:`§106 (LK. 21:12-19)`,citation:{book:`Luke`,chapter:21,verses:`12-19`,pericope_number:106},citation_basis:`printed`},communion_verse:{text:`Rejoice in the Lord, O ye righteous; praise is meet for the upright.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-13.pdf`,locus:`p17 Communion Verse`},sourceLabel:`Communion Verse`,label_inline:!0}}}]},"12-14":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Martyrs Thyrsus, Lucius, Philemon and those with them`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY MARTYRS THYRSUS, LUCIUS, PHILEMON & THOSE WITH THEM`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 14th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2A`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-14.pdf`,note:`Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall: 3 stichera of the martyrs at Lord I have cried, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology appointed. ODS vol. III has no fixed 12-14 entry. A SHORT service: the three stichera of the Theotokos for Alleluia days, a Theotokion and Stavrotheotokion, and then Matins; NO aposticha rubric and NO TROPARION is printed anywhere in the file. One canon by Theophanes; a sessional hymn after Ode III; a kontakion after Ode VI with no ikos; no exapostilarion; nothing for the Liturgy. The ODE V heading is printed doubled.`,troparion:{absent:!0,reason:`not_printed_in_source`,basis:`close_reading`,note:`No troparion is printed anywhere in 12-14.pdf.`},kontakion:{text:`Reviling the impious tyrant, * O champions of faith and piety, * ye denounced his bestial thirst for blood, * and, fortified by the help of Christ, * O Thyrsus and Lucius, * ye vanquished his wrathful opposition. ** With those who suffered with you, pray ye on our behalf.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the holy martyrs`},sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy martyrs, in Tone II`,spec_mel:`The steadfast ...`,tone:2},general_fallback:{type:`Martyrs`,name:`Thyrsus, Lucius and Philemon`,basis:`The page heads the service "the holy martyrs" (plural) and prints no troparion, so the General Menaion service to several martyrs supplies it (Tone I, "We beseech Thee, O Lord"). What the OCA sings for these martyrs was not checked: there is no OCA text for 14 December.`},vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`theotokos_stichera_rubric`,`theotokos_stichera`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`The wondrous Thyrsus, * the divinely wise Callinicus, * and the glorious Lucius, * confessing the uncreated Trinity, * with most courageous resolve * endured torments most grievous and intense, * and as victors have received crowns of victory, * becoming fellow citizens ** with the immaterial hosts.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,tone:4,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`The great Philemon, * Adria most noetically rich * and the wise Apollonius * quenched the flame of polytheism with torrents of blood, * watered all the earth * with divine streams of the knowledge of God, * and dry up rivers of the passions with showers of healing * and grace divine, ** in that they are our fervent defenders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`The glorious martyrs, * the most beauteous flowers * blossomed forth in the meadow, * emitting the divine fragrance of the Spirit, * and perfuming the thoughts * of those who with faith honor their annual memorial, * their sufferings and struggles, * and their godly end. ** Wherefore, they dwell, rejoicing, in never-waning light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`}],theotokos_stichera_rubric:{text:`But if Alleluia be chanted at Matins instead of “God is the Lord ...,” we chant the following Stichera of the Theotokos before the foregoing, in the same melody:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 Stichera of the Theotokos rubric (Alleluia days)`}},theotokos_stichera:[{text:`O Lady, rain down upon me * the depths of thy mercy, * and as thou art merciful, O maiden, * give drink to my heart, which hath been consumed by the burning heat of the passions; * cause drops of compunction * to pour forth continually, I pray, * whereby I may be deemed worthy of the consolation, O pure one, * which those who shed tears in sincerity ** shall receive.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lady, take pity on me * who am shaken by the assaults of the demons * and cast into the pit of destruction; * and establish me upon the rock of the virtues. * Destroying the counsels of the enemy, * grant that I may follow * the precepts of thy Son and our God, * that I may receive remission ** on the day of judgment.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I have fallen among vile and murderous thieves, * O most immaculate one, * and by their assaults, O maiden, * I have been stripped of the incorrupt garments of heavenly splendor, * and have been pitilessly wounded by them * and cast down in a place of affliction, * barely alive. * Yet go thou before me, extend thy hand ** and raise me up, I pray.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 Sticheron of the Theotokos 3`},label:`plain`}],lic_closer:{text:`I lie upon the bed of despondency, O all-immaculate one, * and pass my life in slothfulness, * and I fear the time of mine end, O Theotokos. * Let not the all-evil serpent * mercilessly rend my lowly soul asunder * like a lion. * Wherefore, going before me in thy goodness * before mine end, ** raise me up to repentance.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`The most pure one, * beholding Christ, the lover of mankind, crucified, * His side pierced by a lance, * cried out, lamenting: * “What is this, O my Son? * How have these thankless people rewarded Thee * for the good things Thou hast done for them? * Dost Thou hasten to leave me childless, O most Beloved? ** I marvel, O compassionate One, at Thy voluntary crucifixion!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakion`],canon_rubric:{text:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and this canon of the holy martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone VI:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Both canons from the Oktoechos; and this canon of the holy martyrs, with 4 Troparia, the composition of Theophanes, in Tone VI:`,composer:`Theophanes`,tone:6,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`When Israel walked on foot in the sea as on dry land, * on seeing their pursuer Pharaoh drowned, * they cried: * Let us sing to God * a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Standing before the throne of God, arrayed in the beauties of martyrdom and resplendent with divine effulgence, O passion-bearers, illumine us who hymn your memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring divine beauty, ye reckoned the beauties of life to be as naught, O spiritual athletes of Christ; and dying in body, ye have been deemed worthy to receive life without end.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Denouncing the delusion of idolatry in a godly manner, O passion-bearing martyrs, ye endured the burning of manifold pangs and have now attained the life which is devoid of pain.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, thou hast given birth to the uncircumscribable Word, Who became circumscribed in a human body. Him do thou beseech, that those who glorify thee be delivered from corruption and the assault of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`There is none as holy as Thou, * O Lord my God, * who hast exalted the horn of Thy faithful O good One, * and strengthened us upon the rock * of Thy confession.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The minions of darkness, cruelly lacerating thy body, O Thyrsus mighty in love, were unable to weaken the strength of thy mind, which was fortified by divine love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O wondrous martyr Philemon, thy faith in the Lord was truly constant, and thereby thou didst put the false religion of the enemy to shame, crying aloud: “I am a servant of Christ!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst go forth boldly to do battle with the enemy, O martyr, armed not with shield and spear, but divinely defending thyself with steadfast faith; and thou didst manfully cast him down to the ground.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`One of the Holy Trinity, having become incarnate through thy pure blood in two natures, O all-pure one, hath issued forth divinely, saving the descendants of Adam in His goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Christ is my power, * my God and my Lord, * the holy Church divinely singeth, * crying with a pure mind, * keeping festival in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Desiring to confess the one Lord and God of all, Who alone is compassionate, through their sufferings the martyrs have received His kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Strengthened by the power of the Cross, O most noetically rich martyr Thyrsus, like a youth thou didst endure the laceration of thy body, the raging of the fire, and the onslaught of wild beasts and the sea.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adorned with the wounds of thy struggles as a warrior of Christ, O martyred spiritual athlete Lucius, thou didst render thy soul more radiant than the brilliance of the sun.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O blessed Mary, thou art the setting aright of mortals, and we know thee, alone among women, to be the Mother who knew not a man, the immaculate Virgin, the undefiled maiden.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Illumine with Thy divine light, I pray, O good One, * the souls of those who with love rise early to pray to Thee, * that they may know Thee, O Word of God, * as the true God, * Who recalleth us from the darkness of sin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Sanctified in godly splendor by most divine rays, O all-praised martyrs, ye sailed across the inconstant abyss of ungodliness and have passed over to divine tranquility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Cruelly dragged across the ground and wounded by tortures, O all-praised martyrs, ye have received the honors of heaven, having now become fellow citizens with the angels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Manifestly preferring to die for Christ Who loved thee, O divinely blessed martyr Philemon, thou didst treat the wounds inflicted on thy body as though they were made by the darts of children.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Mary, good Lady of the word, save those who with all their soul confess thee to be the Theotokos; for thee, who art the Theotokos, have we acquired as our invincible intercessor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Beholding the sea of life surging with the tempest of temptations, * I run to Thy calm haven, and cry to Thee: * Raise up my life from corruption, * O greatly merciful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Moved by the winds of the divine Spirit, O wise martyrs, ye most joyously saved the entry of your souls for the noetic havens, delighting together therein in deification.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Mounting the flaming chariot, O spiritual athletes, ye were caught up to the heavens by the blood ye shed, and having attained to the glory of God, ye have received crowns of victory from Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Philemon and Lucius, Apollonius and the ever-memorable Thyrsus, the four divine and radiant martyrs, have been enriched by partaking immaterially of the effulgence of the Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`He Who as God transcendeth all creation, noetic and visible, passed, incarnate, through thy womb, O Virgin Mother, preserving thee incorrupt, as thou wast before birthgiving.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`An angel made the furnace bedew the holy children. * But the command of God consumed the Chaldeans * and prevailed upon the tyrant to cry: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With divine rains ye extinguished the furnace of polytheism, all-joyously aflame with divine love, O spiritual athletes; and ye now chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Casting your divine net to ensnare the persecutor, O right wondrous ones, ye drew him forth from the depths of delusion and brought him to Christ, chanting with fervor: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Showing unshakable resolve and a courageous mind, ye shook the foundations of delusion, O spiritual athletes, and ye now piously chant: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Past description is thy conception, O Bride of God; for thou hast given birth to God the Word, Who hath delivered mankind from all irrationality, and thou givest us the words to cry aloud: O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst make flame bedew the holy children, * and didst burn the sacrifice of a righteous man with water. * For Thou alone, O Christ, dost do all as Thou willest, * Thee do we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Defending yourselves with the shield of piety, and taking up the Cross as a spear, O Thyrsus of valiant mind, thou didst cut down the hordes of the invisible foe, O divine glory of the martyrs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Aflame with love for the Almighty, thou didst manfully enter the tribunal of the tyrant, and, having suffered patiently, thou didst break asunder the great serpent, O spiritual athlete Philemon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Showing forth the power of the enemy to be drowned in the depths of thy courage and patience, O Adrian, thou wast deemed worthy of the kingdom which remaineth unshaken throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Confessing thee to be the true Theotokos, like the angel we cry out to thee: Rejoice! For thou alone on earth hast given birth to our Joy, O pure, blessed and joyous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`It is impossible for mankind to see God * upon Whom the orders of angels dare not gaze; * but through thee, O all-pure one, * did the Word Incarnate become a man * and with the heavenly Hosts * Him we magnify and thee we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Emulating the suffering of Christ, ye endured the trial of many torments, O blessed ones; and when your heads were severed, ye were numbered among the ranks of heaven, resplendent with glory and adorned with divine radiance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst dye thy robe purple in thy blood, O wise Thyrsus, and having gloriously arrayed thyself therein, and wielding the Cross as it were a scepter, thou dost now reign with Christ, rejoicing with all the passion-bearers, O divinely blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The angelic hosts marveled at your struggles, wounds, opposition and violent death, O blessed ones; and dwelling with them, O all-praised ones, be ye mindful of those who celebrate your memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`In the guise of human flesh the Word appeared, born from thy womb, O pure and divinely joyous Virgin Mary, and, having endured suffering, He hath drawn to Himself a multitude of martyrs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Protected well by the shield of piety, and arrayed in the armor of the Cross, the right wondrous martyrs of Christ humbled the legions of the tyrant; and, crowned by Him with the wreath of victory, they join chorus unceasingly with the hosts on high, and entreat the Savior to save our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode III sessional`},label:`plain`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy martyrs, in Tone IV`,spec_mel:`Joseph marveled ...`,tone:4},{text:`Tempest-tossed by the threefold-waves of the passions, * I who lack a conscience fervently call upon thee, O most pure one: * Disdain me not, lest I perish, wretch that I am, * O thou who hast given birth to the Abyss of mercy; * for I have no other hope than thee. * Let me not become a joy unto mine enemies, * nor a byword, for I trust in thee. * For whatsoever thou desirest thou canst do, ** in that thou art the Mother of the God of all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`glory`,`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`The Virgin and ewe-lamb, beholding on the Cross the Lamb Who was born of her without seed, His side pierced by a spear, was wounded and with grief and cried aloud, exclaiming amid her pain: “What is this new mystery? How is it that Thou diest Who alone art Lord of life? Wherefore, arise, raising up our fallen forefather!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-14.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}]},"12-15":{_encoded:[`c0.identity`,`c0.vespers`,`c0.matins`,`c0.liturgy`],commemorations:[{kind:`saint`,name:`the holy Hieromartyr Eleutherius and our venerable father Paul of Latros`,title:{text:`COMMEMORATION OF THE HOLY HIEROMARTYR ELEUTHERIUS`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 title`},sourceLabel:`THE 15th DAY OF THE MONTH OF DECEMBER`},rank:`simple`,fekula_section:`2B`,oca_primary:!0,source_file:`12-15.pdf`,note:`ONE printed service for two saints: one entry, items tagged with \`saint\`. THE TITLE NAMES ST. ELEUTHERIUS ALONE; the service gives three stichera, a troparion, a kontakion, a sessional hymn, a canon and an exapostilarion to "the venerable one", whom the hymns call Paul and "pride of Mount Latros": Paul of Latros (an identification from the text; his name stands in no heading). Rank by the encoding_rule_v2.md 1.1 waterfall, step 6: six stichera at Lord I have cried split 3 + 3 between two saints, no Polyeleos, no Great Doxology; ODS vol. III has no fixed 12-15 entry. Fekula 2B (a double service). No Glory at Lord I have cried and no aposticha rubric. "One canon from the Oktoechos, and two canons of the saints": the hieromartyr's by Joseph, the venerable one's on the irmoi of the Nativity. The kontakion of the venerable one stands after Ode III with no ikos; the kontakion and ikos of the hieromartyr after Ode VI. At Liturgy the two troparia and two kontakia are printed, the hieromartyr's first; no readings. The ODE VI heading is printed doubled.`,vespers:{order:[`lic_rubric`,`lic`,`lic_closer`,`lic_stavrotheotokion`,`troparia`,`troparion_closer_rubric`],lic_rubric:{text:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 6 Stichera: 3 of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone IV:`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC rubric`}},lic:[{text:`Thou didst become a most sacred vessel of the divine Spirit, * having cleansed thy soul of the passions, O most sacred one. * Hence, thou didst receive the holy and divine anointing, * becoming a hierarch, * a divinely wise leader of the people, * and an invincible martyr * of Him Who endured sufferings for our sake * and hath poured forth dispassion, ** O spiritual athlete Eleutherius.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 1`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,tone:4,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`Seeing thee finishing well the contest, * she who gave birth to thee * desired to run the same race as thee; * and, embracing thee * in the midst of the arena, O wise one, * she was slain like a heifer. * With her we entreat thee, * O most blessed Eleutherius: ** Beseech the Lord and Savior on our behalf.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 2`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`Thou didst prevail over thy body, * which was wounded by blows * and brought into contact with fire; * for thou didst furnish thy mind with wings through invincible desire * and the most comely beauty of the divine One Who loveth us, * by Whose sweet desire thou wast wounded, * O adornment of martyrs, ornament of hierarchs, * converser with angels, ** O spiritual athlete Eleutherius.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 3`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,spec_mel:`Thou hast given a sign ...`},{text:`O Paul, adornment of monastics, * beauteous scion of the wilderness, * boast of the venerable, pride of Mount Latros, * confirmation of the faithful: * by thy supplications to the Master * deliver from every evil circumstance * and con-demnation to the fire * those who with love celebrate thy most honored memory ** and kiss the shrine of thy relics.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 4`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`And 3 Stichera of the venerable one, in Tone II`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`,tone:2},{text:`Having made thyself a temple of the Trinity, * O divinely blessed father, * thou didst erect a temple dedicated to the Trinity; * and having entered the trackless wilderness of Mount Latros, * as Moses did Mount Sinai, * thou didst make thine abode thereon, * where, receiving the divine law, * thou didst truly instruct multitudes of monastics, O most wondrous one, ** with great excellence.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 5`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`},{text:`As thou hast boldness before God, * pray thou, O venerable one, * that the flock which thou didst gather together * with great effort * be preserved from the temptations of the enemy * and the assaults of the heathen, * from fire and sword and every attack of the evil one; * for, having thee as our guardian and protection, O blessed one, ** we have acquired thee as our hope with God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p1 LIC 6`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,spec_mel:`When from the Tree ...`}],lic_closer:{text:`The only uncontainable God, * Who became a man in His goodness, * didst thou bear in thy womb without restraint and confinement, * O most holy Bride of God. * Wherefore, I beseech thee: * Release me from the passions * which restrain and confine me, * that having traversed the straight and narrow path, ** I may attain unto that which leadeth to life, O Virgin.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Glory/Both now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,tone:2,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion, in the same melody`},lic_stavrotheotokion:{text:`Upon beholding her Lamb * led of His own will to the slaughter as a man, * the unblemished ewe-lamb, cried aloud weeping: * “Dost Thou now hasten to leave childless, * the one who gave Thee birth, O Christ? * What is this that Thou hast done, O Redeemer of all? * Even so I will hymn and glorify Thine extreme goodness * which passeth understanding and all telling, ** O Lover of mankind!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p2 LIC Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0},troparia:[{text:`As thou didst share in the ways of the apostles * and didst occupy their throne, * thou didst find thine activity to be a passage to divine vision, * O divinely inspired one. * Wherefore, ordering the word of truth, * thou didst suffer for the Faith even to the shedding of thy blood, ** O Hieromartyr Eleutherius, entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the holy hieromartyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`O all-glorious Paul, * we hymn thee as one who dwelleth together with the bodiless hosts * and as a companion of all the venerable, * we beseech thee, to ever pray thou for us, ** that we may find mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p2 Troparion of the venerable one`},label:`glory`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],troparion_closer_rubric:{text:`Both now ..., Theotokion, or Stavrotheotokion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p2 Both now, Theotokion or Stavrotheotokion`}}},matins:{order:[`canon_rubric`,`canons`,`kontakia_ode3`,`sessional_ode3`,`kontakia_ode6`,`exapostilarion_glory`,`exapostilarion_closer`],canon_rubric:{text:`One canon from the Oktoechos, and two canons of the saints.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Canon rubric`}},canons:[{title:`Canon of the holy hieromartyr, the acrostic whereof is: “Show me to be free of the passions, O all-blessed one”, the composition of Joseph, in Tone I:`,composer:`Joseph`,tone:1,acrostic:`Show me to be free of the passions, O all-blessed one`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us all chant a triumphant hymn unto God * Who wrought wondrous miracles * with His upraised arm, * and saved Israel, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`By thy radiant supplications, O martyr Eleutherius, free me, who am held captive by the darkness of the passions, that I may hymn thee, the servant of Christ, with divine hymns.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst shine forth with the most pure rays of suffering, O most sacred one, with thy blood didst thou dye thy priestly raiment, and become radiant through the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Cleaving unto God from thy youth with a most pure mind, thou didst drive carnal understanding away from thy soul and became enriched with the abundant grace of miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like a throne of fire thou didst bear the Creator, and like an animate bridal-chamber and a beautiful palace thou didst contain the King Who became as we are, apart from change and mingling of natures.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Let my heart be established in Thy will O Christ God, * Who hath established a second heaven over the waters, * and founded the earth upon the waters, * O all-powerful One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O wise one who didst will to suffer for Christ, thou didst endure the wounding of thy body, finding delight in thy pangs and afflictions; wherefore, thou hast now received a life without pain.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Holding fast with the fervent desire for the Creator, O divinely wise spiritual athlete Eleutherius, bedewed by the fire of the Spirit thou didst submit thyself to fiery testing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shown forth as most sacred among priests and a martyr most steadfast among the martyrs, O blessed one, thou hast received a twofold crown, continually beholding the face of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst bud forth the Staff of strength whereby we are made steadfast; for the staff of Aaron, which once put forth branches, prefigured thee, O land untouched by the plough, O pure turtle-dove, O Ever-virgin!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Foreseeing in the Spirit O prophet Habbakuk, * the incarnation of the Word, * thou didst proclaim, crying aloud: * When the years draw nigh, Thou shalt be known; * when the season cometh, Thou shalt be shown forth! * Glory to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Neither the gaping mouths of the lions, nor the raging of the fire, nor cruel threats were able to weaken the endurance of thy strength, O initiate of the sacred mysteries; but, as firm as adamant, thou didst delight in tortures, aflame with divine zeal.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Full of life-bearing waters, thy mouth poured forth rivers of divine doctrines, O hieromartyr, engulfing the mockery of the iniquitous and watering the hearts of those who acknowledge Christ as God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Glorifying thee greatly, thy Creator, for Whom thou wast zealous to suffer, O spiritual athlete, sent a dove bearing angelic food to thee who didst become angelic through the most radiant splendors of suffering.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The angelic armies were in awe, beholding how He Who is invisible became visible, through thee assuming a guise like unto us, O Virgin Birthgiver of God. Him do thou beseech, that He grant salvation unto all who glorify thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Grant us Thy peace, O Son of God, * for we know no other God than Thee, * and we call upon Thy Name, * for Thou art the God of the living and the dead.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The most wicked enemy, plotting to lead thee astray through deceitful words, O martyr, was shown to be put to scorn, the most crafty sage of malice being outwitted by thy wisdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Mounting the chariot of the divine virtues, O glorious one, thou didst reach the summit of martyrdom and didst cast down the vaunted pride of the wicked demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Desiring to behold the beauty of Jesus, O venerable one, thou didst adorn thyself with the beauty of martyrdom, and departed to Him, crowned with a wreath of splendor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Every mind marvels at the wonder of thee, O pure one; for thou hast given birth to God in the flesh and fed the Nurturer with milk, without having experienced the temptation of a man, as thou thyself knowest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Emulating the prophet Jonah, I cry aloud: * Free Thou my life from corruption, O good One; * and save me who crieth out: * O Savior of the world, Glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`The excellent shepherd of the flock of Christ, the most eloquent pastor, the path of struggles, is glorified, having glorified God with his members.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Given life through visions of God, thou didst steadfastly render lifeless the greatly crafty foe, O ever-memorable wise one, glory of the martyrs and rule of the priesthood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Enduring wounds, entering the fire of thine own will, thou didst put down the onslaughts of the savage beasts, possessing constant love for the Creator.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Revealed as a tabernacle of sanctity, O Mary, sanctify my wretched soul, which hath been defiled by the pleasures, and make it a receptacle of divine glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Thy children who were in the furnace O Savior, * were neither touched nor troubled by The fire. * Whereupon the three sang, as with a single mouth * Thy praises and blessed Thee, saying: * 'O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou.'`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Shattered, O wise one, thou didst cry out: “May Christ now be magnified in my flesh! I fear neither the boiling of the cauldron, nor am I daunted by death or the assaults of wild beasts, for the sake of life!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`“Seeking the beauty of the one God, I desire to receive His glory alone! Let my whole body be broken and burned!” didst thou cry aloud, O glorious one; “I seek the freedom which doth enslave me to Christ!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Looking toward the life to come, O blessed one, thou didst truly die to the world, and, burned with the wounds of torture, thou didst shine forth like gold and hast been laid up in the treasuries of the mansions of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The most pure Word, of God, Who was born of thy womb, found thee alone to be most pure, O all-immaculate Bride of God, puriying us the faithful of the defilements which have come upon us through the passions and lack of restraint.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Him of whom the angels and all the hosts of heaven are in awe * as their Lord and Creator, * ye priests hymn, ye children praise, * ye peoples bless and supremely exalt * throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Blossoming, thou didst put forth a garden beauteous in the splendors of martyrdom, O adornment of the martyrs. Ye have now shown yourselves to be flowers of paradise, emitting a divine fragrance in a most godly manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy mother mingleth her own blood with the outpouring of the blood of thee who wast born from her; for, embracing thy body, O wise one, she was slain by the sword and liveth forevermore.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy shrine poureth forth the waters of healings and rivers of miracles upon those in need, who wash away the defilements of soul-destroying passions, O martyred hierarch, throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Like rain Christ, the only Benefactor, descended upon thy womb, O Virgin, truly watering all creation, and drying up the turbid rivers of the madness of idolatry.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`The ever-flowing wellspring of life, * light-bearing candlestick of grace, * the animate temple, and most pure cloud, * wider than the heavens and the earth, * the Theotokos do we the faithful magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As the mouth of God, rescuing vain-minded people from the mouth of the alien, thou didst show them to be heirs of grace; and suffering mightily, thou livest with priests and passion-bearers, O Eleutherius.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let Eleutherius be faithfully praised: the pure phial of the Spirit, the beautiful abode of the virtues, the innocent lamb, the ever-burning lamp, the foundation of hierarchs and martyrs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Truly thou dost live in never-waning light, having become the most radiant light of the Sun; wherefore, by thy supplications to God, O Eleutherius deliver from the darkness of the passions those who celebrate thy radiant memory today.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Spare us who hymn Thee, O Lord, Thou ineffable Offspring of the Virgin, in that Thou alone art our Benefactor Who lovest mankind, delivering Thy servants from perils, passions and tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}},{title:`Canon of the venerable one, in Tone I:`,tone:1,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ is born, render ye glory. * Christ cometh from heaven, meet ye Him. * Christ is on earth, be ye exalted. * O all the earth, sing unto the Lord, * and sing praises in gladness, O ye people, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`New hymnody of praise do I hasten to bring to mine open lips, O God-bearing Paul. By thy prayers grant me the grace to speak, O venerable one, that I may recount thine honored struggles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Taking up the yoke of the Lord from thy youth, O venerable one, and sowing the wheat of the Spirit in the furrows of thy heart, thou didst reap the grain which maketh firm men's souls, O divinely blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through manifold efforts thou didst receive the kingdom on high, having lived on earth like an incorporeal being and passed through life like an angel in thy body. And now, standing in the highest before the Trinity, be thou mindful of us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Incorporeal and supremely good One, receiving my corruptible flesh from thy body, and lying in the manger of His own will, O Bride of God, hath deified that which He received by uniting Himself with it.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p3 Ode 1 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},3:{irmos:{text:`To the Son who was begotten of the Father * without change before all ages, * and in the last times, without seed, was made flesh of the Virgin, * to Christ our God let us cry aloud: * Thou hast raised up our horn, holy art Thou, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`O thy courage! O the valor of thy soul, O glorious one! For, desiring to break the jaws of the invisible lions, thou didst carry two large stones at night, as a weight upon thy shoulders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Who can fittingly recount thy struggles? For, treading the hard paths in the wilderness, thou didst eat wild plants, learning to sweeten thy meals with the pangs of asceticism.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Moses the God-seer of old was deemed worthy of a divine vision in the bush, and the most honored Paul manifestly recognized within himself the fire which appeared from on high, burning without being consumed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Word, Who as God art beginningless in essence and art equally worshipped with the Father: in being born of the Virgin Thou hast received a beginning in time, manifesting Thyself as man by nature; and becoming a babe, O Christ, Thou didst reveal Thyself as an infant wrapped in swaddling bands.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p4 Ode 3 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Rod of the root of Jesse, * and flower that blossomed from his stem, * O Christ, Thou hast sprung from the Virgin. * From the Mountain overshadowed by the forest * Thou hast come, made flesh from her that knew not wedlock, * O God who art not formed from matter. * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Once, in the time of thy youth, when thou wast overcome by sleep and didst weaken while standing all night, thine honored teacher Peter, seeing this, smote thee in the face; and, having smote thee, he straightway soothed thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Conversing privily with God, having drawn nigh to Him directly, our father Paul was never overcome by sleep after the blow dealt him by his teacher; and becoming like unto the incorporeal ones, he ever remained vigilant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Shown forth as a most sacred vessel, thou didst receive the heavenly myrrh of Christ in thy heart; and, having brightly lighted the lamp of thy patient abstinence with a virtuous life, thou didst hasten to the divine Bridegroom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Word Who hast heaven for Thy throne and the earth for Thy footstool, becoming incarnate Thou didst enter the womb of the Virgin and made Thine abode in a wretched cave; yet as King and the God-man Thou didst receive gifts from the magi, the kings of Persia.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p6 Ode 4 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},5:{irmos:{text:`As Thou art the God of peace and Father of compassions, * Thou hast sent unto us Thine angel of great counsel, * granting us peace. * Wherefore guided towards the light of the knowledge of God, * and watching by night we glorify Thee, * O Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Having cleansed thy mind of the mire of the passions, thou didst become an unblemished mirror, ever receiving the radiance of the Spirit, wherefore vanquished, the tempter who taught our ancestors the weakness of evil in the garden was put to shame by thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having acquired Christ God, Who is Wisdom, abiding in thy heart, thou didst trample beneath thy beautiful feet the foolish sage of evil who attempted to deceive thee with divers ideas, O divinely wise Paul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As a receptacle of the Light, a son of the Day, as though he were a lion thou didst deceive the prince of darkness who assailed thee with earthquakes and a rain of stones, seeking to terrify thee with his arrogance, and raging against thee, O Paul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Incarnate of thee, O Ever-virgin maiden Bride of God, the beginningless Word, Who through thee lowered Himself to lie as a babe in a manger of dumb beasts, hath delivered from irrationality our race, that of the first Adam who was driven from Eden.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p7 Ode 5 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The sea monster spat forth Jonah as it had received him, * like a babe from the womb: * while the Word, having dwelt in the Virgin and taken flesh, * came forth from her yet kept her incorrupt. * For being Himself not subject to decay. * He preserved His Mother free from all harm.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`As the Savior, Christ our God fed a vast multitude with a few loaves of bread, so did Paul, the initiate of Christ's mysteries, with the little water contained in a tiny cruse gladden a multitude, filling them to satiety with its abundance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`By thy supplications, O wondrous one, thou didst cause burning heat to cease and lifted a dire famine; and with waters poured forth from on high thou dost irrigate the earth and give drink to its dry furrows, causing it to put forth richly, multiplying the crops thereof.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Amid thy pangs thou didst receive the life which is devoid of pain, and thou causest the affliction of cruel pangs to cease for those who with faith ask to receive healing from thee, O all-honored one, thou adornment of the fathers. Wherefore; loose thou the pangs of my body and soul, I pray thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Word of the Father, the timeless Son of God, the pre-eternal Offspring of the pure and divine maiden and Mother, Who as man became a babe and as God is uncontainable, is now contained by the cave. Wherefore, marveling, we all worship the great mystery.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ode 6 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Scorning the impious decree of the godless one, * the children brought up together in godliness * feared not the threat of fire, * but standing in the midst of the flames, they sang: * “O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Shining forth like the sun, thou didst straightway illumine the East, and ascending thy pillar, standing as in the midst of the heavens, thou hast gladdened the whole world with thy teachings, crying: O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst withdraw, fleeing the billows of the world, and, making thine abode in the wilderness, as saith the Psalms, O divinely blessed one, thou didst receive God in thy heart, Who preserved thee with angelic protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With spiritual eyes thou didst behold the tortures of the next world, and pained in heart by thy loving soul, thou didst ever water thyself with tears, not like David, who only at night drenched his couch with tears.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The Incorporeal One is become incarnate, the Timeless One cometh under time, The Lord Who wrappeth the earth in mist is wrapped in swaddling bands for our sake, Himself appearing, past understanding, unchanged through her who knew not a man.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p9 Ode 7 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The furnace moist with dew showed forth an image * of a wonder past nature, * for it burned not the youths whom it had received; * neither did the fire of the Godhead consume the Virgin * when it descended into her womb. * Wherefore, chanting, we sing: * Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`With David thou didst chant a melodious hymn, well-tuned on all strings, saying: “O King of all, Thy consolations have divinely gladdened my soul by Thy loving gesture!” Wherefore, rejoicing, thou didst cry aloud: Let all creation bless the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Granting thee that which is contrary to carnal love and preserving thee from thy youth with His right hand, the Creator thrice divinely fed thee with greens who from childhood trampled down every lust; and by the hand of an angel He gave such to thee who, loving the life of the angels, hast been glorified, O God-bearing Paul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The three men, bound and condemned, were able to escape execution as deserters from general service, invisibly freed from their bonds by thy name, O all-glorious father; for thou didst deliver those in fetters from misfortunes, and they were borne away by the hand alone of Him Who holdeth all things.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`She who gave birth to the Sun of righteousness by a star summoneth the magi with gold, myrrh and frankincense, who worship Him Who hath newly and immutably become a babe. Him the shepherds magnified and the multitude of angels hymned, glorifying Him as God in essence and man by nature.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p10 Ode 8 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]},9:{irmos:{text:`A strange and most wondrous mystery do I see: * the cave is heaven; * the Virgin the throne of the cherubim; * the manger a room, in which Christ God, * whom nothing can contain, is laid. * Whom we praise and magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 irmos`},sourceLabel:`Irmos`,label_inline:!0},items:[{text:`Thy boldness crieth out to God, and thou hast wrought wondrous works even after thy departure unto Him; for thou hast freed many from divers infirmities by the oil of thine effulgence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Possessed of a most radiant soul, O venerable one, and wholly anointed as with the ointment of grace, by oil thou dispellest demons, cleansing lepers and those confused in mind, and causing cruel scabs to fall away.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Stumbling, Satan the most wicked one, falleth headlong like a most savage wild beast, upon beholding thee stretching forth the oil of thy lamp like myrrh for the healing of divers ailments; and, seized with fear, he hath been vanquished.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 troparion 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`In latter times, O Mother who knew not a man, thou didst conceive in thy womb the Son Whom the Father begat incorruptibly before time. Him do the heavens show forth by the star and the earth by a cave in the ground.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Ode 9 Theotokion`},label:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`,label_inline:!0}]}}}],kontakia_ode3:[{text:`From thy youth, O wise one, thou didst manfully desire that which passeth under-standing * and didst forsake the tumult of the world. * For thy divine way of life thou didst become a dwelling-place of the Trinity, * illumining those who have recourse to thee with faith. ** Wherefore, we cry out: Rejoice, O most noetically rich Paul!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Kontakion of the venerable one (after Ode III)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`To thee, the champion leader ...`,tone:8}],sessional_ode3:[{text:`Having acquired a mind free of the passions, thou wast a most dutiful servant of God, and didst free from delusion those who hearkened well unto thee; and having suffered as priest and martyr, O Eleutherius, thou hast received a twofold crown. Pray thou, that we be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (Eleutherius)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone I`,spec_mel:`Thy tomb, O Savior ...`,tone:1},{text:`Steered by the power of the Almighty, and impelled by the mast and sail of the Cross, thou didst pass easily through the storm of life and hast reached the truly divine havens; and having acquired a heavy cargo of the virtues, thou didst bring it to the Master of all, and didst hear from Him: Well done, O good servant. Wherefore, O blessed Paul, entreat Christ God, that He grant remission of sins unto those who with love honor thy holy memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional (Paul)`},label:`glory`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Sessional Hymn of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,spec_mel:`Of the Wisdom ...`,tone:8},{text:`Having fallen into the temptations of great cunning laid for me by enemies visible and invisible, caught in the tempest of my countless offenses, I make haste to the haven of thy goodness, O pure one, as to my fervent assistance and protection. Wherefore, O most pure one, pray thou earnestly to Him Who becameth incarnate of thee without seed on behalf of all thy servants who unceasingly entreat thee, O most pure one, ever beseeching Him to grant remission of sins unto those who hymn thy glory as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion, in Tone VIII`,tone:8},{text:`The Virgin and Mother of the Redeemer, standing before the Cross and lamenting with tears of anguish, cried out maternally: What strange and most glorious thing is this that I behold, O my Son? Thou that pourest forth dispassion upon all men art crucified upon a Cross between two condemned thieves, Thy side pierced, and Thou art given gall to drink by hands which Thou Thyself hast made! But arise and grant remission of sins unto those who hymn Thy divine Passion with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p5 Ode III sessional Stavrotheotokion`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,label:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`,label_inline:!0}],kontakia_ode6:[{text:`We all praise thee as the adornment of priests * and the proclamation of passion-bearers, * O venerable hieromartyr Eleutherius, * and we entreat thee: * From multifarious misfortunes free those * who celebrate thy memory with love, ** praying unceasingly for us all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Kontakion of the holy hieromartyr (after Ode VI)`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone II`,spec_mel:`The steadfast ...`,tone:2},{text:`As Thou alone art the compassionate God Who is the Lover of mankind, O loving Bestower of life, look Thou upon the darkness of my soul, and with Thine omnipotent right hand free me from the oppression of the passions, O Word, that I may hymn Thy hierarch Eleutherius; for, truly acknowledging Thee from his mother's womb, he became sanctified, and like Samuel was offered by his sacred mother to Thee, the Creator, unceasingly praying for us all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p8 Ikos of the holy hieromartyr`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Ikos`,label_inline:!0}],exapostilarion_glory:{text:`As David saith, thou didst flourish in the house of the word like a palm-tree, O venerable father, now multiplying the fruits of thy labors a hundredfold: Wherefore, drowning the hordes of the demons in the showers of thy tears, O blessed Paul, thou hast received honor from Christ O all-wise one, and a crown of victory, and the grace of rich and abundant miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Exapostilarion of the venerable one, at Glory`},sourceLabel:`Exapostilarion from the Oktoechos; Glory ..., Exapostilarion of the venerable one`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,spec_mel:`With the disciples let us ascend ...`},exapostilarion_closer:{text:`He Who on high is glorified as God by the angels, O pure one, ineffably dwelt with those below without leaving the bosom of the Father; and thou wast the cause of His salvation, inexpressibly lending flesh to Him of thy pure blood, O pure one. Him do thou beseech, that He grant deliverance from transgressions to thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p11 Exapostilarion Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion`}},liturgy:{order:[`troparia`,`kontakia`],troparia:[{text:`As thou didst share in the ways of the apostles * and didst occupy their throne, * thou didst find thine activity to be a passage to divine vision, * O divinely inspired one. * Wherefore, ordering the word of truth, * thou didst suffer for the Faith even to the shedding of thy blood, ** O Hieromartyr Eleutherius, entreat Christ God, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p12 Troparion of the holy hieromartyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone IV`,tone:4},{text:`O all-glorious Paul, * we hymn thee as one who dwelleth together with the bodiless hosts * and as a companion of all the venerable, * we beseech thee, to ever pray thou for us, ** that we may find mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p12 Troparion of the venerable one at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`Troparion of the venerable one, in Tone IV`,tone:4}],kontakia:[{text:`We all praise thee as the adornment of priests * and the proclamation of passion-bearers, * O venerable hieromartyr Eleutherius, * and we entreat thee: * From multifarious misfortunes free those * who celebrate thy memory with love, ** praying unceasingly for us all.`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p12 Kontakion of the holy hieromartyr at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Eleutherius`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the holy hieromartyr, in Tone II`,tone:2},{text:`From thy youth, O wise one, thou didst manfully desire that which passeth under-standing * and didst forsake the tumult of the world. * For thy divine way of life thou didst become a dwelling-place of the Trinity, * illumining those who have recourse to thee with faith. ** Wherefore, we cry out: Rejoice, O most noetically rich Paul!`,tier:2,src:{file:`12-15.pdf`,locus:`p12 Kontakion of the venerable one at Liturgy`},label:`plain`,saint:`Paul of Latros`,sourceLabel:`Kontakion of the venerable one, in Tone VIII`,tone:8}]}}]}};export{e as default};